('GRE_2','GRE_2_3807','emergency','ɪ''mɝdʒənsi','ɪ''mɜːdʒ(ə)nsɪ','[n] 紧急情况, 突然事件, 非常时刻, 紧急事件','Lifeguards are trained to deal with emergencies.  救生员接受过应对紧急情况的训练。'),
('GRE_2','GRE_2_3808','gripe','ɡraɪp','graɪp','[n] 紧握, 柄, 把手, 控制, 苦恼',''),
('GRE_2','GRE_2_3809','catatonic',',kætə''tɑnɪk','kætə''tɒnɪk','[n] 紧张性精神症患者','With an almost catatonic concentration, almost without blinking or licking my lips, I read the entire book from first to last word without stopping.  近乎精神紧张，我没眨眼或舔嘴唇，停也没停就把整本书看完了。'),
('GRE_2','GRE_2_3810','exertion','ɪɡ''zɝʃən','ɪɡ''zɜːʃn','[n] 尽力, 努力, 发挥, 行使, 运用','The afternoon’s exertions had left us feeling exhausted.  下午太劳累了，我们感到精疲力竭。'),
('GRE_2','GRE_2_3811','tenor','''tɛnɚ','''tenə','[n] 进程, 路程, 要旨, 大意, 男高音, 誊本','Arthur Davies sings the tenor solo.  阿瑟•戴维斯表演男高音独唱。'),
('GRE_2','GRE_2_3812','offense','ə''fɛns','ə''fens','[n] 进攻','The Bears are going to have to work on their offense this season.  本赛季熊队必须要加强进攻了。'),
('GRE_2','GRE_2_3813','gumption','''ɡʌmpʃən','''gʌm(p)ʃ(ə)n','[n] 进取心, 气概','In part, that''s because the economic power of fuhyo — rumor — is a force that even gumption and initiative can''t combat.  从某种意义上来说，这是因为有害谣言的经济破坏力是进取心和主动性都无法压倒的。'),
('GRE_2','GRE_2_3814','ingress','''ɪnɡrɛs','''ɪngres','[n] 进入, 入口处, 准许进入',''),
('GRE_2','GRE_2_3815','dilemma','dɪˈlemə','dɪ''lemə; daɪ-','[n] 进退两难的局面, 困难的选择','a moral dilemma  道德上进退两难的窘境'),
('GRE_2','GRE_2_3816','purlieus','','','[n] 近郊；邻近地区',''),
('GRE_2','GRE_2_3817','myopia','maɪ''opɪə','maɪ''əʊpɪə','[n] 近视','Serious eye strain can lead to persistent headaches, muscle pain in the head, neck and upper back, as well as long term problems like myopia.  严重的眼疲劳会导致长期的头痛，头部，颈部和上发背的肌肉疼痛，也可能会引起一个长期的问题近视。'),
('GRE_2','GRE_2_3818','ascetic','ə''sɛtɪk','ə''setɪk','[n] 禁欲者, 苦行修道者',''),
('GRE_2','GRE_2_3819','asceticism','ə''sɛtɪsɪzəm','ə''setɪsɪz(ə)m','[n] 禁欲主义, 苦行','Puritanism is based on autonomy of local congregations, simplicity of worship, asceticism, egalitarianism, and a call to the past with restoration of original values through purification.  清教主义是建立在对地方集合，崇拜的简化，禁欲主义，平均主义以及通过净化召唤回具有原始价值过去的自治上。'),
('GRE_2','GRE_2_3820','embargo','ɪm''bɑrɡo','em''bɑːgəʊ; ɪm-','[n] 禁止出入港口, 禁运','The United Nations imposed an arms embargo against the country.  联合国对该国施行了武器贸易禁运。'),
('GRE_2','GRE_2_3821','stalk','stɔk','stɔːk','[n] 茎, 柄, 梗, 秆','celery stalks  芹菜茎'),
('GRE_2','GRE_2_3822','stem','stɛm','stem','[n] 茎, 干, 词干, 茎干','long-stemmed wine glasses  高脚酒杯'),
('GRE_2','GRE_2_3823','longitude','''lɑndʒətud','''lɒn(d)ʒɪtjuːd; ''lɒŋgɪ-','[n] 经度, 经线','The town lies at longitude 12˚ east.  这个镇位于东经12度。'),
('GRE_2','GRE_2_3824','empiricism','ɛm''pɪrə''sɪzəm','em''pɪrɪsɪz(ə)m','[n] 经验主义, 经验论, 庸医的医术',''),
('GRE_2','GRE_2_3825','consternation',',kɑnstɚ''neʃən','kɒnstə''neɪʃ(ə)n','[n] 惊愕, 恐怖, 惊惶失措','The government’s plans have caused considerable consternation among many Americans.  政府的计划在许多美国人中间引起了相当大的恐慌。'),
('GRE_2','GRE_2_3826','horror','''hɔrɚ','''hɒrə','[n] 惊骇, 恐怖, 惨事, 极端厌恶','You should have seen the look of horror on his face.  你真该看看他脸上恐惧的表情。'),
('GRE_2','GRE_2_3827','panic','''pænɪk','''pænɪk','[n] 惊慌, 恐慌, 没有理由的','a feeling of sheer panic  惊恐万分的感觉'),
('GRE_2','GRE_2_3828','prodigy','''prɑdədʒi','''prɒdɪdʒɪ','[n] 惊人的事物, 天才(特指神童), 奇观, 奇事','The Russian tennis prodigy is well on the way to becoming the youngest world champion of all time.  这位俄罗斯网球奇才已很有望成为历史上最年轻的世界冠军。'),
('GRE_2','GRE_2_3829','quintessence','kwɪn''tɛsns','kwɪn''tes(ə)ns','[n] 精萃, 精华, 典范','He was the quintessence of all that Eva most deeply loathed.  他是个典型的伊娃深深憎恶之人。'),
('GRE_2','GRE_2_3830','moxie','''mɑksi','''mɒksɪ','[n] 精力, 勇气, 胆量','He’s a small kid, but he has plenty of moxie.  他是个小孩，但浑身是胆。'),
('GRE_2','GRE_2_3831','psychosis','saɪ''kosɪs','saɪ''kəʊsɪs','[n] 精神','He may have some kind of neurosis or psychosis later in life.  他在以后的生活中可能会有某种神经官能症或精神错乱。'),
('GRE_2','GRE_2_3832','spunk','spʌŋk','spʌŋk','[n] 精神, 勇气, 胆量, 火星, 引火木柴','She had a lot of spunk.  她很有胆量。'),
('GRE_2','GRE_2_3833','psychiatry','saɪ''kaɪətri','saɪ''kaɪətrɪ','[n] 精神病学, 精神病治疗法',''),
('GRE_2','GRE_2_3834','insanity','ɪn''sænəti','ɪn''sænətɪ','[n] 精神错乱, 疯狂, 愚顽','The court acquitted Campbell on the grounds of temporary insanity.  法庭以坎贝尔一时精神错乱为由判他无罪释放。'),
('GRE_2','GRE_2_3835','lunacy','''lunəsi','''luːnəsɪ','[n] 精神失常, 精神病',''),
('GRE_2','GRE_2_3836','proficient','prə''fɪʃnt','prə''fɪʃ(ə)nt','[n] 精通','As with the transition from competent to proficient, the transition to Expert is also non-linear.  正如从“胜任”到“精通”的转变一样，转变为“专家”也是非线性的过程。'),
('GRE_2','GRE_2_3837','refinement','rɪ''faɪnmənt','rɪ''faɪnm(ə)nt','[n] 精致, (言谈, 举止等的)文雅, 精巧','Older cars inevitably lack the latest safety refinements.  较老式的汽车难免缺乏最新的安全改进。'),
('GRE_2','GRE_2_3838','epigram','''epiɡræm','''epɪgræm','[n] 警句, 讽刺短诗',''),
('GRE_2','GRE_2_3839','tocsin','''tɑksɪn','''tɒksɪn','[n] 警钟, 警报','The Government, with an army in its hand, hesitated; the night was almost upon them, and the Saint-Merry tocsin began to make itself heard.  政府手里有着军队，却还在犹豫不决，天快黑了，人们开始听到圣美里的警钟。'),
('GRE_2','GRE_2_3840','purge','pɝdʒ','pɜːdʒ','[n] 净化, 清除, 泻药','The army have called for a more thorough purge of people associated with the late president.  军队已要求对已故总统的关联人物来一次更彻底地清除。'),
('GRE_2','GRE_2_3841','purgation','pɝ''geʃən','pɜː''geɪʃ(ə)n','[n] 净化, 洗涤, 清洗, 洗罪',''),
('GRE_2','GRE_2_3842','arena','ə''rinə','ə''riːnə','[n] 竞技场, 舞台','a sports arena  运动场'),
('GRE_2','GRE_2_3843','emulation',',ɛmjə''leʃən',',emjʊ''leɪʃən','[n] 竞争, 效法','His spirit of assiduous study is worthy of emulation.  他刻苦钻研的精神， 值得效法。'),
('GRE_2','GRE_2_3844','obeisance','o''bisns','ə(ʊ)''beɪs(ə)ns','[n] 敬礼, 鞠躬, 顿首, 服从','While he was still young and strong all paid obeisance to him.  他年轻力壮时所有人都对他毕恭毕敬。'),
('GRE_2','GRE_2_3845','awe','ɔ','ɔː','[n] 敬畏','He felt great awe for the landscape.  景色令他赞叹不已。'),
('GRE_2','GRE_2_3846','homage','''hɑmɪdʒ','''hɒmɪdʒ','[n] 敬意','The film pays homage to Martin Scorsese’s ‘Mean Streets’.  该影片向马丁·斯科塞斯的《穷街陋巷》致敬。'),
('GRE_2','GRE_2_3847','entanglement','ɪn''tæŋɡlmənt','ɪn''tæŋg(ə)lm(ə)nt; en-','[n] 纠缠','...a military and political entanglement the president probably doesn''t want.  …一个总统很可能不想要的军事政治纠葛。'),
('GRE_2','GRE_2_3848','rectification',',rɛktəfə''keʃən',',rektɪfɪ''keɪʃən','[n] 纠正, 整顿, 校正, 精馏, 整流','...the rectification of an injustice.  ...一种不公正的矫正。'),
('GRE_2','GRE_2_3849','dimple','''dɪmpəl','''dɪmp(ə)l','[n] 酒窝, 涟漪','Bess spoke up, smiling so that her dimples showed.  贝丝大声发言，微笑着，使脸上露出了两个酒窝。'),
