('GRE_2','GRE_2_3870','playwright','''pleraɪt','''pleɪraɪt','[n] 剧作家','The playwright does something remarkable in this scene, but without any impression of straining after an effect.  剧作家在这场中有许多惊人妙笔，但并不给人留下竭力追求表面效果的印象。'),
('GRE_2','GRE_2_3871','appropriation','ə,proprɪ''eʃən','ə,prəʊprɪ''eɪʃ(ə)n','[n] 据为己有, 占有, 挪用(只指定用途的一笔), 拨款','The government raised defence appropriations by 12 percent.  政府将国防拨款提高了12%。'),
('GRE_2','GRE_2_3872','hurricane','hʌrɪˌken','''hʌrɪk(ə)n; -keɪn','[n] 飓风, 狂风','The hurricane devastated a large section of the coast.  飓风毁坏了沿海地区的大部分。'),
('GRE_2','GRE_2_3873','sawdust','''sɔ''dʌst','''sɔːdʌst','[n] 锯屑','...a layer of sawdust.  …一层锯末。'),
