('GRE_2','GRE_2_6295','peculate','''pekjuleit','''pekjʊleɪt','[v] 挪用, 盗用','It means that we can modify and peculate the code.  这意味着我们可以盗用或修改其代码。'),
('GRE_2','GRE_2_6296','ascend','ə''sɛnd','ə''send','[v] 攀登, 上升','The plane ascended rapidly.  飞机迅速爬升。'),
('GRE_2','GRE_2_6297','hover','''hʌvɚ','''hɒvə','[v] 盘旋','After rising through the air it stops to hover outside the window of a building several storeys high.  在空气中上升后，它在一幢几层楼高的建筑物的窗前停止升高，进入盘旋状态。'),
('GRE_2','GRE_2_6298','hobble','''hɑbl','''hɒb(ə)l','[v] 蹒跚','The Spain midfielder missed the midweek Champions League victory over Porto because of the hamstring problem which had seen him hobble out of the win against Burnley.  西班牙中场在上周与伯尔利的比赛中蹒跚下场，正因为这次腿部的伤势使他错过了周中对阵波尔图的冠军杯比赛。'),
('GRE_2','GRE_2_6299','adjudicate','ə''dʒudɪket','ə''dʒuːdɪkeɪt','[v] 判决, 宣判, 裁定','The Dean adjudicates any faculty disputes.  系主任裁决教师间的纠纷。'),
('GRE_2','GRE_2_6300','rave','rev','reɪv','[v] 咆哮','He was still ranting and raving the next morning.  第二天上午他仍在大叫大嚷。'),
('GRE_2','GRE_2_6301','growl','ɡraʊl','graʊl','[v] 咆哮, 发牢骚地说','‘Get out of my way,’ he growled.  “滚开。”他低声咆哮道。'),
('GRE_2','GRE_2_6302','indemnify','ɪn''dɛmnɪfaɪ','ɪn''demnɪfaɪ','[v] 赔偿','They agreed to indemnify the taxpayers against any loss.  他们同意赔偿纳税人的任何损失。'),
('GRE_2','GRE_2_6303','repudiate','rɪ''pjudɪet','rɪ''pjuːdɪeɪt','[v] 批判','Leaders urged people to turn out in large numbers to repudiate the violence.  领导们力劝人们集体出面来声讨该暴力。'),
('GRE_2','GRE_2_6304','excoriate',',ɛks''kɔrɪet','ɪk''skɔːrɪeɪt; eks-','[v] 批判','an excoriating review in ‘The Times’  《泰晤士报》刊登的一篇措辞严厉的评论'),
('GRE_2','GRE_2_6305','authorize','''ɔθəraɪz','''ɔ:θəraiz','[v] 批准','an authorized biography  授权传记'),
('GRE_2','GRE_2_6306','split','splɪt','splɪt','[v] 劈开, (使)裂开, 分裂, 分离','It was feared that the issue would split the church.  人们担心这一问题会导致教会分裂。'),
('GRE_2','GRE_2_6307','yaw','jɔ','jɔː','[v] 偏航','As the plane climbed to 370 feet, it started yawing.  飞机攀升到370英尺高时开始偏航。'),
('GRE_2','GRE_2_6308','wangle','''wæŋgl','''wæŋg(ə)l','[v] 骗取',''),
('GRE_2','GRE_2_6309','blanch','blæntʃ','blɑːn(t)ʃ','[v] 漂白, 使变白, 遮断阳光发白','Patrick visibly blanched.  帕特里克的脸色明显地变得苍白。'),
('GRE_2','GRE_2_6310','mollify','''mɑlɪfaɪ','''mɒlɪfaɪ','[v] 平息','He attempted to mollify her.  他想安抚她。'),
('GRE_2','GRE_2_6311','persecute','''pɝsɪkjut','''pɜːsɪkjuːt','[v] 迫害','The Puritans left England to escape being persecuted.  清教徒离开了英国以躲避迫害。'),
('GRE_2','GRE_2_6312','undermine','''ʌndɚ''maɪn','ʌndə''maɪn','[v] 破坏','The continued fighting threatens to undermine efforts to negotiate an agreement.  持续的战斗有可能破坏通过谈判达成协议的努力。'),
('GRE_2','GRE_2_6313','infringe','ɪn''frɪndʒ','ɪn''frɪn(d)ʒ','[v] 破坏, 侵犯, 违反','A backup copy of a computer program does not infringe copyright.  计算机程序的备份不侵犯版权。'),
('GRE_2','GRE_2_6314','rupture','''rʌptʃɚ','''rʌptʃə','[v] 破裂, 裂开, 断绝(关系等), 割裂','The pipe will rupture at its weakest point.  管道最薄弱的地方会破裂的。'),
('GRE_2','GRE_2_6315','expire','ɪk''spaɪɚ','ɪk''spaɪə; ek-','[v] 期满, 终止, 呼气, 断气, 届满','The chairman’s term of office has already expired.  主席任期已满。'),
('GRE_2','GRE_2_6316','cozen','''kʌzən','''kʌz(ə)n','[v] 欺骗, 瞒','What devil was ''t that thus hath cozen''d you at hoodman-blind?  是什么魔鬼如此欺骗了你这个瞎眼的女人？'),
('GRE_2','GRE_2_6317','enlightened','ɪn''laɪtnd','ɪn''laɪt(ə)nd','[v] 启迪','She brought me to the field and enlightened me.  她将我领进了这个领域，给我启迪。'),
('GRE_2','GRE_2_6318','edify','','''edɪfaɪ','[v] 启发','If you study my project, it might edify your mind.  “我想是你把我看成自我主义者了。” 汤姆说，“如果你研究一下我的工程，你的思想会受到启发。'),
('GRE_2','GRE_2_6319','spurn','spə:n','spɜːn','[v] 弃绝','She spurned all offers of help.  她骄傲地拒绝一切帮助。'),
('GRE_2','GRE_2_6320','slink','slɪŋk','slɪŋk','[v] 潜逃',''),
('GRE_2','GRE_2_6321','repatriate',',ri''petrɪet','riː''pætrɪeɪt; -''peɪ-','[v] 遣返','After the war, prisoners were repatriated.  战后，战俘被遣返。'),
('GRE_2','GRE_2_6322','decry','dɪ''kraɪ','dɪ''kraɪ','[v] 谴责','It may be tempting for some to decry incentives as nothing but a poisonous fruit of Con-Lib responsibility thinking.  对一些人谴责激励机制只是作为“新政治”责任思考的毒果这样的结论本身是很冒险的。'),
('GRE_2','GRE_2_6323','ravish','''rævɪʃ','''rævɪʃ','[v] 强夺','She''ll never know how close she came to being dragged off and ravished.  她永远都不会知道她差一点就被人拖走强暴了。'),
('GRE_2','GRE_2_6324','importune',',ɪmpɔr''tun',',ɪmpɔː''tjuːn','[v] 强求','One can no longer walk the streets without seeing beggars importuning passersby.  走在这些街道上总能看到乞丐纠缠行人乞讨。'),
('GRE_2','GRE_2_6325','plunder','''plʌndɚ','''plʌndə','[v] 抢劫','The rich provinces of Asia Minor were plundered by the invaders.  小亚细亚的富饶地区遭到侵略者的劫掠。'),
('GRE_2','GRE_2_6326','extort','ɪk''stɔrt','ɪk''stɔːt; ek-','[v] 敲诈, 逼取, 强取, 勒索','Corrupt government officials were extorting money from him.  腐败的政府官员那时正向他勒索钱财。'),
('GRE_2','GRE_2_6327','declaim','dɪ''klem','dɪ''kleɪm','[v] 巧辩, 演讲, 高声朗读',''),
('GRE_2','GRE_2_6328','whittle','''wɪtl','''wɪt(ə)l','[v] 切, 削, 削减, 损害','We need to whittle down the list of guests for the party.  我们需要缩减聚会的客人名单。'),
('GRE_2','GRE_2_6329','sever','''sɛvɚ','''sevə','[v] 切断','Martin’s hand was severed in the accident.  马丁的一只手在事故中被切断了。'),
('GRE_2','GRE_2_6330','sunder','''sʌndɚ','''sʌndə','[v] 切开, 分离','The city is being sundered by racial tension.  该城市因民族关系紧张而正在分裂。'),
