('PEPGaoZhong_11','PEPGaoZhong_11_189','Telemachus','','ti''leməkəs; tə-','忒勒玛科斯（Odysseus 和 Penelope 之子）','Telemachus, in Homer’s story of the Odyssey, tipped his vehicle vertically against a wall, while others removed their wheels in the evening (Gordon, 1978) to prevent warping.  荷马史诗里的忒勒马科斯在晚上把他的车竖直靠墙，而其他的车则被卸去了轮毂以防止变形（戈登，1978）。'),
