('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_37','culture','''kʌltʃɚ','''kʌltʃə','[n] 文化,文明','We speak Danish at home so that the boys don’t lose touch with their language and culture.  我们在家说丹麦语，这样男孩子们就不会脱离他们的语言和文化。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_38','infant','''ɪnfənt','''ɪnf(ə)nt','[n] 婴儿','An infant’s skin is very sensitive.  幼儿的皮肤非常敏感。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_39','left','lɛft','left','[adj] 左边的; [adv] 向左; [n] 左边','She held out her left hand.  她伸出左手。'),
