('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_760','seventeenth',',sɛvn''tinθ',',sevən''tiːnθ','[num] 第十七,十七分之一','In the UK, too, religion seems to be generating an animosity not seen since the seventeenth century.  在英国也是同样，似乎自从十七世纪之后，信仰就不再产生憎恨和仇视了一般。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_761','skin','skɪn','skɪn','[n] 皮肤','She had thick black hair and smooth dark skin.  她一头浓密的黑发，皮肤黝黑光滑。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_762','shelter','''ʃɛltɚ','''ʃeltə','[n] 掩蔽,庇护所; [v] 掩蔽,躲避','The men took shelter in a bombed-out farmhouse.  那些男人躲在一间被炸毁的农舍里。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_763','inside','''ɪn''saɪd','ɪn''saɪd','[ad&prep] 在…里面,少于; [n&a] 里面(的)','He concealed the key inside his tie.  他把钥匙藏在领带里面。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_764','rainfall','''ren''fɔl','''reɪnfɔːl','[n] 降雨,降雨量','We’ve had a long period of low rainfall.  我们已有很长一段时间雨量偏低。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_765','try','traɪ','traɪ','[v&n] 尝试,试验','Let’s have a rest and then we’ll try again.  我们休息一下，然后再试。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_766','something','''sʌmθɪŋ','''sʌmθɪŋ','[pron] 某事,某物; [adv] 有点,大约','There’s something in my eye.  我眼睛里有什么东西。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_767','gain','ɡen','geɪn','[n&v] 获得,增益','After gaining independence in 1957, it was renamed ‘Ghana’.  1957年获得独立后，该国改名为“加纳”。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_768','habit','''hæbɪt','''hæbɪt','[n] 习惯,习性','Regular exercise is a good habit.  经常锻炼是个好习惯。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_769','ceramic','sə''ræmɪk','sɪ''ræmɪk','[adj] 陶器的; [n] 陶瓷制品','This takes a little while to switch all of your plastic storage containers over to ceramic, glass or stainless steel but its definitely worthwhile.  把你所有的塑料存储容器换成陶瓷的，玻璃的，或者不锈钢的你会浪费你一点时间。 但这绝对是值得的。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_770','famous','''feməs','''feɪməs','[adj] 著名的,出名的,','a famous actor  著名演员'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_771','report','rɪ''pɔrt','rɪ''pɔːt','[n] 报告; [v] 报导,汇报','According to recent news reports , two of the victims are Americans.  根据近期的新闻报道，受害者中有两名是美国人。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_772','moral','''mɔrəl','''mɒr(ə)l','[adj] 道德(上)的,精神的','It is easy to have an opinion on a moral issue like the death penalty for murder.  对于判谋杀犯死刑这种涉及伦理道德的问题，有个观点并非难事。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_773','buy','baɪ','baɪ','[v] 买; [n] 购买,买卖','People say the judge had been bought by the Mafia.  人们都说法官被黑手党收买了。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_774','sleep','slip','sliːp','[vi&n] 睡,睡觉','I usually sleep on my back.  我一般仰卧着睡觉。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_775','decision','dɪ''sɪʒn','dɪ''sɪʒ(ə)n','[n] 决定,决议','Do you ever wonder if you made the right decision?  你怀疑过自己所作的决定是否正确吗？'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_776','stable','''stebl','''steɪb(ə)l','[adj] 稳定的','A wide base will make the structure much more stable.  宽大的底座会使结构牢固许多。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_777','remember','rɪ''mɛmbɚ','rɪ''membə','[v] 回忆起,记得','Do you remember Rosa Davies?  你记得罗莎·戴维斯吗？'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_778','series','''sɪriz','''sɪəriːz; -rɪz','[n] 系列,连续','the series of events that led to the outbreak of war  导致战争爆发的一系列事件'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_779','white','waɪt','wʌɪt','[n&ad] 白色(的)','The mayor is very popular among whites.  市长很受白人欢迎。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_780','due','du','djuː','[adj] 应有的; [n] 应得物','Any money due you will be sent by cheque through the post.  应该支付给你的款项将会以支票邮寄给你。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_781','song','sɔŋ','sɒŋ','[n] 歌(曲)','We used to listen to pop songs on the radio.  我们以前常常听收音机里播放的流行歌曲。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_782','soft','sɔft','sɒft','[adj] 软的,温和的','soft music  轻柔的音乐'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_783','lichen','''laɪkən','''laɪk(ə)n; ''lɪtʃ(ə)n','[n] 青苔,苔藓',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_784','stem','stɛm','stem','[n] 茎,干; [v] 起源于; [v] 堵住','long-stemmed wine glasses  高脚酒杯'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_785','car','kɑr','kɑː','[n] 汽车','Dan got out of the car and locked the door.  丹下了车，锁上车门。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_786','habitat','''hæbə''tæt','''hæbɪtæt','[n] 栖息地,住处','watching monkeys in their natural habitat  观察自然生活环境中的猴子'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_787','bur','bɚ','bə:','[n] 刺果',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_788','unique','jʊ''nik','juː''niːk','[adj] 唯一的,独特的','a unique opportunity to study these rare creatures  研究这些珍稀动物的难得机会'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_789','coastal','''kostl','''kəʊstl','[adj] 海岸的,沿海的','the coastal waters of Britain  英国的近海水域'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_790','whereas','''wɛr''æz','weər''æz','[conj] 然而,反之,尽管','The old system was fairly complicated whereas the new system is really very simple.  旧系统相当复杂，而新系统却很简单。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_791','consequence','''kɑnsəkwɛns','''kɒnsɪkw(ə)ns','[n] 结果','Her lawyer said she understood the consequences of her actions and was prepared to go to jail.  她的律师说她明白自己行为的后果并准备去坐牢。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_792','California',',kælɪ''fɔnjə',',kælɪ''fɔ:njə','[n] 加利福尼亚,加州','California borders the Pacific Ocean.  加利福尼亚州与太平洋毗连。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_793','trail','trel','treɪl','[n] 踪迹; [v] 追踪','The hunters lost the tiger’s trail in the middle of the jungle.  猎人们在丛林深处失去了老虎的踪迹。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_794','rely','rɪ''laɪ','rɪ''laɪ','[v] 依赖,依靠','They relied heavily on the advice of their professional advisers.  他们非常依赖专业顾问的建议。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_795','tribe','traɪb','traɪb','[n] 部落,部族','a tribe of Aborigines known as the Dolphin People  一个叫“海豚族”的澳大利亚土著部落'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_796','average','''ævərɪdʒ','''æv(ə)rɪdʒ','[n&a] 平均(的); [v] 平均','The December figures brought the annual average for 2001 up to 10.6 per cent.  12月的数据将2001年的年平均水平提升到10.6%。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_797','appropriate','əˈpropriɪt','ə''prəʊprɪət','[adj] 适当的','The timing of the announcement was particularly appropriate .  通告发布的时机很合适。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_798','here','hɪr','hɪə','[adv] 在这里,这时','What are you doing here?  你们在这里干什么？'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_799','nor','nɔr','nɔː; nə','[conj] 也不','He can neither read nor write (= he cannot read or write ).  他既不会读也不会写。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_800','external','ɪk''stɝnl','ɪk''stɜːn(ə)l; ek-','[n&a] 外部(的)','The open cities will be testing grounds for our external policies.  使开放城市成为对外政策的窗口。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_801','insert','''ɪnsɝt','ɪn''sɜːt','[v] 插入,嵌入','He took a small key from his pocket and slowly inserted it into the lock.  他从衣袋里掏出一把小钥匙，然后缓缓地将其插入锁孔里。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_802','stud','stʌd','stʌd','[v] 镶嵌,点缀','the park was studded with daisies'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_803','proportion','prə''pɔrʃən','prə''pɔːʃ(ə)n','[n] 比例','The proportion of women in the profession had risen to 17.3%.  从事那个职业的女性比例已经增长到17.3%。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_804','concept','''kɑnsɛpt','''kɒnsept','[n] 观念,概念','a new concept in business travel  商务旅行的新理念'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_805','geometric',',dʒiə''mɛtrɪk',',dʒɪə''metrɪk','[adj] 几何(学)的','a geometric design  几何图形设计'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_806','inner','''ɪnɚ','ɪnə','[adj] 内部的,里面的,内心的','an inner room  内室'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_807','resemble','rɪ''zɛmbl','rɪ''zemb(ə)l','[v] 象,类似于','It’s amazing how closely Brian and Steve resemble each other.  布赖恩和史蒂夫真是惊人地相像。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_808','scale','skel','skeɪl','[n] 规模,等级,比例','A structural survey revealed the full scale of the damage.  结构检验揭示了实际受损程度。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_809','dark','dɑrk','dɑːk','[n] 黑暗','my childish fear of the dark  我对黑暗孩子般的恐惧'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_810','intense','ɪn''tɛns','ɪn''tens','[adj] 强烈的,激烈的','Young people today are under intense pressure to succeed.  如今的年轻人面临要出人头地的巨大压力。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_811','dominate','''dɑmɪnet','''dɒmɪneɪt','[v] 支配,占优势','The industry is dominated by five multinational companies.  这个行业受五家跨国公司控制。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_812','wild','waɪld','waɪld','[adj] 野生的; [n] 荒野','{"COLLOINEXA":["wild animals"]}  野生动物'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_813','ton','tʌn','tʌn','[n] 吨,大量','I’ve got tons of work to do.  我有很多工作要做。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_814','ship','ʃɪp','ʃɪp','[n] 船; [v] 航运,载运','the ship’s captain  这艘船的船长'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_815','significance','sɪɡ''nɪfɪkəns','sɪg''nɪfɪk(ə)ns','[n] 意义,重要性','Ideas about the social significance of religion have changed over time.  有关宗教的社会意义的观念已随时间的流逝发生了改变。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_816','Mexico','''mɛksɪko','''meksɪkəʊ','[n] 墨西哥(拉丁美洲国家)','We want to prove that in Mexico.  我们要在墨西哥证明这一点。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_817','ordinary','''ɔrdnɛri','''ɔːdɪn(ə)rɪ; -d(ə)n-','[adj] 平常的,普通的','It’s just an ordinary camera.  这只是普通的相机。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_818','case','kes','keɪs','[n] 事例,情形','Tom’s career is a case in point (= a clear example of something that you are discussing or explaining ) .  汤姆的事业就是个明证。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_819','compose','kəm''poz','kəm''pəʊz','[v] 组成,写作','Barrington has composed the music for a new production of ‘A Midsummer Night’s Dream’.  巴林顿为新版的《仲夏夜之梦》谱了曲。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_820','Rome','rəum','rəum','[n] 罗马','He passed one night in Rome.  他在罗马过了一夜。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_821','permit','pɚ''mɪt','pə''mɪt','[n] 通行证,执照; [v] 许可,允许','Smoking is only permitted in the public lounge.  只允许在公共休息室里抽烟。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_822','capable','''kepəbl','''keɪpəb(ə)l','[adj] 有能力的,能干的','I don’t think he’s capable of murder.  我认为他没有能力杀人。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_823','fully','''fʊli','''fʊlɪ','[adv] 充分地,完全地','The restaurant is fully booked this evening.  今晚这家餐厅订满了。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_824','factual','''fæktʃuəl','''fæktʃʊəl; -tjʊəl','[adj] 事实的,实际的','Try to keep your account of events as factual as possible.  你要尽量如实地说明情况。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_825','tiny','''taɪni','''taɪnɪ','[adj] 很少的,微小的','a tiny community in the Midwest  中西部地区一个极小的社区'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_826','mouth','maʊθ','maʊθ','[n] 口,嘴','He lifted his glass to his mouth.  他把玻璃杯举到嘴边。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_827','connection','kə''nɛkʃən','kəˈnekʃn','[n] 连接,关系','Police have so far failed to establish a connection between the two murders.  到目前为止警方尚未确定两宗凶杀案之间有关联。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_828','Philadelphia',',filə''delfjə; -fiə',',filə''delfjə; -fiə','[n] 费城(美国宾西法尼亚州东南部港市)','And I loved Philadelphia.  而且，我喜欢费城。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_829','strength','strɛŋθ','streŋθ; streŋkθ','[n] 力,力量','I’m trying to build up my strength .  我在努力增强体力。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_830','professional','prə''fɛʃənl','prə''feʃ(ə)n(ə)l','[adj] 专业的,职业的','This business plan looks very professional.  这个商业计划看上去很有专业水平。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_831','virtually','ˈvɜrtʃuəli','ˈvəːtʃʊəli','[adv] 事实上,实质上','Virtually all cooking was done over coal-fired ranges.  事实上所有的烹饪都是在烧煤的炉灶上完成的。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_832','diet','''daɪət','''daɪət','[n] 通常所吃的食物,会议','She doesn’t eat a very healthy diet .  她的饮食不是很健康。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_833','phenomenon','fə''nɑmɪnən','fɪ''nɒmɪnən','[n] 现象','Homelessness is not a new phenomenon .  无家可归已不是什么新现象。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_834','permanent','''pɝmənənt','''pɜːm(ə)nənt','[adj] 永久的,持久的','He gave up a permanent job in order to freelance.  他放弃了固定工作，为的是当一名自由职业者。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_835','column','''kɑləm','''kɒləm','[n] 圆柱,专栏','He writes a weekly column for ‘The Times’.  他每周为《泰晤士报》写一篇专栏文章。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_836','warmer','''wɔrmɚ','''wɔːmə','[n] 使热的人,温热装置','a plate warmer  暖盘器'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_837','rest','rɛst','rest','[n&v] 休息','You look exhausted! Why don’t you take a rest?  你看上去累坏了！ 为什么不休息一下呢？'),
