('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_899','crack','kræk','kræk','[n] 裂缝,噼啪声; [v] (使)破裂','She opened the door a crack and peeped into the room.  她把门打开一条缝，往房间里偷看。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_900','dissolve','dɪ''zɑlv','dɪ''zɒlv','[v] 溶解,解散','Stir until the sugar dissolves.  一直搅拌到糖溶解掉。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_901','moisture','''mɔɪstʃɚ','''mɒɪstʃə','[n] 潮湿,湿气','Plants use their roots to absorb moisture from the soil.  植物利用根从土壤中吸收水分。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_902','vapor','ˈveɪpər','ˈveɪpə(r)','[n] 水蒸气','So, if you start with sodium vapor and chlorine gas, electron transfer will occur.  所以，如果从以钠蒸汽和氯气开始，电子传递就会发生了。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_903','equipment','ɪ''kwɪpmənt','ɪ''kwɪpm(ə)nt','[n] 装备,设备','a shop selling camping equipment  出售露营装备的商店'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_904','threaten','''θrɛtn','''θret(ə)n','[v] 恐吓,威胁','Postal workers are threatening a strike if they don’t receive a pay increase.  邮政工人威胁如果不加薪，他们就要罢工。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_905','succession','sək''sɛʃən','sək''seʃ(ə)n','[n] 连续,继承','She won the championship four times in succession.  她连续四次夺得冠军。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_906','annual','''ænjuəl','''ænjʊəl','[adj] 年度的','The school trip has become an annual event.  学校组织的旅行成了一年一度的活动。'),
