('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_1006','archaeological','','','[adj] 考古学的','The work fills (in) a gap which has hitherto existed in our archaeological literature.  这部著作填补了我国考古学文献中的一个空白。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_1007','universe','''junɪvɝs','''juːnɪvɜːs','[n] 宇宙,万物','Einstein''s equations showed the universe to be expanding.  爱因斯坦的方程式表明宇宙正在扩大。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_1008','impulse','''ɪmpʌls','''ɪmpʌls','[n] 冲动; [vt] 推动','The eye converts light signals to nerve impulses.  眼睛把光信号转变成神经冲动。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_1009','debris','də''bri','''debriː; ''deɪbriː','[n] 碎片,残骸','She was hit by flying debris from the blast.  她被爆炸产生的飞散碎片击中。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_1010','unknown',',ʌn''non','ʌn''nəʊn','[adj] 不知道的,未知的','The murderer’s identity remains unknown.  杀人凶手身份仍然不明。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_1011','tooth','tuθ','tuːθ','[n] 牙齿','Sugar is bad for your teeth.  糖对牙齿不好。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_1012','twenty','''twɛnti','''twentɪ','[num] 二十,二十个','a small village twenty miles from Nairobi  距内罗毕20英里的一个小村庄'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_1013','office','''ɔfɪs','''ɒfɪs','[n] 办公室,事务所','The department occupies an office just a mile from the White House.  该部门就在离白宫一英里远的地方有个办公楼。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_1014','wet','wɛt','wet','[adj] 湿的,多雨的','I’ve washed your shirt but it’s still wet.  我把你的衬衫洗过了，不过现在还是湿的。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_1015','texture','''tɛkstʃɚ','''tekstʃə','[n] 质地,(材料等的)结构','a designer who experiments with different colours and textures  尝试不同色彩和材质的设计师'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_1016','remarkable','rɪ''mɑrkəbl','rɪ''mɑːkəb(ə)l','[adj] 非凡的,显著的','She has made remarkable progress.  她取得了显著的进步。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_1017','enormous','ɪ''nɔrməs','ɪ''nɔːməs','[adj] 巨大的,庞大的','an enormous bunch of flowers  巨大的花束'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_1018','archaeologist',',ɑrkɪ''ɑlədʒɪst',',ɑːkɪ''ɒlədʒɪst','[n] 考古学家','In fact, she was an archaeologist.  其实她是一个考古学家。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_1019','neither','ˈniðɚ; ˈnaɪðɚ','ˈnaɪðə; ˈniːðə','[a&pron] 两者都不; [conj] 既不也不','Neither Oleg’s mother nor his father spoke English.  奥列格的父母都不会说英语。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_1020','formal','''fɔrml','''fɔːm(ə)l','[adj] 正式的,正规的','formal recognition of the reformed church  改革后的教会所获得的官方承认'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_1021','perspective','pɚ''spɛktɪv','pə''spektɪv','[n] 视角,观点,远景',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_1022','cetacean','sɪ''teʃən','sɪ''teɪʃn','[n] 鲸类动物','Based on what we know, I’d guess that cetacean culture is intermediate between humans and chimpanzees.  根据我们所知道的情况，我猜鲸目动物文化介于人类和黑猩猩之间。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_1023','sunlight','''sʌnlaɪt','''sʌnlaɪt','[n] 日光,阳光','The water sparkled in the bright sunlight.  水面在灿烂的阳光下闪闪发亮。'),
