('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_1847','switch','swɪtʃ','swɪtʃ','[n] 开关 vt转换, 转变','Where’s the light switch ?  电灯开关在哪儿？'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_1848','southwestern',',sauθ''westən',',saʊθ''westən','[adj] 西南的, 来自西南的','southwestern Colorado  科罗拉多的西南部'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_1849','infantile','''ɪnfəntaɪl','''ɪnf(ə)ntaɪl','[adj] 幼稚的，幼儿的','infantile jokes  幼稚的玩笑'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_1850','brother','''brʌðɚ','''brʌðə','[n] 兄弟','I have two brothers, William and Mark.  我有两个兄弟，威廉和马克。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_1851','crucial','''krʊʃəl','''kruːʃ(ə)l','[adj] 至关紧要的','The conservation of tropical forests is of crucial importance .  保护热带雨林至关重要。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_1852','amnesia','æm''niʒə','æm''niːzɪə','[n] 健忘症','We tend to think that a person who is a complete victim of amnesia is still the same person as before.  我们倾向于认为，一个彻底的健忘症患者，他与以前没有患病时仍然是同一个人。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_1853','toy','tɔɪ','tɒɪ','[n] 玩具','some toys for the baby  宝宝玩的一些玩具'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_1854','silent','''saɪlənt','''saɪlənt','[adj] 寂静的, 沉默的','The large house was silent and lonely.  这幢大房子寂静荒凉。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_1855','nutritional','njʊ''trɪʃənl','njuː''trɪʃənəl','[adj] 营养的,滋养的','Cooking vegetables for too long lessens their nutritional value.  烹饪蔬菜时间过长有损其营养价值。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_1856','taste','test','teɪst','[v] 品尝, 体验','It’s always best to keep tasting the food while you’re cooking it.  做菜的时候最好是边做边尝。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_1857','contradict','''kɑntrə''dɪkt','kɒntrə''dɪkt','[v] 同矛盾, 同抵触','The witness statements contradict each other and the facts remain unclear.  目击者的说法互相矛盾，真相依然未明。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_1858','verbal','''vɝbl','''vɜːb(ə)l','[adj] 口头的','They were jostled and subjected to a torrent of verbal abuse.  他们被推来搡去，并受到了潮水般的辱骂。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_1859','attach','ə''tætʃ','ə''tætʃ','[v] 缚上, 配属,隶属于','It is possible to attach executable program files to e-mail.  可以在电子邮件上附上可执行程序文件。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_1860','supplement','''sʌplɪmənt','''sʌplɪm(ə)nt','[n] 补充, 附录','vitamins and other dietary supplements  各种维生素和其他膳食补充剂'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_1861','delivery','dɪ''lɪvəri','dɪ''lɪv(ə)rɪ','[n] 递送,交付,传输','Most Indian restaurants offer free delivery.  大多数印度餐馆提供免费外送服务。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_1862','span','spæn','spæn','[n] 跨度v横越',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_1863','comparable','''kɑmpərəbl','''kɒmp(ə)rəb(ə)l','[adj] 可比较的, 比得上的','A car of comparable size would cost far more abroad.  同样大小的汽车在国外要贵得多。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_1864','satisfy','''sætɪsfaɪ','''sætɪsfaɪ','[v] 满足,使满意','Nothing I did would ever satisfy my father.  我做什么都不能让父亲满意。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_1865','panel','''pænl','''pæn(ə)l','[n] 面，板,专门小组','He assembled a panel of scholars to advise him.  他集结了一个学者小组为他出谋划策。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_1866','react','ri''ækt','rɪ''ækt','[v] 起反应, 起作用','He reacted angrily to the suggestion that he had lied.  说他撒谎，他非常生气。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_1867','freshwater','''frɛʃwɔtɚ','''freʃwɔːtə','[n] 淡水','There are bright prospects for freshwater fish farming.  淡水养鱼大有可为。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_1868','successive','sək''sɛsɪv','sək''sesɪv','[adj] 连续的, 接连的','The team has had five successive victories.  这支球队已经连胜五场了。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_1869','official','əˈfɪʃəl; oʊˈfɪʃəl','ə''fɪʃ(ə)l','[n] 官员; [adj] 官方的,正式的','You''d better declare the camera to the official.  你最好把照相机向海关官员申报纳税。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_1870','save','sev','seɪv','[v] 解救, 保存','We’ll save the rest of the food and have it later.  我们把剩下的食物留着以后吃。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_1871','appreciate','ə''priʃɪet','ə''priːʃɪeɪt; -sɪ-','[v] 赏识, 感激','Thanks ever so much for your help, I really appreciate it.  多谢你的帮助，我真的很感激。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_1872','friend','frɛnd','frend','[n] 朋友, 赞助者, 助手','Jerry, this is my friend Sue.  杰里，这是我的朋友休。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_1873','outline','''aʊtlaɪn','''aʊtlaɪn','[n] 大纲; [v] 描画轮廓,略述','a research proposal outline  研究计划梗概'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_1874','crustal','''krʌstl','''krʌstəl','[adj] 地壳的','As geologic forces pulled the crustal plate apart, new volcanoes formed in parts of the rift.  当地质作用力（试图）把地壳版块分开，版块开裂的一些地方就会形成新的火山。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_1875','threat','θrɛt','θret','[n] 恐吓, 凶兆, 威胁','Your threats don’t scare me.  你的那些威胁吓不倒我。'),
