('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_1968','genetic','dʒə''nɛtɪk','dʒɪ''netɪk','[adj] 遗传的, 起源的','genetic defects  遗传性缺陷'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_1969','page','','peɪdʒ','[n] 页,记录','The full address is given on page 15.  详细地址见第15页。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_1970','accumulator','ə''kjumjəletɚ','ə''kjuːmjʊleɪtə','[n] 蓄电池,积聚者','Here is our accumulator which has that nitrogen overpressure which upon loss of pressure in the core would automatically insert coolant into the core should there be a break.  这是我们的蓄电池，那已经氮过度增压,面临着在核心里压力的损失,那会自动的加入冷却剂到,核心去，然后就会产生一个破裂。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_1971','chief','tʃif','tʃiːf','[n] 首领; [adj] 主要的, 首要的','Most health chiefs believe the reforms have gone too far.  大多数卫生部领导人都觉得改革搞得过火了。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_1972','imitation',',ɪmɪ''teʃən','ɪmɪ''teɪʃ(ə)n','[n] 模仿, 效法','The remake of ‘Casablanca’ was a pale imitation (= something that is much less good than the thing it imitates ) of the original movie.  重拍的《卡萨布兰卡》远不如原版。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_1973','beneficial',',bɛnɪ''fɪʃl','benɪ''fɪʃ(ə)l','[adj] 有利的, 有益的','a drug that has a beneficial effect on the immune system  有益于免疫系统的一种药物'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_1974','lip','lɪp','lɪp','[n] 嘴唇','She had big eyes and full lips (= large and round lips ).  她眼睛大大的，嘴唇很丰满。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_1975','fertilizer','''fɝtəlaɪzɚ','''fɜːtɪlaɪzə','[n] 肥料','...farming without any purchased chemical, fertilizer or pesticide.  …不使用任何购买的化学品、肥料或杀虫剂的耕作。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_1976','rainwater','''renwɔtɚ','''reɪnwɔːtə','[n] 雨水','Farmers say they need less rainwater if they use fertilizer trees.  农民们说，如果它们使用肥料树，就只需要很少的雨水。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_1977','satire','''sætaɪɚ','''sætaɪə','[n] 讽刺(文学)','the characteristic use of satire in Jonson’s work  琼森作品中讽刺手法的独到运用'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_1978','epoch','''ɛpək','''iːpɒk; ''epɒk','[n] 新纪元, 时代','the Victorian epoch  维多利亚时代'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_1979','impressive','ɪm''prɛsɪv','ɪm''presɪv','[adj] 给人深刻印象的, 感人的','The figures certainly look impressive.  这些数字看上去确实很可观。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_1980','brush','brʌʃ','brʌʃ','[n] 刷子, 毛刷, 画笔 vt刷, 掸, 拂','a scrubbing brush  硬毛刷，板刷'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_1981','Massachusetts','','','[n] 马萨诸塞(美国州名)','I live in Massachusetts.  我住在马萨诸塞州。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_1982','realism','''riəlɪzəm','''rɪəlɪz(ə)m','[n] 现实主义','the realism of the horses on the carousel  旋转木马上各个木马的逼真形态'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_1983','watch','wɑtʃ','wɒtʃ','[v] 看,注视,照顾','Do you mind if I watch?  你介意我看着吗？'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_1984','foundation','faʊn''deʃən','faʊn''deɪʃ(ə)n','[n] 基础, 根本','It took the builders three weeks to lay the foundations .  建筑工人花了三星期的时间打地基。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_1985','evident','''ɛvɪdənt','''evɪd(ə)nt','[adj] 明显的, 显然的','Bob ate his lunch with evident enjoyment.  显然鲍勃吃午饭吃得津津有味。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_1986','marry','''mæri','''mærɪ','[v] 娶, 嫁,和结婚','He married Bea in 1925.  他在1925年娶了贝亚。'),
