('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_1988','orient','''orɪənt','''ɔːrɪənt; ''ɒr-','[v] 使适应,使朝向 n东方','You will need the time to orient yourself to your new way of eating.  你需要时间适应新的吃法。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_1989','barren','''bærən','''bær(ə)n','[adj] 不生育的,贫瘠的; [n] 荒地','Thousands of years ago the surface was barren desert.  很久很久以前，地面还是一片荒漠。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_1990','prosperity','prɑ''spɛrəti','prɒ''sperɪtɪ','[n] 繁荣','a time of economic prosperity  经济繁荣时期'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_1991','lava','''lɑvə','''lɑːvə','[n] 熔岩, 火山岩','Mexico''s Mount Colima began spewing lava and ash last night.  墨西哥科利马山昨晚开始喷发熔岩和火山灰。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_1992','pace','pes','peɪs','[n] 步调 v踱步','He moved at a brisk pace down the rue St. Antoine.  他沿着圣安托万街轻快地走着。'),
