('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_1996','descriptive','dɪ''skrɪptɪv','dɪ''skrɪptɪv','[adj] 描述的, 叙述的','the descriptive passages in the novel  小说中的描写性段落'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_1997','ruminant','','''ruːmɪnənt','[n&a] 反刍动物(的), 沉思的','Food chemists probably can improve upon the efficiency and economics of the ruminant’s conversion of cellulose to nutrients.  反刍动物将纤维素转化为营养素的效率和经济性有可能经过食品化学家来改进。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_1998','stoneware','''ston''wɛr','''stəʊnweə','[n] 瓷器','...hand-painted blue-and-white stoneware.  ...手绘青花粗陶器。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_1999','mirror','''mɪrɚ','''mɪrə','[n] 镜子; [v] 反映,映出','He spends hours in front of the mirror !  他老是照镜子！'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_2000','barb','bɑrb','bɑːb','[n] 鱼钩; [v] 装倒钩于',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_2001','forage','''fɔrɪdʒ','''fɒrɪdʒ','[n] 草料','Such forage fish already account for nearly a fifth of the world’s total annual catch; another fifth goes to feed pigs and poultry.  这样的饲料鱼已经差不多占每年世界总捕鱼量的五分之一；另有五分之一被用于喂猪和家禽。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_2002','norm','nɔrm','nɔːm','[n] 标准,规范','Joyce’s style of writing was a striking departure from the literary norm.  乔伊斯的写作风格与传统的文学风格大相径庭。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_2003','nitinol','','','[n] [冶]镍钛诺(镍和钛的非磁性合金)','Engineers have produced prototype engines that are driven by the force of nitinol springing from one shape to another as it alternately encounters hot and cold water.  工程师们已制造出一些发动机样机，利用镍钛合金在交替遇热水和冷水时迅速改变形状所产生的力做推动力。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_2004','chick','tʃɪk','tʃɪk','[n] 小鸡','a mother hen with her chicks  和小鸡在一起的鸡妈妈'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_2005','condense','kən''dɛns','kən''dens','[v] (使)浓缩, 精简','condensed soup  浓汤'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_2006','cope','kop','kəʊp','[v] 应付,处理','Sometimes I find it hard to cope.  有时候我觉得很难应付。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_2007','frost','frɔst','frɒst','[n] 霜; [v] 结霜','the risk of frost damage to crops  庄稼遭受霜冻灾害的危险'),
