('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_2207','slip','slɪp','slɪp','[n&v] 滑倒,滑动','Wright slipped but managed to keep hold of the ball.  赖特滑了一下，但球还抓在手里。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_2208','illuminate','ɪ''lumɪnet','ɪ''l(j)uːmɪneɪt','[v] 照明,阐释, 说明','A single candle illuminated his face.  一支蜡烛照亮了他的脸。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_2209','influential',',ɪnflu''ɛnʃl',',ɪnflʊ''enʃ(ə)l','[adj] 有影响的, 有势力的','He had influential friends.  他有一些有影响力的朋友。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_2210','spear','spɪr','spɪə','[n] 矛, 枪','I fended off his sword thrust with my spear.  他一刀砍来， 我拿枪架住。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_2211','behave','bɪ''hev','bɪ''heɪv','[v] 表现,行为, 举止','She behaved in a very responsible way .  她表现得很有责任心。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_2212','equip','ɪ''kwɪp','ɪ''kwɪp','[v] 装备, 配备','They try to equip their vehicles with gadgets to deal with every possible contingency.  他们尽量给他们的车辆配备各种小装置以应付任何可能的突发状况。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_2213','fourth','fɔrθ','fɔːθ','[num] 第四个','Then, we plot the different graphs so that they each take up one fourth of the screen.  然后，我们绘制不同的曲线图，从而它们可以每个图占据屏幕的四分之一。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_2214','everyday','''ɛvrɪde','''evrɪdeɪ; -''deɪ','[adj] 每天的，日常的','the problems of everyday life  日常生活中的问题'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_2215','realistic',',riə''lɪstɪk','rɪə''lɪstɪk','[adj] 现实(主义)的','Is this a realistic target?  这个目标能够实现吗？'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_2216','review','rɪ''vju','rɪ''vjuː','[vt&n] 回顾,复习,评论','a film review  影评'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_2217','iodine','aɪədaɪn','''aɪədiːn; -aɪn; -ɪn','[n] 碘, 碘酒','The cut burns from the iodine.  伤口因涂了碘酒而疼痛。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_2218','hypothalamus',',haɪpə''θæləməs',',haɪpə(ʊ)''θæləməs','[n] [解剖]视丘下部','The stress response is controlled by the hypothalamus.  反应激烈是由丘脑下部控制的。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_2219','tablet','''tæblət','''tæblɪt','[n] 药片','She took a couple of headache tablets .  她吃了几片头痛药。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_2220','songbird','''sɔŋbɝd','''sɒŋbɜːd','[n] 鸣禽,鸣鸟','The zebra finch is a tiny Australian songbird.  斑胸草雀是一种来自澳洲的小型鸣禽。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_2221','aside','ə''saɪd','ə''saɪd','[adv] 在旁边,到旁边','He pushed his half-eaten salad aside and left.  他推开吃了一半的色拉走了。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_2222','illusion','ɪ''luʒn','ɪ''l(j)uːʒ(ə)n','[n] 幻想','She was under no illusion that he loved her.  她不再幻想他爱她了。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_2223','cliff','klɪf','klɪf','[n] 悬崖, 绝壁','The car rolled over the edge of a cliff.  汽车翻下了悬崖边。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_2224','else','ɛls','els','[adj] 别的,其他的 ad另外','If I can''t make a living at painting, at least I can teach someone else to paint.  如果我不能以画画谋生的话，至少我能教别人画画。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_2225','interplay',',ɪntɚ''plɛi','''ɪntəpleɪ','[n] 相互影响','...the interplay of political, economic, social and cultural factors.  ...政治、经济，社会和文化因素的互相影响。'),
