('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_2609','trip','trɪp','trɪp','[n] 旅行，旅游','Two lucky employees won a round-the-world trip.  两名幸运的雇员赢得一次环游世界的机会。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_2610','resistant','rɪ''zɪstənt','rɪ''zɪstənt','[adj] 抵抗的, 有抵抗力的','Some people are very resistant to the idea of exercise.  一些人对锻炼的主意非常抵制。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_2611','peculiar','pɪ''kjulɪɚ','pɪ''kjuːlɪə','[adj] 奇怪的, 特殊的, 独特的','There was a peculiar smell in the kitchen.  厨房里有一股怪味。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_2612','preparation',',prɛpə''reʃən',',prepə''reɪʃ(ə)n','[n] 准备,预备','This dish is good for dinner parties because much of the preparation can be done ahead of time.  这道菜适合宴会，因为很多准备工作可以事先做好。'),
