('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_2782','chemically','','','[adv] 用化学, 以化学方法','Biscuits and crackers are chemically leavened.  饼干和脆饼干是用化学方法发酵的。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_2783','rotation','ro''teʃən','rə(ʊ)''teɪʃ(ə)n','[n] 旋转','The blades spin at 100 rotations per minute.  叶片每分钟转100圈。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_2784','peculiarity','pɪ''kjʊlɪ''ærəti','pɪ,kjuːlɪ''ærɪtɪ','[n] 特性, 怪癖','Margaret regarded her mother’s peculiarities with a fond tolerance.  玛格丽特宽容地看待母亲的怪癖。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_2785','uncertain','ʌn''sɝtn','ʌn''sɜːt(ə)n; -tɪn','[adj] 不确定的,不稳定的,','My whole future now seemed uncertain.  现在我的前途似乎是个未知数。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_2786','fluke','fluk','fluːk','[n] 侥幸，偶然的机会','He agreed that the second goal was a fluke.  他也认为第二个进球实属侥幸。'),
