('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_2929','complement','ˈkɑːmplɪment','''kɒmplɪm(ə)nt','[n] 补足物','The green wallpaper is the perfect complement to the old pine of the dresser.  绿色墙纸是旧松木梳妆台的完美衬托。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_2930','humid','''hjumɪd','''hjuːmɪd','[adj] 充满潮湿的, 湿润的','Tokyo is extremely humid in mid-summer.  仲夏的东京十分潮湿。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_2931','limb','lɪm','lɪm','[n] 肢, 翼, 分支','She would be able to stretch out her cramped limbs and rest for a few hours.  她将可以伸开蜷缩的四肢，休息几个小时。'),
