('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3129','accomplishment','ə''kɑmplɪʃmənt','ə''kʌmplɪʃm(ə)nt; ə''kɒm-','[n] 成就, 完成','It was a major accomplishment for a player who had been injured so recently.  对于一个刚受过伤的选手来说，这是很好的成绩。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3130','routine','rʊ''tin','ruː''tiːn','[n] 例行公事, 常规','John’s departure had upset their daily routine .  约翰的离去打乱了他们的日常生活。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3131','nourish','''nɜrɪʃ','''nʌrɪʃ','[v] 滋养, 使健壮,','The cream contains vitamin A to nourish the skin.  这种护肤霜含有滋养肌肤的维生素A。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3132','busy','''bɪzi','''bɪzɪ','[adj] 忙碌的','She’s busy now – can you phone later?  她现在正忙，你稍后打来好吗？'),
