('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3385','silicon','''sɪlɪkən','''sɪlɪk(ə)n','[n] [化]硅','But the brittleness of silicon limits its uses.  但是，硅的脆性也限制了其应用范围。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3386','stony','''stoni','''stəʊnɪ','[adj] 多石的, 无情的','stony soil  石质土'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3387','steep','stip','stiːp','[adj] 陡峭的,急剧的','The road became rocky and steep.  路变得崎岖陡峭起来。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3388','evening','''ivnɪŋ','''iːv(ə)nɪŋ','[n] 傍晚, 晚间','I do most of my studying in the evening.  我学习大都在晚上。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3389','depart','dɪ''pɑrt','dɪ''pɑːt','[v] 离开，出发','Flights by Air Europe depart Gatwick on Tuesdays.  欧洲航空公司的航班每逢周二从盖特威克机场起飞。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3390','consistently','kən''sɪstəntli','kən''sistəntli','[adv] 一致地；始终如一地','Instead, we should be articulating guidelines that answer consistently the questions: Who should we support in the Middle East?  而我们应该作为回答这一系列一致问题的清晰指向标。 例如，“在中东我们应该支持谁？”'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3391','cajun','','''keidʒən','[n] 移居美国路易斯安纳州的法人后裔','...the first book ever written in Cajun.  ...用美国路易斯安纳州的法国后裔讲的法语方言写成的第一本书。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3392','intrinsically','ɪn''trɪnsɪkli','ɪn''trɪnsɪkəlɪ','[adv] 内在地, 固有地','You enjoy being with the beloved just as much as, and often even more than, you like doing the intrinsically valuable activities.  你想要和心爱的人在一起的愿望，与你想从事具有内在价值的活动的愿望一样大，甚至更大。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3393','rod','rɑd','rɒd','[n] 杆, 棒','a measuring rod  测量杆'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3394','bread','brɛd','bred','[n] 面包, 生计','Would you like some bread with your soup?  你喝汤时要吃点面包吗？'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3395','glow','ɡlo','gləʊ','[v] 发光, 发热','The bedside lamp glowed dimly.  床头灯发出暗淡的光。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3396','flush','flʌʃ','flʌʃ','[v] 冲洗；(脸)发红','Susan flushed deeply and looked away.  苏珊脸涨得通红，目光转向别处。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3397','geologically',',dʒiə''lɔdʒikəli','','[adv] 地质学上','Apollo astronauts used seismometers during their visits to the Moon and discovered that the gray orb isn''t a totally dead place, geologically speaking.  阿波罗航天飞船的宇航员们登月时使用地震检波器发现：这个灰色的星球，从地质学角度上讲，并不完全是一个死气沉沉的地方。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3398','gratify','''grætə''fai','''grætɪfaɪ','[v] 使满足','He was gratified by Lucy’s response.  他对露西的回答很满意。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3399','crane','kren','kreɪn','[n] 起重机','The little prefabricated hut was lifted away by a huge crane.  那间小小的预制棚屋被一台巨大的起重机吊走了。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3400','ledge','lɛdʒ','ledʒ','[n] 岩架,岩石突出部','We crept carefully along the narrow ledge.  我们小心翼翼地沿着狭窄的岩架爬行。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3401','knife','naɪf','naɪf','[n] 刀, 餐刀','a knife and fork  一副刀叉'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3402','squash','skwɔʃ','skwɒʃ','[v] 压碎；硬塞n美国南瓜','The cake got a bit squashed on the way here.  蛋糕在送来这里的路上有点压坏了。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3403','cowboy','''kaʊbɔɪ','''kaʊbɒɪ','[n] 牧童；牛仔','Boys used to play at cowboys and Indians.  男孩子们过去常玩牛仔和印第安人的游戏。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3404','notable','''notəbl','''nəʊtəb(ə)l','[adj] 值得注意的, 显著的','Every country in the world signed the treaty, with one notable exception - the United States.  全世界每个国家都签署了那份条约，只有一个国家反其道而行之，就是美国。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3405','erect','ɪ''rɛkt','ɪ''rekt','[v] 建造,竖立,使直立','an imposing town hall, erected in 1892  一座气势宏伟的市政厅，建于1892年'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3406','maritime','''mærɪtaɪm','''mærɪtaɪm','[adj] 海上的, 海事的','San Francisco has lost nearly all of its maritime industry.  旧金山几乎失去了所有海运业。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3407','vastly','ˈvæstli','ˈvɑ:stli','[adv] 巨大地；广阔地','These institutions, which range from local courts to the United Nations, have vastly reduced the risk of violence both within and between nations.  这些从地方法院到联合国的各种机构极大地降低了国家之间和国家内部的暴力威胁。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3408','bicycle','''baɪsɪkl','''baɪsɪkl','[n] 脚踏车, 自行车','Can James ride a bicycle yet?  詹姆斯会骑自行车了吗？'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3409','fascinate','''fæsə''net','''fæsɪneɪt','[v] 使着迷','Politics fascinated Franklin''s father.  政治让富兰克林的父亲着迷。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3410','shellfish','''ʃɛl''fɪʃ','''ʃelfɪʃ','[n] 贝, 甲壳类动物','Fish and shellfish are the specialties.  鱼和甲壳类水生动物是特产。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3411','dy','','','[n] [化]镝(=dysprosium)',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3412','inferior','ɪn''fɪrɪɚ','ɪn''fɪərɪə','[adj] 下等的, 下级的','I felt very inferior among all those academics.  与那些大学教师在一起，我自惭形秽。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3413','rub','rʌb','rʌb','[v] 擦,擦掉','You’ll have to rub harder if you want to get it clean.  如果你想把它弄干净，就得更使劲地擦。'),
