('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3825','anxious','''æŋkʃəs','''æŋ(k)ʃəs','[adj] 渴望的, 忧虑的','She gave me an anxious look.  她焦急地看了我一眼。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3826','harness','''hɑrnɪs','''hɑːnɪs','[n] 马具; [v] 治理，束以马具',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3827','adoption','ə''dɑpʃən','ə''dɒpʃ(ə)n','[n] 采用, 收养','She decided to put the baby up for adoption .  她决定让人收养那个婴儿。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3828','vie','vaɪ','vaɪ','[v] 竞争','California is vying with other states to capture a piece of the growing communications market.  加州正在与各州竞争，以求在不断扩大的通讯市场上获得份额。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3829','instruct','ɪn''strʌkt','ɪn''strʌkt','[v] 教导, 指示','Eva went straight to the hotel, as instructed (= as she had been told ).  伊娃按照指示径直去了宾馆。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3830','carol','''kærəl','''kær(ə)l','[n] 颂歌, 欢乐的歌','The singing of Christmas carols is a custom derived from early dance routines of pagan origin.  唱圣诞歌这一传统源自异教早期的舞蹈仪式。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3831','god','ɡɑd','ɡɒd','[n] 神, 上帝','Prayer is a way of talking to God.  祈祷是同上帝交流的一种方式。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3832','girl','ɡɝl','gɜːl','[n] 女孩','Both boys and girls can apply to join the choir.  男孩和女孩均可申请加入合唱团。'),
