('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3908','vague','veɡ','veɪg','[adj] 不明确的,模糊的','The governor gave only a vague outline of his tax plan.  州长只是含糊地大致说了一下他的税务计划。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3909','lawlike','','','[adj] 似法律的','If you think causation just ultimately is a matter of one thing following another, lawlike connexion'' then why shouldn''t there be lawlike connexions between mind and body.  如果你将因果关系最终理解为,某物质作为另一物质的结果而发生，我们把它称为“似律性连接”，what，we，call，‘,接下来我们不应该将它应用于大脑和肉体之间的关系。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3910','oppositely','','','[adv] 相反地, 相对地',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3911','anecdotal',',ænɪk''dotl',',ænɪk''dəʊtl','[adj] 轶事的,趣闻的','His findings are based on anecdotal evidence rather than serious research.  他的发现依据的是传闻轶事，而不是认真的调查研究。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3912','ounce','aʊns','aʊns','[n] 盎司','One ounce of almonds contains nearly half the recommended daily amount.  一盎司杏仁大约包含每日需求量的一半。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3913','disorder','dɪs''ɔrdɚ','dɪs''ɔːdə','[n] 混乱 vt扰乱','His whole system was thrown into disorder .  他的全套系统被搞得乱七八糟。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3914','defeat','dɪ''fit','dɪ''fiːt','[vt&n] 击败,战败','She was a woman who hated to admit defeat.  她是个不愿认输的女人。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3915','synchronization',',sɪnkrənaɪ''zeʃən',',sɪŋkrənaɪ''zeɪʃən','[n] 同步化','What happens to systems not under the control of the synchronization service?  系统不在同步服务的控制范围内，会发生什么？'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3916','dress','drɛs','dres','[n] 连衣裙,女装 v打扮','Sheila wore a long red dress.  希拉穿了一条红色的连衣长裙。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3917','biographer','baɪˈɑːɡrəfər','baɪˈɒɡrəfə(r)','[n] 传记作者','...Picasso''s biographer.  …毕加索的传记作者。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3918','creativity',',krie''tɪvəti',',kriːeɪ''tɪvɪtɪ','[n] 创造(力)','artistic creativity  艺术创造力'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3919','illness','''ɪlnəs','ˈɪlnəs','[n] 疾病, 生病','She had all the normal childhood illnesses.  儿童的常见病她小时候都得过。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3920','curriculum','kə''rɪkjələm','kə''rɪkjʊləm','[n] 课程','Languages are an essential part of the school curriculum.  语言是学校课程中必不可少的部分。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3921','Anglo','''æŋɡləu','''æŋɡləu','[n] 盎格鲁, 英裔美国人',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3922','revival','rɪ''vaɪvl','rɪ''vaɪv(ə)l','[n] 复兴, 复活','The US and the UK have expectations of economic revival.  美国和英国对经济复苏有所期待。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3923','Hampshire','''hæmpʃə','''hæmpʃə','[n] 汉普郡(英国南部之一郡)','Only in 1809, when she returned to Hampshire and settled in the cottage on the Chawton estate of her brother Edward, could she devote herself to her work again.  在那儿，写作几不可能。 直到1809年，她回到汉普郡，安置在兄长爱德华在查顿的一所小屋中，才能够再次全心投入到自己的工作中去。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3924','worthwhile','''wɝθ''waɪl','wɜːθ''waɪl','[adj] 值得做的','He wanted to do a worthwhile job.  他想做有意义的工作。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3925','spy','spaɪ','spaɪ','[n] 间谍, 侦探 v侦察','She worked as a spy for the American government.  她为美国政府收集情报。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3926','instinctive','ɪn''stɪŋktɪv','ɪn''stɪŋ(k)tɪv','[adj] 本能的,直觉的','a mother’s instinctive love  母亲本能的爱'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3927','signaler','','','[n] 信号员','Zahavi''s handicap principle - This principle states that in order to be honest, a signal must be costly to the signaler.  扎哈维的障碍原则 -这一原则的国家，为了老实说，信号必须是昂贵的信号。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3928','retire','rɪ''taɪɚ','rɪ''taɪə','[v] 退休','At the age when most people retire, he is ready to face a new career.  在大多数人退休的年纪，他准备要面对一项新事业。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3929','turbulence','''tɝbjələns','''tɜːbjʊl(ə)ns','[n] 骚乱, 动荡','A period of political turbulence followed the civil war.  内战结束之后紧接着的是一段政治动荡时期。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3930','paradigm','''pærə''daɪm','''pærədaɪm','[n] 范例','...a new paradigm of production.  …一种新的生产范例。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3931','insight','''ɪn''saɪt','''ɪnsaɪt','[n] 洞察力, 见识','a woman of great insight  一位极有眼光的妇女'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3932','penchant','''pentʃənt','ˈpɒŋʃɒŋ','[n] 喜好(倾向)','a penchant for fast cars  对跑车的酷爱'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3933','sinkhole','','''sɪŋkhəʊl','[n] 污水池','The sinkhole was caused by rains and an underground sewage flow.  这个塌方的污水池是由于雨水和地下污水流动造成的。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3934','neptune','''nɛptjun','ˈneptju:n','[n] [天]海王星',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3935','cyanide','''saɪə,naɪd','''saɪənaɪd','[n] [化]氰化物','His death has all the signs of cyanide poisoning.  他的死亡具有氰化物中毒的所有迹象。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3936','gin','dʒɪn','dʒɪn','[n] 杜松烧酒  v开始','...another gin and tonic.  …又一杯加奎宁水的杜松子酒。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3937','flax','flæks','flæks','[n] 亚麻','Cherries, sunflower and flax seeds have traces of this hormone.  樱桃，向日葵籽和亚麻籽都含有这种荷尔蒙。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3938','revolve','rɪ''vɔlv','rɪ''vɒlv','[v] 旋转','The wheel began to revolve.  轮子开始旋转。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3939','withdraw','wɪð''drɔ','wɪð''drɔː','[v] 收回,撤消','After much persuasion he agreed to withdraw his resignation.  几经劝说，他同意收回辞呈。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3940','purple','''pɝpl','''pɜːp(ə)l','[adj] 紫色的','His face turned purple with rage.  他气得脸色发紫。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3941','comprise','kəm''praɪz','kəm''praɪz','[v] 包含, 由组成','The house comprises two bedrooms, a kitchen, and a living room.  这座房子有两间卧室、一间厨房和一间起居室。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3942','timer','''taɪmɚ','''taɪmə','[n] 计时员, 定时器','Set the timer on the cooker for three minutes.  把炉子上的定时器设定为三分钟。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3943','supplant','sə''plænt','sə''plɑːnt','[v] 排挤，取代','Barker was soon supplanted as party leader.  巴克在党内的领导地位很快就被人取代了。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3944','harpsichord','''hɑ:psikɔ:d','''hɑːpsɪkɔːd','[n] 大键琴','One piece was the harpsichord part for the Concerto in G (molto allegro) and the other was the Prelude in G major.  一件是G大调协奏曲的大提琴部分，另外一件是G大调协奏曲的序曲。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3945','peaceful','''pisfəl','''piːsfʊl; -f(ə)l','[adj] a 和平的, 平静的','We had a peaceful afternoon without the children.  孩子们不在，我们度过了一个宁静的下午。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3946','reign','ren','reɪn','[n] 君主统治; [v] 统治, 支配','...Queen Victoria''s reign.  …维多利亚女王的统治时期。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3947','appreciation','ə,priʃɪ''eʃən','əpriːʃɪ''eɪʃ(ə)n; -sɪ-','[n] 感谢, 感激','He was presented with a watch in appreciation of his long service.  他获赠一块手表，作为对其长期服务的感谢。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3948','tempt','tɛmpt','tem(p)t','[v] 吸引,诱惑','If you leave valuables in your car it will tempt thieves.  如果把贵重物品留在车上，会招来小偷的。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3949','boast','bost','bəʊst','[v&n] 自夸','‘I wouldn’t be afraid,’ she boasted.  “我才不怕呢。”她吹嘘道。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3950','revitalize',',ri''vaɪtəlaɪz',',ri:''vaitəlaiz','[v] 新生','They hope to revitalize the neighborhood by providing better housing.  他们希望通过提供更好的住房条件使这个社区恢复活力。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3951','spiritual','''spɪrɪtʃʊəl','''spɪrɪtʃʊəl; -tjʊəl','[adj] 精神上的','Painting helps fill a spiritual need for beauty.  绘画可以满足对美的精神需求。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3952','clan','klæn','klæn','[n] 氏族,部落','the Campbell clan  坎贝尔家族'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3953','fictional','''fikʃənl','''fɪkʃənl','[adj] 虚构的,小说的','fictional characters  虚构的人物'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3954','heterogeneous','''hɛtərə''dʒinɪəs',',het(ə)rə(ʊ)''dʒiːnɪəs; -''dʒen-','[adj] 异种的, 异质的','a heterogeneous collection of buildings  风格各异的一组建筑'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3955','diversion','dəˈvɝʒən; dəˈvɝʃən; daɪˈvɝʒən; daɪˈvɝʃən','daɪ''vɜːʃ(ə)n; dɪ-','[n] 转向, 转移','...the illegal diversion of profits from secret arms sales.  …销售秘密武器所得收益的非法转移。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3956','protrude','pro''trud','prə''truːd','[v] 突出','...a huge round mass of smooth rock protruding from the water.  …从水中突出来的一块光滑的圆形巨石。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3957','recrystallize','','','[v] ( 使) 再结晶','After the die, it takes some time for polymer molecules to get reoriented to a random manner again, and to recrystallize.  经过模具之后，聚合物分子需要一定的时间进行重新定型回复到随机方向，并再次结晶。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3958','warp','wɔrp','wɔːp','[v] 弯曲,歪曲','Left out in the heat of the sun, tapes easily warp or get stuck in their cases.  放在太阳底下暴晒后，磁带容易翘曲变形或卡带。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3959','Nevada','nə''vædə','ni''vædə; -''vɑ:-','[n] 内华达州(美国西部内陆州)','If you did all that and come from a broken home in Nevada, so much the better.  如果你做到了以上所有这些并且来自内华达州的一个破裂家庭，那就更好了。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3960','amusement','ə''mjuzmənt','ə''mjuːzm(ə)nt','[n] 娱乐, 消遣','What do you do for amusement in this town?  你们镇上有什么消遣？'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3961','monetary','''mʌnɪtɛri','''mʌnɪt(ə)rɪ','[adj] 货币的, 金融的','the government’s tight monetary policy  政府从紧的货币政策'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3962','reed','rid','riːd','[n] 芦苇','Reeds grew in clumps all along the river bank.  沿河岸长着一丛丛芦苇。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3963','legislature','''lɛdʒɪsletʃɚ','''ledʒɪslətʃə','[n] 立法机关','The proposals before the legislature include the creation of two special courts to deal exclusively with violent crimes.  摆在议会面前的提案包括建立两个特殊法庭专门审理暴力犯罪案件。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3964','baboon','bæ''buːn','bə''buːn','[n] [动]狒狒','With the baboon you first reward a hop, then a bigger hop, then an even bigger hop.  对狒狒，你先奖励它的小进步，然后是大一点的进步，接着是更大的进步。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3965','wedge','wɛdʒ','wedʒ','[n] 楔 vt楔入, 楔进','Garnish with lemon wedges.  用几角柠檬片作装饰。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3966','overgraze','','','[vt] 使过度放牧',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3967','embed','ɪm''bɛd','ɪm''bed; em-','[v] 使插入, 嵌入','One of the bullets passed through Andrea''s chest before embedding itself in a wall.  其中一颗子弹穿过安德烈亚的胸膛然后嵌入一面墙中。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3968','blowhole','''blohol','''bləʊhəʊl','[n] 喷水孔, 通风孔','The real nose however is the blowhole on top of the head.  而真正的鼻孔其实是它们头顶的喷水孔。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3969','imagist','','','[n&a] 意像派者(的)',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3970','antenna','æn''tɛnə','æn''tenə','[n] 天线','television antennas  电视机天线'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3971','receptor','rɪ''sɛptɚ','rɪ''septə','[n] 接受器','...the information receptors in our brain.  …我们大脑中的信息感受器。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3972','magenta','mə''dʒɛntə','mə''dʒentə','[n&a] 红紫色(的)','Its colors are green, magenta, orange and blue.  它的颜色是绿色，品红色，橙色以及蓝色。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3973','valse','','','[v] 轻轻地走; [n] 华尔兹',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3974','rebellion','rɪ''bɛljən','rɪ''beljən','[n] 反叛，反抗','an armed rebellion  武装叛乱'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3975','discoverer','dis''kʌvərə','','[n] 发现者','Madame Curie will always be remembered as the discoverer of radium.  居里夫人作为镭的发现者将永远为人们所怀念。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3976','charcoal','''tʃɑrkol','''tʃɑːkəʊl','[n] 木炭','cooking over a charcoal fire  在炭火上做饭'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3977','conifer','''kɑnəfɚ','''kɒnɪfə; ''kəʊn-','[n] [植]松类, 针叶树','Red squirrels cut conifer cones from trees and bury them in plant litter on the forest floor.  红松鼠会将针叶树上的果实割下来，然后埋在森林地面的落叶中。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3978','botanist','''bɑtənɪst','''bɒtənɪst','[n] 植物学家','A botanist can differentiate varieties of plants.  植物学家能区分各种不同的植物。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3979','narrator','næ''retɚ','nə''reɪtə','[n] 讲述者','“I can never look now at the Milky Way”, said the narrator in “The Sentinel”, “without wondering from which of those banked clouds of stars the emissaries are coming.  “现在，我再也看不到银河了。” 在《哨兵》中，他借叙述者的口说道，“没错，那层层叠叠的星云中，我们期待的使者正在向这里赶来。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3980','critically','''krɪtɪkli','''krɪtɪklɪ','[adv] 批评性地, 危急地','Mike looked at her critically.  迈克挑剔地打量着她。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3981','Inca','''iŋkə','''ɪŋkə','[n] 印加人(古代秘鲁土著人)','With this big stick, Inca kings began eyeing the lands and resources of others.  有了这根军事大棒，印加帝王开始觊觎别人的土地和资源。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3982','woolen','''wʊlɪn','''wulən','[adj] 毛线的; [n] 毛制品','And whenever I saw woolen products advertised, I stopped to see what was on offer.  无论我在哪儿看见关于羊毛制品的广告，我都会停下来看看。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3983','dialogue','''daɪəlɑɡ','''daɪəlɒg','[n] 对话','a boring movie full of bad dialog  充满差劲对白的乏味电影'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3984','void','vɔɪd','vɒɪd','[adj] 无效的','Her eyes were void of all expression.  她的眼神一片茫然。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3985','variously','','','[adv] 不同地, 各种各样地','His fortune has been variously estimated at between $1 and $2 billion.  对他的财富有各种猜测，从10亿美元到20亿美元不等。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3986','dictate','''dɪktet','dɪk''teɪt','[v] 口授；命令','Federal funds have to be used as dictated by Washington.  联邦款项得按照华盛顿规定的途径使用。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3987','incursion','ɪn''kɝʒn','ɪn''kɜːʃ(ə)n','[n] 侵犯，入侵','...armed incursions into border areas by rebel forces.  ...叛军武装入侵边境地区。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3988','sweet','swit','swiːt','[adj] 甜的','This tea is too sweet.  这茶太甜了。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3989','decode','','','[v] 解码, 译解','The software decodes the information embedded in the satellite broadcasts.  这种软件能够解读衞星广播中的信息。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3990','advantageous','''ædvən''tedʒəs','ædvən''teɪdʒəs','[adj] 有利的','He was now in a more advantageous position.  他现在的位置更有利。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3991','legend','''lɛdʒənd','''ledʒ(ə)nd','[n] 传说','Local legend has it that (= says that ) the island was the original Garden of Eden.  当地传说这个岛就是伊甸园的原型。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3992','toll','tol','təʊl','[n] 过路(桥)费','Most people who drive the toll roads don''t use them every day.  大部分开车上收费公路的人不是每天都走公路。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3993','deliberate','dɪ''lɪbərət','dɪ''lɪb(ə)rət','[adj] 故意的,深思熟虑的','a deliberate attempt to humiliate her  对她的故意羞辱'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3994','milk','mɪlk','mɪlk','[n] 乳, 牛奶','a bottle of milk  一瓶奶'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3995','subside','səb''saɪd','səb''saɪd','[v] 下沉,平静','Simon waited until the laughter subsided.  西蒙一直等到笑声平息下来。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3996','socially','''soʃəli','''səʊʃəlɪ','[adv] 社交上；社会上',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3997','inventory','''ɪnvəntɔri','''ɪnv(ə)nt(ə)rɪ','[n] 详细目录, 存货(清单)','...one inventory of twelve sails for each yacht.  …为每艘游艇配备12张帆的存货。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3998','twin','twɪn','twɪn','[n] 双胞胎中一人; [v] 使成对','The twins are now eight months old.  这对双胞胎现在已经八个月大了。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_3999','drastic','''dræstɪk','''dræstɪk; ''drɑː-','[adj] 激烈的, 极端的','drastic cuts in government spending  政府开支的急剧削减'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4000','chapel','''tʃæpl','''tʃæp(ə)l','[n] 小教堂','Bethan goes to chapel every Sunday.  贝唐每个星期天都去教堂做礼拜。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4001','tenement','''tɛnəmənt','''tenəm(ə)nt','[n] 公寓','...streets of low-cost tenements.  …低成本旧式公寓街。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4002','daguerreotype','də''ɡɛrətaɪp','də''gerətaɪp','[n] (早期)银板照相','Louis-Jacques-Mandé Daguerre (November 18, 1787–July 10, 1851) was a French artist and chemist, recognized for his invention of the daguerreotype process of photography.  路易·雅克·曼德·达盖尔（1787年11月18日——1851年7月1日）是法国美术家和化学家，因发明银版照相法而闻名。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4003','staple','''stepl','''steɪp(ə)l','[v] 订 a主要的',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4004','fatty','''fæti','''fætɪ','[adj] 脂肪的','fatty foods  高脂食品'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4005','mainland','''menlænd','''meɪnlənd; -lænd','[n] 大陆','flights between a Greek island and the mainland  希腊一海岛和本土之间的航班'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4006','disrupt','dɪs''rʌpt','dɪs''rʌpt','[v] 使中断，扰乱','Traffic was disrupted by a hoax bomb.  有人虚报有炸弹，造成了交通混乱。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4007','rend','rɛnd','rend','[v] 撕裂，猛拉',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4008','maser','''meizər','''meɪzə','[n] 微波激射器','His discoveries, which won him the Nobel prize, led to the caesium atomic clock and the hydrogen maser.  这一获得诺贝尔奖的发现产生了铯原子钟和氢微波激射器。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4009','spinal','''spaɪnl','''spaɪn(ə)l','[adj] 脊椎骨; [n] 脊髓麻醉','spinal injuries  脊柱损伤'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4010','clockwise','''klɑk''waɪz','''klɒkwaɪz','[adv] ／ a顺时针方向地(的)','Screw the lid on clockwise.  按顺时针方向拧紧盖子。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4011','generic','dʒə''nɛrɪk','dʒɪ''nerɪk','[adj] 种类的，类属的','With this generic list node structure, you can now define lists and list operations that work regardless of the type of data stored in them.  使用这个通用的列表节点结构，您现在可以定义列表和不需要考虑存储在列表中的数据类型的列表操作。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4012','resin','''rɛzn','''rezɪn','[n] 树脂 vt涂树脂于','...a tropical tree that is bled regularly for its resin.  …定期被采割树脂的一棵热带树。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4013','backward','''bækwɚd','''bækwəd','[a&ad] 向后的, 落后的','The backward place has changed into an industrial centre.  那落后的地方变成了工业中心。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4014','carving','''kɑrvɪŋ','''kɑːvɪŋ','[n] 雕刻(品)','...a wood carving of a human hand.  …一尊人手木雕。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4015','frown','fraʊn','fraʊn','[v] ／ n皱眉，蹙额','She frowned as she read the letter.  她看着信皱起了眉头。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4016','feasible','''fizəbl','''fiːzɪb(ə)l','[adj] 可行的','a feasible solution  可行的解决方法'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4017','distrust','dɪs''trʌst','dɪs''trʌst','[n&vt] 不信任，怀疑','Local people regard the police with suspicion and distrust.  当地人对警察持怀疑、不信任的态度。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4018','incredible','ɪn''krɛdəbl','ɪn''kredɪb(ə)l','[adj] 不可信的；不可思议的','It’s incredible that he survived the fall.  他跌下去竟然能够生还，真不可思议。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4019','smother','''smʌðɚ','''smʌðə','[v] 窒息','A teenage mother was accused of smothering her 3-month-old daughter.  一个少女妈妈被指控闷死自己三个月大的女儿。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4020','stain','sten','steɪn','[n] 污点v染污','Remove stains by soaking in a mild solution of bleach.  用温和的漂白溶液浸泡以去除污渍。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4021','cavern','''kævɚn','''kæv(ə)n','[n] 洞穴，大山洞','And the Hare said to him, ''The piece of red gold that thou seekest is in the cavern that is behind thee.  小野兔告诉他说：“你所寻找的那块红色的金子就在你身后的大洞穴里。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4022','minuscule','''mɪnəskjul','''mɪnəskjuːl','[n&a] 草写小字(的)',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4023','envelop','ɪn''vɛləp','ɪn''veləp; en-','[v] 包封, 遮盖','the enveloping darkness  笼罩四周的黑暗'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4024','fortunately','''fɔrtʃənətli','ˈfɔːtʃənətli','[adv] 幸运地，幸亏','Fortunately, everything worked out all right in the end.  幸运的是，最后一切顺利。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4025','dormant','''dɔrmənt','''dɔːm(ə)nt','[adj] 冬眠的','a huge dormant volcano  一座巨大的休眠火山'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4026','coppersmith','''kɔpəsmiθ','''kɒpəsmɪθ','[n] 铜匠','The pawnshop had sold the plates of his Flora after the expiration of thirteen months. Some coppersmith had made stewpans of them.  那当铺，过了十三个月，便把他那套《植物图说》的铜版全卖了，几个铜匠拿去做了些平底锅。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4027','intrinsic','ɪn''trɪnsɪk','ɪn''trɪnsɪk','[adj] 内在的, 固有的','the intrinsic interest of the subject  该话题本身的趣味'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4028','portability','potə''bɪləti',',pɔːtə''bɪlətɪ','[n] 可携带, 轻便',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4029','pest','pɛst','pest','[n] 害虫','a chemical used in pest control  用于防治虫害的一种化学品'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4030','potato','pə''teto','pə''teɪtəʊ','[n] 马铃薯','Marie stood at the sink, peeling potatoes (= cutting off the skin ) .  玛丽站在洗涤槽边削土豆皮。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4031','clarify','''klærəfaɪ','''klærɪfaɪ','[v] 澄清, 阐明','Reporters asked him to clarify his position (= say exactly what his beliefs are ) on welfare reform.  记者们要求他阐明他在福利改革问题上的立场。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4032','extermination','','','[n] 消灭, 根绝','The following is a list of roach extermination techniques using simple tools.  下面列出了一系列使用简单工具的小强消灭术。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4033','suburbanization','','','[n] 市郊化','Like many of New York’s mass suburbanization efforts, such creatures are better in theory than in practice.  如同纽约大规模郊区化的众多尝试一样，这些生物最好还是呆在字面上，不要跑出来吓人。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4034','succulent','''sʌkjələnt','''sʌkjʊl(ə)nt','[adj] 多汁的','a succulent steak  美味多汁的牛排'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4035','medal','''mɛdl','''med(ə)l','[n] 奖牌，奖章','She won a gold medal at the last Olympics.  她在上届奥运会上赢得一枚金牌。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4036','micron','''maɪkrɑn','''maɪkrɒn','[n] 微米,百万分之一米','For example, if you say that something is "a few microns across", explain that a micron is one-millionth of a metre, and "about one hundredth the width of a human hair".  例如，如果您说某事物只有几微米，那么就要解释一微米是百万分之一米，大约是人头发宽度的百分之一。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4037','publicize','''pʌblɪsaɪz','''pʌblisaiz','[v] 宣传','television’s failure to publicize the unemployment issue  电视未能报道失业问题'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4038','spout','spaʊt','spaʊt','[v] 喷出','He replaced the boiler when the last one began to spout flames.  原来的锅炉开始喷射火焰之后他便更换了一个。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4039','catastrophic',',kætə''strɑfɪk','kætə''strɒfɪk','[adj] 悲惨的, 灾难的','A tidal wave caused by the earthquake hit the coast causing catastrophic damage.  地震引发的海啸袭击了海岸，造成了灾难性的损失。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4040','sensory','''sɛnsəri','''sens(ə)rɪ','[adj] 知觉的, 感觉的','sensory stimuli such as music  音乐等的感官刺激'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4041','fodder','''fɑdɚ','''fɒdə','[n] 饲料, 草料','...fodder for horses.  …马的饲料。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4042','photoflash','''fotə,flæʃ','''fəʊtə,flæʃ','[n] （照相）闪光灯','Seven years later, through his work with Harold Eugene Edgerton of MIT, he made several photographic experiences of capturing sequences of actions using photoflash to immobilize the scene.  7年以后，通过与麻省理工学院 Harold Eugene Edgerton的合作，他进行了几次摄影的尝试，捕捉一系列运动的场景通过闪光灯来使画面固定。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4043','substantiated','','','[vt] 证实, 实体化','There is little scientific evidence to substantiate the claims.  几乎没有能证实这些断言的科学证据。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4044','cramp','kræmp','kræmp','[n] 痉挛; [v] 限制，束缚','Several players were suffering from cramp.  有几名球员抽筋了。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4045','reversal','rɪ''vɝsl','rɪ''vɜːs(ə)l','[n] 翻转, 倒转, 反转','Some Internet firms have suffered a painful reversal of fortune (= they were successful but now they are not ) .  一些网络公司遭逢厄运。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4046','psychologically','saɪkə''lɑdʒɪkli','saɪ''kɒlədʒɪklɪ','[adv] 精神上地, 心理上地','"Simply being on antipsychotic medications could not have brought about such acceptance, " she stressed. "And this acceptance set me free psychologically.  “单纯的服用抗精神病药物不能诱使这种接受态度，”她强调“这种接受让我心理上释放了。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4047','virtuosity',',vɝtʃu''ɑsəti',',vɜːtʃʊ''ɒsɪtɪ','[n] 艺术鉴别力','At that time, his virtuosity on the trumpet had no parallel in jazz.  那时，他高超的小号吹奏技巧在爵士乐界无人能比。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4048','leafy','''lifi','''liːfɪ','[adj] 叶状的；叶茂的','leafy green vegetables such as spinach  菠菜之类的绿叶蔬菜'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4049','perishable','''pɛrɪʃəbl','''perɪʃəb(ə)l','[adj] 容易腐烂的','perishable goods such as butter, milk, fruit and fish  黄油、牛奶、水果和鱼等易变质的商品'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4050','retract','rɪ''trækt','rɪ''trækt','[v] 缩回, 撤销','He confessed to the murder but later retracted his statement.  他承认谋杀，但后来又翻供了。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4051','Israel','ˈɪzrɪəl','ˈɪzreɪəl','[n] [地名] 以色列','Our only problem is with Israel.  我们的问题只是以色列。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4052','retrieval','rɪ''trivl','rɪ''triːvl','[n] 取回，补偿','...electronic storage and retrieval systems.  …电子存储和读取系统。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4053','insist','ɪn''sɪst','ɪn''sɪst','[v] 坚持, 强调','Stay for supper – I insist!  留下来吃晚餐——一定的！'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4054','inject','ɪn''dʒɛkt','ɪn''dʒekt','[v] 注射, 注入','His son was injected with strong drugs.  他的儿子被注射了强效的药。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4055','domelike','','','[adj] 穹顶状的','A domelike gunner''s enclosure projecting from the fuselage of a combat aircraft.  战斗机上圆顶形的封闭式结构，炮手的位置，从飞机机身上突出。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4056','savannah','sə''vænə','sə''vænə','[n] (南美)大草原','Only 60 years ago, the land around Moyale was savannah with plenty of grass, big trees and elephants, lions and rhino.  仅仅60年前，莫耶尔周围是一片有丰沛的草、树木、大象、狮子和犀牛的大草原。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4057','snake','snek','sneɪk','[n] 蛇','A snake slithered across our path.  一条蛇蜿蜒爬过我们的小路。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4058','pour','pɔr','pɔː','[v] 灌,注,倾泻','She poured coffee for everyone.  她为每个人都倒了咖啡。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4059','navigator','''nævɪɡetɚ','''nævɪgeɪtə','[n] 航海家','That first citation is from 1557 and comes to us from a great navigator and map maker of the time.  这第一条引证出自1557年，而且它还将一位当时伟大的航海家和地理绘图者带入我们的视野。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4060','vacuum','''vækjʊəm','''vækjʊəm','[n] 真空','His presence should fill the power vacuum that has been developing over the past few days.  他的出现应该能填补过去几天中形成的权力空缺。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4061','elliot','','','[n] 埃利奥特(男子名)',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4062','perry','''pɛri','''perɪ','[n] 梨子酒',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4063','liter','litɚ','ˈli:tə(r)','[n] 公升','So this is moles per liter per second, right? It''s disappearance of some concentration for time.  所以这里的单位是摩尔每升每秒，对吗？这代表浓度随着时间的减少。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4064','arthropod','''ɑrθrə,pɑd','''ɑːθrəpɒd','[n&a] 节肢动物(的)','The Japanese Spider Crab is the biggest arthropod on Earth--their legs are believed to grow up to 12 feet long.  日本的蟹型蜘蛛是地球上最大的节肢动物，它们的腿被认为能够长到12英尺长。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4065','airflow','''ɛrflo','''eəfləʊ','[n] 气流','This airflow pushes waste toward the bottom of the toilet, drawing it into a bag, holding solid waste, but letting the air through.  这样一来，排泄物会被气流抽到马桶底部的一个袋中，固体部分被收集起来，空气则被过滤掉。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4066','departure','dɪ''pɑrtʃɚ','dɪ''pɑːtʃə','[n] 启程, 出发','There are several departures for New York every day.  每天有好几个班次去纽约。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4067','momentum','mo''mɛntəm','mə''mentəm','[n] 动力, 势头','incentives to maintain the momentum of European integration  保持欧洲一体化发展势头的激励措施'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4068','spearhead','''spɪr''hɛd','''spɪəhed','[v] 充当先锋','the troops who spearheaded the rescue mission  在救援任务中充当先锋的部队'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4069','unjust','''ʌn''dʒʌst','ʌn''dʒʌst','[adj] 不公平的','unjust laws  不公正的法律'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4070','industrialism','ɪn''dʌstrɪəlɪzəm','ɪn''dʌstrɪəlɪz(ə)m','[n] 产业主义,工业制度','Coal consumption in Manchester was measured in millions of tonnes, and its smoke became, as Lewis Mumford remarked, "the very incense of the new industrialism".  估计曼彻斯特消耗了数百万吨的煤炭，引用路易斯·芒福德的话说，这个城市上空飘着的烟“就是新工业主义的香气”。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4071','drug','drʌg','drʌg','[n] 药','a drug used in the treatment of cancer  用于治疗癌症的一种药物'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4072','environmentally','ɪn,vaɪrən''mɛntlɪ','en,vairən''mentli','[adv] 在环境方面地',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4073','gem','dʒɛm','dʒem','[n] 宝石, 珍宝','precious gems  珍贵的宝石'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4074','detract','dɪ''trækt','dɪ''trækt','[v] 转移',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4075','swirl','swɝl','swɜːl','[n&v] 旋转，漩涡','...small swirls of chocolate cream.  …小块旋涡形的奶油夹心巧克力。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4076','bluefin','','','[n] 金枪鱼','The International Commission for the Conservation of Atlantic Tunas recently voted to lower bluefin fishing quotas.  大西洋金枪鱼保护国际委员最近宣布了降低金枪鱼捕捞的配额。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4077','radiant','''redɪənt','''reɪdɪənt','[adj] 发光的, 辐射的','She looked radiant in a white silk dress.  她身穿白色真丝礼服，看上去光彩照人。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4078','potent','''potnt','''pəʊt(ə)nt','[adj] 强有力的,有效的','potent drugs  强效药物'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4079','sociobiology',',səusiəubai''ɔlədʒi, -ʃi-',',səʊsɪəʊbaɪ''ɒlədʒɪ; ,səʊʃɪəʊ-','[n] 生物社会学','The social science middle-ground, lately known as sociobiology, claims that we learn at least some specific cultural behaviors on the basis of biological need and evolution.  社会科学的中间立场近来被称为“社会生物学”，它认为我们至少学习了一些以生物需要和进化为基础的特有的文化行为。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4080','ideological',',aɪdɪə''lɑdʒɪkl',',aɪdɪəʊ''lɒdʒɪkəl','[adj] 意识形态的','The party is split by ideological differences.  意识形态上的差异造成该政党分裂。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4081','solidarity',',sɑlɪ''dærəti',',sɒlɪ''dærɪtɪ','[n] 团结','a gesture of solidarity  团结的表示'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4082','providence','''prɑvɪdəns','''prɒvɪd(ə)ns','[n] 深谋远虑，远见',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4083','catharsis','kə''θɑrsɪs','kə''θɑːsɪs','[n] 宣泄，净化','Music is a means of catharsis for me.  音乐是我宣泄情感的一种途径。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4084','contradictory',',kɑntrə''dɪktəri','kɒntrə''dɪkt(ə)rɪ','[adj] 相矛盾的','Customs officials have made a series of contradictory statements about the equipment.  海关官员们对于这种设备做出了一系列相互矛盾的陈述。'),
