('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4095','humanity','hjʊ''mænəti','hjʊ''mænɪtɪ','[n] 人性','We want a clean healthy environment for all humanity .  我们希望全人类拥有一个干净健康的生存环境。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4096','budget','''bʌdʒɪt','''bʌdʒɪt','[n] 预算 v做预算','We had a really tight budget .  我们的预算很紧。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4097','magnesium','mæg''nizɪrm','mæg''niːzɪəm','[n] [化]镁','This could be magnesium.  这也可能是镁。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4098','engulf','ɛnˈɡʌlf','ɪn''gʌlf; en-','[v] 吞没','despair so great it threatened to engulf him  几乎要将他压垮的绝望情绪'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4099','frigid','''frɪdʒɪd','''frɪdʒɪd','[adj] 寒冷的','The guard looked at us with a frigid stare.  守卫冷冷地盯着我们。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4100','grandiose','''ɡrændɪos','''grændɪəʊs','[adj] 宏伟的,堂皇的','These proposals have nothing to do with grandiose schemes for reinventing market capitalism.  这些提议与改造市场资本主义的宏伟计划毫不相干。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4101','citizenship','''sɪtɪzənʃɪp','''sɪtɪzən,ʃɪp','[n] 公民的身份','McGuirk holds dual citizenship (= the legal right of being a citizen in two countries ) in Ireland and the US.  麦吉尔克拥有爱尔兰和美国的双重国籍。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4102','despondent','dɪ''spɑndənt','dɪ''spɒnd(ə)nt','[adj] 失望的, 沮丧的','Gill had been out of work for a year and was getting very despondent.  吉尔失业一年了，开始变得非常消沉。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4103','identifiable','aɪ,dɛntɪ''faɪəbl','aɪdentɪ''fæɪəb(ə)l','[adj] 可辨认的','In the corridor were four dirty, ragged bundles, just identifiable as human beings.  走廊里有4堆脏兮兮、衣衫褴褛的东西，依稀可辨出人形。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4104','cellular','''sɛljəlɚ','''seljʊlə','[adj] 细胞组成的，多孔的','a cellular network  蜂窝式网络系统'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4105','universality',',jʊnəvɝ''sæləti',',juːnɪvɜː''sælətɪ','[n] 普遍性, 一般性','Secondly, the relationship between universality and specificity.  第二，普遍性与特殊性的关系。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4106','widen','''waɪdn','''waɪd(ə)n','[v] 加宽,扩展','They’re widening the road.  他们正在拓宽马路。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4107','Impressionism','ɪm''prɛʃən,ɪzəm','ɪm''preʃənɪzəm','[n] 印象派, 印象主义','Impressionism has long been one of the most popular art movements.  长期以来，印象主义一直是最具有影响力的艺术运动之一。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4108','steer','stɪr','stɪə','[v] 操纵, 驾驶','He was steering with only one hand.  他只用一只手在驾驶。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4109','moderately','''mɑdərətli','''mɒd(ə)rətlɪ','[adv] 适度地','He drinks moderately.  他喝酒有节制。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4110','writing','''raɪtɪŋ','''raɪtɪŋ','[n] 笔迹, 作品','Some of his most powerful writing is based on his childhood experiences.  他的一些最震慑人心的作品是根据儿时经历写成的。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4111','symbolism','''sɪmbəlɪzəm','''sɪmbəlɪz(ə)m','[n] 象征主义','religious symbolism  宗教象征主义'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4112','acute','ə''kjut','ə''kjuːt','[adj] 敏锐的, 急性的','acute arthritis  急性关节炎'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4113','romance','ro''mæns','rə(ʊ)''mæns; ''rəʊmæns','[n] 恋爱关系；浪漫气氛','The romance had gone out of their relationship.  他们之间已经没有了爱意。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4114','bowl','bol','bəʊl','[n] 碗','Mix all the ingredients thoroughly in a large bowl.  将所有配料放在大碗里搅拌均匀。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4115','unreliable',',ʌnrɪ''laɪəbl','ʌnrɪ''laɪəb(ə)l','[adj] 不可靠的','The car’s becoming very unreliable.  这辆汽车的性能变得非常不稳定。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4116','unfortunate','ʌn''fɔrtʃənət','ʌn''fɔːtʃ(ə)nət','[adj] 不幸的','When we entered the room, the teacher was yelling at some unfortunate student.  我们进教室的时候，老师正在对着一个倒霉的学生吼叫。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4117','weekly','''wikli','''wiːklɪ','[adj] 每周的 ad一周一次地 n周报','a weekly current affairs programme  一周一档的时事节目'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4118','compensation',',kɑmpɛn''seʃən','kɒmpen''seɪʃ(ə)n','[n] 补偿, 赔偿','People who are wrongly arrested may be paid compensation .  被误抓的人有可能得到补偿费。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4119','vine','vaɪn','vaɪn','[n] 葡萄树；藤本植物','Every square metre of soil was used, mainly for olives, vines, and almonds.  每一平方米的土壤都用上了，主要是种植橄榄、葡萄藤和杏树。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4120','hardness','''hɑrdnɪs','''hɑːdnəs','[n] 硬度','With regard to hardness, the diamond is in a class by itself.  讲硬度， 金刚钻是独一无二的。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4121','aerodynamic',',ɛrodaɪ''næmɪk','','[adj] 空气动力学的','aerodynamic efficiency  空气动力效率'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4122','command','kə''mænd','kə''mɑːnd','[n&v] 命令；指挥','By 1944, Fletcher had command of a B-17 bomber and a ten-man crew.  到1944年，弗莱彻已负责指挥一架B-17轰炸机和十名机组人员。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4123','arbitrary','ˈɑːrbətreri','''ɑːbɪt(rə)rɪ','[adj] 任意的, 武断的','an arbitrary decision  武断的决定'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4124','pianist','''pɪənɪst','''pɪənɪst','[n] 钢琴家','She was an accomplished pianist, a superb swimmer, and a gifted artist.  她曾是一位很有造诣的钢琴家、一流的游泳健将和天才艺术家。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4125','slender','''slɛndɚ','''slendə','[adj] 苗条的, 微薄的','She is slender and stylish.  她身材修长，穿着时髦。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4126','admit','əd''mɪt','əd''mɪt','[v] 承认,准许','‘Okay, so maybe I was a little bit scared,’ Jenny admitted.  “行了，也许我是有点害怕。”珍妮承认道。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4127','alp','ælp','ælp','[n] 高山',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4128','commonplace','''kɑmən''ples','''kɒmənpleɪs','[n] 寻常的事物','Women’s groups have become a commonplace.  妇女团体已经成了常见事物。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4129','vase','veɪs; veɪz','vɑːz','[n] (花)瓶','...a vase of red roses.  …一个插着红玫瑰的花瓶。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4130','deliberately','dɪ''lɪbərətli','','[adv] 故意地','He deliberately upset her.  他故意惹她不开心。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4131','recommend','''rɛkə''mɛnd','rekə''mend','[v] 推荐,劝告','Doctors strongly recommend that fathers should be present at their baby’s birth.  医生极力建议孩子出生时父亲应该在场。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4132','dual','''dʊəl','''djuːəl','[adj] 双的, 二重的','a dual system of education  二元[双元]教育体系'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4133','mouse','maʊs','maʊs','[n] 鼠','The cat laid a dead mouse at my feet.  猫把一只死老鼠放在我的脚边。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4134','craftsmanship','''kræftsmənʃɪp','''krɑːf(t)smənʃɪp','[n] 技术','high standards of craftsmanship  很高的工艺水准'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4135','beast','bist','biːst','[n] 野兽，牲畜','You beast! Let go!  你这畜生，放开我！'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4136','affinity','ə''fɪnəti','ə''fɪnɪtɪ','[n] 密切关系,类同',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4137','diagonal','daɪ''æɡənl','daɪ''æg(ə)n(ə)l','[n&a] 对角线(的)','Next, move to the diagonal section at the back-right side of the diamond.  下一个,在钻石的背面-正确的边移到对角线的区段。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4138','exhaust','ɪɡ''zɔst','ɪg''zɔːst; eg-','[v] 使筋疲力尽,耗尽','A full day’s teaching exhausts me.  讲一整天课令我精疲力竭。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4139','resemblance','rɪ''zɛmbləns','rɪ''zembl(ə)ns','[n] 相似，形似','There was a remarkable resemblance between him and Pete.  他和皮特有一个惊人的相似之处。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4140','nontraditional',',nɔntrə''diʃənəl',',nɒntrə''dɪʃənəl','[adj] 非传统的','nontraditional lifestyles'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4141','disprove',',dɪs''pruv','dɪs''pruːv','[v] 反驳,证明为误','These figures disproved Smith’s argument.  这些数据证明史密斯的论点是错误的。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4142','skeptical','''skɛptɪkl','''skeptɪkəl','[adj] 怀疑的','So how do we strengthen our skeptical skills?  那么，我们如何加强自身的怀疑技能呢？'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4143','shirt','ʃɝt','ʃɜːt','[n] 衬衫','I have to wear a shirt and tie to work.  我上班要穿衬衫打领带。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4144','plenty','''plɛnti','''plentɪ','[n] 丰富, 大量','a land of plenty  一片富饶的土地'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4145','appropriately','ə''proprɪ,etlɪ','əˈprəʊpriətli','[adv] 适当地','Try to dress appropriately for each occasion.  试图为每个场合适当地打扮。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4146','emotionally','ɪ''moʃənli','ɪˈməʊʃənəli','[adv] 感情上地, 冲动地',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4147','freshly','','''freʃlɪ','[adv] 新近，刚才','...freshly baked bread.  …刚烤出的面包。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4148','unbelievable',',ʌnbɪ''livəbl','ʌnbɪ''liːvəb(ə)l','[adj] 难以置信的','It is unbelievable, but I like that.  这很难以置信，但是我喜欢它。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4149','simultaneous',',saɪml''tenɪəs',',sɪm(ə)l''teɪnɪəs','[adj] 同时发生的,同步的','They grabbed each other’s hands in simultaneous panic.  他们俩同时惊慌起来，相互抓住对方的手。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4150','induce','ɪn''dus','ɪn''djuːs','[v] 促使,引诱','Patients with eating disorders may use drugs to induce vomiting.  患有进食障碍的人可使用药物催吐。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4151','woodworker','''wud,wə:kə','''wʊd,wɜːkə','[n] 木工','Recalling the talented woodworker, the finest tools are useless without the creative application of a trained and talented artisan.  回到前面的木工身上，如果没有天赋和相关的培训，最好的工具也没有用处。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4152','conversation',',kɑnvɚ''seʃən','kɒnvə''seɪʃ(ə)n','[n] 会话','a telephone conversation  电话交谈'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4153','translate','træns''let','træns''leɪt; trɑːns-; -nz-','[v] 翻译','Poetry doesn’t usually translate well.  诗歌通常都译不好。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4154','transaction','træn''zækʃən','træn''zækʃ(ə)n; trɑːn-; -''sæk-','[n] 交易，业务','The bank charges a fixed rate for each transaction.  银行对每一笔业务收取固定费用。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4155','eager','''igɚ','''iːgə','[adj] 热心于, 渴望着','He’s a bright kid and eager to learn.  他是个聪明的孩子，热爱学习。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4156','skillful','''skɪlfəl','''skilful','[adj] 熟练的, 灵巧的','With a skillful movement he rounded the small fishing-boat.  他以灵巧的动作使小渔船调过头来。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4157','fate','fet','feɪt','[n] 天数,命运','I wouldn’t wish such a fate on my worst enemy.  就算是我不共戴天的仇敌，我也不希望他遭遇这样的命运。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4158','possession','pə''zɛʃən','pə''zeʃ(ə)n','[n] 财产, 所有','He had sold all his possessions and left the country.  他变卖所有财产后离境了。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4159','invariably','ɪn''vɛrɪəbli','ɪn''veərɪəblɪ','[adv] 不变地，始终如一地','It invariably rains when I go there.  我每次去那儿都下雨。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4160','Babylonian',',bæbi''ləunjən',',bæbi''ləunjən','[n] 巴比伦人(的), 巴比伦语（的）','It allowed Hebrew society and Judaism to strengthen for another crucial century—by which time the Babylonian king Nebuchadrezzar could banish the Hebrew people but not obliterate them or their faith.  它使得希伯莱社会和犹太教在关键的一个世纪内不断强大。 在这重要的时间内，巴比伦王尼布甲尼最多撒流放希伯莱人，而无法消灭他们，抑或扼杀他们的信仰。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4161','urbanization',',ɝbənɪ''zeʃən',',ɜːbənaɪ''zeɪʃən','[n] 都市化','Much of this, she says, is due to increased urbanization.  而这些，主要是由于不断增加的都市化造成的。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4162','tram','træm','træm','[n] 有轨电车','You can get to the beach easily from the centre of town by tram.  你可以很容易地在市中心坐有轨电车到达海滩。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4163','sulfur','''sʌlfɚ','''sʌlfə','[n] [化] 硫磺','But no one knew where the sulfur came from.  但是，没有人知道硫来自何处。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4164','stripe','straɪp','straɪp','[n] 条纹','a shirt with black and white stripes  黑白条纹衬衫'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4165','ought','ɔt','ɔːt','[aux] 应当, 应该','All of us ought to go.  我们大家都应该去。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4166','volatile','''vɑlətl','''vɒlətaɪl','[adj] 动荡不定的,反复无常的','an increasingly volatile political situation  日益动荡的政治局势'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4167','densely','''dɛnsli','''densli','[adv] 浓密地','The most densely developed areas appear white and gray, while suburban areas appear grayish green—a mixture of houses, streets, and lawns.  图中人口最稠密的发达地区呈现为白色或灰色，郊区则是由房屋、街道和草坪组成的灰绿色。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4168','biography','baɪ''ɑɡrəfi','baɪ''ɒgrəfɪ','[n] 传记','...recent biographies of Stalin.  …近年的斯大林传记。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4169','inscribe','ɪn''skraɪb','ɪn''skraɪb','[v] 题写','Inside the cover someone had inscribed the words ‘To Thomas, with love’.  在书的内封上，有人题写了“托马斯惠存”几个字。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4170','intercity',',ɪntɚ''sɪti','ɪntə''sɪtɪ','[adj] 城市间的','intercity rivalry  城市之间的竞争'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4171','alongside','ə''lɔŋ''saɪd','əlɒŋ''saɪd','[prep&ad] 在旁边','We use the whiteboards alongside one of the walls, where you just write down your name if you have a question.  用其中一面墙壁旁边的白色书写板，如果有问题，你只要在那里写下你的名字。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4172','erratic','ɪ''rætɪk','ɪ''rætɪk','[adj] 古怪的，飘忽不定的','His breathing was becoming erratic.  他的呼吸越来越不均匀。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4173','overly','''ovɚli','''əʊvəlɪ','[adv] 过度地, 极度地','Employers may become overly cautious about taking on new staff.  雇主在雇用新员工的问题上可能会过于谨慎。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4174','uplift','''ʌplɪft','ʌp''lɪft','[v] 提高；振奋(精神)','We need a little something to help sometimes, to uplift us and make us feel better.  我们有时需要一些事来帮助我们打起精神并且让我们感觉好点儿。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4175','workday','''wɝkde','''wɜːkdeɪ','[n] 工作日','a 10-hour workday  十小时工作日'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4176','golden','''ɡoldən','''gəʊld(ə)n','[adj] 金(黄)色的；金的','golden hair  金发'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4177','officially','ə''fɪʃəli','ə''fɪʃəlɪ','[adv] 职务上, 正式','The new church was officially opened on July 5th.  新教堂于7月5日正式启用。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4178','sacrifice','''sækrɪfaɪs','''sækrɪfaɪs','[n& vt] 牺牲，献祭','The minister stressed the need for economic sacrifice.  部长强调了在经济上作出牺牲的必要性。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4179','trick','trɪk','trɪk','[n] 诡计; [v] 欺诈','Pretending he doesn’t remember is an old trick of his.  假装不记得是他的老花招了。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4180','melody','''mɛlədi','''melədɪ','[n] 旋律，曲调','They played some lovely melodies.  他们演奏了一些动听的曲子。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4181','array','ə''re','ə''reɪ','[n&v] 展示,排列','We visited the local markets and saw wonderful arrays of fruit and vegetables.  我们参观了当地的市场，看到了漂亮地摆放着的水果蔬菜。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4182','thunderstorm','''θʌndɚstɔrm','''θʌndəstɔːm','[n] 雷暴雨','We enjoyed the picnic until a thunderstorm intervened.  一场暴风雨影响了我们野餐时的兴致。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4183','frog','frɔɡ','frɒg','[n] 青蛙','The tadpole has become a frog.  这个蝌蚪已长成青蛙。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4184','deception','dɪ''sɛpʃən','dɪ''sepʃ(ə)n','[n] 欺骗, 诡计','She didn’t have the courage to admit to her deception.  她没有勇气承认自己的欺骗行为。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4185','snap','snæp','snæp','[v] 喀嚓折断,拍快照 n吧嗒声','He shifted his weight and a twig snapped.  他挪了挪身子，一根树枝随即喀嚓一声折断了。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4186','typify','''tɪpɪfaɪ','''tɪpɪfaɪ','[v] 代表','These two buildings typify the rich extremes of local architecture.  这两座建筑物代表着当地建筑风格的迥异。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4187','gently','''dʒɛntli','''dʒentlɪ','[adv] 轻轻地, 温柔地','‘You go back to bed now,’ he said gently.  “你回去睡觉吧。”他温柔地说道。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4188','astronomical',',æstrə''nɑmɪkl','æstrə''nɒmɪk(ə)l','[adj] 天文学的, 巨大的','Houses in the subdivision are going for astronomical prices.  该小区里的房子在以天价出售。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4189','quantify','''kwɑntɪfaɪ','''kwɒntɪfaɪ','[v] 用数量表示,量化','an attempt to quantify the region’s social and economic decline  对该地区社会和经济衰退进行量化的尝试'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4190','startle','''stɑrtl','''stɑːt(ə)l','[v] 震惊','Sorry, I didn’t mean to startle you.  抱歉，我不是故意吓你一跳的。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4191','peregrine','','','[n] 游隼 a外来的,移住的','Fringe benefits here include a cigar club, the fastest lifts in the world, and the chance to snap peregrine falcons as they migrate past your no doubt hermetically sealed expanse of window.  这里的额外好处包括了一个雪茄俱乐部，世界上最快速的电梯，以及当游隼迁徙飞过你的绝对密封的巨大玻璃窗户时，抓住它们的机会。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4192','optimal','''ɑptəml','''ɒptɪm(ə)l','[adj] 最理想的','If you find yourself waiting to be great, yearning for the optimal time when you can “afford” to do more, then you are saying at some level, if you can’t help everyone, you help no one.  如果你发现自己等着变得伟大 渴望着最佳时间当你可以 负担得起 去做更多事情的时候 那么在一定程度上说，如果你不能帮助每个人，你对谁都没有好处。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4193','tapestry','''tæpəstri','''tæpɪstrɪ','[n] 挂毯','a colourful tapestry depicting a hunting scene  描绘狩猎场面的彩色壁毯'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4194','polish','''pɑlɪʃ','''pɒlɪʃ','[v] 磨光，擦亮','I spent all afternoon polishing the silver.  我整个下午都在擦拭银器。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4195','capability','ˌkeɪpəˈbɪləti','ˌkeɪpəˈbɪləti','[n] 能力，才能','the country’s manufacturing capability  该国的生产能力'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4196','mechanization',',mɛkənɪ''zeʃən',',mekənaɪ''zeɪʃən','[n] 机械化','We are speeding up the mechanization of our agriculture.  我们正在加快农业机械化的步伐。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4197','influx','''ɪnflʌks','''ɪnflʌks','[n] 流入','...problems caused by the influx of refugees.  …难民大量涌入所造成的问题。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4198','sculptural','''skʌlptʃərəl','','[adj] 雕刻的','He enjoyed working with clay as a sculptural form.  他喜欢用黏土来做雕塑。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4199','calm','kɑm','kɑːm','[adj] 镇定的,平静的 v(使)平静','Glen was calm and composed at the funeral.  格伦在葬礼上表现得平静而镇定。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4200','announce','ə''naʊns','ə''naʊns','[v] 宣布,宣告','They announced their engagement in ‘The Times’.  他们在《泰晤士报》上宣布了订婚的消息。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4201','leisure','''liʒɚ','''leʒə','[n] 闲暇, 休闲','Most people now enjoy shorter working hours and more leisure time.  现在大多数人都喜欢工作时间短些，闲暇时间多些。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4202','essence','''ɛsns','''es(ə)ns','[n] 本质，实质','In essence his message was very simple.  实质上他想表达的意思很简单。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4203','landmass','''lændmæs','''lændmæs','[n] 大陆','Veiled beneath the Persian Gulf, a once-fertile landmass may have supported some of the earliest humans outside Africa some 75,000 to 100,000 years ago, a new review of research suggests.  一项新的研究评论表明，在波斯湾的海底，也许存在过一片肥沃的土地，它曾在约75,000到100,000年前供养着除非洲大陆之外最早的人类先祖。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4204','shrimp','ʃrɪmp','ʃrɪmp','[n] 小虾 v捕虾',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4205','ornamentation',',ɔrnəmɛn''teʃən','ɔːnəmen''teɪʃ(ə)n','[n] 装饰','a bronze plate with gold ornamentation  带有金饰的青铜盘子'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4206','freely','''frili','''friːlɪ','[adv] 自由地；慷慨地','the country’s first freely elected president  该国首位自由选举产生的总统'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4207','undesirable',',ʌndɪ''zaɪərəbl','ʌndɪ''zaɪərəb(ə)l','[adj] 令人不悦的，讨厌的','punishment of undesirable behaviour  对不良行为的惩罚'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4208','globe','ɡlob','gləʊb','[n] 球体,地球仪','We export our goods all over the globe.  我们的商品出口到世界各地。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4209','grasshopper','''ɡræshɑpɚ','''grɑːshɒpə','[n] 蚱蜢，蝗虫','One day a grasshopper came upon an ant at work in a garden.  一天， 蚱蜢碰到了一只正在花园里干活的蚂蚁。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4210','elegant','''ɛləgənt','''elɪg(ə)nt','[adj] 优雅的, 雅致的','a tall, elegant young woman  身材高挑、举止优雅的年轻女子'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4211','shiny','''ʃaɪni','''ʃaɪnɪ','[adj] 发光的；磨光的','shiny black shoes  锃亮的黑皮鞋'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4212','glassmaker','''ɡlæs,mekɚ','''ɡlɑːs,meɪkə','[n] 玻璃工人','A glassmaker places a rounded piece of clay material on the end of a long metal stick.  一个玻璃制造商的地方长的金属棍年底的粘土材料的圆形片。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4213','spectacularly','spɛkˈtækjəlɚli','spekˈtækjʊlə(r)li','[adv] 壮观地, 令人吃惊地',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4214','nss','','','[n] 卫星导航系统(供氮系统)',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4215','submerge','səb''mɝdʒ','səb''mɜːdʒ','[v] 浸没，淹没','The tunnel entrance was submerged by rising sea water.  隧道入口被涨起的海水淹没。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4216','terminology',',tɝmə''nɑlədʒi',',tɜːmɪ''nɒlədʒɪ','[n] 术语(学)','computer terminology  计算机术语'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4217','unclear',',ʌn''klɪr','ʌn''klɪə','[adj] 不清楚的','The terms of the contract are very unclear.  合同的条款非常含糊。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4218','unimportant','''ʌnɪm''pɔrtnt','ʌnɪm''pɔːt(ə)nt','[adj] 不重要的','unimportant details  无关紧要的细枝末节'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4219','ubiquitous','ju''bɪkwɪtəs','juː''bɪkwɪtəs','[adj] 到处存在的','Coffee shops are ubiquitous these days.  如今好像到处都是咖啡馆。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4220','demise','dɪ''maɪz','dɪ''maɪz','[n] 死亡,让位','the mystery surrounding Elena’s untimely demise  埃琳娜猝然早逝之谜'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4221','conspicuous','kən''spɪkjʊəs','kən''spɪkjʊəs','[adj] 显著的, 显眼的','The notice must be displayed in a conspicuous place.  通告一定要贴在显眼的地方。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4222','error','''ɛrɚ','''erə','[n] 错误, 过失','an error message  出错信息'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4223','deadly','''dɛdli','''dedlɪ','[adj] 致命的','a deadly poison  致命的毒药'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4224','barter','''bɑrtɚ','''bɑːtə','[v] 交易','They have been bartering wheat for cotton and timber.  他们一直在用小麦交换棉花和木材。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4225','nomadic','nəu''mædik, nɔ-','nəʊ''mædɪk','[adj] 游牧的, 流浪的','nomadic herdsmen  游牧民'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4226','merge','mɝdʒ','mɜːdʒ','[v] 结合,合并','The company plans to merge its subsidiaries in the US.  该公司计划合并其在美国的几家子公司。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4227','seashore','''siʃɔr','''siːʃɔː(r)','[n] 海岸, 海滨','She takes her inspiration from shells and stones she finds on the seashore.  她从她在海岸边发现的贝壳和石头里获取灵感。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4228','nonhuman','','','[adj] 非人类的','Hostility towards outsiders is characteristic of both human and nonhuman animals.  敌视外来者是人类和其他动物共有的特征。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4229','cottage','''kɑtɪdʒ','''kɒtɪdʒ','[n] 村舍,小别墅','a country cottage  乡间小屋'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4230','fairground','''fɛrɡraʊnd','''feəgraʊnd','[n] 游乐场, 集市','Measuring appeal is as exact a science as guessing the number of sweets in a jar at the fairground.  对吸引力的衡量就像猜测露天游乐场中一个罐子里有多少糖果一样充满“技术性”。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4231','lengthen','''lɛŋθən','''leŋθ(ə)n; -ŋkθ-','[v] 变长,延伸','Can you lengthen this skirt for me?  你能不能帮我把这条裙子改长？'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4232','candle','''kændl','''kænd(ə)l','[n] 蜡烛','The candle flickered in the wind.  烛光在风中闪烁不定。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4233','kilogram','''kɪləɡræm','ˈkɪləɡræm','[n] [物]千克, 公斤','...a parcel weighing around 4.5 kilograms.  …一个重约4.5公斤的包裹。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4234','naturalism','''nætʃrəlɪzəm','''nætʃ(ə)rəlɪz(ə)m','[n] 自然主义','Still, I sympathize with one motive behind naturalism — the aspiration to think in a scientific spirit.  尽管如此，我还是支持自然主义背后的一个动机——用科学精神来思考的渴望。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4235','input','''ɪn''pʊt','''ɪnpʊt','[n] 输入，投入','If the input data specified it, the file will close and the process terminates.  如果输入数据指定，该文件就会关闭，数据处理终止。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4236','delight','dɪ''laɪt','dɪ''laɪt','[n&v] 高兴,欣喜','Her fabulous recipes will delight anyone who loves chocolate.  她那些绝妙的配方将使每一个爱吃巧克力的人感到愉悦。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4237','telegraph','''tɛlɪɡræf','''telɪgrɑːf','[n&v] (打)电报','Once he knew where we were, Lewis telegraphed every few hours.  一知道我们在哪里，刘易斯就每隔几小时发一份电报来。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4238','stance','stæns','stɑːns; stæns','[n] 站姿，立场','a fighting stance  搏击姿势'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4239','kitchen','''kɪtʃɪn','''kɪtʃɪn; -tʃ(ə)n','[n] 厨房','Sam went into the kitchen to make a pot of tea.  萨姆走进厨房去沏一壶茶。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4240','tour','tʊr','tʊə','[n&v] 旅行，游历','He devilled her during the tour.  他在旅行中拿她打趣逗乐。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4241','maple','''mepl','''meɪp(ə)l','[n] 枫树','...a solid maple worktop.  …一张结实的枫木工作台。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4242','contraction','kən''trækʃən','kən''trækʃ(ə)n','[n] 收缩','the contraction of metal as it cools  金属冷却时的收缩'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4243','hinge','hɪndʒ','hɪn(d)ʒ','[n] （门、盖等的）铰链','The wider the hinge, the further it folds.  铰链角度越大，它能折的距离越远。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4244','biotic','baɪ''ɑtɪk','baɪ''ɒtɪk','[adj] 有关生命的,生物的','The researchers think that their biotic games could be educational to help people learn about biology, and they also think that such a forum could serve as a place to conduct real experiments.  研究人员认为他们的生物游戏有教育意义，可以帮助人们学习生物知识，他们还认为这样的论坛可以作为进行真实实验的场地。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4245','maturity','mə''tʃʊrəti','mə''tʃʊərətɪ','[n] 成熟,(票据)到期','Beth shows a maturity way beyond her 16 years.  贝丝表现出一种远远超出她16岁年龄的成熟。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4246','honest','''ɑnɪst','''ɒnɪst','[adj] 诚实的, 正直的','He was a hard-working, honest man.  他勤奋老实。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4247','firewood','''faɪɚwʊd','''faɪəwʊd','[n] 木柴, 柴火','Young Geoffrey made money by chopping and selling firewood.  年轻的杰弗里靠砍柴卖柴挣钱。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4248','barn','bɑrn','bɑːn','[n] [农]谷仓, 畜棚, 畜舍, 机器房',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4249','joke','dʒok','dʒəʊk','[n] 笑话, 玩笑','I couldn’t go out with someone for a joke, could you?  我可不能拿谈恋爱当儿戏，对不对？'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4250','granular','''grænjəlɚ','''grænjʊlə','[adj] 由小粒而成的,粒状的','...a granular fertilizer.  ...一种粒状化肥。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4251','preindustrial',',priɪn''dʌstriəl',',priːɪn''dʌstrɪəl','[adj] 未工业化的, 工业化前的','Am I suggesting that we should return to the preindustrial mode of production or to nineteenth-century "free enterprise" capitalism?  我是否在建议我们应回到工业化前的生产模式或回到十九世纪"自由企业"资本主义时期呢？'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4252','thaw','θɔ','θɔː','[n] 融化,解冻','The thaw begins in March.  解冻期从3月份开始。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4253','quarry','''kwɔri','''kwɒrɪ','[n] 采石场; [v] 挖出','a slate quarry  板岩采石场'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4254','ethology','','iː''θɒlədʒɪ','[n] 动物行动学, 人种学','On the next page, we''ll delve into the world of ethology .  下面一页我们将探究一下动物行为学的世界。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4255','amendment','ə''mɛndmənt','ə''men(d)m(ə)nt','[n] 改善, 改正','constitutional amendments  宪法修正案'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4256','curious','''kjʊrɪəs','''kjʊərɪəs','[adj] 好奇的, 奇特的','Puppies are naturally curious.  小狗天生好奇。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4257','faith','feθ','feɪθ','[n] 信仰, 信念','People have lost faith in the government.  人们已失去了对政府的信心。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4258','overtake',',ovɚ''tek','əʊvə''teɪk','[v] 追上，超过','He pulled out to overtake the van.  他把车驶出所在车道想超过那辆小货车。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4259','neck','nɛk','nek','[n] 脖子, 颈','Mike rubbed the back of his neck.  迈克揉了揉后颈。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4260','impurity','ɪm''pjʊrəti','ɪm''pjʊərɪtɪ','[n] 不纯；杂质','All natural minerals contain impurities.  凡天然矿物都含有杂质。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4261','formidable','''fɔrmɪdəbl','''fɔːmɪdəb(ə)l; fɔː''mɪd-','[adj] 可怕的；难以克服的','The building is grey, formidable, not at all picturesque.  那幢建筑呈灰色，气势凛然，与漂亮沾不上边。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4262','acceptable','ək''sɛptəbl','ək''septəb(ə)l','[adj] 可接受的, 合意的','Students who achieve an acceptable standard will progress to degree studies.  达到一定程度的学生可以进一步攻读学位。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4263','forager','','','[n] 强征(粮食)者',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4264','impend','ɪmˈpɛnd','ɪm''pend','[v] 迫近，逼近',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4265','glasslike','','','[adj] 玻璃状的','One animal captured on video looks like a flower, covered with glasslike needles, but scientists think it is probably a carnivorous sponge.  在视频中拍摄到的一种动物看上去像是朵花，覆盖着玻璃状的针，不过科学家认为这可能是一种食肉海绵。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4266','translucent','træns''lusnt','træns''luːs(ə)nt; trɑːns-; -nz-','[adj] 半透明的','Blue veins showed through her translucent skin.  她半透明的皮肤下青筋显现。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4267','topsoil','''tɑp''sɔɪl','''tɒpsɒɪl','[n] 表层土','Dump the topsoil here.  把表土倒在这里。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4268','interrelationship',',ɪntərɪ''leʃnʃɪp','','[n] 相互关系','...the interrelationships between unemployment, crime, and imprisonment.  ...失业、犯罪和监禁之间的相互关系。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4269','blade','bled','bleɪd','[n] 刀刃, 刀片','a razor blade  剃刀刀片'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4270','pocket','''pɑkɪt','''pɒkɪt','[n] 衣袋，小袋','Luke came in with his hands in his pockets.  卢克走了进来，双手插在口袋里。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4271','hillside','''hɪl''saɪd','''hɪlsaɪd','[n] 山腰','The airplane crashed on a hillside.  飞机在山坡上坠毁。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4272','beside','bɪ''saɪd','bɪ''saɪd','[prep] 在…旁边,和…相比','Wendy came up and sat beside me.  温迪走过来，坐在我身边。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4273','subscribe','səb''skraɪb','səb''skraɪb','[v] 订阅, 签名,捐赠','My main reason for subscribing to New Scientist is to keep abreast of advances in science.  我订阅《新科学家》的主要原因是要跟上科学的进步。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4274','buffer','''bʌfɚ','''bʌfə','[n] 缓冲器','Keep savings as a buffer against unexpected cash needs.  备有存款来作为急需现金时的缓冲。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4275','embody','ɪm''bɑdi','ɪm''bɒdɪ; em-','[v] 使具体化','Jack Kennedy embodied all the hopes of the 1960s.  杰克•肯尼迪体现了20世纪60年代的全部希望。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4276','happy','''hæpɪ','''hæpɪ','[adj] 快乐的，幸福的','It’s a lovely house and we’ve been very happy here.  房子很漂亮，我们住在这里非常开心。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4277','net','nɛt','net','[n] 网, 网络','Bruce spends most evenings surfing the Net (= looking at information in different places on the Internet ).  布鲁斯晚上大多在网上浏览信息。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4278','litter','''lɪtɚ','''lɪtə','[n] 垃圾 v乱扔东西','If you see litter in the corridor, pick it up.  如果你看到走廊里有垃圾，就把它捡起来。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4279','outsider','''aʊt''saɪdɚ','aʊt''saɪdə','[n] 外行, 局外人','I’m an outsider, the only foreign woman in the group.  我是个外人，是这群人里唯一的外国女人。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4280','aragonite','ə''rægə,naɪt','''ærəg(ə)naɪt','[n] [矿]霰石, 文石','So will corals, especially those whose skeletons are composed of aragonite, a particularly unstable form of calcium carbonate.  珊瑚礁对此也受到同样的危险，对于骨骼由霰石（极不稳定的碳酸钙）构成的珊瑚来说，情况更是如此。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4281','convenience','kən''vinɪəns','kən''viːnɪəns','[n] 便利,适宜','Ready meals sell well because of their convenience.  即食餐因为方便销路好。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4282','promotion','prə''moʃən','prə''məʊʃn','[n] 提升；促进','I want a job with good prospects for promotion.  我想要一份有良好晋升机会的工作。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4283','unaltered','ʌn''ɔltɚd','ʌn''ɔːltəd; ʌn''ɒl-','[adj] 未被改变的','The rest of the apartment had fortunately remained unaltered since that time.  从那时起公寓的其余部分就幸运地未曾改变过。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4284','bath','','bɑːθ','[n] 沐浴, 浴室','After a week of camping, I really needed a bath.  我露营了一个星期，实在得洗个澡了。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4285','directional','də''rɛkʃənl','dɪ''rekʃ(ə)n(ə)l; daɪ-','[adj] 方向的','Unless he was equipped with a directional microphone, he was out of earshot.  除非给他配备一个定向扬声器，否则谁也听不见他。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4286','holding','''holdɪŋ','''həʊldɪŋ','[n] 保持，固定',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4287','romantic','ro''mæntɪk','rə(ʊ)''mæntɪk','[adj] 传奇式的, 浪漫的','‘Tom always sends me red roses on my birthday.’ ‘How romantic!’  “我过生日时汤姆总是给我送红玫瑰。”“多浪漫啊！”'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4288','treeless','','','[adj] 没有树木的','a treeless landscape  寸木不生的地貌'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4289','recorder','rɪ''kɔrdɚ','rɪ''kɔːdə','[n] 记录员, 记录器','Data recorders also pinpoint mechanical faults rapidly, reducing repair times.  数据记录仪器也能很快查明机械故障，减少维修时间。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4290','seller','''sɛlɚ','''selə','[n] 售货者','...a flower seller.  …一个卖花的人。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4291','noticeably','''notɪsəbli','''nəutisəbli','[adv] 显著地，显然',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4292','plunge','plʌndʒ','plʌn(d)ʒ','[v& n] 投入, 跳进','...a plunge into cold water.  …向着冰冷的水中的纵身一跳。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4293','eradicate','ɪ''rædɪket','ɪ''rædɪkeɪt','[v] 根除','an attempt to eradicate inflation  为消除通货膨胀所作的努力'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4294','caste','kæst','kɑːst','[n] 印度的世袭阶级','Most of the upper castes worship the goddess Kali.  大部分的印度上层种姓都信奉卡莉女神。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4295','inherit','ɪn''hɛrɪt','ɪn''herɪt','[v] 继承','inherited wealth  继承的财富'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4296','gosling','''ɡɑzlɪŋ','''gɒzlɪŋ','[n] 小鹅，年轻无知的人',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4297','formally','''fɔrmli','''fɔːməlɪ','[adv] 正式地, 形式上','We announced a decision formally recognizing the new government.  我们宣布了一个决定，正式承认新政府。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4298','rattle','''rætl','''ræt(ə)l','[v] 嘎嘎作响n咯咯声;吵闹声','Dan banged on her door and rattled the handle.  丹砰砰地敲她的门，还把门把手拽得咯吱作响。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4299','residence','''rɛzɪdəns','''rezɪd(ə)ns','[n] 居住, 住处','the ambassador’s official residence  大使官邸'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4300','antecedent','''æntə''sidnt',',æntɪ''siːd(ə)nt','[adj] 先行的; [n] 祖先','That''s an antecedent standard. Moral desert.  道德应得，那是一个先行标准。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4301','stake','stek','steɪk','[n] 树桩','tent stakes  帐篷桩'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4302','disloyalty','dis''lɔiəlti','dɪs''lɒɪ(ə)ltɪ','[n] 不忠实','Charges had already been made against certain officials suspected of disloyalty.  已对某些被怀疑有不忠行为的官员提出指控。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4303','certainty','''sɝtnti','''sɜːt(ə)ntɪ; -tɪn-','[n] 确定, 确实的事情','The result is impossible to predict with any degree of certainty .  这一结果完全无法确切预测。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4304','nystatin','','','[n] [微]制霉菌素','Localised disease may be treated at first with relatively inexpensive drugs such as nystatin, miconazole or clotrimazole.  治疗局部感染可先使用较为便宜的药物，如制霉菌素、咪康唑或克霉唑等。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4305','compile','kəm''paɪl','kəm''paɪl','[v] 编译, 编辑','The document was compiled by the Department of Health.  这份文件是由卫生部汇编的。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4306','prodigious','prə''dɪdʒəs','prə''dɪdʒəs','[adj] 巨大的, 惊人的','the artist’s prodigious output  那位艺术家惊人的高产'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4307','mural','''mjʊrəl','''mjʊər(ə)l','[adj] 墙壁的  n壁画','This work is clearly connected with The Last Supper: the Christ has the same ethereal and elusive quality as the faded figure at the centre of Leonardo''s sublime mural.  这幅画显然和《最后的晚餐》有某种关联：画中的基督，和达·芬奇最伟大的壁画中心那已褪色的基督形象一样，同样空灵缥缈。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4308','fountain','''faʊntn','ˈfaʊntən','[n] 喷泉','...the fountains on the 16th Street Mall.  …第16街商业区的喷泉。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4309','gatherer','''ɡæðərɚ','','[n] 收集者, 收集器','information gatherers  信息收集者'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4310','shoemaking','','','[n] 制鞋','In fact, he once took a hiatus from acting to study shoemaking.  事实上，他曾经一度中断演艺生涯跑去学习制鞋。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4311','electrically','','ɪ''lektrɪkəlɪ','[adv] 用电力;有关电地',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4312','generous','''dʒɛnərəs','''dʒen(ə)rəs','[adj] 慷慨的,丰富的','a generous glass of wine  一大杯葡萄酒'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4313','sprawl','sprɔl','sprɔːl','[v] 伸开','He sprawled out on the sofa.  他摊开手脚躺在沙发上。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4314','petal','''pɛtl','''pet(ə)l','[n] 花瓣','rose petals  玫瑰花瓣'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4315','technologically','','','[adv] 科技地','However, if the inhabitants are technologically inferior, you should find a small tribe of primitives as soon as possible.  然而，如果这些居民的科技次于地球，你应该尽快找到一个小的原始部落。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4316','proportionately','','','[adv] 相称地, 成比例地',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4317','germanium','dʒɝ''menɪəm','dʒɜː''meɪnɪəm','[n] 锗','It s also the first germanium laser to operate at room temperature.  这同样也是第一速在室温下得到控制的锗激光。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4318','likelihood','''laɪklɪhʊd','''laɪklɪhʊd','[n] 可能(性)','If I refused, it would in all likelihood mean I’d lose my job.  如果我拒绝，那我十有八九会丢掉工作。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4319','charter','''tʃɑrtɚ','''tʃɑːtə','[v] 租 n宪章','We chartered a boat to take us to some of the smaller islands.  我们包了一条船带我们到一些较小的岛上去。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4320','threshold','''θrɛʃhold','''θreʃəʊld; ''θreʃ,həʊld','[n] 门槛, 开端','She opened the door and stepped across the threshold.  她打开门，跨过门槛。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4321','sparse','spɑrs','spɑːs','[adj] 稀少的, 稀疏的','his sparse brown hair  他那稀疏的棕色头发'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4322','statuary','''stætʃuɛri','''stætjʊərɪ; -tʃʊə-','[n] 雕象','a fine collection of Greek statuary  一批精美的希腊雕塑藏品'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4323','hypha','''haɪfə','''haɪfə','[n] [植]菌丝','The state in certain fungi in which each compartment of a hypha contains two nuclei, each derived from a different parent.  双核某种真菌中的状态，在这种真菌中，每个菌丝体都含有两个核，而每个核都是从不同的母体上衍生的。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4324','farsighted','''fɑr''saɪtɪd','''fɑː''saɪtɪd','[adj] 有先见之明的, 远视的','Haven''t farsighted economists been telling us that in the future we will work less, not more?  有远见的经济学家们不是一直在告诉我们，将来我们会工作得更少而不是更多吗？'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4325','fatten','''fætn','''fæt(ə)n','[v] 养肥；使肥沃','They have kept the price of sugar artificially high and so fattened the company''s profits.  他们一直人为地使糖价居高不下，以此为公司牟利。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4326','spit','spɪt','spɪt','[n] 唾液 v吐(唾沫)','And ink from soot and spit.  墨水用煤灰和唾液来做。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4327','crawl','krɔl','krɔːl','[vi&n] 爬行, 蠕动','The traffic had slowed to a crawl.  车辆放慢速度，缓缓行进。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4328','cautious','''kɔʃəs','''kɔːʃəs','[adj] 谨慎的, 小心的','a cautious driver  一位谨慎的司机'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4329','expanse','ɪk''spæns','ɪk''spæns; ek-','[n] 广阔；宽阔的区域','The Mandarin Oriental''s pool is small in real life, suitable only for a quick dip… nothing like the vast, blue expanse of water in the marketing photo.  文华东方的游泳池在现实中是很小的，只适合快速浸泡一下......一点都不像宣传照片上那一大片宽阔的蓝色水域。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4330','dawn','dɔn','dɔːn','[n] 黎明 vi破晓,开始出现','When dawn broke (= the first light of the day appeared ) , we were still 50 miles from Calcutta.  破晓的时候，我们离加尔各答还有50英里。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4331','pram','præm','præm','[n] 婴儿车','a young woman pushing a pram  推着婴儿车的年轻女子'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4332','purify','''pjʊrɪfaɪ','''pjʊərɪfaɪ','[v] 使纯净','chemicals used to purify the water  用于净化水质的化学品'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4333','wonderful','ˈwʌndərfl','''wʌndəfʊl; -f(ə)l','[adj] 精彩的, 极好的','The cold, misty air felt wonderful on his face.  那凉凉的雾气使他脸上感觉好极了。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4334','Sanskrit','''sænskrit','''sænskrit','[n& a] 梵语(的)','They got the name from Persian who in turn got it from Sanskrit, from the Indians themselves.  他们从波斯人那里得知的名字，而波斯人是依次从梵文、从印第安人他们自己得知的名字。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4335','orbital','''ɔrbɪtl','''ɔːbɪt(ə)l','[adj] 轨道的','the Earth’s orbital path  地球的运行轨道'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4336','quit','kwɪt','kwɪt','[v] 离开, 辞职','He quit his job after an argument with a colleague.  他和一个同事争吵后就辞职了。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4337','confront','kən''frʌnt','kən''frʌnt','[v] 面临, 对抗','The problems confronting the new government were enormous.  新政府面临的难题是巨大的。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4338','bison','''baɪsn','''baɪs(ə)n','[n] (美洲)野牛','Sixty acres of woods and ponds are home to camels, zebra, bison, water buffalo, ostrich and antelope.  六十英亩的森林和池塘是骆驼，斑马，野牛，水牛，鸵鸟和羚羊的家园。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4339','sideways','''saɪdwez','''saɪdweɪz','[a&ad] 旁的, 横向的',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4340','hyksos','''hiksɔs','''hiksɔs','[n] 希克索斯王朝(古埃及王朝之一)',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4341','arduous','''ɑrdʒuəs','''ɑːdjʊəs','[adj] 费力的, 辛勤的',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4342','boulder','''boldɚ','''bəʊldə','[n] 大石头','Imagine trying to balance a chest of drawers on just one of its legs, on top of a boulder, and you get an idea of what Gray gets up to.  想像自己尝试仅仅依靠衣柜的一个腿把它平稳地放到一个大圆石上，你就知道格雷达到了什么境界。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4343','saint','sent','seɪnt','[n] 圣人, 圣徒','Saint Patrick  圣帕特里克'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4344','bathhouse','''bæθ,haʊs','''bɑːθhaʊs','[n] 公共浴室, 澡堂,','For personal hygiene, Wang and her family go to a public bathhouse in the neighborhood.  至于个人卫生问题，王秀丽一家去附近的公共澡堂洗澡。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4345','dilute','daɪ''l(j)ut','daɪ''l(j)uːt; dɪ-','[v] 稀释，冲淡','diluted fruit juice  稀释的果汁'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4346','principally','''prɪnsəpli','''prɪnsɪp(ə)lɪ','[adv] 主要地','The money is principally invested in stocks and shares.  这笔钱主要投资于股票。'),
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO words (book_slug, slug, word, phonetic_us, phonetic_uk, meaning, example) VALUES,
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4347','imbalance','ɪm''bæləns','ɪm''bæl(ə)ns','[n] 不平衡,不均衡','a hormonal imbalance  内分泌失调'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4348','ionize','''aɪənaɪz','''aɪənaɪz','[v] 使离子化 ,电离','So if we can figure out the binding energy, we can also figure out how much energy we have to put into our atom in order to a eject or ionize an electron.  所以如果我们可以计算出结合能，我们也可以计算出,我们需要注入多少能量到原子中,去逐出或电离一个电子。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4349','immigration',',ɪmɪ''ɡreʃən','ɪmɪ''ɡreɪʃn','[n] 移民入境','He called for a common European policy on immigration.  他要求欧洲国家实施共同的移民政策。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4350','agitation',',ædʒɪ''teʃən','ædʒɪ''teɪʃ(ə)n','[n] 鼓动，焦虑','She was in a state of considerable agitation.  她处于相当焦虑的状态。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4351','vivid','''vɪvɪd','''vɪvɪd','[adj] 生动的，栩栩如生的','I’ve got vivid memories of that summer.  我对那年夏天记忆犹新。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4352','necessitate','nə''sɛsɪtet','nɪ''sesɪteɪt','[v] 使成为必需,迫使','Lack of money necessitated a change of plan.  由于缺乏资金，只能改变计划。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4353','Hollywood','ˈhɑliˌwʊd','ˈhɒlɪˌwʊd','[n] 好莱坞','...a major Hollywood studio.  ...一家好莱坞大制片厂。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4354','poverty','''pɑvɚti','''pɒvətɪ','[n] 贫穷, 贫困','Millions of elderly people live in poverty .  数百万老年人生活在贫困之中。'),
