('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4378','eclipse','ɪ''klɪps','ɪ''klɪps','[n] (日、月)食 vt形成(日、月)食','an eclipse of the sun  日食'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4379','refute','ri''fjʊt','rɪ''fjuːt','[v] 驳斥，驳倒','It was the kind of rumour that it is impossible to refute.  这是那种不可能推翻的谣言。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4380','updraft','''ʌpdræft','''ʌpdrɑːft','[n] 上升气流','Peak updraft strength is slightly enhanced with hodograph curvature, 29.0 m/s in B versus 26.1 in C.  山顶上升气流强度随速矢端迹曲率加大而稍有加强，在（图上）B点是每秒29米，C点是每秒26.1米。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4381','deliberation','dɪ,lɪbə''reʃən','dɪ,lɪbə''reɪʃ(ə)n','[n] 仔细考虑；商量','After much deliberation, first prize was awarded to Derek Murray.  经仔细商议，一等奖颁给了德里克·默里。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4382','flagpole','''flæɡpol','''flægpəʊl','[n] 旗杆','The new Namibian flag was hoisted up the flagpole.  纳米比亚的新国旗被升到旗杆顶上。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4383','invoke','ɪn''vok','ɪn''vəʊk','[v] 恳求','St. Genevieve is often invoked against plagues.  人们经常祈求圣女日南斐法来消除瘟疫。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4384','hypersensitive',',haɪpɚ''sɛnsətɪv','haɪpə''sensɪtɪv','[adj] 过份敏感的','Student teachers were hypersensitive to any criticism of their performance.  实习教师对任何针对他们表现的批评意见都异常敏感。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4385','unavoidable',',ʌnə''vɔɪdəbl','ʌnə''vɒɪdəb(ə)l','[adj] 不可避免的','There are now fears that war is unavoidable.  人们现在担心战争不可避免。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4386','lucky','''lʌki','''lʌkɪ','[adj] 幸运的, 吉祥的','I didn’t really know your name – it was just a lucky guess .  我并不知道你的名字―只是运气好猜中的。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4387','upcoming','''ʌpkʌmɪŋ','ʌp''kʌmɪŋ','[adj] 即将来临的','the upcoming elections  即将举行的选举'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4388','February','''fɛbrʊ''ɛri','''febrʊərɪ; ''febjʊərɪ','[n] 二月(略作Feb)','He joined the Army in February 1943.  他1943年2月参军。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4389','lug','lʌɡ','lʌg','[v] (用力)拖拉','Nobody wants to lug around huge suitcases full of clothes.  没有人愿意拖着装满衣服的大箱子到处转。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4390','broadly','''brɔdli','''brɔːdlɪ','[adv] 宽广地, 广泛','The president broadly got what he wanted out of his meeting.  总统大体上得到了他想从会议中得到的东西。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4391','friendship','''frɛndʃɪp','''fren(d)ʃɪp','[n] 友谊, 友好','her close friendship with her aunt  她与姑母的亲密友谊'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4392','twain','twein','tweɪn','[n] 两, 双, 二',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4393','pathogen','''pæθədʒən','''pæθədʒ(ə)n','[n] [微生物]病菌, 病原体','This would introduce only a small number of GM plants into the environment, so farmers could choose not to harvest them while still benefiting from their pathogen-detecting ability.  这只需要把少量转基因作物引入到环境中，因此农民可以选择不收获它们，同时仍然享受它们的病原体探测能力的益处。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4394','memorable','''mɛmərəbl','''mem(ə)rəb(ə)l','[adj] 难忘的,重大的','We want to make this a truly memorable day for the children.  我们想让今天成为孩子们永远难忘的日子。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4395','auditory','''ɔdətɔri','''ɔːdɪt(ə)rɪ','[adj] 耳的, 听觉的','...the limits of the human auditory range.  …人类听觉范围的局限。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4396','avant','ə''vɑnt','ə''vɒnt','[adj] 先锋的,激进的','The first Dada performances were put on by a group of avant-garde poets, writers and performances artists at Cabaret Voltaire.  第一个达达表演是由一群先锋派诗人、作家和表演艺术家们在伏尔泰夜总会上演的。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4397','tertiary','''tɝʃɪ''ɛri','''tɜːʃ(ə)rɪ','[adj] 第三的, 第三位的','He must have come to know those philosophers through secondary or tertiary sources.  他一定是通过第二手或第三手资料了解那些哲学家的。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4398','submarine',',sʌbmə''rin','''sʌbməriːn; sʌbmə''riːn','[n] 潜水艇','a nuclear submarine  核潜艇'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4399','locality','lo''kæləti','lə(ʊ)''kælɪtɪ','[n] 位置, 地点','weather reports from several different localities  来自几个不同地区的天气报告'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4400','questionable','''kwɛstʃənəbl','''kwestʃ(ə)nəb(ə)l','[adj] 可疑的','The statistics are highly questionable.  这个统计数据大有问题。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4401','Inuit','''injuit','','[n] 因纽特人,  因纽特语','He pays heed to the observations of the Inuit.  他留意到因纽特人的观察结果。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4402','alga','''ælgɚ','''ælgə','[n] 藻类,海藻','Even more strangely, the researchers think the salamanders might inherit the alga from their parents.  更奇怪的是，研究人员认为这些海藻是火蜥蜴从它们父母那里继承来的。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4403','dialect','''daɪə''lɛkt','''daɪəlekt','[n] 方言','the local dialect  当地方言'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4404','respectively','rɪ''spɛktɪvli','rɪ''spektɪvlɪ','[adv] 分别地, 各个地','The cups and saucers cost £5 and £3 respectively.  茶杯和茶碟的价钱分别为5英镑和3英镑。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4405','absent','ˈæbsənt','''æbs(ə)nt','[adj] 缺席的；缺乏的','He has been absent from his desk for two weeks.  他已经两个星期没来了。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4406','feldspar','''fɛldspɑr','''feldspɑː','[n] [矿]长石','The results indicate that the jade mainly consists of illite and a small quantity of feldspar, quartz, hematite, siderite and rutile, which is argillaceous sedimentary rock.  结果表明，其矿物成分以伊利石为主，含有少量的长石、石英、赤铁矿、菱铁矿和金红石，为泥质沉积岩。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4407','biology','baɪ''ɑlədʒi','baɪ''ɒlədʒɪ','[n] (生物)学','a degree in biology  生物学学位'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4408','fatal','''fetl','''feɪt(ə)l','[adj] 致命的，灾难性的','potentially fatal diseases  潜在致命的疾病'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4409','romanticism','ro''mæntə''sɪzəm','rə(ʊ)''mæntɪsɪz(ə)m','[n] 浪漫精神, 浪漫主义','Her determined romanticism was worrying me.  她坚定的浪漫主义正让我担心着呢。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4410','needlework','''nidlwɝk','''niːd(ə)lwɜːk','[n] 刺绣, 缝纫','...watching my mother and grandmothers doing needlework.  ...看我母亲和外祖母做针线活。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4411','palace','''pælis','''pælɪs','[n] 宫, 宫殿','Buckingham Palace  白金汉宫'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4412','ingenious','ɪn''dʒinɪəs','ɪn''dʒiːnɪəs','[adj] 设计独特的，巧妙的','Many fish have ingenious ways of protecting their eggs from predators.  很多鱼都有绝妙的方法来保护它们产的卵不被捕食者吃掉。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4413','framework','''fremwɝk','''freɪmwɜːk','[n] 框架, 体系, 结构','We have to act within the existing legal framework.  我们必须在现行的法律框架下行事。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4414','imposition',',ɪmpə''zɪʃən','ɪmpə''zɪʃ(ə)n','[n] 强迫接受',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4415','meantime','''min''taɪm','''miːntaɪm','[n&ad] 同时, 其间','In the meantime, you have to insulate yourself from his moods.  同时，你必须将你自己隔绝在他的情绪之外。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4416','caribou','''kærɪbu','''kærɪbuː','[n] 北美产驯鹿(=Rangifer)','“For example, if you look at a northern community, they might have a substantial amount of caribou in their diet and they might dry the meat in the home, ” he said.  他还说：“例如，如果你观察一下北方社区，居民们的饮食中或许有相当多的驯鹿肉，而他们可能在室内把肉晾干。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4417','attentive','ə''tɛntɪv','ə''tentɪv','[adj] 注意的, 留意的','an attentive audience  聚精会神的听众'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4418','lifelong','''laɪf''lɔŋ','''laɪflɒŋ','[adj] 终生的','She became a lifelong friend of ours.  她成了我们一辈子的朋友。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4419','August','ɔɡəst','ɔ:ˈgʌst','[n] 八月(略作Aug)','The world premiere took place in August 1956.  全球首映是在1956年8月。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4420','motionless','''moʃnləs','''məʊʃnləs','[adj] 不动的, 静止的','Graham remained motionless.  格雷厄姆一动不动。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4421','renewable','rɪ''nuəbl','rɪ''njuːəbəl','[adj] 可更新的, 可再生的','It’s a six-month lease but it’s renewable.  租期六个月，但是可以续签。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4422','aural','''ɔrəl','''ɔːr(ə)l','[adj] 听觉的','an aural stimulus  听觉刺激'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4423','amateur','ˈæmətər','''æmətə; -tʃə; -tjʊə; ,æmə''tɜː','[n] 业余爱好者','a gifted amateur  有天赋的业余爱好者'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4424','tangle','''tæŋɡl','''tæŋg(ə)l','[v] (使)乱作一团 n混乱','My hair tangles easily.  我的头发很容易打结。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4425','onset','''ɑnsɛt','''ɒnset','[n] 开始；攻击','the onset of winter  冬天的来临'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4426','flank','flæŋk','flæŋk','[n] 肋，侧边','We were attacked on our left flank.  我们的左翼受到攻击。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4427','ornamental',',ɔrnə''mɛntl','ɔːnə''ment(ə)l','[adj] 装饰的  n装饰品','...an ornamental fountain.  …一个装饰性喷泉。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4428','connective','kə''nɛktɪv','kə''nektɪv','[adj] 连合的, 连接的','Examples may include servers, disk storage devices, tape storage devices, and connective devices associated with these items.  例子包括服务器、磁盘存储设备、磁带存储设备，和与这些相联系的连接设备。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4429','meaningless','''minɪŋləs','''miːnɪŋlɪs','[adj] 无意义的','He said a few meaningless words to his hostess and looked around the room.  他向女主人说了几句无关紧要的话，又环视了一下房间。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4430','capitalist','''kæpɪtəlɪst','''kæpɪt(ə)lɪst','[adj] 资本主义的 n资本家','the capitalist system  资本主义制度'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4431','estate','ɪ''stet','ɪ''steɪt; e-','[n] 财产, 地产','His estate was valued at $150,000.  他的遗产价值为15万美元。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4432','cenotes','sɪ''note','sɪ''nəʊteɪ','[n] 天然井',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4433','mesquite','','''meskiːt; me''skiːt','[n] 豆科灌木','The mesquite common on North American deserts in both tree and shrub forms, does not begin to grow above ground until its root system is completely developed, ensuring the plant a supply of moisture.  牧豆树属植物不论是乔木和灌木，在北美沙漠中常常可见，在它根部系统完全生长发达到能保证提供充足的水分时才长出地面。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4434','actively','''æktivli','''æktivli','[adv] 活跃地, 积极地','You can actively argue with your mind.  你可以积极地和你的思想争论。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4435','prison','''prɪzn','''prɪz(ə)n','[n] 监狱','He visits his dad in prison every week.  他每周都去探望狱中的父亲。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4436','whistle','''wɪsl','''wɪs(ə)l','[v] 吹口哨，鸣笛 n哨子','Adam whistled happily on his way to work.  亚当在上班路上愉快地吹着口哨。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4437','seedling','''sidlɪŋ','''siːdlɪŋ','[n] 幼苗','The two species effectively team up to break down young rice plants for their nutrients, causing a plant disease known as rice seedling blight.  这两个物种结合起来，能有效地分解水稻的幼苗作为它们的营养来源，并造成水稻幼苗的枯萎。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4438','lace','les','leɪs','[n] 花边,系带 vt用系带束紧','a handkerchief trimmed with lace  饰有蕾丝花边的手绢'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4439','constrict','kən''strɪkt','kən''strɪkt','[v] 压缩','Caffeine constricts the blood vessels in your body.  咖啡因会使体内的血管收缩。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4440','electromagnetic','ɪ,lɛktromæɡ''nɛtɪk','ɪ,lektrə(ʊ)mæg''netɪk','[adj] 电磁的','electromagnetic waves  电磁波'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4441','Virginian','','','[n] 弗吉尼亚州的人','He was Robert E. Lee. Lee was a Virginian and had served in the United States army for more than thirty years.  李是维吉尼亚人，他在美国军队中服役已有三十多年时间。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4442','dryness','''draɪnɪs','''draɪnɪs','[n] 干燥','When used in our food, heart-healthy olive oil provides an adequate source of fat to prevent dryness.  橄榄油用于食物中，能提供充足的脂质以防止食物干燥，而不会加重心脏负担。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4443','locale','lo''kæl','ləʊ''kɑːl','[n] 现场, 场所','people who see the countryside as a locale for recreation  把乡间视为娱乐消遣之地的人'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4444','rodeo','''rodɪo','''rəʊdɪəʊ; rə(ʊ)''deɪəʊ','[n] 马术竞技表演会, 将牛、马驱集在一起',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4445','endurance','ɪn''dʊrəns','ɪn''djʊər(ə)ns; en-','[n] 忍耐(力), 持久(力)','She was pushed beyond her powers of endurance.  她被逼得忍无可忍。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4446','tribute','''trɪbjut','''trɪbjuːt','[n] 颂词，称赞','The players wore black armbands as a tribute to their late teammate.  球员们戴着黑纱悼念已故的队友。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4447','mussel','''mʌsl','''mʌsəl','[n] [动]贻贝, 蚌类','Paul is then left to choose one box to open to retrieve the mussel.  然后让保罗选择打开其中一个箱子来获得贻贝。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4448','cyan','''saɪən','''saɪən','[n] 蓝绿色, 青色','Obviously the choice colour palette is down to you, but here I’m using a mix of green and cyan.  当然你也可以选用自己喜欢的颜色，在这里我就选择了我选择的是蓝绿色的渐变。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4449','jungle','''dʒʌŋɡl','''dʒʌŋg(ə)l','[n] (热带)丛林','the Amazon jungle  亚马孙丛林'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4450','clam','klæm','klæm','[n] 蛤','clam chowder (= a type of soup )  蛤蜊杂烩汤'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4451','angry','''æŋɡri','''æŋgrɪ','[adj] 发怒的，生气的','I was angry because he hadn’t told me his plans.  我很生气，因为他没有告诉我他的计划。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4452','usher','''ʌʃɚ','''ʌʃə','[v] 引，领，陪同','I ushered him into the office.  我领他进了办公室。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4453','fusion','''fjʊʒən','''fjuːʒ(ə)n','[n] 熔化,融合','Her work is a fusion of several different styles.  她的作品是几种不同风格的融合。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4454','scarcely','''skɛrsli','''skeəslɪ','[adv] 几乎不, 简直没有','The city had scarcely changed in 20 years.  这座城市20年中几乎没有什么改变。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4455','herald','''hɛrəld','''her(ə)ld','[n] 使者; [v] 预报, 标志','Janet Jackson''s new album has been heralded by a massive media campaign.  珍妮特·杰克逊的新唱片已在媒体上进行了大规模的宣传。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4456','mismatch','''mɪsmætʃ','''mɪsmætʃ','[n&v] 配错, 不相匹配','There is a mismatch between the skills offered by people and the skills needed by industry.  人们所提供的技能和行业所需要的技能并不匹配。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4457','stitch','stɪtʃ','stɪtʃ','[v] 缝, 缝合','Mary is stitching a bedspread.  玛丽在缝床罩。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4458','suspicious','sə''spɪʃəs','sə''spɪʃəs','[adj] 可疑的,多疑的','His reluctance to answer my questions made me suspicious .  他不愿回答我的问题，这引起我的怀疑。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4459','monarch','''mɑnɚk','''mɒnək','[n] 君主','The monarch was ousted by a military coup.  那君主被军事政变者废黜了。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4460','extol','ɪk''stol','ɪk''stəʊl; ek-','[v] 赞美',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4461','squat','skwɑt','skwɒt','[v] 蹲(下)','We squatted beside the pool and watched the diver sink slowly down.  我们蹲在池边，看潜水员慢慢沉下水。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4462','rope','rop','rəʊp','[n] 绳, 索','They tied a rope around my waist and pulled me up.  他们在我腰间系了一根粗绳子，把我拉了上去。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4463','verse','vɝs','vɜːs','[n] 诗(句)','a book of comic verse  一本滑稽诗集'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4464','spoon','spʊn','spuːn','[n] 匙，调羹',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4465','chaos','''keɑs','''keɪɒs','[n] 混乱，紊乱','The country was plunged into economic chaos.  这个国家陷入了经济大混乱。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4466','prizefight','''praizfait','''praɪzfaɪt','[n] 职业拳击赛','He is training for a prizefight.  他正在为一次职业拳赛进行训练。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4467','inactivity',',ɪnæk''tɪvəti',',ɪnæk''tɪvɪtɪ','[n] 不活动, 迟钝','Don’t suddenly take up violent exercise after years of inactivity.  多年没锻炼不要突然进行剧烈运动。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4468','confident','''kɑnfɪdənt','''kɒnfɪd(ə)nt','[adj] 自信的, 确信的','Despite her disability, Philippa is very confident.  菲莉帕虽然有残疾，却很自信。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4469','shipment','''ʃɪpmənt','''ʃɪpm(ə)nt','[n] 装船, 出货','The goods are ready for shipment.  货物已经准备好装运。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4470','unprotected',',ʌnprə''tɛktɪd','ʌnprə''tektɪd','[adj] 无保护的, 未做防护措施的','Thieves often target unprotected vehicles.  窃贼常常瞄准未采取防护措施的车辆。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4471','spawn','spɔn','spɔːn','[v] 产卵; [n] 卵','New technology has spawned new business opportunities.  新技术创造了大量新的商机。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4472','lobe','lob','ləʊb','[n] 耳垂，(肺，肝等的)叶','...damage to the temporal lobe of the brain.  ...对大脑颞叶的损伤。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4473','plummet','''plʌmɪt','''plʌmɪt','[n] 铅锤 vi垂直落下',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4474','biologically','','','[adv] 生物学地','We also, biologically, don''t compensate for these calories when we eat.  而且，生物学上，我们在吃时不赔偿这些卡路里。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4475','firearm','''faɪr''ɑrm','''faɪərɑːm','[n] 火器,枪炮','He was charged with illegal possession of a firearm.  他被控非法持有火器。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4476','communal','kəˈmjunəl','''kɒmjʊn(ə)l; kə''mjuː-','[adj] 公共的，集体的','a communal bathroom  一个公用浴室'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4477','kick','kɪk','kɪk','[v] 踢','He kicked the door hard.  他用力踢门。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4478','boost','bʊst','buːst','[v] 推进','The new resort area has boosted tourism.  新的度假区促进了旅游业的发展。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4479','linguist','''lɪŋgwɪst','''lɪŋgwɪst','[n] 语言学家','He had a scholarly air and was an accomplished linguist.  他有一种学者的风度，而且是个熟练掌握多国语言的人。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4480','cortex','''kɔrtɛks','''kɔːteks','[n] 外皮, （大脑）皮层','...the cerebral cortex.  ...大脑皮层。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4481','objectively','əbˈdʒɛktɪvlɪ','əb''dʒektɪvlɪ','[adv] 客观地','Look at your skills objectively when deciding on a career change.  在决定改行时要客观地考虑自己的技能。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4482','chilly','''tʃɪli','''tʃɪlɪ','[adj] 寒冷的','Getting chilly, isn’t it?  天冷了，是不是？'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4483','artifact','''ɑrtə,fækt','''ɑ:təˌfækt','[n] 人造物品',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4484','statesman','''stetsmən','''steɪtsmən','[n] 政治家','a respected elder statesman  一位受人尊敬的政界元老'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4485','curator','kjʊ''retɚ','kjʊ(ə)''reɪtə','[n] 管理者','James Phillips, curator of near east and north african exhibits, said little was known about the origins of the model.  近东和北非展厅的管理者詹姆斯? 菲利普斯说关于这尊模特的起源人们知之甚少。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4486','tally','''tæli','''tælɪ','[n] 记分  vi符合','They do not keep a tally of visitors to the palace, but it is very popular.  他们没有对来宫殿的游客作一个记录，不过这个地方非常受欢迎的。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4487','corporation',',kɔrpə''reʃən','kɔːpə''reɪʃ(ə)n','[n] 公司, 法人','He works for a large American corporation.  他在一家美国大公司工作。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4488','expertise','''ɛkspɝ''tiz',',ekspɜː''tiːz','[n] 专门知识(或技能等)，专长','She was not an accountant and didn''t have the expertise to verify all of the financial details.  她不是会计，不具有核查所有这些财政细目的专业知识。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4489','coincide',',koɪn''saɪd',',kəʊɪn''saɪd','[v] 一致, 符合','The interests of the US and those of the islanders may not coincide.  美国的利益和这些岛民的利益可能并不一致。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4490','operator','''ɑpəretɚ','''ɒpəreɪtə','[n] 操作员, 技工','computers which can be used by untrained operators  未经训练的操作者也可使用的电脑'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4491','originator','ə''rɪdʒənətɚ','ə''rɪdʒɪneɪtə(r)','[n] 创始人, 发起人','...the originator of the theory of relativity.  ...相对论的提出者。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4492','pacifier','''pæsɪfaɪɚ','''pæsɪfaɪə','[n] 调停者，和解人',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4493','Indus','','''indəs','[n] 印度河（印度西北部的河流）','One arrangement now under strain is the 1960 Indus Waters Treaty between India and Pakistan.  目前处境紧张的一项协议是1960年印度和巴基斯坦签订的印度河水域条约。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4494','asymmetrical',',esɪ''mɛtrɪkl','eɪsɪ''metrɪkl','[adj] 不对称的,不均匀的','asymmetrical patterns  不对称图案'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4495','lady','''ledi','''leɪdɪ','[n] 女士,夫人,小姐','Lady Spencer  斯宾塞夫人'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4496','quantifiable','''kwɑntə,faɪəbl','''kwɔntifaiəbl','[adj] 可以计量的, 可量化的','A clearly quantifiable measure of quality is not necessary.  一种确切的可计量的质量检测是不必要的。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4497','pul','pul','puːl','[n] 普尔(阿富汗辅币单位)',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4498','temper','''tɛmpɚ','''tempə','[n] 脾气,韧度 vt调和','That temper of hers will get her into trouble one of these days.  她那种脾气早晚会让她惹麻烦的。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4499','humanness','','','[n] 为人,人性','I now ask you to recognize the Christ within, and to return to me my humanness.  现在我要求你们发现自己的内在基督，把我的人性还给我。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4500','companion','kəm''pænɪən','kəm''pænjən','[n] 同伴, 共事者','For ten years he had been her constant companion .  十年来他一直陪伴她左右。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4501','slave','sleɪv','sleɪv','[n] 奴隶','a slave to fashion  时尚的奴隶'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4502','pinniped','''pɪnəpɛd','''pɪnɪped','[adj] 鳍足类的','The legs were strong and ended in long feet very much like those of a modern pinniped.  它的后肢很强壮，底部有长足，非常像现在的鳍足类动物。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4503','companionship','kəm''pænjən''ʃɪp','kəm''pænjənʃɪp','[n] 友谊','When Stan died, I missed his companionship.  斯坦去世后，我怀念我们的友情。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4504','archaeocyte','','','[n] 原始(生殖)细胞','Many incomplete skeletons were found but they included, for the first time in an archaeocyte, a complete hind leg that features a foot with three tiny toes.  尽管发现的这些骨骼并不完整，但这是专家们第一次在原始动物身上发现完整的后肢，它有三个小脚趾作为的足部特征。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4505','protective','prə''tɛktɪv','prə''tektɪv','[adj] 给予保护的, 保护的','protective clothing  防护服'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4506','incidental','''ɪnsə''dɛntl','ɪnsɪ''dent(ə)l','[adj] 偶然的；附带的','Increased motivation is more than an incidental benefit of reward schemes.  积极性提高不仅仅是奖励计划附带的益处。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4507','intruder','ɪn''trudɚ','ɪn''truːdə','[n] 入侵者','The police think the intruder got in through an unlocked window.  警察认为闯入者是从一扇没上锁的窗子进入的。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4508','conjunction','kən''dʒʌŋkʃən','kən''dʒʌŋ(k)ʃ(ə)n','[n] 联合, 关联','In conjunction with LIFE.com, we bring you a list of the gifts that you should avoid as much as that next glass of eggnog you''re considering right now.  但，有些礼物是绝对不应该出现在圣诞树下的，我们和《生活》网站，联合评选出一个送礼最应回避的名单，就像你此刻不应该再多喝一杯蛋酒一样。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4509','ornate','ɔr''net','ɔː''neɪt','[adj] 华丽的, 装饰的','an ornate gold mirror  华丽的金镜子'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4510','intentionally','','','[adv] 有意地,故意地','Or you can choose to accelerate your growth and intentionally devour life and all it offers.  又或许你可以选择加速自己的成长，故意地挥霍生活及其提供的一切。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4511','impractical','ɪm''præktɪkl','ɪm''præktɪk(ə)l','[adj] 不切实际的,不实用的','The road toll scheme was dismissed as impractical.  公路收费计划由于不切实际而遭到否定。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4512','steal','stil','stiːl','[v] 偷, 窃取','Boys broke into a shop and stole £45 in cash.  男孩们闯进一家商店，盗走了45英镑现金。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4513','rhetoric','''rɛtərɪk','''retərɪk','[n] 雄辩言辞,修辞学','The speech was dismissed by some people as merely political rhetoric .  有些人认为这场演讲只是华而不实的政治空谈。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4514','clump','klʌmp','klʌmp','[n] (树，草)丛; [v] 使成一丛','...a clump of trees bordering a side road.  …一丛长在小道边的树木。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4515','immaturity','ɪmə''tjʊrəti',',ɪmə''tʃɔːrɪtɪ; ,ɪmə''tʃʊərɪtɪ; ,ɪmə''tjɔːrɪtɪ; ,ɪmə''tjʊərɪtɪ','[n] 不成熟','Photographs of the boy showed his physical immaturity.  该男孩的那些照片显示了他生理上的不成熟。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4516','understandable','''ʌndɚ''stændəbl','ʌndə''stændəbl','[adj] 可理解的,能够懂的','It is understandable that parents are angry, and looking for someone to blame.  父母生气了想找个人出气，这是可以理解的。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4517','register','''rɛdʒɪstɚ','''redʒɪstə','[n& vt] 登记(表)，注册','Have you signed the hotel register ?  你在酒店登记簿上签名了吗？'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4518','offset',',ɔf''sɛt','''ɒfset','[v] 补偿，抵消','Cuts in food prices will be offset by direct payments to farmers.  食品降价将通过直接付款给农民的方式进行补偿。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4519','faculty','''fæklti','''fæk(ə)ltɪ','[n] 能力，院系，全体教员','the Engineering Faculty  工程学院'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4520','divorce','dɪ''vɔrs','dɪ''vɔːs','[n&v] 离婚, 脱离','Why doesn’t she get a divorce ?  她为什么不离婚呢？'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4521','daytime','''detaɪm','''deɪtaɪm','[n] 白天, 日间','Can I take your daytime telephone number (= the number of the telephone you use during the day ) ?  你能把你的日间电话号码给我吗？'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4522','dare','dɛr','deə','[v] 敢, 挑战','He wanted to ask her, but he didn’t dare.  他想问她，但又不敢。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4523','overcrowd',',əuvə''kraud','əʊvə''kraʊd','[v] 过度拥挤','Do not overcrowd the fish.  不要过度拥挤的鱼。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4524','marvelous','''mɑrvələs','ˈmɑːvələs','[adj] 令人惊异的, 非凡的','All the initial parameters of the system quickly converge upon termination, when history tells us human society is a system that displays marvelous continuing expansion.  系统的所有初始参数迅速向着终点汇聚，可历史却告诉我们，人类社会是一种显示非凡的不断膨胀的系统。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4525','foolish','''fulɪʃ','''fuːlɪʃ','[adj] 愚蠢的，荒谬的','I’ve never heard anything so foolish in all my life.  我这辈子从没听到过这么愚蠢的话。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4526','opportunistic',',ɑpɚtu''nɪstɪk','ɒpətjuː''nɪstɪk','[adj] 机会主义的, 投机取巧的','Many of the party''s members joined only for opportunistic reasons.  这个政党的许多成员入党纯粹是出于投机。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4527','brine','braɪn','braɪn','[n] 盐水','fish pickled in brine  用盐水腌制的鱼'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4528','naive','naɪ''iv','naɪ''iːv; nɑː''iːv','[adj] 天真的','a naive young girl  天真的小女孩'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4529','merchandise','''mɝtʃəndaɪs','''mɜːtʃ(ə)ndaɪs; -z','[n] 商品, 货物','A range of official Disney merchandise was on sale.  一系列正版的迪士尼商品在出售。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4530','jade','dʒed','dʒeɪd','[n] 玉，翡翠','a jade necklace  翡翠项链'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4531','lapis','''lepɪs','''læpɪs','[n] [化]天青石(常用于化学中的矿物命名)','Featuring painting, illumination and calligraphy, the imagery is worked in bright color — predominantly lapis — and several tones of gold.  图像的色彩绚丽，主要为天青石色，亦配有几种不同色调的金色。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4532','breakthrough','''brek''θrʊ','''breɪkθruː','[n] 突破','The company looks poised to make a significant breakthrough in China.  该公司看上去稳将在中国实现一次重大突破。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4533','manager','''mænɪdʒɚ','''mænɪdʒə','[n] 经理, 管理人员','one of our regional managers  我们的一位地区经理'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4534','compositional',',kɑmpə''zɪʃənl','','[adj] 合成的,组成的',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4535','youngster','''jʌŋstɚ','''jʌŋstə','[n] 年青人,  少年','Other youngsters are not so lucky.  其他的年轻人没有这么幸运。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4536','ideologically',',aidiə''lɔdʒikali',',aidiə''lɔdʒikali','[adv] 意识形态上地, 思想上地',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4537','interpersonal','''ɪntɚ''pɝsnl','ɪntə''pɜːs(ə)n(ə)l','[adj] 人与人之间的, 人际关系的','interpersonal skills  人际交往技巧'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4538','Afghanistan','æf''gænə,stæn','æfˈɡænɪˌstɑːn','[n] 阿富汗(西南亚国家)','We have a factory in Afghanistan.  在阿富汗我们有一个工厂。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4539','lazuli','','','[n] 天青石','Rembrandt didn''t go to the local art shop and buy tubes of paint. He had to grind and mix his paints from things such as lapis lazuli to make blue.  伦勃朗没法在美术商店买到一管管的颜料，他只能自己研磨做颜料，比如把天青石磨成粉来当蓝色颜料用。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4540','electronically','i,lek''trɔnikli',',ɪlek''trɒnɪklɪ','[adv] 电子地, 通过电子手段',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4541','sewage','''sʊɪdʒ','''suːɪdʒ','[n] 污水, 污物','Chlorine is used in sewage treatment.  氯被用于污水处理。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4542','authorize','''ɔθəraɪz','''ɔ:θəraiz','[v] 批准','an authorized biography  授权传记'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4543','municipal','mju''nɪsɪpl','mjʊ''nɪsɪp(ə)l','[adj] 市政的','the municipal waste dump  城市垃圾场'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4544','imagery','''ɪmɪdʒəri','''ɪmɪdʒ(ə)rɪ','[n] 意象, 肖像','Their dreams commonly involved complex stories with visual imagery.  他们的梦里常常有很多复杂的情节，充满了生动的画面。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4545','refreeze','','','[vt] 再结冰, 重新冻结','In this process the water can refreeze, creating additional cracks in the more vulnerable warm ice, according to the study.  根据该项研究，在这个过程中，水可以重新冻结，在更脆弱的暖冰中造成更多裂缝。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4546','hydrologic','','','[adj] 水文的','While evaporation from the oceans is the primary vehicle for driving the surface-to-atmosphere portion of the hydrologic cycle, transpiration is also significant.  海洋的蒸发作用是水文循环中的主要方式，它使得水从地球表面进入大气层中，蒸腾作用也具有举足轻重的地位。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4547','dietary','''daɪə,tɛri','''daɪət(ə)rɪ','[adj] 饮食的; [n] 规定的食物','special dietary requirements  特殊的饮食要求'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4548','hydropower','''haɪdro,paʊɚ','''haɪdrə(ʊ)paʊə','[n] 水力发出的电力','If we do it ourselves, only cheap energy from hydropower will do.  如果靠自力更生，只有靠水电站带来的廉价能源了。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4549','granule','''grænjʊl','''grænjuːl','[n] 小粒，微粒','coffee granules  咖啡颗粒'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4550','further','''fɝðɚ','''fɜːðə','[a&ad] 更远的,更进一步地','Your encouragement will stimulate me to further efforts.  你的鼓励会激发我进一步努力。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4551','recreational',',rɛkri''eʃənəl','rekrɪ''eɪʃənl','[adj] 娱乐的, 消遣的','...parks and other recreational facilities.  …公园及其它娱乐设施。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4552','insecure',',ɪnsɪ''kjʊr','ˌɪnsɪˈkjʊə(r)','[adj] 不安全的,不稳固的','Many of them work in low-paid insecure jobs.  他们当中的许多人都做着薪水低、不稳定的工作。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4553','dealing','''dilɪŋ','''diːlɪŋ','[n] 行为, 交易','penalties for drug dealing  对贩毒的处罚'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4554','circumvent',',sɝkəm''vɛnt','sɜːkəm''vent','[v] 绕行,设法避开','We went north in order to circumvent the mountains.  我们往北走以绕开这些山。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4555','chunk','tʃʌŋk','tʃʌŋk','[n] 大块,相当大的部分（数量）','ice chunks  大冰块'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4556','staff','stæf','stɑːf','[n] 全体职工，全体人员','The entire staff has done an outstanding job this year.  今年全体员工工作都非常出色。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4557','achondrite','e''kɑn,draɪt','ə''kɒndraɪt','[n] 不含球粒陨石','GR99027 meteorite from Blue Ice Area in Antarctica is an achondrite.  来自南极格罗夫山蓝冰地区的GR99027陨石为一无球粒陨石。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4558','asset','''æsɛt','''æset','[n] 资产','the value of a company’s assets  公司的资产价值'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4559','navigable','''nævɪɡəbl','''nævɪgəb(ə)l','[adj] 可航行的,可操纵的','...the navigable portion of the Nile.  ...尼罗河的适航河段。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4560','flutter','''flʌtɚ','''flʌtə','[v] 振翼；飘动','Dead leaves fluttered slowly to the ground.  枯叶缓缓飘落到地上。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4561','pitch','pɪtʃ','pɪtʃ','[n] 球场,强度v扔,猛然倒下','He ran the length of the pitch and scored.  他跑过全场，得分了。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4562','multiplicity',',mʌltɪ''plɪsəti',',mʌltɪ''plɪsɪtɪ','[n] 多样性','It also explains why we use a specific multiplicity in the correspondence.  它还解释了我们在通讯中使用特定多重性的原因。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4563','figuratively','''fɪgjərətɪvli','''figjurətivli','[adv] 比喻地','As much as I love my job as a newspaper reporter, I will never work myself into the ground, literally or figuratively.  尽管我热爱我的工作——报社记者，但我绝不会让自己因为工作把自己送入“坟墓”里面，不管是字面上还是比喻。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4564','crime','kraɪm','kraɪm','[n] 犯罪','We moved here because there was very little crime.  我们搬到这里来是因为这里的犯罪率很低。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4565','speaker','''spikɚ','''spiːkə','[n] 说话者, 演讲人','The keynote speaker (= main or most important speaker ) was Robert Venturi, the architect.  主要发言人是建筑师罗伯特·文图里。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4566','undermine','''ʌndɚ''maɪn','ʌndə''maɪn','[v] 破坏','The continued fighting threatens to undermine efforts to negotiate an agreement.  持续的战斗有可能破坏通过谈判达成协议的努力。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4567','greener','''ɡri:nə','''ɡriːnə','[n] 生手',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4568','entrepreneurial',',ɑntrəprə''njʊrɪəl',',ɒntrəprə''nɜːrɪəl; -''njʊərɪəl','[adj] 企业家的,  企业性质的','...her prodigious entrepreneurial flair.  …她惊人的创业天赋。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4569','foliage','''folɪɪdʒ','''fəʊlɪɪdʒ','[n] 树叶,植物','dark green foliage  墨绿色的叶子'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4570','vice','vaɪs','vaɪs','[n] 缺点, 恶习','Smoking is my only vice.  吸烟是我唯一的恶习。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4571','supreme','suˈprim','suː''priːm','[adj] 最高的, 至上的','the Supreme Allied Commander in Europe  欧洲盟军最高指挥官'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4572','maximize','''mæksɪmaɪz','''mæksimaiz','[v] 取最大值, 最佳化','We need to maximize the space.  我们要充分利用空间。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4573','bushman','''buʃmən','''buʃmən','[n] 丛林居民',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4574','grade','ɡred','greɪd','[n] 等级; [v] 评分,分等级','The best grades of tea are expensive.  最上等的茶叶价格很贵。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4575','marshy','''mɑ:ʃi','''mɑːʃɪ','[adj] 沼泽般的,湿软的','The low, marshy land runs out for miles toward the gulf.  这片低洼的沼泽地沿海湾方向延伸数英里。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4576','anxiety','æŋ''zaɪəti','æŋ''zaɪətɪ','[n] 忧虑, 焦急','his feelings of anxiety  他焦虑的心情'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4577','retirement','rɪ''taɪɚmənt','rɪ''taɪəm(ə)nt','[n] 退休','She took early retirement (= retired at an earlier age than usual ) last year.  她去年提前退休了。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4578','sympathetic',',sɪmpə''θɛtɪk','sɪmpə''θetɪk','[adj] 同情的','a sympathetic friend  一个有同情心的朋友'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4579','manifestation','''mænəfɛ''steʃən',',mænɪfe''steɪʃ(ə)n','[n] 显示, 表现','Different animals in the colony had different manifestations of the disease.  同一群体的不同动物对同一疾病有不同的表现形式。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4580','excitement','ɪk''saɪtmənt','ɪk''saɪtmənt','[n] 刺激, 兴奋','We were both new to the excitements of life in the big city.  我们俩都是初次感受大城市多姿多彩的生活。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4581','porcupine','''pɔrkjə''paɪn','''pɔːkjʊpaɪn','[n] [动]豪猪','In Maine, the most commonly counted roadkill species is the North American porcupine.  在缅因州，公路交通事故中杀死的动物种类是北美箭猪。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4582','amaze','ə''mez','ə''meɪz','[v] 使吃惊','Dave amazed his friends by suddenly getting married.  戴夫突然结婚，令朋友们非常吃惊。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4583','barge','bɑrdʒ','bɑːdʒ','[n] 驳船 vi猛撞','Carrying goods by train costs nearly three times more than carrying them by barge.  用火车运货的费用几乎比用货船高出3倍。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4584','keyboard','''ki''bɔrd','''kiːbɔːd','[n] 键盘','a computer keyboard  计算机键盘'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4585','hook','hʊk','hʊk','[n] 钩; [v] 钩住','Tom hung his coat on the hook behind the door.  汤姆把外套挂在门后的衣钩上。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4586','experimentation','ɪk,spɛrɪmɛn''teʃən','ɪk,sperɪmen''teɪʃən','[n] 实验','The issue of animal experimentation is an emotive subject.  动物实验问题是个敏感的话题。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4587','percussion','pɚ''kʌʃən','pə''kʌʃ(ə)n','[n] 碰撞, 打击乐器','Tonight we have Paul Duke on percussion (= playing a percussion instrument ) .  今晚我们请到保罗·杜克先生负责打击乐。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4588','plausible','''plɔzəbl','''plɔːzɪb(ə)l','[adj] 似真实合理的','His story certainly sounds plausible.  他的叙述听上去当然很合理。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4589','crisscross','''krɪs,krɔs','''krɪs,krɒs','[v] 交叉, 来回移动; [n] 十字形','They spent the next two years crisscrossing the country by bus.  接下来的两年他们乘公共汽车在乡间来回奔波。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4590','blink','blɪŋk','blɪŋk','[v&n] 眨眼, 闪烁','I blinked as I came out into the sunlight.  我走出来，在太阳光下直眨眼睛。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4591','rift','rɪft','rɪft','[n] 裂口; [v] 裂开','He set out to heal the rifts in the party.  他着手弥合党内的裂痕。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4592','radiator','''redɪ''etɚ','''reɪdɪeɪtə','[n] 暖气片，散热器','We bled the car radiator off.  我们排放汽车散热器中的气。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4593','myriad','''miriəd','''mɪrɪəd','[adj] 无数的 n无数','the myriad causes of homelessness  导致人们无家可归的种种原因'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4594','clavichord','''klævɪkɔrd','''klævɪkɔːd','[n] 翼琴(钢琴的前身)','It is called a clavichord.  它被称作古钢琴。 这是一个被动语态的句子。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4595','trilobite','''traɪləbaɪt','''traɪlə(ʊ)baɪt; ''trɪ-','[n] [古生]三叶虫','It looks like a cyborg trilobite; just the thing you want to caress while scrolling through the next chapter of “Victorians on Venus”.  它看起来像一只电子三叶虫，当你在电脑上阅读蒸汽朋克小说的时候，这款鼠标用起来准让你爱不释手。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4596','converter','kən''vɝtɚ','kən''vɜːtə','[n] 转炉','a converter that allows you to view digital television on your old TV  让你可以在旧电视机上收看数字电视的转换器'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4597','layout','''leaʊt','''leɪaʊt','[n] 布局，安排','All the flats in the building had the same layout.  大楼里所有的公寓布局都是一样的。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4598','claw','klɔ','klɔː','[n] (脚)爪','The cat dug his claws into my leg.  猫的爪子抓进了我的腿中。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4599','repel','rɪ''pɛl','rɪ''pel','[v] 排斥,击退','The army was ready to repel an attack.  军队已准备好击退进攻。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4600','sierra','sɪ''ɛrə','sɪ''erə; sɪ''eərə','[n] [地]齿状山脊, [鱼]马鲛',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4601','legitimate','ləˈdʒɪtəmɪt','lɪ''dʒɪtɪmət','[adj] 合法的','That’s a perfectly legitimate question.  那个问题完全合乎情理。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4602','plus','plʌs','plʌs','[prep] 加上 a正的','Three plus six equals nine (3+6=9).  3 加6等于9。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4603','octopus','''ɑktəpəs','''ɒktəpəs','[n] 章鱼','...plates of octopus.  …一盘盘章鱼肉。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4604','temporal','''tɛmpərəl','''temp(ə)r(ə)l','[adj] 现世的, 暂时的','the temporal character of human existence  人生的短促'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4605','unpredictability','ˌʌnprɪˌdɪktə''bɪlətɪ','ˌʌnprɪˌdɪktə''bɪlətɪ','[n] 不可预测性','The danger lies in its unpredictability. Yet that may also be a reason for hope.  危险就在于其不可预测性，而这也可能是希望尚存的一个原因吧。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4606','minimalist','''mɪnɪmlɪst','''mɪnɪm(ə)lɪst','[n] 最低限要求者',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4607','magical','''mædʒɪkl','''mædʒɪk(ə)l','[adj] 魔术的, 神奇的','that magical evening we spent together  我们一起度过的那个美妙夜晚'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4608','storefront','''stɔr''frʌnt','''stɔːfrʌnt','[n] 店头, 店面','A small storefront leads to an English-language school run by Disney.  一个小的店面通向由迪尼斯经营的英语语言学校。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4609','makeshift','''mek''ʃɪft','''meɪkʃɪft','[adj] 临时的; [n] 临时替代物','The refugees slept in makeshift tents at the side of the road.  逃难者睡在路边临时搭建的帐篷里。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4610','plight','plaɪt','plaɪt','[n] 困境','the country’s economic plight  该国的经济困境'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4611','cactus','''kæktəs','''kæktəs','[n] [植]仙人掌','The giant cactus is the vegetable skycraper.  高大的仙人掌是植物界巨人。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4612','solemn','''sɑləm','''sɒləm','[adj] 庄严的,严肃的','a solemn expression  严肃的表情'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4613','reap','rip','riːp','[v] 收割, 收获','You''ll soon begin to reap the benefits of being fitter.  你很快就会获得身体更健康带来的好处。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4614','improvise','''ɪmprəvaɪz','''ɪmprəvaɪz','[v] 即兴创作','I forgot to bring my notes, so I had to improvise.  我忘了带笔记，只好临时发挥。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4615','ascend','ə''sɛnd','ə''send','[v] 攀登, 上升','The plane ascended rapidly.  飞机迅速爬升。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4616','showman','''ʃomən','''ʃəʊmən','[n] 戏剧制作人, 玩杂耍的','He is the band’s best showman.  他是这支乐队中风头最盛的人。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4617','summit','''sʌmɪt','''sʌmɪt','[n] 顶点, 最高阶层',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4618','appointment','ə''pɔɪntmənt','ə''pɒɪntm(ə)nt','[n] 约会, 指定','All consultations are by appointment only .  就诊必须预约。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4619','lawyer','''lɔjɚ','''lɔːjə; ''lɒɪə','[n] 律师','Prosecution and defence lawyers are expected to deliver closing arguments next week.  原告律师和被告律师下周将要作终结辩论。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4620','Alaskan','','','[n] 阿拉斯加人 a阿拉斯加的','But his obeying the ordinary driving commands of the Alaskan trail is no demonstration that he is yours. Any dog in Alaska would obey you as he obeyed.  他遵守阿拉斯加的驱赶命令并不意味着他就是你的狗，任何阿拉斯加的狗都会像他一样对你俯首贴耳。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4621','constrain','kən''stren','kən''streɪn','[v] 强迫, 限制','Poor soil has constrained the level of crop production.  贫瘠的土地限制了农作物的产量。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4622','exploitation',',ɛksplɔɪ''teʃən','eksplɒɪ''teɪʃ(ə)n','[n] 开发, 开采',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4623','doctrine','''dɑktrɪn','''dɒktrɪn','[n] 教条, 学说','traditional doctrines of divine power  神力的传统教义'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4624','immeasurably','ɪ''mɛʒərəbli','','[adv] 无法计量地, 无限地','They have improved immeasurably since their arrival.  从他们抵达以来，他们已极大程度地改进了。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4625','ambition','æm''bɪʃən','æm''bɪʃ(ə)n','[n] 野心, 雄心','He was young and full of ambition.  他年轻，而且雄心勃勃。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4626','perpetuate','pɚ''pɛtʃuet','pə''petʃʊeɪt; -tjʊ-','[v] 使永存, 使不朽','an education system that perpetuates the divisions in our society  使我们的社会持续分化的一种教育制度'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4627','afterlife','''æftəlaɪf','''ɑːftəlaɪf','[n] 来世, 后来的岁月',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4628','bask','bæsk','bɑːsk','[v] 晒太阳','All through the hot, still days of their holiday Amy basked in the sun.  在整个炎热、寂静的假期里埃米都在晒太阳。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4629','humanitarian','hju,mænɪ''tɛrɪən','hjʊ,mænɪ''teərɪən','[n&a] 人道主义者(的)','And on each of those issues we have said that we would consider that and, in fact, have provided some humanitarian support.  对于每一件这样的事情，我们都说过，我们将会对此进行考虑，事实上，我们向他们提供了人道主义援助。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4630','shoemaker','''ʃʊ''mekɚ','''ʃuːmeɪkə','[n] 鞋匠','Mr Zhu, a shoemaker from Foshan, near Hong Kong, is on his second trip to Africa.  朱先生是一个来自离香港不远的佛山的鞋匠，这是他第二次来非洲。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4631','prairies','','','[n] 大草原','He  has  transformed woodlands and prairies into farms and made lakes and reserviors out of rivers for irrigation purposes or hydroelectric power.  他将林地和草原改造成为农田，使江河变成湖泊和水库，用于灌溉或用于水力发电。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4632','handicraft','''hændɪkræft','''hændɪkrɑːft','[n] 手工艺(品)','a shop selling handicrafts  一家出售手工艺品的商店'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4633','logically','''lɑdʒɪkli','''lɔdʒikli','[adv] 符合逻辑地, 逻辑上地',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4634','airstream','''ɛrstrim','''eəstriːm','[n] 气流','The Growler is able to keep its weapons charged up and humming by lowering special turbines into the airstream that rushes past the plane when it is flying.  咆哮者可将特制的涡轮机降至飞机飞过时留下的气流里来实现对武器进行充电并使其重新进入活跃状态。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4635','whoever','hʊ''ɛvɚ','huːˈɛvə','[pron] 任何人, 无论谁','I’ll take whoever wants to go.  谁想去我就带谁去。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4636','unsafe','ʌn''sef','ʌn''seɪf','[adj] 不安全的','The building is unsafe.  那栋大楼不安全。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4637','flashbulb','','''flæʃbʌlb','[n] [摄]闪光灯泡','Actually even so-called ''flashbulb memories''—like where you were when Kennedy was shot—can be quite inaccurate or easily change over time.  事实上，即使是闪光灯记忆，就像你在肯尼迪被射杀的现场，也是非常不精确的，非常容易改变的。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4638','bovine','''bovaɪn','''bəʊvaɪn','[adj] (似)牛的，迟钝的','bovine diseases  牛病'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4639','thoughtful','''θɔtfl','''θɔːtfʊl; -f(ə)l','[adj] 深思的','a thoughtful look  若有所思的神情'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4640','ignite','ɪɡ''naɪt','ɪg''naɪt','[v] 点火','The petrol tank suddenly ignited.  油箱突然着火了。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4641','icicle','''aɪsɪkl','''aɪsɪk(ə)l','[n] 冰柱','Missis walked in'', she said, `as chill as an icicle, and as high as a princess.  “夫人走进来了，”她说，“跟个冰柱似的，冷冰冰的，又像个公主似的高不可攀。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4642','unbroken','ʌn''brokən','ʌn''brəʊk(ə)n','[adj] 不间断的','their unbroken record of success  他们不断成功的纪录'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4643','funnel','''fʌnl','''fʌn(ə)l','[n] 漏斗,烟囱','...a ship with three masts and two funnels.  …一艘有3根桅杆和2个烟囱的轮船。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4644','fastidious','fæ''stɪdɪəs','fæ''stɪdɪəs','[adj] 过分讲究的, 挑剔的','people who are fastidious about personal hygiene  十分讲究个人卫生的人'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4645','overshadow','''ovɚ''ʃædo','əʊvə''ʃædəʊ','[v] 遮蔽, 使失色','a dark valley overshadowed by towering peaks  被高耸的山峰遮蔽的幽暗山谷'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4646','hare','hɛr','heə','[n] 野兔','Because it makes its home in an extreme environment, the desert hare is biologically designed to radiate excess heat through its lanky limbs and oversized ears.  因为生长在极端环境中，沙漠兔子形成了独特的生物学构造，通过瘦长的四肢和超大的耳朵辐射多余的热量。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4647','consult','kən''sʌlt','kən''sʌlt','[v] 商量, 商议','I can’t believe you sold the car without consulting me!  我真不敢相信你不和我商量一下就把车给卖了！'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4648','inhospitable',',ɪnhɑ''spɪtəbl',',ɪnhɒ''spɪtəb(ə)l; ɪn''hɒspɪt-','[adj] 不好客的,不适于居住的','an inhospitable climate  不宜人的气候'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4649','artistically','','','[adv] 艺术地, 在艺术上',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4650','pigmentation',',pɪɡmɛn''teʃən','pɪgm(ə)n''teɪʃ(ə)n','[n] 染色','The dark pigmentation gives protection from the sun’s rays.  这种天然的深色可避免阳光伤害。'),
