('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4731','respondent','rɪ''spɑndənt','rɪ''spɒnd(ə)nt','[n] 应答者, 被告','Upon receipt of a copy of the arbitration application, the respondent shall, within the time limit prescribed by the Arbitration Rules, submit its defence to the arbitration commission.  被申请人收到仲裁申请书副本后，应当在仲裁规则规定的期限内向仲裁委员会提交答辩书。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4732','portrayal','pɔr''treəl','pɔː''treɪəl','[n] 描画, 描写','...a moving portrayal of St. John the Evangelist by Simone Martini.  …西蒙纳·马蒂尼创作的福音传道者圣约翰的感人画像。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4733','declare','dɪ''klɛr','dɪ''kleə','[v] 宣布，声明','A state of emergency has been declared.  已宣布进入紧急状态。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4734','curtain','''kɝtn','''kɜːt(ə)n','[n] 窗帘','red velvet curtains  红色的丝绒窗帘'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4735','hexagon','''hɛksəɡɑn','''heksəg(ə)n','[n] 六角形, 六边形','He presses the bolt against a small hexagon tattooed on his forearm. The sizes match.  他将螺钉与他前臂的一个小六边形纹身比了比，尺寸是一样的。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4736','poetic','po''ɛtɪk','pəʊ''etɪk','[adj] 诗歌的','poetic expression  诗歌的表达方式'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4737','undisturbed',',ʌndɪ''stɝbd','ʌndɪ''stɜːbd','[adj] 未受干扰的','At last I was able to work undisturbed.  我终于可以安安静静地工作了。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4738','ascent','ə''sɛnt','ə''sent','[n] 上升,提高','the first ascent of Qomolangma  首次攀登珠穆朗玛峰'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4739','Talbot','','','[n] [动]塔尔博特提猎狗','The photograph was taken by William Henry Fox Talbot, the inventor of the negative / positive photographic process.  这张照片是由威廉·亨利·福克斯·塔尔博特摄制，他是负片/正片摄影过程的发明者。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4740','query','''kwɪri','''kwɪərɪ','[n&v] 质问,疑问','Staff are always available to answer your queries.  员工随时为您解答疑问。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4741','evoke','ɪ''vok','ɪ''vəʊk','[v] 唤起, 引起','The photographs evoked strong memories of our holidays in France.  那些照片勾起了我们到法国度假的深刻回忆。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4742','amass','ə''mæs','ə''mæs','[v] 积累，积聚','For 25 years, Darwin amassed evidence to support his theories.  25年间，达尔文收集了大量证据来支持自己的理论。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4743','poll','pol','pəʊl','[n] 民意测验, 投票','A recent poll found that 80% of Californians support the governor.  最近的一项民意调查发现80%的加利福尼亚人支持州长。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4744','causal','''kɔzl','''kɔːz(ə)l','[adj] 原因的','Rawlins stresses that it is impossible to prove a causal link between the drug and the deaths.  罗林斯强调说证实毒品与死亡之间的因果关系是不可能的。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4745','glide','ɡlaɪd','glaɪd','[v&n] 滑行','Waiters glide between tightly packed tables bearing trays of pasta.  侍者们托着一盘盘的意大利面食在拥挤的餐桌间自如穿行。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4746','metalworker','','','[n] 金工工人','Some scholars believe that this astrolabe was created by the prince in collaboration with an unnamed metalworker.  一些学者认为，这个星盘是奥马尔王子与一位无名金属制造工匠共同制作的。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4747','sinuous','''sɪnjʊəs','''sɪnjʊəs','[adj] 蜿蜒的','They followed the sinuous trail deep into the mountains.  他们沿着弯弯曲曲的小径进入深山。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4748','floral','''flɔrəl','''flɔːr(ə)l; ''flɒ-','[adj] 花的,像花的','a scarf with a bold floral pattern  印有鲜艳花卉图案的围巾'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4749','grasp','ɡræsp','grɑːsp','[v] 抓住,领会','At that time, we did not fully grasp the significance of what had happened.  当时，我们没有完全明白所发生之事的重要性。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4750','incongruous','ɪn''kɑŋɡruəs','ɪn''kɒŋgrʊəs','[adj] 不协调的,不一致的','The new theatre looks utterly incongruous in its setting.  这座新剧院和周围的环境格格不入。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4751','overlook',',ovɚ''lʊk','əʊvə''lʊk','[v&n] 俯瞰,忽视','It is easy to overlook a small detail like that.  那样的小细节很容易被忽略。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4752','adventurer','əd''vɛntʃərɚ','əd''ventʃ(ə)rə','[n] 冒险家','an adventurer travelling the world  周游世界的冒险家'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4753','personalize','''pɝsənəlaɪz','''pɜːs(ə)n(ə)laɪz','[v] 个人化, 私人化','Why not do something to personalize your office?  为什么不做点什么使你的办公室有些个性呢？'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4754','tenant','''tɛnənt','''tenənt','[n] 承租人, 房客','The desk was left by the previous tenant.  书桌是上一个房客留下来的。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4755','herbaceous','ɝ''beʃəs','hɜː''beɪʃəs','[adj] 草本植物的','To their surprise, Ms Sagot and Dr Stevens found that all four of the most sociable species are among those forced to use herbaceous plants, and thus to build ramshackle homes.  令他们吃惊的是，萨戈女士和史蒂文斯博士发现，所有最善群居的四个种群是那些迫使运用草本植物并因此建造摇摇欲坠的巢穴的蝙蝠。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4756','sap','sæp','sæp','[n] 树液  vt耗尽','The leaves, bark and sap are also common ingredients of local herbal remedies.  树叶、树皮和树液也是当地草药疗法的常用药材。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4757','respective','rɪ''spɛktɪv','rɪ''spektɪv','[adj] 分别的, 各自的','We all went back to our respective homes to wait for news.  我们都各自回家等待消息。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4758','primordial','praɪ''mɔrdɪəl','praɪ''mɔːdɪəl','[adj] 原始的,最初的','the primordial seas  原始海洋'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4759','oversee','''ovɚ''si','əʊvə''siː','[v] 监督，监管','A team leader was appointed to oversee the project.  任命了一位组长来监管该工程。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4760','deity','''deəti','''deɪɪtɪ; ''diːɪ-','[n] 神, 神性','the deities of ancient Greece  古希腊诸神'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4761','phosphorus','''fɑsfərəs','''fɒsf(ə)rəs','[n] 磷','Because scientists have found a bacterium that can do without phosphorus—live on arsenic instead.  因为科学家已经发现了一种细菌，可以无需磷生活而以砷代替。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4762','unearned',',ʌn''ɝnd','ʌn''ɜːnd','[adj] 不劳而获的','The abolition of incomes unearned by work.  第十一条，取缔不劳而获的收入。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4763','burrow','''bɝro','''bʌrəʊ','[n] 洞穴; [v] 挖地洞','Normally timid, they rarely stray far from their burrows.  它们通常很胆小，极少远离自己的洞穴。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4764','infrequent','ɪn''frikwənt','ɪn''friːkw(ə)nt','[adj] 不频发的,不常见的','They would make infrequent visits to the house.  他们偶尔去看一看那所房子。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4765','acclaim','ə''klem','ə''kleɪm','[n&v] 喝采, 欢呼','Blessed are those who have learned to acclaim you, who walk in the light of your presence, O Lord .  知道向你欢呼的，那民是有福的。 耶和华阿，他们在你脸上的光里行走。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4766','peg','pɛɡ','peg','[n] 小钉; [v] 钉，固定','Sarah hung her coat on the peg.  萨拉把外套挂在衣钩上。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4767','translation','træns''leʃən','træns''leɪʃ(ə)n; trɑːns-; -nz-','[n] 翻译, 译文','She read the letter and gave us a rough translation (= she did not translate everything exactly ) .  她看了信，给我们大概翻译了一下。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4768','yarn','jɑn','jɑːn','[n] 纱线; [v] 讲故事','She still spins the yarn and knits sweaters for her family.  她仍在为她的家人纺线织毛衣。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4769','plasma','''plæzmə','''plæzmə','[n] 血浆','Blood cells like red blood cells float in the plasma.  血细胞就是像在血浆里漂浮的红色血细胞.'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4770','London','ˈlʌndən','ˈlʌndən','[n] 伦敦','He was nursed in London.  他是在伦敦长大的。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4771','originality','ə''rɪdʒə''næləti','ə,rɪdʒɪ''nælɪtɪ','[n] 独创性','Her earlier work shows a lot of originality.  她的早期作品显示出丰富的独创性。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4772','ford','fɔrd','fɔːd','[n] 浅滩 v徒涉',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4773','mortise','''mɔrtɪs','''mɔːtɪs','[n] 榫眼  v用榫接合','And there are any metallic connectives on this bed, joggle is between bed leg and bedplate, craftsman certains ably good mortise, this bed combination is together.  并且这个床上没有任何金属连接物，床腿和床板之间都是榫接的，工匠巧妙地凿好榫眼，将这个床组合在一起。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4774','wander','''wɑndɚ','''wɒndə','[v] 漫步, 徘徊','She wandered aimlessly about the house.  她漫无目的地在房子里走来走去。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4775','mate','met','meɪt','[n] 配偶, 对手','He has found his ideal mate.  他已经找到了理想的配偶。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4776','microbial','maɪ''krobɪəl','maɪ''krəʊbɪəl','[adj] 微生物的,  由细菌引起的','...the question of whether microbial life exists, or once existed, on Mars.  ...这个火星上是否存在或曾经存在过微生物的问题。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4777','intervene',',ɪntɚ''vin','ɪntə''viːn','[v] 干涉，干预','The army will have to intervene to prevent further fighting.  军队将不得不干预以阻止进一步的战斗。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4778','ironwork','''aiənwə:k','''aɪənwɜːk','[n] 铁制品','...the ironwork on the doors.  ...这些门上的铁艺部分。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4779','unearth','ʌn''ɝθ','ʌn''ɜːθ','[v] 掘出','Farmers still sometimes unearth human bones here.  农民们有时仍然能在这里挖到人骨。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4780','microbiologist','','','[n] 微生物学家','I remember when Jurassic Park came out, a microbiologist friend constantly told me how outlandish it was, but within a few years, he said it was interesting how far things have come.  我记得当《侏罗纪公园》出现的时候，一个微生物学家朋友不断的告诉我这影片太奇异了，但是在几年之内，他说影片中的科技到底还有多久才能实现很令人感兴趣。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4781','situate','''sɪtʃʊet','''sɪtʃʊeɪt; -tjʊ-','[v] 位于，坐落在',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4782','mallet','''mælɪt','''mælɪt','[n] 槌棒','I even have a wooden mallet that was used by a judge over 300 years ago during condemnation proceedings in Salem.  我甚至还有一把300多年前的木槌。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4783','alcohol','''ælkəhɔl','''ælkəhɒl','[n] 酒精,酒','I don’t drink alcohol anymore.  我不再喝酒了。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4784','guncotton','''gʌn,kɑtn','''ɡʌn,kɒtən','[n] [军]强棉药',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4785','approval','əˈpruvl','ə''pruːv(ə)l','[n] 赞同,批准, 认可','The president has already given his approval to the plan.  总统已经批准了这个计划。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4786','fathom','''fæðəm','''fæð(ə)m','[n] 长度单位(6英尺)',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4787','accidental',',æksɪ''dɛntl','æksɪ''dent(ə)l','[adj] 意外的，偶然(发生)的','an accidental discharge of toxic waste  有毒废料的意外排放'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4788','disastrous','dɪ''zæstrəs','dɪ''zɑːstrəs','[adj] 灾难性的, 极糟的','a disastrous first marriage  以失败告终的第一次婚姻'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4789','execute','''ɛksɪkjut','''eksɪkjuːt','[v] 执行, 处决','The job involves drawing up and executing a plan of nursing care.  这项工作包括拟订和实施一个护理计划。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4790','supersonic',',supɚ''sɑnɪk','suːpə''sɒnɪk; sjuː-','[n&a] 超声波(的)',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4791','exemplify','ɪɡ''zɛmplɪfaɪ','ɪg''zemplɪfaɪ; eg-','[v] 例证, 例示','All these recipes exemplify my cooking: healthy, delicious and quick.  所有这些食谱例证了我的饭菜：健康、美味、快捷。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4792','sixth','sɪksθ','sɪksθ','[num] 第六, 六分之一','About one sixth of the children admitted to taking drugs.  大约六分之一的儿童承认吸毒。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4793','sex','','','[n] 性别,性','All you see on TV is sex and violence these days.  如今在电视上看到的尽是性和暴力。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4794','pantomime','''pæntəmaɪm','''pæntəmaɪm','[n] 哑剧','They were made welcome with the usual pantomime of exaggerated smiles and gestures.  他们以那种具有夸张的微笑和动作的一般闹剧受到欢迎。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4795','alligator','''ælɪɡetɚ','''ælɪgeɪtə','[n] 产于美洲的鳄鱼',''),
