('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4914','wholesale','''holsel','''həʊlseɪl','[n] 批发; [adj] 大规模的','He does wholesale business, while his brother is engaged in retail business.  他经营批发生意， 他弟弟则经营零售生意。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4915','cart','kɑrt','kɑːt','[n] 大车，手推车',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4916','adrift','ə''drɪft','ə''drɪft','[a&ad] 漂流的,漫无目的',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4917','mystical','''mɪstɪkl','''mɪstɪk(ə)l','[adj] 神秘的','music’s spiritual and mystical powers  音乐的精神力量以及神秘能力'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4918','coerce','ko''ɝs','kəʊ''ɜːs','[v] 强制','The real magic in MochiKit.DOM is its willingness to flexibly coerce various types of objects into the right types during method calls, including doing so recursively.  DOM 真正的魔法在于它在方法调用过程中积极而灵活地把各种对象类型强制转换成正确的类型，包括在递归过程中。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4919','crash','kræʃ','kræʃ','[v] 碰撞，撞击','The jet crashed after take-off.  这架喷气式飞机起飞后就坠毁了。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4920','eccentricity',',ɛksɛn''trɪsəti',',eksen''trɪsɪtɪ','[n] 反常，怪癖','Kate’s mother had a reputation for eccentricity.  凯特的母亲是个出了名的怪人。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4921','distasteful','dɪs''testfl','dɪs''teɪstf(ʊ)l','[adj] 味道差的,反感的','What follows is John’s story. Parts of it may seem distasteful, even shocking.  接下来是约翰的叙述，其中有些部分也许令人不快，甚至令人震惊。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4922','tragedy','''trædʒədi','''trædʒɪdɪ','[n] 悲剧, 惨案','The tragedy happened as they were returning home from a night out.  悲剧发生在他们夜里外出归来的路上。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4923','lantern','''læntɚn','''læntən','[n] 灯笼，提灯','In the course of time, this kind of lantern has become an exclusive of the Shens.  后来， 这种灯笼成了沈家的绝活。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4924','diagram','''daɪəɡræm','''daɪəgræm','[n] 图表','...a circuit diagram.  …电路图。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4925','spell','spɛl','spel','[v] 拼写','How do you spell ‘juice’?  juice 怎么拼？'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4926','durability','','','[n] 经久, 耐久力',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4927','stark','stɑrk','stɑːk','[adj] 荒凉的；严酷的; [adv] 完全','In the cold dawn light, the castle looked stark and forbidding.  在寒冷的曙光中，城堡看上去了无生气，令人生畏。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4928','code','','','[n] 代码 vt把…编码',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4929','revere','rɪ''vɪr','rɪ''vɪə','[v] 尊敬,敬畏','The Chinese revered corn as a gift from heaven.  中国人将谷物奉为天赐礼物。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4930','crush','krʌʃ','krʌʃ','[vt&n] 压碎','His leg was crushed in the accident.  他的腿在事故中被压断。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4931','goose','ɡus','guːs','[n] 鹅','...roast goose.  …烤鹅。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4932','tabulate','''tæbjulet','''tæbjʊleɪt','[v] 把制成表格','Results for the test programme haven''t been tabulated.  试验项目的结果还没有制成表格。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4933','please','pliz','pliːz','[adv] 请 v使高兴','a business that wants to please its customers  希望让顾客满意的一家公司'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4934','uniquely','ju:''ni:kli','ju:''ni:kli','[adv] adv独特地, 唯一地',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4935','birch','bɝtʃ','bɜːtʃ','[n] 桦树, 白桦','In Finland purists insist that only birch bark should be added.  在芬兰，纯化论者坚持说只能加白桦树皮。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4936','adaptability','ə,dæptə''bɪləti','ə,dæptə''bɪlətɪ','[n] 适应性','You can achieve greater flexibility, adaptability, and independence when each layer is only loosely coupled to the layer above and below.  当每个层仅松散耦合到其上和其下的层时，您可以实现更强的灵活性、适应性和独立性。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4937','caledonian','','','[n&a] 苏格兰人(的)',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4938','strive','straɪv','straɪv','[v] 努力, 奋斗','He strives hard to keep himself very fit.  他努力使自己保持非常的健康。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4939','qualitative','''kwɑlətetɪv','''kwɒlɪtətɪv','[adj] 性质上的, 定性的','There are qualitative differences in the way children of different ages and adults think.  不同年龄的儿童和成人在思维方式上有着质的差异。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4940','gram','ɡræm','ɡræm','[n] 克','Then they chose one gram for weighing water in a cubic centimetre.  然后他们将一立方厘米的水的重量定为一克。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4941','prohibitive','prə''hɪbətɪv','prə(ʊ)''hɪbɪtɪv','[adj] 禁止的, 抑制的','prohibitive regulations  禁律'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4942','prospector','''prɑspɛktɚ','prəʊ''spektə','[n] 探勘者, 采矿者','Although he failed as a prospector, he succeeded as a journalist.  他作为采矿者遭遇失败，但作为记者大获成功。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4943','contradiction',',kɑntrə''dɪkʃən','kɒntrə''dɪkʃ(ə)n','[n] 反驳, 矛盾','apparent contradictions in the defendant’s testimony  被告证词中的明显矛盾'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4944','auditorium',',ɔdɪ''tɔrɪəm','ɔːdɪ''tɔːrɪəm','[n] 听众席,观众席,','Anderson was to sing at the Constitution Hall auditorium.  安德森将要在宪法厅的观众席演唱。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4945','remark','rɪ''mɑrk','rɪ''mɑːk','[n] 备注,评论 vt评论','Unfortunately, a local journalist overheard the remark.  不巧一名当地记者无意中听到了这些话。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4946','rote','rot','rəʊt','[n] 死记硬背','In old-fashioned schools, much learning was by rote .  在旧式学校里，很多学习都是靠死记硬背。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4947','battleship','''bætlʃɪp','''bæt(ə)lʃɪp','[n] 战舰','A new battleship was launched from a shipyard.  一艘新战舰从船坞下水。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4948','regime','re''ʒim','reɪ''ʒiːm','[n] 政权制度,政权','The regime got rid of most of its opponents.  该政权清除了大多数反对者。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4949','skepticism','''skɛptɪ,sɪzəm','''skeptisizəm','[n] 怀疑论','I know there are those who don’t believe we can do all these things. I understand the skepticism.  我知道有些人不相信我们可以完成所有这些事情，我理解他们所持的怀疑态度。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4950','economist','ɪ''kɑnəmɪst','ɪ''kɒnəmɪst','[n] 经济学者','Do you have some hints for me, how to become a good economist?  如何成为一名好的经济学家，你有什么给我的提示吗？'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4951','commandment','kə''mændmənt','kə''mɑːndmənt','[n] 戒律','So you would not break the third commandment.  那么你就不会违反第三条戒律。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4952','glimpse','ɡlɪmps','glɪm(p)s','[n] 一瞥v瞥见','Some of the fans had waited 24 hours outside the hotel to catch a glimpse of their heroine.  某些追星族为了一睹女杰的风采已在宾馆外守候了24小时。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4953','preferable','''prɛfrəbl','''pref(ə)rəb(ə)l','[adj] 更好的,更合意的','For this dish, fresh herbs and garlic are preferable.  做这道菜，用新鲜香草和大蒜更好。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4954','delineate','dɪ''lɪnɪet','dɪ''lɪnɪeɪt','[v] 描绘','The document delineates your rights and your obligations.  这份文件阐明了你的权利和义务。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4955','rugged','''rʌɡɪd','''rʌgɪd','[adj] 高低不平的, 崎岖的','a rugged coastline  崎岖不平的海岸线'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4956','referent','''rɛfərənt','''ref(ə)r(ə)nt','[n] 指示物',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4957','inadequacy','ɪn''ædɪkwəsi','ɪn''ædɪkwəsɪ','[n] 不充分',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4958','Gypsy','','','[n&a] 吉普赛人(的),吉普赛语（的）','I''m proud of being brought up by gypsies.  我为自己是吉卜赛人抚养长大的而感到自豪。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4959','outwash','''aʊtwɑʃ','''aʊtwɒʃ','[n] [地质]冰水沉积','This landslide deposit pretty much rules out the idea that the deposits farther upstream are glacial outwash.  这个滑坡沉积物大可以排除远离上游的沉积物是冰川沉积的想法。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4960','crumble','''krʌmbl','''krʌmb(ə)l','[v] 弄碎,崩溃','The old stonework was crumbling away.  古老的石筑部分逐渐崩塌。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4961','dissatisfaction','dɪs''sætɪs''fækʃən','dɪssætɪs''fækʃn','[n] 不满','She has already expressed her dissatisfaction with this aspect of the policy.  她已对政策的这方面表示了不满。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4962','knap','','næp','[v] 敲击',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4963','basaltic','','','[adj] 玄武岩的','Frantz Josef Land is a basaltic plateau split into many islands and covered with ice.  法兰仕约瑟夫地的群岛是由一个玄武岩高原分裂而成的，终年覆盖着冰雪。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4964','plateau','plæ''to','''plætəʊ','[n] 高地, 高原','A broad valley opened up leading to a high, flat plateau of cultivated land.  一个宽阔的山谷展开，通向一片平坦的高原耕地。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4965','carbonic','kɑr''bɑnɪk','kɑː''bɒnɪk','[adj] (含)碳的','Should the carbon dioxide mix with water underground and form carbonic acid, they say, it could leach poisonous materials from rock deep underground that could then seep out.  他们说，一旦二氧化碳与地下水融合极易形成碳酸，而这会把地下岩石中的有毒物质分解出来，从而污染我们的水资源。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4966','lengthy','''lɛŋθi','''leŋθɪ; ''leŋkθɪ','[adj] 冗长的','A lengthy period of training is required.  需要很长一段时间的培训。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4967','intersect','''ɪntɚ''sɛkt','ɪntə''sekt','[v] 贯穿, 交叉','So tell me about. You have done music, where do these things intersect for you?  那么，你已经做过音乐和，艺术，这些事情的交叉点在哪里呢？'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4968','masterpiece','''mæstəpis','''mɑːstəpiːs','[n] 杰作, 名著','Mary Shelley was just 18 when she wrote the horror masterpiece ‘Frankenstein’.  玛丽•雪莱创作《科学怪人》这部恐怖小说名作的时候年仅18岁。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4969','Yale','','','[n] 耶鲁','What is the endowment of Yale?  耶鲁的捐赠基金是什么？'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4970','redwood','''rɛdwʊd','''redwʊd','[n] [植]红杉','Members of the group stand atop the stump of a giant redwood tree.  研究项目组的成员长在一块巨大的红杉树桩之上。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4971','connoisseur',',kɑnə''sɝ',',kɒnə''sɜː','[n] 鉴赏家','a wine connoisseur  品酒专家'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4972','accessory','ək''sɛsəri','ək''ses(ə)rɪ','[n] 附件; [adj] 辅助的','bathroom accessories such as mirrors and towel-rails  镜子和毛巾架等浴室配件'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4973','seriousness','''sɪrɪəsnəs','''sɪərɪəsnəs','[n] 严肃, 认真','With great seriousness he pondered upon the problem.  他极其严肃地仔细考虑问题。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4974','finely','''faɪnli','''faɪnlɪ','[adv] 细微地,美好地','finely chopped onion  剁得细碎的洋葱'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4975','preferentially',',prefə''renʃəli',',prefə''renʃəli','[adj] 优先的, 优待的','Heterosexuals should not be treated preferentially when the state carries out that role.  当国家执行这个作用的时候不应该优先对待异性恋者。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4976','acquisition',',ækwɪ''zɪʃən',',ækwɪ''zɪʃ(ə)n','[n] 获得(物)','the acquisition of language  语言的习得'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4977','march','mɑrtʃ','mɑːtʃ','[n&v] 行军','An estimated 5,000 people marched through the city to demonstrate against the factory closures.  大约有五千人在市里游行示威，抗议关闭工厂。'),
