('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4990','salinization',',selɪnaɪ''zeʃən',',sælɪnaɪ''zeɪʃən','[n] 盐渍化','Rising sea levels, increasing salinization of water tables, and heat stress in association with air pollution are just some of the consequences of great concern in this part of the world.  海平面不断上升，潜水层日益盐化，以及与空气污染有关的热应力只是这个区域极令人担忧的一部分后果。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4991','shrinkage','''ʃrɪŋkɪdʒ','''ʃrɪŋkɪdʒ','[n] 收缩','Pollution led to a shrinkage of grasslands.  污染导致草原面积缩小。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4992','detachment','dɪ''tætʃmənt','dɪ''tætʃm(ə)nt','[n] 冷漠, 脱离','The upright orientation is also the first step in surface detachment for bacteria.  这种直立的方位也是细菌脱离组织表面的第一步。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4993','oblige','ə''blaɪdʒ','ə''blaɪdʒ','[v] 迫使；施恩于','The storm got worse and worse. Finally, I was obliged to abandon the car and continue on foot.  暴风雨越来越猛烈。最终，我被迫弃车徒步前行。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4994','gully','''ɡʌli','''gʌlɪ','[n] 小峡谷, 排水沟','The bodies of the three climbers were located at the bottom of a steep gully.  3名登山者的尸体在一个陡峭的隘谷谷底找到了。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4995','inconclusive',',ɪnkən''klusɪv','ɪnkən''kluːsɪv','[adj] 非决定性的,不确定的','The evidence against the two men was inconclusive.  针对这两个人的不利证据并不令人信服。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4996','innovator','''ɪnə,vetɚ','''ɪnəveɪtə(r)','[n] 改革者, 革新者','He is an innovator in this field.  他是这个领域的革新者。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4997','pulverization','','','[n] 弄成粉, 粉碎','Then I talk impersonally about the possible pulverization of our big cities, with a hundred million dead. I am unable to multiply one man’s suffering by a hundred million.  但是如果我事不关己的谈论对我们城市可能造成的粉碎性攻击时，尽管它关乎数百万计的亡魂，我无法将我面对一个人痛苦的感情复制数百万倍。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4998','homemaking','','','[n] 家政','Titus 2 instructs older women to mentor younger women, and teach them to care for their husbands and children and homemaking responsibilities.  泰特斯 2让年长的女人去教导年轻女子，让她们照看好自己的丈夫、孩子和家庭。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_4999','rebuild',',ri''bɪld','riː''bɪld','[v] 重建, 改造','The church was completely rebuilt in the last century.  这座教堂在上个世纪全面重建。'),
