('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5689','disappearance',',dɪsə''pɪrəns','dɪsə''pɪərəns','[n] 不见,消失','Police are investigating the woman’s disappearance.  警方正在调查这名女子的失踪。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5690','abrupt','ə''brʌpt','ə''brʌpt','[adj] 突然的,陡峭的,生硬的','an abrupt change of plan  计划的突然改变'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5691','nowcasting','','','[n] 预告','To better forecast landslide and debris flow, we localized mesoscale model, the well-known MM5, and the nowcasting technique of satellite and radar also were utilized.  针对滑坡、泥石流，应用MM5中尺度预报模式进行本地化，并结合卫星和雷达的客观雨量预报方法。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5692','readership','''ridɚʃɪp','''riːdəʃɪp','[n] 读者的身分, 读者人数','They are hoping that the paper will have quite a wide readership .  他们希望这份报纸会有很多读者。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5693','pencil','''pɛnsl','''pens(ə)l; -sɪl','[n] 铅笔','a sharp pencil  尖尖的铅笔'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5694','wharf','wɔrf','wɔːf','[n] 码头; [v] 靠在码头','Our ship is on to the wharf.  我们的船靠向码头。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5695','individuality',',ɪndɪ,vɪdʒu''æləti',',ɪndɪvɪdjʊ''ælɪtɪ','[n] 个性,(通常用复数)个人的嗜好','We like our staff to show their individuality rather than wear a uniform.  我们喜欢员工穿出个性，而不是穿制服。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5696','squander','''skwɑndɚ','''skwɒndə','[v] 浪费; [n] 浪费','The home team squandered a number of chances in the first half.  主队在上半场浪费了几次机会。'),
