('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5783','slumber','''slʌmbɚ','''slʌmbə','[n] 睡眠; [v] 睡眠','He passed into a deep slumber.  他酣然入梦。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5784','dart','dɑrt','dɑːt','[n] 标枪, 镖; [v] 投掷','Markov died after being struck by a poison dart.  马尔科夫被毒镖击中后身亡。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5785','prevalence','''prɛvələns','''prev(ə)l(ə)ns; ''prevəl(ə)ns; ''prevələns','[n] 流行,普遍','However, no study on the prevalence of infertility has been conducted in this area.  但是，在这个地区不曾进行过任何关于不孕症流行情况的研究。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5786','cousin','''kʌzn','''kʌz(ə)n','[n] 堂兄弟姊妹, 表兄弟姊妹','My cousin Mark helped me to bring in the bags.  我表弟马克帮我把包提了进来。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5787','negligible','''nɛɡlɪdʒəbl','''neglɪdʒɪb(ə)l','[adj] 可以忽略的, 不予重视的','The damage done to his property was negligible.  对他财产造成的损失微不足道。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5788','finite','''faɪnaɪt','''faɪnaɪt','[adj] 有限的,限定的','the earth’s finite resources  地球有限的资源'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5789','sleeper','''slipɚ','''sliːpə','[n] 睡眠,枕木','ATR says reconstructing dreams is harder because the brain signals during sleep may be "noisier, " and is now researching how to get more meaningful information from a sleeper''s brain.  ATR表示，重现梦境更困难，因为睡梦中大脑信号也许“更嘈杂”。 他们现在正在研究如何从睡眠者的大脑中获取更有意义的信息。'),
