('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5805','cumulative','''kjumjəletɪv','''kjuːmjʊlətɪv','[adj] 累积的','Learning is a cumulative process.  学习是个逐渐积累的过程。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5806','creep','krip','kriːp','[v] 爬, 蹑手蹑脚; [n] 爬行','He crept back up the stairs, trying to avoid the ones that creaked.  他蹑手蹑脚地回楼上，尽量避开那些嘎吱作响的梯级。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5807','tan','tæn','tæn','[n] 日晒后的颜色; [adj] 棕褐色的; [v] 晒成褐色','I wish I could get a tan like that.  但愿我也能晒成那样的棕褐色肤色。'),
