('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5857','impressionistic',',ɪmprɛʃə''nɪstɪk','ɪm,preʃə''nɪstɪk','[adj] 印象派的,给人深刻印象的','His paintings had become more impressionistic as his eyesight dimmed.  随着他的视力减弱，他的画变得越来越富有印象派风格。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5858','faction','''fækʃən','''fækʃ(ə)n','[n] 派别,小集团','struggles between the different factions within the party  党内的派系斗争'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5859','fortuitously','','','[adv] 偶然地,意外地',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5860','thriller','''θrɪlɚ','''θrɪlə','[n] 使人毛骨悚然的东西, 使人毛骨悚然的小说','...a tense psychological thriller.  …一部紧张刺激的心理惊悚小说。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5861','plentifully','','','[adv] 丰富地,富裕地',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5862','monopolize','mə''nɑpə''laɪz','mə''nɔpəlaiz','[v] 独占, 垄断','The company has monopolized the soft drinks market.  该公司垄断了软饮料市场。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5863','burden','''bɝdn','''bɜːd(ə)n','[n] 担子, 负担; [v] 烦扰','His family responsibilities had started to become a burden.  家庭责任已开始成为他的负担。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5864','breadbasket','''brɛdbæskɪt','''bredbɑːskɪt','[n] <俚>胃, 腹',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5865','annihilate','ə''naɪəlet','ə''naɪɪleɪt','[v] 消灭,湮灭','Just one of these bombs could annihilate a city the size of New York.  这种炸弹只要一颗就能彻底毁灭纽约那么大的一座城市。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5866','sectional','''sɛkʃənl','''sekʃ(ə)n(ə)l','[adj] 可组合的,部分的','a sectional sofa  组合沙发'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5867','jealousy','''dʒɛləsi','''dʒeləsɪ','[n] 嫉妒,猜疑','Sexual jealousy is a common motive for murder.  性嫉妒是常见的谋杀动机。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5868','garbage','''ɡɑrbɪdʒ','''gɑːbɪdʒ','[n] 垃圾, 废物','Can you take out the garbage when you go?  你走的时候把垃圾带出去好吗？'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5869','routinely','rʊ''tinli','ru:''ti:nli','[adv] 例行公事地','This vaccine is already routinely used.  这种疫苗的使用已经常规化。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5870','predicament','prɪ''dɪkəmənt','prɪ''dɪkəm(ə)nt','[n] 困境,窘状','the country’s economic predicament  该国的经济困境'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5871','thermometer','θɚ''mɑmɪtɚ','θə''mɒmɪtə','[n] 温度计, 体温计','The thermometer registered over 100˚C.  温度计显示高于100摄氏度。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5872','divergence','dəˈvɜrdʒəns; daɪˈvɜrdʒəns','daɪ''vɜːdʒ(ə)ns','[n] 分歧','There''s a substantial divergence of opinion within the party.  党内意见严重分歧。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5873','oceanography',',oʃə''nɑɡrəfi',',əʊʃə''nɒgrəfɪ','[n] 海洋学','She wanted to introduce students to oceanography so that they might apply their knowledge to solve global challenges like climate change.  她要把海洋学介绍给学生们，希望他们能应用他们所学的知识去解决气候变化等全球性难题。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5874','outbuilding','''aʊt''bɪldɪŋ','''aʊtbɪldɪŋ','[n] [建]外屋, (指车库, 谷仓等)','a farmhouse with a few outbuildings  带几间外屋的农舍'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5875','forbes','''fɔ:bəz','''fɔ:bəz','[n] 福布斯（美国著名财经杂志）',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5876','grama','''grɑmə','''ɡrɑːmə','[n] 美国西部产的一种牧草',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5877','rhyolite','''raɪə,laɪt','''raɪəlaɪt','[n] [地]流纹岩','Topaz occurs in the igneous rock rhyolite.  黄晶通常产于火成岩岩石纹。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5878','decisive','dɪ''saɪsɪv','dɪ''saɪsɪv','[adj] 决定性的,果断的','a decisive leader  果断的领袖'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5879','comparably','','','[adv] 同等地,可比较地',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5880','transmitter','træns''mɪtɚ','trænz''mɪtə; trɑːnz-; -ns-','[n] 转送者,传导物,发射机','...a homemade radio transmitter.  …一台自制的无线电发射机。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5881','exponential','''ɛkspə''nɛnʃəl',',ekspə''nenʃ(ə)l','[n] 指数; [adj] 指数的, 幂数的','This is an exponential function.  因为这里是指数函数。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5882','gesso','''dʒesəu','''dʒesəʊ','[n] (雕刻、绘画用的)石膏, 石膏粉','Processing category:Various dry and wet materials that could be crushed, including chemical raw materials, gesso powders, hulls, grains, and plastics .  加工类别：各种可以粉碎的干湿料物，化工原料、石膏粉、皮类、粮食类、塑料类。棉花类，生物类。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5883','attendant','ə''tɛndənt','ə''tend(ə)nt','[n] 服务员; [adj] 伴随的','a car park attendant  停车场的服务员'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5884','capitalism','''kæpɪtəlɪzəm','''kæpɪt(ə)lɪz(ə)m','[n] 资本主义','...the two fundamentally opposed social systems, capitalism and socialism.  …两种根本对立的社会制度，资本主义与社会主义。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5885','deference','''dɛfərəns','''def(ə)r(ə)ns','[n] 顺从, 尊重','...the older political tradition of deference to great leaders.  …敬重伟大领导人的较老的政治传统。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5886','cumbersome','''kʌmbəsəm','''kʌmbəs(ə)m','[adj] 笨重的,累赘的','Doctors are complaining that the system is cumbersome and bureaucratic.  医生抱怨说该体制复杂繁琐，很官僚。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5887','weft','wɛft','weft','[n] [纺]织物,信号旗','Usage: This detector is applied to plastic looms for stopping operation in case of broken weft and weft-out. It is composed of signal emitter, receiver and controller.  用途：本检测器用于塑料园织机在断纬、完纬时控制主机停车之功能。它由信号发射器， 信号接收器和控制器三部分组成。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5888','dire','''daiə','''daɪə','[adj] 可怕的,极端的','warnings of dire consequences that often don’t come true  对严重后果的警告，尽管这些后果常常不会出现'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5889','pendant','''pɛndənt','''pend(ə)nt','[n] 垂饰, 下垂物','a ruby pendant  红宝石吊坠'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5890','basketmaking','','','[n] 篮子编织',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5891','generalist','''dʒɛnrəlɪst','''dʒen(ə)rəlɪst','[n] 多面手,通才','The presidency is a job for a generalist.  总统的职位是一个多面手做的。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5892','kennel','''kɛnl','''ken(ə)l','[n] 狗窝; [v] 置于狗窝,关进狗窝','Once you have chosen a kennel, make a booking for your pet.  一旦您选定了养狗场，请为您的宠物预约。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5893','postmaster','''postmæstɚ','''pəʊs(t)mɑːstə','[n] 邮局局长','As if from far away, he hears her call to the postmaster to send for the police.  好像是从很远的地方传来的声音，他听见她在让邮政局长打电话叫警察来。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5894','interestingly','''ɪntrəstɪŋlɪ','''ɪntrəstɪŋlɪ','[adv] 有趣地','Interestingly, none of their three children ever married.  有趣的是，他们的三个孩子都一直没有结婚。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5895','perfume','pɚ''fjum','''pɜːfjuːm','[n] 芳香,香水; [v] 使发香,洒香水于','She was wearing the perfume that he’d bought her.  她擦了他买给她的香水。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5896','concomitant','kən''kɑmətənt','kən''kɒmɪt(ə)nt','[adj] 伴随的; [n] 伴随物','war with all its concomitant sufferings  战争及其引起的一切苦难'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5897','patient','''peʃnt','''peɪʃ(ə)nt','[n] 病人; [adj] 耐心的','She sat by the patient.  她守护在病人身旁。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5898','reckless','''rɛkləs','''reklɪs','[adj] 不计后果的,鲁莽的','He was accused of causing death by reckless driving .  他被控因鲁莽驾驶致人死亡。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5899','rigidly','''ridʒidli','''ridʒidli','[adv] 坚硬地, 严格地','Historically, the consensus was to rigidly guard all source code and strictly govern how it was managed.  历史上，共识都将严格地保护所有的源代码，并严谨地支配它如何被管理。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5900','renounce','rɪ''naʊns','rɪ''naʊns','[v] 宣布放弃,断绝关系','Edward renounced his claim to the French throne.  爱德华宣布放弃对法国王位的继承权。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5901','overhang',',ovɚ''hæŋ','əʊvə''hæŋ','[v] 悬于之上,悬垂; [n] 屋檐','Part of the rock wall overhung the path at one point.  部分岩壁悬在了小径一处的上方。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5902','observatory','əb''zɝvətɔri','əb''zɜːvət(ə)rɪ','[adj] 天文台,气象台','An observatory on the back side of the Moon would be a giant leap for astronomy, but there is a for more important reason to return.  即使仅仅在月球的背面设置一个天文台，也将为天文学带来革命性的突破，何况月球的价值远远不止这些。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5903','urbanism','''ɝbən,ɪzəm','''ɜːbənɪzəm','[n] 都市生活,都市化','There is no magic formula explaining our attraction to architecture, construction, destruction, cultures and urbanism.  没有魔法公式能够解释建筑物、建筑、毁坏、文化和都市生活对我们的吸引力。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5904','refrigeration','rifrɪdʒə''reʃən','rɪ,frɪdʒə''reɪʃən','[n] 冷藏, 致冷','Mold can grow even under refrigeration, and aging cheese is a good example of that.  霉菌在冷藏条件下也可以生长，正在成熟的奶酪就是一个很好的例子。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5905','stuff','stʌf','stʌf','[n] 原料,素材资料; [v] 塞满','Volunteers were busy stuffing envelopes.  志愿者正忙着装信封。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5906','harshly','''ha:ʃli','''ha:ʃli','[adv] 严厉地, 苛刻地','You had little cause to judge him so harshly.  你没有什么理由这样严厉地批评他。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5907','chitin','''kaɪtɪn','''kaɪtɪn','[n] 壳质, 角素','The organization of a tiny honeybee yields a pattern for its tinier one-tenth of a gram of wing cells, tissue, and chitin.  一只小蜜蜂的机体所代表的模式，只适用于其十分之一克重的更细小的翅室［5］、组织和壳质。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5908','polymer','''pɑlɪmɚ','''pɒlɪmə','[n] 聚合体','So, what I want to do is go back to this simple polymer configurational model that we introduced before.  那么，我想做的是回到,简单的聚合物构型模型,我们之前介绍过的。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5909','Jules','dʒulz','dʒu:lz','[n] 朱尔斯（男子名）','This is one of my go to meals now … thank you Jules!  这是我现在将要去吃的菜之一… 感谢朱尔斯！'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5910','reviewer','rɪ''vjuɚ','rɪ''vjuːə','[n] 批评家,评论家','...the reviewer for Atlantic Monthly.  …《大西洋月刊》的评论员。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5911','triassic','traɪ''æsɪk','trai''æsik','[adj] [地]三叠纪的; [n] 三叠纪',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5912','adjunct','''ædʒʌŋkt','''ædʒʌŋ(k)t','[n] 附件, 助手; [adj] 附属的','For me, it represents a potent adjunct to antidepressant medications and, for some patients, it’s something you can take in lieu of pills.  对于我，它是一个抗抑郁剂曾用药物的强有力的助手，对一些病人来说，它是能够代替药丸的东西。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5913','glasswork','','''glæs,wərk','[n] 玻璃制品; [v] 制成玻璃状的','Polymer clay pieces often mimic millefiori, a glasswork technique commonly seen in paperweights.  软陶经常模仿千花玻璃的工艺，这是通常用于做纸镇的一种玻璃工艺。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5914','sate','set','seɪt','[v] 使心满意足',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5915','flier','''flaɪɚ','''flaɪə','[n] 飞行者,快车,宣传单',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5916','deplorable','dɪ''plɔrəbl','dɪ''plɔːrəb(ə)l','[adj] 可叹的,凄惨的','The prisoners were held in deplorable conditions .  囚犯被关押在极其恶劣的环境里。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5917','instructor','ɪn''strʌktɚ','ɪn''strʌktə','[n] 教师,指导书','a driving instructor  驾驶教练'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5918','midday',',mɪd''de','mɪd''deɪ','[n] 正午','We stopped off in Colchester for our midday meal .  我们中途在科尔切斯特停留吃了午饭。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5919','auto','''ɔto','''ɔːtəʊ','[n] 自动,<美口>汽车','imported autos  进口汽车'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5920','loneliness','''lonlɪnɪs','''ləʊnlɪnɪs','[n] 孤独, 寂寞','I have so many friends, but deep down, underneath, I have a fear of loneliness.  我有这么多朋友，但是内心深处我还是有一种对孤独的恐惧。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5921','hopeless','ˈhoʊpləs','''həʊpləs','[adj] 没有希望的,不可救药','We tried to stop the flames from spreading, but we knew it was hopeless.  我们试图阻止火势蔓延，但我们知道这是不可能的。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5922','interchangeable',',ɪntɚ''tʃendʒəbl','ɪntə''tʃeɪn(d)ʒəbl','[adj] 可互换的,可交换的','These two words are almost interchangeable.  这两个单词几乎可以互换使用。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5923','bizarre','bɪ''zɑr','bɪ''zɑː','[adj] 奇异的(指态度,容貌,款式等)','a bizarre coincidence  奇怪的巧合'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5924','laundry','''lɔndri','''lɔːndrɪ','[n] 洗衣店, 要洗的衣服','She did the laundry (= washed the clothes etc ) and hung it out to dry.  她洗了衣服，然后挂出去晾干。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5925','definitive','dɪ''fɪnətɪv','dɪ''fɪnɪtɪv','[adj] 最后的,确定的','a definitive agreement to buy the company  收购这家公司的最终协议'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5926','puncture','''pʌŋktʃɚ','''pʌŋ(k)tʃə','[n] 小孔; [v] 刺破','She was cycling home when she had a puncture .  她骑车回家途中轮胎被扎破了。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5927','glandular','''glændʒəlɚ','''glændjʊlə; ''glæn(d)ʒʊlə','[adj] 腺的,腺状的','...the amount of fat and glandular tissue in the breasts.  ...乳房里的脂肪和腺体组织含量。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5928','glycoside','''glaɪkə,saɪd','''glaɪkə(ʊ)saɪd','[n] [化]配醣, 配糖类',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5929','interactive',',ɪntɚ''æktɪv','ɪntər''æktɪv','[adj] 交互式的,相互作用的','interactive computer systems  交互式电脑系统'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5930','preform','pri''fɔrm','priː''fɔːm','[v] 预先形成; [n] 粗加工的成品',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5931','unusable',',ʌn''juzəbl','','[adj] 不能用的,与众不同的','Bombing had made roads and railways unusable.  轰炸使得公路和铁路都不能用。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5932','inducible','','','[adj] 可诱导的,可导致的','In addition, plants have also evolved an adaptive inducible resistance mechanism in response to pathogen invasion.  同时，植物还形成了一套适应性更广的可诱导的抗病机制。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5933','sepal','''sɛpl','''sep(ə)l; ''siːp(ə)l','[n] 萼片','Botany The hood-shaped sepal or corolla of some flowers.  盔状花冠（或花萼）：某些花朵盔状的花萼或花冠。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5934','snippet','''snippit','''snɪpɪt','[n] 小片, 片断','...snippets of popular classical music.  …流行古典音乐的片段。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5935','correlate','''kɔrəlet','''kɒrəleɪt; -rɪ-','[v] 相互关联; [adj] 相互关联的','Attempts to correlate specific language functions with particular parts of the brain have not advanced very far.  试图把特定的语言功能和大脑特定区域相联系的努力还没有取得很大进展。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5936','beetle','','''biːt(ə)l','[n] 甲虫','He studied the Namib beetle, an ingenious species that lives in one of the driest places on earth.  他研究了纳米布甲虫，这是一种机灵的物种，生活在世界上最干燥的地方之一。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5937','glycoprotein','',',glaɪkə(ʊ)''prəʊtiːn','[n] [化]糖蛋白类, 醣蛋白','Straight edge: The miracle fruit (Synsepalum dulcificum), native to West Africa, contains a glycoprotein called miraculin that binds to taste receptors on the tongue and makes sour foods taste sweet.  神秘果：一种原产于西非的水果，内含一种叫神秘果蛋白的糖蛋白。 神秘果蛋白结合在味蕾上以后，吃酸的东西也感到是甜的。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5938','cardiac','''kɑrdɪæk','''kɑːdɪæk','[n] 强心剂; [adj] 心脏的, (胃的)贲门的','cardiac surgery  心脏手术'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5939','glial','''ɡlaɪə','''ɡlaɪəl','[adj] 神经胶质的','The glial tissue is where the largest percentage of brain tumors begin.  胶质组织是绝大多数脑部肿瘤的起源。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5940','autonomic',',ɔtə''nɑmɪk',',ɔːtə''nɒmɪk','[adj] 自治的, 自律的','Concepts such as autonomic computing will have a key role in cloud storage architectures in the future.  在未来，诸如自主计算这样的概念将在云存储架构中起到关键的作用。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5941','ending','''ɛndɪŋ','''endɪŋ','[n] 结尾, 结局','Verbal nouns have the ending -ing.  动名词以-ing结尾。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5942','preoccupation','prɪ,ɑkju''peʃən','prɪ,ɒkjʊ''peɪʃ(ə)n','[n] 全神贯注,当务之急','Karouzos''s poetry shows a profound preoccupation with the Orthodox Church.  卡鲁佐斯的诗歌表现出对东正教的深切关注。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5943','coyote','kaɪˈoti, ˈkaɪˌot','kaɪ''əʊtɪ','[n] 一种产于北美大草原的小狼, 山狗',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5944','endowment','ɪn''daʊmənt','ɪn''daʊm(ə)nt; en-','[n] 捐赠,天资,捐款','...the National Endowment for the Arts.  …美国艺术基金会。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5945','puddle','''pʌdl','''pʌd(ə)l','[n] 水坑, 泥潭; [v] 搅浊,搅泥泞','Children splashed through the puddles.  孩子们噼噼啪啪地踩过一个个小水坑。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5946','flare','flɛr','fleə','[n] 闪光, 闪耀; [v] 闪光,闪耀','The distress flares were spotted by another ship.  遇险信号被另外一艘船发现了。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5947','proboscis','pro''bɑsɪs','prə''bɒsɪs','[n] 鼻子,[昆] 喙','At least they didn''t give me a butterfly''s proboscis, or crab mandibles.  至少他们没有给我一只蝴蝶的鼻子，或者一只螃蟹的下颌。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5948','crimson','''krɪmzn','''krɪmz(ə)n','[adj] 深红色的; [v] 变深红色; [n] 深红色','The leaves turn crimson in autumn.  树叶在秋天变成了深红色。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5949','exhaustion','ɪg''zɔstʃən','ɪg''zɔːstʃ(ə)n; eg-','[n] 耗尽枯竭,疲惫,竭尽','Sheer exhaustion forced him to give up.  他疲惫不堪，只好放弃。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5950','winner','''wɪnɚ','''wɪnə','[n] 胜利者,优胜者','Five lucky winners will each receive a signed copy of the album.  五位幸运的获胜者每人将得到一张签名专辑。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5951','anthropological',',ænθrəpə''lɑdʒɪkl',',ænθrəpə''lɒdʒɪkəl','[adj] 人类学的,人类学上的','But now suppose we approach the question from a -I don''t say from an empirical point of view but from a speculative anthropological point of view.  现在假设我们从一个特定角度来看这个问题,我不会说从一个经验主义的角度,而是从一个推测的人类学的角度来看。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5952','sticky','''stɪki','''stɪkɪ','[adj] 粘的, 粘性的','There’s some sticky stuff in your hair.  你的头发上有什么黏糊糊的东西。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5953','structurally','','','[adv] 在结构上','In this case, the FBML may be structurally correct, but the data is wrong.  在这种情况下，FBML在结构上是正确的，但是数据是错误的。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5954','wholesome','''holsəm','''həʊls(ə)m','[adj] 有益的,健康的,健全的','good wholesome fun  健康有益的娱乐'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5955','polyphony','','pə''lɪf(ə)nɪ','[n] 复调音乐, 多音','Before Louis Armstrong, solos were brief or non-existent, and the urgent sound of an old New Orleans jazz band came from the polyphony of players winding their melodies around each other.  在路易斯阿姆斯特朗之前，独奏是一种可有可无或完全不存在的表演形式，旧式奥尔良乐团中，各路乐手用不同的旋律共同交织出复调音乐，通常急促而又紧凑。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5956','cornet','''kɔrnɪt','''kɔːnɪt','[n] 圆锥形纸袋, 短号',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5957','maize','mez','meɪz','[n] 玉米, 黄色; [adj] 玉米色的','We can grow sorghum or maize on this plot.  这块地可以种高粱或玉米。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5958','chivalry','''ʃɪvəlri','''ʃɪv(ə)lrɪ','[n] 骑士精神, 骑士制度','...the age of chivalry.  ...骑士制度的时代。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5959','unadorned','''ʌnə''dɔ:nd','ʌnə''dɔːnd','[adj] 朴素的,未装饰的','They liked their churches to be unadorned.  他们希望他们的教堂朴素无华。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5960','brave','brev','breɪv','[adj] 勇敢的','brave soldiers  勇敢的士兵'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5961','compatible','kəm''pætəbl','kəm''pætɪb(ə)l','[adj] 谐调的,兼容的','The new software is IBM compatible (= can be used with IBM computers ) .  这个新软件与IBM的计算机兼容。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5962','hotelkeeper','ho''tɛl,kipɚ','həʊ''tel,kiːpə','[n] 旅馆经营者',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5963','inn','ɪn','ɪn','[n] (尤指乡村或公路边的) 旅馆; [vi] 住旅馆','We’re staying at the Holiday Inn.  我们住在假日酒店。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5964','multitude','ˈmʌltɪˌtud, -ˌtjud','''mʌltɪtjuːd','[n] 多数, 群众','I had never seen such a multitude of stars before.  我以前从未见过这么多的星星。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5965','paraphrase','ˈpærəfreɪz','''pærəfreɪz','[v] 解释; [n] 释义','To paraphrase Finkelstein, mathematics is a language, like English.  芬克尔斯坦的意思是，数学是一门语言，就像英语一样。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5966','unselfish','ʌn''sɛlfɪʃ','ʌn''selfɪʃ','[adj] 无私的,慷慨的','She started to get a reputation as an unselfish girl with a heart of gold.  她开始得到有着金子般心灵的无私女孩的名声。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5967','disco','''dɪsko','''dɪskəʊ','[n] 迪斯科舞厅','the school disco  学校的迪斯科舞会'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5968','nonself','','','[n] (有机体的)异物',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5969','ragtime','''ræɡtaɪm','''rægtaɪm','[n] 拉格泰姆音乐; [adj] 使人发笑的','Joplin is considered the foremost composer of ragtime music.  吉普林被认为是拉格泰姆（Ragtime）音乐最重要的作曲家。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5970','unrestricted',',ʌnrɪ''strɪktɪd','ʌnrɪ''strɪktɪd','[adj] 自由的,无限制的','Freedom to pursue extracurricular activities is totally unrestricted.  参加课外活动的自由完全不受限制。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5971','quasar','''kwezɑr','''kweɪzɑː; -sɑː','[n] 恒星状球体, 类星体','This quasar was the only one without a known host galaxy.  这个类星体似乎无依无傍，不在任何一个星系当中。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5972','concertina',',kɑnsɚ''tinə',',kɒnsə''tiːnə','[n] 类似风琴的六角形的乐器',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5973','bedroom','''bɛdrum','''bedruːm; -rʊm','[n] 卧室','a hotel with 50 bedrooms  有50间客房的旅馆'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5974','quill','kwɪl','kwɪl','[n] 羽茎,大翎毛; [vt] 刺穿','She dipped a quill in ink, then began to write.  她把羽毛笔蘸进墨水中，然后开始写字。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5975','bolster','''bolstɚ','''bəʊlstə','[n] 垫子; [v] 支持','I''ll bolster you up.  我支持你。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5976','halt','hɔlt','hɔːlt','[n] 停止,暂停; [v] 停止,使立定','Heavy snowfalls brought traffic to a halt (= made it stop moving ).  大雪使得交通陷于停顿。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5977','exhale','ɛks''hel','ɪks''heɪl; eks-','[v] 呼气,发出','Take a deep breath, then exhale slowly.  深吸一口气，然后慢慢呼出。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5978','angstrom','''æŋstrəm','''æŋstrəm','[n] [物理]埃(长度单位)','I like the angstrom. It is 10 to the minus 10 meters.  我喜欢单位，埃，它等于10的负10次方米。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5979','microscopy','maɪ''krɑskəpi','maɪ''krɒskəpɪ','[n] 显微镜检查,显微镜使用','Not only might it have applications in fields such as microscopy, but it apparently also has the ability to optically store data forever.  它不仅可以在诸如显微镜之类的领域得到应用，显然它同时也具有实现永久性光存储的能力。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5980','narcotic','nɑr''kɑtɪk','nɑː''kɒtɪk','[n] 麻醉药,镇静剂; [adj] 麻醉的','The truth of Johnson’s comment was recently brought home to me by the serene calm of a resident who was treating a particularly complicated narcotic-dependent patient.  最近，一位住院医生对待一位异常复杂的麻醉药依赖病人的平静态度让我领会到了塞缪尔.约翰逊这句话的真谛。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5981','narcosis','','nɑː''kəʊsɪs','[n] 昏迷状态, 麻醉','Patient faint shows narcosis , high fever, convulsions, the skin cadaverous or the purple that show blueness.  病人昏倒呈昏迷状态，高烧，惊厥，皮肤苍白或呈青紫色。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5982','complication',',kɑmplɪ''keʃən','kɒmplɪ''keɪʃ(ə)n','[n] 复杂化, (使复杂的)因素','The fact that the plane was late added a further complication to our journey.  飞机误点给我们的旅行带来了更大的麻烦。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5983','embolism','''ɛmbə,lɪzəm','''embəlɪz(ə)m','[n] 加闰日, 栓塞',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5984','rupture','''rʌptʃɚ','''rʌptʃə','[v] 破裂,裂开; [n] 破裂, 决裂','The pipe will rupture at its weakest point.  管道最薄弱的地方会破裂的。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5985','abrasion','ə''breʒən','ə''breɪʒ(ə)n','[n] 磨损','extra protection against abrasion  防止磨损的额外保护'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5986','proportionally','prəu''pɔ:ʃənəli','prəu''pɔ:ʃənəli','[adv] 成比例地,相称地','However, because of on-chip space limitations, the TLB size can not be increased proportionally.  然而，由于芯片空间的限制，TLB 的大小不能成比例地增加。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5987','virgo','','','[n] 室女宫,室女(星)座',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5988','freighter','''fretɚ','''freɪtə','[n] 货船,承运人','The artificial reef, the Triangle, was put together from a freighter, a barge and -- this is the Palm Beach area, after all -- an old Rolls Royce.  人工鱼礁、百慕大三角通过货船和驳船装运相连在一起，中间的区域便是棕榈滩。 这卡片终究堪比“一辆古老的劳斯莱斯”。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5989','thinly','','','[adv] 稀疏地,瘦','Sow the radish seeds thinly.  把萝卜籽撒播得稀一些。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5990','morality','məˈræləti','məˈræləti','[n] 道德,品行','...standards of morality and justice in society.  …社会中道德和正义的标准。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5991','Andromeda','æn''drɑmədə','æn''drɒmɪdə','[n] 埃塞俄比亚的公主, 仙女座',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5992','yardstick','''jɑrd''stɪk','''jɑːdstɪk','[n] <美> 码尺, 准绳','The book gives a yardstick for measuring assets.  该书为评估资产提供了一种标准。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5993','exalt','ɪɡ''zɔlt','ɪg''zɔːlt; eg-','[v] 晋升','But it can also inspire and uplift and exalt, because power can be used to help people accomplish marvelous things.  但是，权力也可以激励人、振奋人和提升人，因为它可以帮助人们成就非同寻常的事业。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5994','monoxide','mɔ''nɔksaid, mə-','mə''nɒksaɪd','[n] 一氧化物','Then, if the mix of waste is correct, the carbon and oxygen atoms involved recombine to form carbon monoxide and the hydrogen atoms link up into diatomic hydrogen molecules.  接下去，如果废物的组合是合适的，碳原子和氧原子会重新组合形成一氧化碳，而氢原子则结合起来形成双原子的氢分子。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5995','comply','kəm''plaɪ','kəm''plaɪ','[v] 顺从,答应','The commander said that the army would comply with the ceasefire.  指挥官说过部队会遵从停火协议。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5996','owe','o','əʊ','[v] 欠(债等),感激','How much do I owe you (= often used to show that you want to pay for something )?  我该付你多少钱？'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5997','ingot','''ɪŋgət','''ɪŋgət','[n] [冶]锭铁, 工业纯铁','...gold ingots.  ...金锭。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5998','premature',',primə''tʃʊr','''premətjʊə','[adj] 未成熟的,早熟的','his premature death due to cancer  他因癌症而早逝'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_5999','grievance','''grivəns','''griːv(ə)ns','[n] 委屈, 冤情, 不平','anyone who has a legitimate grievance against the company  凡是有正当理由对公司感到不满的人'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6000','conjectural','kən''dʒɛktʃərəl','kən''dʒektʃ(ə)r(ə)l','[adj] 推测的,好推测的','There is something undeniably conjectural about such claims.  此类声明中绝对有推测的成分。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6001','knot','nɑt','nɒt','[n] (绳等的)结; [v] 打结','One lace had broken and been tied in a knot.  一根带子已经断了，被打成一个结。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6002','notch','nɑtʃ','nɒtʃ','[n] 槽口,刻痕; [v] 刻凹痕','Cut a notch near one end of the stick.  在手杖的一端刻一个V形记号。'),
