('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6007','attire','ə''taiə','ə''taɪə','[n] 服装; [v] 打扮','business attire  商务着装，正装'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6008','corrosion','kə''roʒən','kə''rəʊʒ(ə)n','[n] 侵蚀,腐蚀状态','They are sprayed with oil to prevent corrosion.  它们被喷了油以防腐蚀。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6009','upright','''ʌpraɪt','''ʌpraɪt','[adj] 正直的; [n] 垂直, 竖立','Katie was still awake, sitting bolt upright(= sitting with her back very straight ) staring at the television.  凯蒂还醒着，坐得笔直，眼睛盯着电视。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6010','unravel','ʌn''rævl',',ʌn''rævəl','[v] 拆开,拆开','He could unravel a knot that others wouldn''t even attempt.  他能解开其他人甚至不敢尝试的绳结。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6011','glassmaking','','','[n] 玻璃(或玻璃器皿等)制造(术)','In 1868, when the industry was still struggling to re-establish other forms of glassmaking, 3,662 tons of beads were exported.  到了1868年，即便岛上的工匠们在埋头对玻璃吹制技术重新探索时，玻璃珠的出口量也达到了3,662吨。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6012','Katherine','','''kæθərin','[n] 凯瑟琳（女子名）','She chummed around with Katherine.  她与凯瑟琳结为密友。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6013','malleability','','','[n] 有延展性, 柔韧性',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6014','deft','deft','deft','[adj] 敏捷熟练的, 灵巧的','He sketched her with quick, deft strokes.  他给她画素描，下笔又快又熟练。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6015','robust','ro''bʌst','rə(ʊ)''bʌst','[adj] 精力充沛的','The Secretary of State has made a robust defence of the agreement.  国务卿对这项协议进行了强有力的辩护。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6016','baedeker','','','[n] 旅行指南, 入门手册',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6017','sword','sɔːrd','sɔːd','[n] 剑','The treaty hung like a sword of Damocles over French politics.  这个条约好像一把达摩克利斯之剑悬在法国政坛之上。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6018','microfossil','','','[n] 微体化石,微化石','This achievement provides the microfossil materials for the study of the lower ordovician in Northern Guizhou.  这一成果对于贵州北部下奥陶统的研究，提供了微体化石资料。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6019','entomb','ɪn''tum','ɪn''tuːm; en-','[v] 埋葬, 成为的坟墓','The city was entombed in volcanic lava.  那个城市被火山熔岩掩埋了。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6020','burgher','''bɝɡɚ','''bɜːgə','[n] 公民, 市民','Even take the word burgher or bourgeois.  比如说"市民"或称之为"布尔乔亚"'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6021','puffin','''pʌfɪn','''pʌfɪn','[n] [鸟]角嘴海雀','Despite 2010 starting and ending with much of the country swathed in snow, threatened species such as the puffin and the rare heath fritillary butterfly enjoyed successful breeding seasons.  尽管2010年开始和结束时，英国的大部分地区都被大雪覆盖，对人们来说不算是好天气。 但英国的国民托管组织声称：在这一年里，英国的很多濒危物种，比如埃克斯莫尔的珍稀希斯豹纹蝶、坎布里亚郡的网纹毛毡衣蝶还有法内尔岛上的海雀，都很享受这适合繁殖的一年，数量大大增加。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6022','insoluble','ɪn''sɑljəbl','ɪn''sɒljʊb(ə)l','[adj] 不能溶解的, 不能解决的','insoluble conflicts within the department  部门内难以调和的冲突'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6023','reliability','rɪ,laɪə''bɪləti','rɪ,laɪə''bɪlətɪ','[n] 可靠性','I can assure you of the reliability of the information.  我可以向你保证这消息是可靠的。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6024','unemployed',',ʌnɪm''plɔɪd','ʌnɪm''plɒɪd; -em-','[adj] 失业的, 未被利用的','an unemployed actor  没戏演的演员'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6025','immobility','','','[n] 牢固,不动','This is due to a stagnation of blood in the veins caused by prolonged immobility, which can promote blood clot formation in veins.  其原因是由于长时间不动，造成静脉血液停滞，促使静脉中血凝块形成。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6026','preside','prɪ''zaɪd','prɪ''zaɪd','[v] 主持,管理','I shall be pleased to preside at your meetings.  我很高兴主持你们的会议。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6027','spacious','''speʃəs','''speɪʃəs','[adj] 广大的,大规模的','a spacious living area  宽敞的居住空间'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6028','hydrographic','','','[adj] 水道测量数的,水道学的',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6029','portraiture','''pɔrtrətʃɚ','''pɔːtrɪtʃə','[n] 肖像画法','The dispute illuminates the primitive nature of our attitude to portraiture.  这一争论阐释了我们对肖像画的态度的本性。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6030','talented','''tæləntɪd','''tæləntɪd','[adj] 有才能的','a talented actor  一名很有天赋的演员'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6031','homework','''hom''wɝk','''həʊmwɜːk','[n] 家庭作业, 副业','For homework, finish the exercise on page 14.  家庭作业是完成第14页的练习。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6032','filmmaker','','''fɪlm,meɪkə','[n] 电影摄制者',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6033','understate','''ʌndɚ''stet','ʌndə''steɪt','[v] 打着折扣说,有意轻描淡写','The press have tended to understate the extent of the problem.  媒体想淡化问题的严重程度。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6034','narrate','næret','nə''reɪt','[v] 叙述,作解说','a wildlife film narrated by David Attenborough  一部由大卫•艾登堡解说的野生动物影片'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6035','lean','lin','liːn','[n] 倾斜,倚靠; [v] 依靠,倾斜; [adj] 贫乏的','trees leaning in the wind  在风中东倒西歪的树木'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6036','consort','''kɑn,sɔrt','''kɒnsɔːt','[v] 结交,符合; [n] 配偶','The public has accepted Camilla, Prince Charles’s former mistress, as his consort.  公众接受了作为前任情妇的卡米拉成为查尔斯王子的新配偶。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6037','gannet','''ɡænɪt','''gænɪt','[n] 塘鹅','Rescue workers carefully clean an oil-soaked northern gannet bird at a facility in Fort Jackson, Louisiana.  救援人员在路易斯安娜州杰克逊堡（ Fort Jackson）的一处救援场所仔细地清理一只浸透了油污的北塘鹅。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6038','underwing','''ʌndəwiŋ','''ʌndəwɪŋ','[n] 后翅, 后翅色彩瑰丽的蛾',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6039','exorbitant','ɪɡ''zɔrbɪtənt','ɪg''zɔːbɪt(ə)nt','[adj] （要价等）过高的,（性格等）过分的','Exorbitant housing prices have created an acute shortage of affordable housing for the poor.  过高的房价使穷人负担得起的房源严重短缺。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6040','gondwanaland','ɡɔnd''wɑ:nəlænd','ɡɔnd''wɑ:nəlænd','[n] [地]冈瓦纳大陆',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6041','gunpowder','''ɡʌnpaʊdɚ','''gʌnpaʊdə','[n] 黑色火药, 有烟火药',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6042','herring','''hɛrɪŋ','''herɪŋ','[n] 青鱼, 鲱','...a can of herring.  …鲱鱼罐头。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6043','earner','''ɝnɚ','''ɜːnə','[n] 赚钱的人','the country’s biggest export earner  该国利润最高的出口商品'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6044','angular','''æŋɡjəlɚ','''æŋgjʊlə','[adj] [生物] 有角的,生硬的,笨拙的','a cubist painting with angular shapes  一幅有棱角图案的立体派绘画'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6045','wren','rɛn','ren','[n] [动] 鹪鹩','And the lion keeps something for you, and the mangrove swamp and the coral and the spider and the wren.  狮子，红树林沼泽、珊瑚，还有蜘蛛和鹪鹩也为你保存了某些东西。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6046','weary','''wɪri','''wɪərɪ','[adj] 疲倦的,厌倦的; [v] 疲倦,厌倦','She found Rachel in the kitchen, looking old and weary.  她发现雷切尔在厨房里，看上去苍老而疲惫。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6047','kinglet','''kɪŋlɪt','''kɪŋlɪt','[n] <贬>懦弱的国王,小国君主',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6048','uniformity',',jʊnə''fɔrməti','juːnɪ''fɔːmɪtɪ','[n] 一致,均匀','There seems to be no uniformity among the various systems.  各系统之间似乎没有统一性。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6049','screw','skru','skruː','[n] 螺丝钉,螺旋; [v] 调节,旋','Fix the frame in position and tighten the screws .  把框子固定在正确位置上，拧紧螺丝。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6050','priestess','''pri:stis','''priːstɪs','[n] 女祭司, (基督教会以外的)神职人员','...the priestess of the temple.  …该寺院里的女祭司。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6051','neoclassical',',nio''klæsɪkl','niːəʊ''klæsɪk(ə)l','[adj] 新古典主义的','a palace built in a neoclassical style  新古典主义风格的宫殿'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6052','thousandfold','''θaʊznd''fold','''θaʊzəndfəʊld','[adv] 千倍地; [adj] 千倍的','He suffers a thousandfold more from his so-called freedom than from his imprisonment in natural existence.  比之人所谓的天赋存在的自由，他遭受千倍的是天赋存在的枷锁。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6053','enjoyment','ɪn''dʒɔɪmənt','ɪn''dʒɒɪmənt','[n] 享乐, 快乐','Acting has brought me enormous enjoyment.  演戏给我带来莫大的快乐。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6054','forester','''fɔrɪstɚ','''fɒrɪstə','[n] 林务官, 森林人',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6055','spoilage','''spɔɪlɪdʒ','''spɒɪlɪdʒ','[n] 损坏','Nutrition education can help with some problems and may prevent improper storage or spoilage.  营养教育可以解决一些问题，并能防止不当的贮存或腐坏发生。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6056','nonthreatening','','','[adj] 非胁迫的','Even when issues have come up in the course of implementation, DeSutter said, the ensuing dialogues always have been carried out in a professional, serious and nonthreatening manner.  德萨特说，即使在执行过程中出现问题，随后开展的对话总是以专业化、严肃和非威胁的方式进行。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6057','solder','''sɑdɚ','''səʊldə; ''sɒldə','[n] 焊料; [v] 焊接','Each sculptural planter is made-to-order with handmade glass and lead-free solder and comes with everything you need but the plants.  每个艺术花盆都是定制的。 它们由手工制作的玻璃和无铅焊料接合而成，交付使用时，万事俱备，只欠花卉。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6058','tumble','''tʌmbl','''tʌmb(ə)l','[n] 跌倒,翻斤斗; [v] 翻倒, 摔倒','It’s possible that stocks could take a tumble next year.  明年股票有可能会大跌。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6059','harshness','','','[n] 粗糙的事物, 严肃, 刺耳',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6060','collagen','''kɑlədʒən','''kɒlədʒ(ə)n','[n] 胶原质','Lemons, oranges and any other citrus fruit form collagen resulting to holding the skin cells together. It is necessary to drink fruit juices and eat fruit every day.  柠檬，橘子和任何其他柑橘类水果形成胶原蛋白，从而新生皮肤细胞组织，所以每天要多喝果汁多吃水果。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6061','surgeon','''sɝdʒən','''sɜːdʒ(ə)n','[n] 外科医生','...a heart surgeon.  …一位心脏外科医生。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6062','idle','''aɪdl','''aɪd(ə)l','[adj] 空闲的,懒惰的; [v] 虚度, 闲散','I cannot afford to leave the land lying idle.  我不能让土地闲置。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6063','sumptuous','''sʌmptʃuəs','''sʌm(p)tjʊəs','[adj] 奢侈的,华丽的','a sumptuous feast  盛宴'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6064','synchrotron','''siŋkrəutrɔn, ''sin-','''sɪŋkrə(ʊ)trɒn','[n] 同步加速器','The synchrotron accelerator was built at Fermilab and the first patients were treated in 1990.  该同步加速器在费米实验室建造，首例病人于1990年接受治疗。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6065','landlord','''lændlɔrd','''læn(d)lɔːd','[n] 房东,地主','His landlord doubled the rent.  他的房东把房租提高了一倍。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6066','familiarity','fə,mɪlɪ''ærəti','fəmɪlɪ''ærɪtɪ','[n] 熟悉,通晓,精通','I miss the familiarity of home.  我怀念家的那种亲切感。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6067','stringent','''strɪndʒənt','''strɪn(d)ʒ(ə)nt','[adj] 严厉的,迫切的','stringent anti-noise regulations  严格的防噪音条例'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6068','signature','''sɪgnətʃɚ','''sɪgnətʃə','[n] 签名,信号','Her signature is totally illegible (= cannot be read ) .  她的签字完全无法辨认。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6069','cabinetmaker','''kæbɪnətmekɚ','''kæbɪnɪt,meɪkə','[n] 家具师,细工木匠',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6070','chord','kɔrd','kɔːd','[n] 弦,和音','I could play a few chords on the guitar and sing a song.  我能弹一些击他和弦唱一首歌。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6071','supervisory','''sju:pə,vaizəri','''sjuːpə,vaɪzərɪ','[adj] 监督的','Most supervisory boards meet only twice a year.  大多数监理会一年只开两次会。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6072','resentment','rɪ''zɛntmənt','rɪ''zentm(ə)nt','[n] 怨恨,愤恨','She expressed resentment at being interviewed by a social worker.  她对于被一个社会工作者面试表示了怨恨。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6073','purposely','''pɝpəsli','''pɜːpəslɪ','[adv] 故意地,蓄意地','A clause in the contract had been left purposely vague.  合同中有一个条款被故意定得模棱两可。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6074','irresponsibly','','','[adv] 不负责任地,不可靠地','If a pastor doesn''t bring up the cohabitation issue, they''re acting irresponsibly.  如果牧师不提出同居问题，那么他们的行为可能会很不负责任。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6075','quench','kwɛntʃ','kwen(t)ʃ','[v] 结束,熄灭','Then the men of David sware unto him, saying, Thou shalt go no more out with us to battle, that thou quench not the light of Israel.  当日，跟随大卫的人向大卫起誓说，以后你不可再与我们一同出战，恐怕熄灭以色列的灯。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6076','grapple','''græpl','''græp(ə)l','[v] 格斗,抓住; [n] 格斗','The police warned the public that it would be dangerous to grapple with the wanted man, as he was armed.  警察当局警告公众，与那个通缉犯格斗是危险的，因为他携带武器。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6077','haunt','hɔnt','hɔːnt','[v] 出没于','The pub is said to be haunted by the ghost of a former landlord.  据说这个酒吧里经常有一位前任房主的鬼魂出没。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6078','revealingly','','','[adv] 启发人地,袒胸露肩地',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6079','obedience','ə''bidjəns','ə''biːdɪəns','[n] 服众, 顺从','obedience classes for dogs and their owners  为狗和主人安排的服从训练课'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6080','rearrange',',riə''rendʒ','riːə''reɪn(d)ʒ','[v] 再排列,重新整理','She set about rearranging the furniture in the living room.  她开始重新摆放起居室的家具。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6081','roar','rɔr','rɔː','[n] 吼叫, 怒号; [v] 滚动,咆哮','the roar of the crowd  人群的喊叫声'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6082','armory','''ɑrməri','''ɑ:məri','[n] 兵工厂,军械库','One photo shows cadets playfully pointing revolvers at colleagues in a room that appears to be an armory.  一张照片显示了学员们在军械库里拿左轮手枪开玩笑似的指着同事。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6083','tuck','tʌk','tʌk','[n] 缝摺, 活力; [v] 卷起,大口的吃','You tuck your secret away in an unexpected place, like an MP3 or a photo file, to conceal the fact you even shared any information at all.  你将你的秘密“卷起来”，放在一个意想不到的地方，比如MP3或照片文件，这样就掩盖了你曾经分享信息的事实。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6084','slippery','''slɪpəri','''slɪp(ə)rɪ','[adj] 滑的,光滑的','In places, the path can be wet and slippery.  路上有些地方可能又湿又滑。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6085','courtship','''kɔ:tʃip','''kɔːtʃɪp','[n] 求爱, 求爱时期','courtship rituals  求偶仪式'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6086','sleek','slik','sliːk','[adj] 圆滑的,使…光滑','...sleek black hair.  …乌黑光滑的头发。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6087','corselet','''kɔrslɪt','''kɔːs(ə)lɪt','[n] 盔甲,胸衣','Cutlass and corselet of steel, and his trusty sword of Damascus.  钢刀，盔甲，和他素来倚重的大马士革利剑。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6088','keel','kil','kiːl','[n] 龙骨(船的脊骨),平底船; [v] 装以龙骨,倾覆','The keel hit the rock first.  船龙骨先撞到岩石。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6089','needle','''nidl','''niːd(ə)l','[n] 针; [v] 缝纫,刺激','She carried hypodermic needles and syringes in her bag.  她包里带着皮下注射针和针筒。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6090','secrecy','''sikrəsi','''siːkrɪsɪ','[n] 秘密,保密','I must stress the need for absolute secrecy about the project.  我必须强调这项计划一定要绝对保密。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6091','lira','''lɪrə','''lɪərə','[n] 里拉（意大利货币单位）','Coin-operated telephones took 100, 200 and 500 lire coins.  投币电话接受100，200和500里拉的硬币。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6092','livelihood','''laɪvlɪhʊd','''laɪvlɪhʊd','[n] 生计,谋生','It’s difficult to earn a livelihood as an artist.  搞艺术很难谋生。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6093','impediment','ɪm''pɛdɪmənt','ɪm''pedɪm(ə)nt','[n] 妨碍,口吃, 障碍物','a speech impediment  言语障碍'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6094','bow','baʊ','baʊ','[n] 弓,弓形; [v] 鞠躬,弯腰','a bow and arrow  弓箭'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6095','nurture','''nɝtʃɚ','''nɜːtʃə','[n] 养育,教育; [v] 养育,给与营养物','The human organism learns partly by nature, partly by nurture.  人的学习能力部分是先天的，部分是后天培育的。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6096','silhouette',',sɪlu''ɛt',',sɪlʊ''et','[n] 侧面影象,轮廓; [v] 使…照出影子来','silhouette pictures of snowmen and reindeer  雪人和驯鹿的剪影画'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6097','inward','''ɪnwɚd','''ɪnwəd','[adv] 向内,在内; [adj] 向内的,内在的','He pushed open the front door, which swung inward with a groan.  他推开前门，门呀的一声向里开了。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6098','misinterpret','''mɪsɪn''tɝprɪt','mɪsɪn''tɜːprɪt','[v] 曲解','Some parts of the report could be misinterpreted.  报告的某些部分可能会被误解。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6099','marketable','''mɑrkɪtəbl','''mɑːkɪtəb(ə)l','[adj] 市场的,可销售的','The program is designed to provide students with real, marketable skills.  本计划旨在让学生掌握符合市场需求的真正技能。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6100','mudstone','''mʌd,ston','''mʌdstəʊn','[n] [地]泥岩','Rocks sculptured by erosion, richly tinted mudstone hills and canyons, luminous sand dunes, and lush oases populate Death Valley National Park.  在死亡谷国家公园里，有着腐蚀而成的岩石雕刻、富有着色泥岩的山丘和峡谷、发光的沙丘和郁郁葱葱的绿洲。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6101','carcass','''kɑrkəs','''kɑ:kəs','[n] (屠宰后)畜体','A cluster of vultures crouched on the carcass of a dead buffalo.  一群秃鹫伏在一头水牛的尸体上啄食。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6102','subdivide','''sʌbdɪvaɪd','sʌbdɪ''vaɪd','[v] 再分, 细分','Over time, developers subdivided the land.  开发商们渐渐地把这块土地进行了再分割。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6103','meteoritic','','','[adj] 陨星的,陨石的','Were they meteoritic matter from space, reflected light from polar icebergs or a high-altitude version of lightning?  它们是太空里的彗星物质、极地冰山反射的光，还是高空的闪电？'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6104','offshoot','''ɔfʃut','''ɒfʃuːt','[n] 分支, 支流','the Mafia and its offshoots  黑手党组织及其分支'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6105','inborn',',ɪn''bɔrn','''ɪnbɔːn; ɪn''bɔːn','[adj] 天生的,生来的','Mammals have an inborn fear of snakes.  哺乳动物天生害怕蛇。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6106','stereotypical',',steriə''tipikl',',steriə''tipikl','[adj] 老一套的,陈规的','These are men whose masculinity does not conform to stereotypical images of the unfeeling male.  这些阳刚的男人不符合那种冷血男人的成见形象。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6107','manipulation','mə,nɪpjʊ''leʃən','mə,nɪpjʊ''leɪʃ(ə)n','[n] 处理,操纵','They make a lot of money by clever manipulation of the Stock Market.  他们巧妙地操纵股票市场而大赚其钱。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6108','lifelike','''laɪf''laɪk','''laɪflaɪk','[adj] 栩栩如生的,逼真的','a very lifelike statue  一尊栩栩如生的塑像'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6109','bipedal','baɪ''pɛdəl','baɪ''piːd(ə)l','[adj] 两足动物的,两足的','One of these gene machines, a social and bipedal ape, began to imitate.  这些“基因机器”其中的一个，一个群居的两足人猿开始了模仿。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6110','antiquate','''æntə,kwet','''æntɪkweɪt','[adj] 旧式的,过时的',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6111','chondritic','','','[adj] 球粒状陨石的','The main features of a rare meteorite is rare: 1, non-chondritic meteorites were structure;  罕见珍稀陨石的主要特征是：1、陨石呈无球粒结构；'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6112','replicate','''rɛplɪket','''replɪkeɪt','[v] 复制; [adj] 复制的','There is a need for further research to replicate these findings.  需要进一步的研究来验证这些结果。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6113','painful','''penfl','''peɪnfʊl; -f(ə)l','[adj] 疼痛的,使痛苦的','stiff painful joints  僵硬疼痛的关节'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6114','weldon','','','[n] 韦尔登（男子名）',''),
