('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6136','duchenne','','','[n] 杜氏营养不良症',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6137','reopen',',ri''opən','riː''əʊp(ə)n','[v] 重开,再开始','The swimming pool will reopen in May.  游泳池将于5月份重新开放。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6138','immutable','ɪ''mjutəbl','ɪ''mjuːtəb(ə)l','[adj] 不变的,不可变的','This decision should not be seen as immutable.  不该把这个决定看成是不可改变的。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6139','pave','pev','peɪv','[v] 铺,安排','a paved courtyard  地面铺砌过的院子'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6140','permeability',',pɝmɪə''bɪləti','pɜːmɪə''bɪlɪtɪ','[n] 渗透性','The most interesting dimension of this is what Google Search Appliance says about the increasing permeability of a company and the outside world.  其中，最有趣的一点是谷歌搜索设备所反映的“公司和外部世界日益增加的渗透性”。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6141','afterwards','''æftɚwɚdz','''ɑːftəwədz','[adv] 然后, 后来地','Charles arrived shortly afterwards .  过了不多久，查尔斯来了。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6142','consolidation','kən,sɑlə''deʃən','kən,sɒlɪ''deɪʃən','[n] 巩固, 合并','Enable users to submit consolidation nodes, even if not all leaf nodes have been opened.  允许用户提交合并结点，即使并非所有的叶子节点都已打开。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6143','waterfowl','''wɔtɚfaʊl','''wɔːtəfaʊl','[n] 水鸟, 水禽','the varied waterfowl of North America  北美洲种类繁多的水鸟'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6144','efficacious',',efi''keiʃəs',',efɪ''keɪʃəs','[adj] 有效的,灵验的','an equally efficacious method of treatment  同样有效的治疗方法'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6145','permeable','''pɝmɪəbl','''pɜːmɪəb(ə)l','[adj] 有浸透性的, 能透过的','the permeable cell membrane  渗透性的细胞膜'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6146','fanwise','''fænwaiz','''fænwaɪz','ad&; [adj] 呈扇形展开的',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6147','riverbed','''rɪvɚ,bɛd','''rɪvəbed','[n] 河床','Samburu man leads his cattle out of the village and across a swath of arid land toward a water well dug into a desiccated Kenyan riverbed.  一位桑布鲁男子赶着牛群走出村落，穿过一片干燥的土地，朝着在干燥河床上挖掘的一口水井进发。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6148','destine','''dɛstɪn','''destɪn','[v] 注定, 预定','Over these three years, miss her, read her person, what is he an eldest brother?But his love, destine and leave sorry!  这三年以来，想她，念她的人，何止他大哥一个？可是他的爱，注定是要留下遗憾的！'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6149','expertly','''ɛkspɚtli','','[adv] 熟练地','The nurse dressed the wound expertly.  护士熟练地敷药包扎了伤口。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6150','stipulate','''stɪpjulet','''stɪpjʊleɪt','[v] 规定, 保证','Laws stipulate the maximum interest rate that banks can charge.  法律对银行可以收取的最高利率作了规定。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6151','sandbar','''sændbɑr','','[n] 沙洲','The ship was hung up on a sandbar.  那艘船在沙洲搁浅了。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6152','contingent','kən''tɪndʒənt','kən''tɪndʒ(ə)nt','[adj] 可能发生的, 附随的; [n] 偶然的事情','The enthymeme and the example must, then, deal with what is in the main contingent, the example being an induction, and the enthymeme a syllogism, about such matters.  推理论证和例证法因而必须处理主要的偶然事件，例证法是对此类事项的归纳推理，推理论证则是对其的三段论。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6153','congenial','kən''dʒinɪəl','kən''dʒiːnɪəl','[adj] 意气相投的,性格相似的','Frank was a very congenial colleague.  弗兰克是一位很好相处的同事。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6154','faucet','''fɔsɪt','''fɔːsɪt','[n] 龙头, (连接管子的)插口','If God turns off one faucet, he can turn on another.  如果上帝关住一个你的水龙头，他能开启另一个”。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6155','alienate','''eiljəneit','''eɪlɪəneɪt','[v] 疏远','The latest tax proposals will alienate many voters.  最新的纳税提案将失去远许多选民的支持。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6156','implicit','ɪm''plɪsɪt','ɪm''plɪsɪt','[adj] 暗示的,盲从的',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6157','preponderance','prɪ''pɑndərəns','prɪ''pɒnd(ə)r(ə)ns','[n] 优势,占优势','There is a preponderance of female students in the music department.  在音乐系里女学生占大多数。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6158','imperfect','ɪm''pɝfɪkt','ɪm''pɜːfɪkt','[adj] 有缺点的,未完成的; [n] 未完成体','the imperfect world we live in  我们生活于其中的不完美的世界'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6159','homeotherm','','','[n] <主美>恒温动物','An organism that generates heat to maintain its body temperature, typically above the temperature of its surroundings; a homeotherm.  恒温动物能产生热量维持体温的生物体，其体温典型高于其周围环境的温度；温血动物。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6160','envy','''ɛnvi','''envɪ','[n] 羡慕,嫉妒; [v] 羡慕,嫉妒','She could see that all the other girls were green with envy(= feeling a lot of envy ).  她看得出其他女孩都很眼红。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6161','drape','drep','dreɪp','[n] 窗帘; [v] 使褶皱','He pulled the drapes shut, locked the door behind him.  他拉上长帘,锁上了身后的门。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6162','drip','drɪp','drɪp','[n] 水滴; [v] (使)滴下','I put some plastic buckets on the floor to catch the drips.  我把几个塑料桶放在地板上接滴下来的水。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6163','jewel','''dʒuəl','''dʒuːəl','[n] 宝石','She loved dressing up and wearing priceless jewels.  她喜欢穿上盛装，戴上极为昂贵的珠宝首饰。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6164','practicality','''præktɪ''kæləti',',præktɪ''kælɪtɪ','[n] 实用性,实际','doubts about the practicality of your suggestion  对于你所提建议的可行性的怀疑'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6165','pictorial','pɪk''tɔrɪəl','pɪk''tɔːrɪəl','[adj] 图示的; [n] 画报','a pictorial record of their journey  他们旅程的照片记录'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6166','bland','blænd','blænd','[adj] 温和的,乏味的; [v] 变得乏味','a few bland comments  不痛不痒的几句评语'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6167','mortal','''mɔrtl','''mɔːt(ə)l','[n] 凡人,人类; [adj] 必死的,致命的','Her father’s death reminded her that she was mortal.  父亲的去世让她认识到终有一天她也会死去。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6168','unschooled',',ʌn''sku:ld','ʌn''skuːld','[adj] 天生的,未受学校教育的','...unskilled work done by unschooled people.  ...未受过正式教育的人做出的不精巧的活计。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6169','harmless','''hɑrmləs','''hɑ:mləs','[adj] 无害的','Her brother’s a bit simple, but he’s quite harmless.  她的弟弟有点愚钝，不过他决不会伤害别人。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6170','burgeon','''bɝdʒən','''bɜːdʒ(ə)n','[n] 嫩芽; [v] 萌芽','When spring is coming all trees begin to burgeon .  当春天到来的时候，所有树开始发芽。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6171','ashcan','''æʃkæn','''æʃkæn','[n] 垃圾桶, 深水炸弹',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6172','literalness','','','[n] 文字的,表面意义上的','Although the doesn''t up help what, can do a good listen to, we each other of the trust have the basal, that foundation be the guest the top literalness exchanges.  翡瑟虽然帮不上什么，但是可以做一个很好的倾听者，我们彼此的信任是有基础的，那个基础就是博客上文字的交流。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6173','flyspeck','''flaɪ,spɛk','''flaɪspek','[n] 污点,小斑; [v] 弄脏','Or is it a flyspeck looking like a bird?  或只是苍蝇留下的看起来像鸟的斑点？'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6174','rennin','','''renɪn','[n] 高血压蛋白原酶',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6175','hormonal','hɔr''monl','hɔː''məʊn(ə)l','[adj] 荷尔蒙的,激素的','...our individual hormonal balance.  …我们个体的荷尔蒙平衡。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6176','angiotensin',',ændʒɪo''tɛnsən',',ændʒɪə(ʊ)''tensɪn','[n] [医]血管紧缩素','The drugs lower blood pressure by stopping the hormone angiotensin narrowing the body''s blood vessels.  这种药物通过阻止激素血管紧缩素缩小身体内的血管，从而降低血压。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6177','deprivation',',dɛprɪ''veʃən','deprɪ''veɪʃ(ə)n','[n] 剥夺','Millions more suffer from serious sleep deprivation caused by long work hours.  还有数百万人由于工作时数长导致他们严重睡眠不足。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6178','aldosterone','æl''dɑstə,ron','æl''dɒstərəʊn','[n] [生化]醛甾酮,醛固酮','As well as binding cortisol, it could respond to other hormones such as aldosterone and deoxycorticosterone.  在结合应激激素的同时，它还能够对其他激素产生响应，例如醛固酮和去氧皮质酮。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6179','mandate','''mændet','''mændeɪt','[n] (书面)命令,训令; [v] 委任统治','Matters debated in meetings do not become a mandate automatically.  会议上讨论的事宜并不能自动成为一项指令。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6180','henceforth',',hɛns''fɔrθ','hens''fɔːθ; ''hensfɔːθ','[adv] 今后,自此以后','multiple sclerosis (henceforth referred to as MS)  多发性硬化（以下称为MS）'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6181','mammalian','mæˈmeɪlɪən','mæ''meɪlɪən','[n] 哺乳动物; [adj] 哺乳动物的','But is it more than just the infusion of the catecholamine neurotransmitter, dopamine, or the mammalian hormone oxytocin?  而它也许不止是儿茶酚胺类神经递质注入剂、多巴胺、或哺乳类动物的荷尔蒙催产素？'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6182','unfairly','ʌn''fɛəli','','[adv] 不公平地,不正当地','And that''s going to require some very hard choices. And we''re going to have to do that in a way that does not add unfairly to the burdens that the average American already faces.  他还称,"这就需要作出一些十分困难的选择.我们达到此目的所采取的方式,将不会向普通美国人已面临的负担中,增加不公平的累赘."'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6183','irrelevant','ɪ''rɛləvənt','ɪ''relɪv(ə)nt','[adj] 不相干的,不切题的','We’re focussing too much on irrelevant details.  我们过于关注不相干的细节。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6184','jury','''dʒʊri','''dʒʊərɪ','[n] [律] 陪审团; [adj] [海]临时应急的','the members of the jury  陪审团成员'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6185','burdensome','''bɝdnsəm','''bɜːdns(ə)m','[adj] 繁重的,难以承担的','...a burdensome debt.  …一笔沉重的债务。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6186','confederate','kən''fɛdəret','kən''fed(ə)rət','[n] 同盟者,同盟国; [adj] 同盟的; [v] (使)联盟, 联合','The young woman was his confederate, of course.  这个年轻女子当然是他的同谋。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6187','pardon','''pɑrdn','ˈpɑːdn','[v] 原谅,宽恕; [n] 原谅','He craved the teacher''s pardon.  他恳求老师原谅他。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6188','convict','kən''vɪkt','kən''vɪkt','[v] 证明有罪; [n] 罪犯','a convicted murderer  已定罪的谋杀犯'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6189','authorization',',ɔθərɪ''zeʃən','ɔːθəraɪ''zeɪʃ(ə)n','[n] 授权,认可','You need special authorization to park here.  在此停车要有特别的许可。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6190','gymnastic','dʒɪm''næstɪks','dʒɪm''næstɪk','[adj] 体操的,体育的; [n] 训练课程','On our return from school our drawing and gymnastic masters would be ready for us.  放学回来，我们的图画和体操老师已在家里恭候多时了。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6191','stagger','''stægɚ','''stægə','[v] 蹒跚,交错; [adj] 交错的','He managed to stagger home.  他好不容易才蹒跚着走回家。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6192','peacetime','''pis''taɪm','''piːstaɪm','[n] 和平时期; [adj] 和平时期的','We could afford to reduce defence spending in peacetime without excessive risk.  在和平时期我们可以减少国防开支而并不引起风险增加。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6193','readjust',',riə''dʒʌst','riːə''dʒʌst','[v] 重新调整,再调整','It takes time to readjust after a divorce.  离婚后需要时间重新适应。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6194','rivalry','''raɪvlri','''raɪv(ə)lrɪ','[n] 竞争,竞赛,敌对','The two players have developed a friendly rivalry .  这两名选手之间已形成一种友好的竞争关系。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6195','nobility','no''bɪləti','nə(ʊ)''bɪlɪtɪ','[n] 高贵,贵族','the nobility of his intentions  他崇高的志向'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6196','revive','rɪ''vaɪv','rɪ''vaɪv','[v] 苏醒, (使)复兴','Local people have decided to revive this centuries-old tradition.  当地人决定复兴这一延续了数个世纪的传统。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6197','ponderous','''pɑndərəs','''pɒnd(ə)rəs','[adj] 笨重的,沉闷的','an elephant’s ponderous walk  大象笨拙的步态'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6198','thresher','''θrɛʃɚ','''θreʃə','[n] 打谷者, 打谷机, [鱼]长尾鲨',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6199','utensil','jʊ''tɛnsl','juː''tens(ə)l','[n] 器具','kitchen utensils  厨房用具'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6200','knight','naɪt','naɪt','[n] (欧洲中世纪的)骑士; [v] 授以爵位','knights in armour  身披盔甲的骑士'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6201','intentional','ɪn''tɛnʃənl','ɪn''tenʃ(ə)n(ə)l','[adj] 故意的,策划的','I did trip him, but it wasn’t intentional.  我的确把他绊倒了，但不是故意的。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6202','thrifty','''θrɪfti','''θrɪftɪ','[adj] 节约的','hard-working, thrifty people  勤劳节俭的人们'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6203','enactment','ɪ''næktmənt','ɪ''næktm(ə)nt; e-','[n] 设定,制定','We support the call for the enactment of a Bill of Rights.  我们支持《权利法案》制定的呼吁。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6204','proclaim','prə''klem','prə''kleɪm','[v] 宣布,声明,显露','The President proclaimed the republic’s independence.  总统宣布共和国独立。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6205','seafood','''sifud','''siːfuːd','[n] 海产食品, 海味','a seafood restaurant  海鲜餐馆'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6206','besiege','bɪ''sidʒ','bɪ''siːdʒ','[v] 围困,围攻','In April 655, Osman’s palace was besieged by rebels.  公元655年4月，奥斯曼的宫殿遭到叛军围攻。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6207','unsubstantiated',',ʌnsəb''stænʃɪetɪd','ʌnsəb''stænʃɪeɪtɪd','[adj] 未经证实的,无事实根据的','unsubstantiated allegations of child abuse  未经证实的虐待儿童的指控'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6208','unaware',',ʌnə''wɛr','ʌnə''weə','[adj] 不知道的, 没觉察到的','Many people are unaware of just how much food and drink they consume.  许多人不知道自己到底消耗掉多少食物和饮料。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6209','semimolten','','','[adj] 半熔的',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6210','incinerate','in''sinəreit','ɪn''sɪnəreɪt','[v] 把烧成灰,烧弃','All the infected clothing was incinerated.  所有沾染了细菌的衣服都被焚化了。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6211','topographical','','','[adj] 地志的,地形学的','This is a suburb with very narrow streets, because it was not mapped out by the municipal topographical office.  这个郊区地区的街道非常狭窄，因为没有经过市政地形办公室的规划。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6212','festival','ˈfɛstəvəl','''festɪv(ə)l','[n] 节日,喜庆日; [adj] 节日的,快乐的','Christmas is one of the main festivals in the Christian Calendar.  圣诞节是基督教历的重大节日之一。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6213','canyon','''kænjən','''kænjən','[n] <美>峡谷, 溪谷','The canyon is famous for producing echoes.  这个峡谷以回声而闻名。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6214','falconer','','''fɔː(l)k(ə)nə; ''fɒlk(ə)nə','[n] 以鹰狩猎者,养鹰者',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6215','lien','''liən','liːn; ''liːən','[n] 留置权,抵押品所产生的利息',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6216','prejudice','''prɛdʒədɪs','''predʒʊdɪs','[n] 偏见,损害; [v] 损害,有偏见','Women still face prejudice in the workplace.  女性在职场中仍然面临歧视。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6217','starfish','''stɑr''fɪʃ','''stɑːfɪʃ','[n] 海星','She lays a kindly hand like a tiny starfish on my knee.  她和善地伸出手，像小海星一样放在我的膝盖上。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6218','extraordinarily','ɪk''strɔdɪn(ə)rəlɪ','ɪk''strɔːd(ə)n(ə)rəlɪ','[adv] 非常,格外地',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6219','dismember','dɪs''mɛmbɚ','dɪs''membə','[v] 肢解,割断手足','She then dismembered him, hiding parts of his body in the cellar.  她接着将他的尸体肢解，把几块碎尸藏进了地窖。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6220','unquestionably','ʌn''kwɛstʃənəbli','','[adv] 无可非议地,确凿地','The Eiffel Tower is unquestionably one of Paris’s most familiar landmarks.  埃菲尔铁塔无疑是巴黎最为人熟知的地标之一。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6221','phylum','''faɪləm','''faɪləm','[n] (生物分类学上的)门, 语群',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6222','spinet','ˈspɪnɪt','spɪ''net; ''spɪnɪt','[n] 古时的小型竖琴, 小型立式钢琴',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6223','avail','ə''vel','ə''veɪl','[v] 有益于,有帮助; [n] 效用, 利益',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6224','supremacy','su''prɛməsi','s(j)uː''preməsɪ','[n] 地位最高的人,至高,霸权','Japan’s unchallenged supremacy in the field of electronics  日本在电子领域无人挑战的领先地位'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6225','rumor','''rʊmɚ','ˈruːmə','[n] 流言,谣言; [v] 谣传, 传闻','The rumor rocked the whole city.  谣言使整个城市惊慌不安。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6226','passageway','''pæsɪdʒ,we','''pæsɪdʒweɪ','[n] 过道,出入口','He led me down a narrow passageway.  他带着我穿过一条狭窄的过道。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6227','Gothic','','','[n] 哥特式; [adj] 哥特式的,野蛮的','Gothic tattoos run along her back, and deep knife scars trace her shoulder.  她的背上布满了哥特式纹身，肩头上有深深的刀疤。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6228','bluff','blʌf','blʌf','[n] 断崖,诈骗; [adj] 绝壁的; [v] 诈骗','One of the choppers set down on the beach below them, the other on the bluff above.  有一架直升机在他们下面的海滩上降落，其余的直接降落在断崖上。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6229','versatility',',vɝsə''tɪləti',',vɜːsə''tɪləti:','[n] 多功能性','Its versatility, flexibility, and wide range of implementations and environments make it difficult to describe procedures to cover all cases.  其通用性、灵活性以及广泛的实现和环境，使得描述能涵盖所有情况的过程非常困难。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6230','tonal','''tonl','''təʊn(ə)l','[adj] 音调的','The tonal range she uses is wide and varied.  她使用的色调丰富多彩。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6231','pedal','''pɛdl','''ped(ə)l','[n] 踏板; [v] 踩的踏板','She put her foot down on the accelerator pedal.  她踩下了油门踏板。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6232','inconvenient',',ɪnkən''vinɪənt','ɪnkən''viːnɪənt','[adj] 不便的,打扰的','Monday’s a bit inconvenient for me. How about Wednesday?  周一我不太方便，周三如何？'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6233','contributor','kən''trɪbjətɚ','kən''trɪbjʊtə','[n] 贡献者,捐助者','campaign contributors  竞选捐助人'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6234','overcultivation','','','[n] 耕种过度',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6235','penetration',',pɛnɪ''treʃən','penɪ''treɪʃ(ə)n','[n] 穿过, 渗透, 突破','Cover the entire device to prevent water penetration.  把整台设备都罩住以免进水。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6236','subtract','səb''trækt','səb''trækt','[v] (～ from)减去, 减','Mandy subtracted the date of birth from the date of death.  曼迪从死亡的日期减去了出生的日期。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6237','hearth','hɑrθ','hɑːθ','[n] 壁炉地面, 家庭（生活）','It was winter and there was a huge fire roaring in the hearth.  时值冬天，壁炉里的炉火在熊熊燃烧。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6238','saguaro','sə''ɡwɑro','sə''gwɑːrəʊ; -''wɑː-','[n] 仙人掌之一种','A saguaro cactus stands tall amid a frenzy of lightning bolts in Arizona.  亚利桑那州，一株巨人柱仙人掌矗立在一团狂暴的闪电中。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6239','transcend','træn''sɛnd','træn''send; trɑːn-','[v] 超越, 胜过','The desire for peace transcended political differences.  对和平的渴望超越了政治分歧。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6240','taproot','','''tæpruːt','[n] [植]主根, 直根','A largely Protestant nation that can trace its theological taproot to Martin Luther ought to know better.  作为一个主要由新教徒构成的国家，有必要了解到它的神学根源来自于马丁·路德。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6241','firing','''faɪərɪŋ','''faɪərɪŋ','[n] 开火, 生火; [v] 开火,烧制','They saw a big flash and a huge ball of fire reaching hundreds of feet into the sky.  他们看到一道强光和一个巨大的火球直冲天空达几百英尺。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6242','distributor','dɪ''strɪbjətɚ','dɪ''strɪbjʊtə','[n] 发行人,经销商','...Spain''s largest distributor of petroleum products.  …西班牙最大的石油产品经销商。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6243','signify','''sɪɡnɪfaɪ','''sɪgnɪfaɪ','[v] 颇为重要, 意味','These were not the only changes that signified the end of boyhood.  这些不是表示男孩时代已结束的惟一变化。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6244','heed','hid','hiːd','[n] 注意,留意; [v] 注意,留意','The government was taking little heed of these threats.  政府对这些威胁几乎不当回事。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6245','seminar','''sɛmɪnɑr','''semɪnɑː','[n] 研究会,讨论发表会','a Shakespeare seminar  莎士比亚研讨班'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6246','flavor','''flevɚ','''fleɪvə','[n] 情味, 风味; [v] 加味于',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6247','dissatisfy','dɪs''sætɪs,fai','dɪ(s)''sætɪsfaɪ','[v] 使感觉不满, 不满足',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6248','adequacy','''ædəkwəsi','''ædɪkwəsɪ','[n] 适当, 足够','There are questions to be raised about the adequacy of the inmates'' legal representation.  关于监犯的法定代表是否够格会有一些问题被提出。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6249','uninteresting','ʌn''ɪntrəstɪŋ','ʌn''ɪnt(ə)rɪstɪŋ','[adj] 无趣味的，乏味的','Their media have earned the reputation for being rather dull and uninteresting.  他们的媒体得到的名声是乏味无聊。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6250','minstrel','''mɪnstrəl','''mɪnstr(ə)l','[n] 吟游诗人(或歌手)','Alfred the Great acted his own spy, visiting Danish camps disguised as a minstrel.  他扮作吟游歌手到丹麦军队的营地里侦察。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6251','irreversible',',ɪrɪ''vɝsəbl','ɪrɪ''vɜːsɪb(ə)l','[adj] 不可逆的,不能取消的','Fossil fuels have caused irreversible damage to the environment.  矿物燃料已对环境造成了不可挽回的破坏。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6252','commend','kə''mɛnd','kə''mend','[v] 称赞, 表扬, 推荐','The paper was highly commended in the UK Press Awards.  该报获得了“英国新闻奖”的高度褒奖。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6253','ling','lɪŋ','lɪŋ','[n] 鳕鱼, 石南之一种',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6254','phosphate','''fɑsfet','''fɒsfeɪt','[n] 磷酸盐','The role of these glands is to regulate calcium and phosphate in our bloodstream.  这些腺体的作用是稳定血液中钙质和磷酸盐的含量。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6255','apiece','ə''pis','ə''piːs','[adv] 每个, 每人, 各','The pictures are worth about £10,000 apiece.  这些画每幅价值约一万英镑。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6256','walker','''wɔkɚ','''wɔːkə','[n] 徒步者, 参加竞走者','The area is popular with walkers.  这地方很受徒步者欢迎。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6257','distinctly','dɪ''stɪŋktli','dɪ''stɪŋ(k)tlɪ','[adv] 清楚地, 显然','Speak clearly and distinctly.  说话要清楚明白。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6258','deteriorate','dɪ''tɪrɪəret','dɪ''tɪərɪəreɪt','[v] (使)恶化','Ethel’s health has deteriorated.  埃塞尔的健康状况恶化了。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6259','taut','tɔt','tɔːt','[adj] (绳子)拉紧的,紧张的; [vt] 使纠缠','The rope was stretched taut.  绳子绷紧了。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6260','spur','spɝ','spɜː','[n] 踢马剌; [v] 鞭策, 刺激','Lower taxes would spur investment and help economic growth.  降低税率将刺激投资，有助于经济增长。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6261','stretcher','''strɛtʃɚ','''stretʃə','[n] 担架, 延伸器','The two ambulance attendants quickly put Plover on a stretcher and got him into the ambulance.  这两名救护车的救护员迅速把普洛弗放在担架上并抬进了那辆救护车。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6262','hoof','huf','huːf','[n] 蹄 v踢','The horses'' hooves often could not get a proper grip.  这些马的蹄子经常踩不稳。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6263','discolor','dɪs''kʌlɚ','dis''kʌlə','[v] 使脱色, (使)变色,(使)退色',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6264','foreleg','''fɔrlɛɡ','''fɔːleg','[n] 前肢(指四肢或多肢动物的)前脚','In a proper depiction the hindleg would be forward too, having moved before the foreleg.  正确的姿势应是，右后腿早应向前迈，并且应该在跨出前腿之前就迈出后腿。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6265','buckskin','''bʌkskɪn','''bʌkskɪn','[n] 鹿皮裤, 鹿皮',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6266','fortify','''fɔrtɪfaɪ','''fɔːtɪfaɪ','[v] 增强(体力,结构等); [v] 筑防御工事','Her position was fortified by election successes and economic recovery.  她的地位因为选举获胜及经济复苏而得到巩固。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6267','suspender','sə''spɛndɚ','','[n] 吊裤带, 悬挂物, 吊杆, 袜吊','He also wore a pair of suspenders.  他也穿着吊带裤。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6268','buckle','','''bʌk(ə)l','[n] 带扣 v扣住, 变弯曲','He wore a belt with a large brass buckle.  他系了一根有很大黄铜扣的皮带。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6269','chafe','tʃef','tʃeɪf','[v] (将皮肤等)擦热, 使恼火','My shorts were chafing my thighs.  我的短裤蹭得我大腿疼。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6270','tourniquet','''tɝnəkət','''tʊənɪkeɪ; ''tɔː-','[n] 止血带, 压脉器','That will work as a tourniquet.  就和止血带的功用一样了。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6271','bandanna','bæn''dænə','','[n] 大手帕','These days, her bandanna is usually red.  这些天，她的印花大手帕通常是红色的。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6272','charm','tʃɑrm','tʃɑːm','[n] 吸引力, 魅力; [v] 迷人, 使陶醉','Joe’s boyish charm  乔身上的稚趣'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6273','vestigial','vɛ''stɪdʒɪəl','ve''stɪdʒɪəl; -dʒ(ə)l','[adj] 退化的,发育不全的','The legs of snakes are vestigial or absent altogether.  蛇的腿已经退化或完全消失。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6274','harem','''hærəm','''hɑːriːm; hɑː''riːm; ''heərəm','[n] （伊斯兰教教徒之）闺房, 为一个雄性动物所控制的许多雌性动物',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6275','nonfunctional','','','[adj] 不运行的',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6276','everest','ˈɛvərɪst','''evərɪst','[n] 珠穆朗玛峰(世界最高峰)',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6277','trench','trɛntʃ','tren(t)ʃ','[n] 沟渠, 堑壕; [v] 掘沟, 挖战壕','Workers dug a trench for gas lines.  工人们挖了一条沟来铺设煤气管道。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6278','Monroe','mən''rəu','mən''rəu','[n] 门罗(m)','Monroe followed Madison as president.  门罗接替麦迪逊当上总统。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6279','concede','kən''sid','kən''siːd','[v] 勉强, 承认, 退让 vi让步','‘That’s the only possible solution.’ ‘Yes, I suppose so,’ Charles conceded.  “那是唯一可行的解决办法。”“对，我想是。”查尔斯承认道。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6280','jawbone','''dʒɔbon','''dʒɔːbəʊn','[n] 颚骨, 下颚骨, 信用 v赊买',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6281','selective','sɪ''lɛktɪv','sɪ''lektɪv','[adj] 选择的, 选择性的','selective schools  择优录取学生的学校'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6282','Iraq','ɪ''rɑk','ɪ''rɑ:k','[n] 伊拉克共和国','So why go to Iraq when you can go to Canada?  因此，如果你可以去加拿大的话，为什么要去伊拉克呢？'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6283','grande','''ɡrændə; ''ɡrɑŋdi','gra:nd','[adj] 重大的，显要的',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6284','facelift','''feslɪft','','[n] 整容手术（除去面部皱纹）','I had a facelift in 1995, which went wrong.  我在1995年做了一次失败的面部拉皮手术。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6285','donation','do''neʃən','də(ʊ)''neɪʃ(ə)n','[n] 捐赠品, 捐款, 贡献','There have been generous donations from EU funds.  欧盟基金给予了慷慨的捐款。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6286','massif','mæ''sif','''mæsɪf; mæ''siːf','[n] 山丘','Tanakhat Monastery complex is located on a hill of a very picturesque massif.  塔纳哈修道院坐落在一处风景如画的山丘上。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6287','atlas','','','[n] 地图, 地图集',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6288','wireless','''waɪərləs','ˈwʌɪəlɪs','[adj] 无线的; [n] 无线','...the fast-growing wireless communication market.  …快速增长的无线通讯市场。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6289','sterilize','''stɛrəlaɪz','''sterəlaiz','[v] 杀菌, 消毒, 使成不毛','Sterilize the bottles with boiling water.  用沸水把这些瓶子消毒。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6290','reenter','ri''ɛntɚ',',riː''entə','[n] 重进入, 再加入; [v] 重返','After waiting a while, and with a fresh canary, the miners could safely reenter the mine.  过一段时间之后，如果新换上的金丝雀安然无恙，矿工们又可以安全地重返矿井。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6291','retard','''rɪtɑrd','''rɪtɑːd','[v] 延迟, 妨碍; [n] 延迟','Continuing violence will retard negotiations over the country''s future.  持续不断的暴力活动会阻碍关于国家未来的谈判的进行。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6292','logic','''lɑdʒɪk','''lɒdʒɪk','[n] 逻辑, 逻辑学; [adj] 逻辑的','There isa certain logicin their choice of architect.  他们对建筑师的选择是有一定道理的。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6293','rot','rɑt','rɒt','[v] (使)腐烂, (使)腐败 n腐烂, 腐败','Candy will rot your teeth.  吃糖会腐蚀牙齿。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6294','satisfaction',',sætɪs''fækʃən','sætɪs''fækʃ(ə)n','[n] 满意, 满足, 令人满意的事物','She got great satisfaction from helping people to learn.  她在帮助人们学习的过程中得到很大的满足。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6295','rapport','ræ''pɔr','ræ''pɔː','[n] 和谐, 亲善','And last but not least, people with whom you can build a rapport and camaraderie with.  一直到最后、并非最不重要的一个人，与你建立起和谐融洽的友谊。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6296','elevate','''ɛlɪvet','''elɪveɪt','[v] 举起, 提升的职位','He was elevated to the post of president.  他被提拔到总裁的职位。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6297','gripe','ɡraɪp','graɪp','[n] 紧握, 柄; [v] 握紧',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6298','gossip','''ɡɑsɪp','''gɒsɪp','[n] 闲话, 闲谈','Phil’s in there, having a gossip with Maggie.  菲尔在那里面跟玛吉闲聊。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6299','attendance','ə''tɛndəns','ə''tend(ə)ns','[n] 出席, 出席的人数','We have an average attendance of 4,000 fans per game.  每场比赛平均有4,000名球迷来观战。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6300','socialization',',soʃələ''zeʃən',',səʊʃəlaɪ''zeɪʃən','[n] 社会化, 社会主义化','Schools play an important part in the socialization of our children.  学校对儿童适应社会的过程起着重要的作用。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6301','Irish','ˈaɪrɪʃ','''aiəriʃ','[n&a] 爱尔兰人(的),爱尔兰语（的）','I am starting to sense that maybe I and people like me are to blame because it is we, the Irish people, who are paying with our jobs, livelihoods, health care and education.  我开始感觉到或许就是我以及像我这样的人，该受责备，因为就是我们，让爱尔兰人民，正在为我们的工作、生活、医疗卫生和教育买单。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6302','eyewitness','''aɪwɪtnəs','''aɪwɪtnɪs','[n] 目击者, 见证人','One eyewitness said he saw her talking to a man in a blue car.  一名目击者说他看见她在跟一个坐在蓝色汽车里的男子说话。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6303','conglomerate','kən''ɡlɑːmərət','kən''glɒm(ə)rət','[v] 聚结; [n] 企业集团','an international conglomerate  国际大型联合企业'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6304','gang','ɡæŋ','gæŋ','[n] (一)伙, (一)群','Several gangs were operating in the area.  有好几个犯罪团伙在这个地区活动。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6305','entail','ɪn''tel','ɪn''teɪl; en-','[v] 使必需, 使蒙受; [n] [建]限定继承权','A new computer system entails a lot of re-training.  使用新的计算机系统需要大量的再培训。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6306','punch','','pʌn(t)ʃ','[v] 冲孔, 打孔','The guard punched my ticket and I got on.  守卫在我的票上打孔后，我就上去了。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6307','railhead','''relhɛd','''reɪlhed','[n] 铺设中的铁路末端, 终点',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6308','preferential',',prɛfə''rɛnʃl',',prefə''renʃ(ə)l','[adj] 优先的；选择的','preferential credit terms for reliable borrowers  向可靠借款人提供的优惠信贷条件'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6309','cerebral','sə''ribrəl','''serɪbr(ə)l; sə''riːbr(ə)l','[adj] 脑的, 大脑的','a cerebral haemorrhage  脑出[溢]血'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6310','Kenya','ˈkiːnjə','ˈkɛnjə','[n] 肯尼亚','Let us now fuse together now as one people who want to do something for the people of Kenya. Let us strengthen the foundation of multiparty democracy in our country.  现在让我们融汇在一起，团结起来，就像希望为肯尼亚人民作一些事情的同一个人，让我们一起巩固我国多党民主制的基础。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6311','alphabet','''ælfə''bɛt','''ælfəbet','[n] 字母表','The modern Russian alphabet has 31 letters.  现代俄语字母表有31个字母。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6312','cleanly','''klinli','''kliːnlɪ','[adv] 干净地, 清洁地','The branch snapped cleanly in two.  树枝啪的一下断成两截。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6313','quina','''kwaɪnɚ','''kiːnə','[n] [植]金鸡纳树皮, 奎宁',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6314','unresolved',',ʌnrɪ''zɑlvd','ʌnrɪ''zɒlvd','[adj] 未解决的，未决定的','the unresolved issue of who will pay for the project  项目由谁出资这个悬而未决的问题'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6315','lunch','lʌntʃ','lʌn(t)ʃ','[n] 午餐','What’s for lunch?  午饭吃什么？'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6316','exhilarate','ɪɡ''zɪləret','ɪg''zɪləreɪt; eg-','[v] 使高兴, 使愉快',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6317','choreography',',kɔrɪ''ɑɡrəfi',',kɒrɪ''ɒgrəfɪ','[n] 舞蹈术, 舞台舞蹈','The choreography of Eric Hawkins is considered radical by ballet audiences.  埃里克·霍金斯的舞蹈编排被芭蕾舞剧的观众认为是不同凡响的。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6318','teem','tim','tiːm','[v] 大量出现','God, said, ‘Let the waters teem with countless living creatures, and let birds fly above the earth across the vault of heaven.  上帝说：“水中要有万种游鱼，地上要有无数飞鸟”于是上帝创造出种类繁多的大小鱼类及飞鸟。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6319','lately','''letli','''leɪtlɪ','[adv] 近来, 最近','What have you been doing lately?  你最近在干什么？'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6320','scarcity','''skɛrsəti','''skeəsɪtɪ','[n] 缺乏, 不足','...an ever increasing scarcity of water.  …越来越匮乏的水资源。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6321','premiere','prɪ''mɪr','''premɪeə','[v] 初次公演; [n] 初次的演出; [adj] 杰出的','The documentary premiered at the Jerusalem Film Festival.  那部记录片在耶路撒冷电影节上首映。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6322','screening','''skrinɪŋ','''skriːnɪŋ','[n] 放映; [v] 遮蔽,筛选','a screening of Spielberg’s new movie  斯皮尔伯格的新片放映'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6323','exemplary','ɪɡ''zɛmpləri','ɪg''zemplərɪ; eg-','[adj] 典范的,惩戒性的','a company with an exemplary record on environmental issues  在处理环境问题方面可作为楷模的公司'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6324','Austrian','''ɔstriən','','[n] 奥地利人; [adj] 奥地利的, 奥地利人的','When I began to cough, I blamed it on the Austrian cigarettes.  当我开始咳嗽时，我把这事怪在抽奥地利的香烟上。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6325','watershed','''wɔtɚʃɛd','''wɔːtəʃed','[n] 分水岭','The election of Mary Robinson in 1990 was a watershed in Irish politics.  1990年玛丽·鲁滨逊的当选是爱尔兰政治的分水岭。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6326','periodization','','','[n] (历史等的)时期(或时代)划分',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6327','homemaker','''hommekɚ','''həʊmmeɪkə(r)','[n] 主妇','Whether you are a carpenter or a therapist, a homemaker or a professor, it makes no difference.  不论你是一个木匠或是一个治疗师，一个家庭主妇还是教授，这都没有区别。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6328','chronicle','''krɑnɪkl','''krɒnɪk(ə)l','[n] 编年史; [v] 编入编年史','...this vast chronicle of Napoleonic times.  …这本关于拿破仑时期的大部头编年史。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6329','substrate','''sʌbstret','''sʌbstreɪt','[n] （土地）底层,基础','As chemical precursors stream onto the surface of a rolling metal or plastic substrate, they react with one another to form a network of nanoparticles.  各化学母质流向滚动中的金属或塑料基片的表面，他们互相作用，形成一层纳米级微粒网状结构。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6330','sustenance','''sʌstənəns','''sʌst(ə)nəns; -tɪn-','[n] 食物, 生计, (受)支持','Without sustenance, the animals will soon die.  没有食物，动物很快就会死亡。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6331','charitable','''tʃærətəbl','''tʃærɪtəb(ə)l','[adj] 慈善事业的,慷慨的,仁慈的','charitable groups  慈善团体'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6332','tremendously','trɪ''mɛndəsli','tri''mendəsli','[adv] 非常地,可怕地,惊人地',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6333','outlook','''aʊtlʊk','''aʊtlʊk','[n] 景色, 展望','a very pleasing outlook from the bedroom window  从卧室窗户看出去的宜人景色'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6334','perceptive','pɚ''sɛptɪv','pə''septɪv','[adj] 感知的,知觉的','a perceptive young man  一个观察敏锐的年轻人'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6335','legacy','''lɛgəsi','''legəsɪ','[n] 遗赠(物), 遗产','She received a small legacy from her aunt.  她从姨妈那里继承了一小笔遗产。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6336','painstaking','''penztekɪŋ','''peɪnzteɪkɪŋ','[n] 辛苦; [adj] 辛苦的, 辛勤的','You said in your address that "developing excellence is a slow, painstaking process".  你在你的致词中说“发展卓越性是一个缓慢艰苦的过程”。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6337','unsure',',ʌn''ʃʊr','ʌn''ʃʊə','[adj] 没有自信的, 不确定的','Chris seemed nervous and unsure of herself.  克丽丝显得紧张，没有自信。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6338','loess','''loɪs','''ləʊɪs; lɜːs','[n] 黄土','Could there have been a really large dam that caused a deep lake in both Zharu and the main valleys and is older than the loess deposits?  这儿有可能有一个真正巨大的大坝，导致扎如和主峡谷之间的深湖，并且时间比黄土沉积物还久远吗？'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6339','reflectivity','','','[n] 反射率','With these layers downloaded, you can combine them with the base reflectivity image to produce a more easily readable image map.  下载了这些图层之后，您可以把它们与基本反射率图像结合起来生成更易于阅读的图像地图。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6340','dishabituate','',',dɪshə''bɪtjʊeɪt','[vt] 使戒除(或放弃)习惯,使不习惯',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6341','roughness','''rʌfnɪs','rʌfnɪs','[n] 粗糙, 未加工, 粗糙程度',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6342','responsiveness','rɪ''spɑnsɪvnɪs','ri''spɔnsivnis','[n] 响应能力,有同情心','Performance testing to gauge the scalability and responsiveness of new services should always be part of the plan.  性能测试用于测定新服务的可伸缩性和响应能力，应当是计划的一部分。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6343','partition','pɑr''tɪʃən','pɑː''tɪʃ(ə)n','[v] 区分, 分割 n分割, 划分','Korea was partitioned in 1945.  朝鲜是1945年被分割的。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6344','electro','ɪ''lɛktro','ɪ''lektrəʊ','[n] 电镀物品, 电版',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6345','neutrality','nu''træləti','njuː''trælɪtɪ','[n] 中立, 中性','Net neutrality, or not?  网络中立或不?'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6346','alkaline','''ælkə''laɪn','''ælkəlaɪn','[adj] 碱性的，碱的','Some soils are actually too alkaline for certain plant life.  有些土壤的碱性，实际上对某些植物的生长是过高的。'),
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO words (book_slug, slug, word, phonetic_us, phonetic_uk, meaning, example) VALUES,
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6347','ballad','''bæləd','''bæləd','[n] 民歌, 流行歌曲','...an eighteenth century ballad about some lost children called the Babes in the Wood.  …一首关于迷路儿童的名为《丛林中的宝贝》的18世纪民间叙事诗。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6348','ratify','''rætɪfaɪ','''rætɪfaɪ','[v] 批准, 认可','The parliaments of Australia and Indonesia have yet to ratify the treaty.  澳大利亚和印度尼西亚议会还未批准该条约。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6349','conflate','kən''fleit','kən''fleɪt','[v] 合并','He conflates two images from Kipling’s short stories in the film.  影片中，他把吉卜林短篇小说中的两个人物形象合并在一起。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6350','cardboard','''kɑrdbɔrd','''kɑːdbɔːd','[n] 纸板','a sheet of cardboard  一张卡纸'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6351','catechism','''kætəkɪzəm','''kætɪkɪz(ə)m','[n] 问答教学法, 问答集','We were taught to recite the catechism.  我们学会背诵教义问答。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6352','convection','kən''vɛkʃən','kən''vekʃ(ə)n','[n] 传送, 对流','...clouds which lift warm, moist air by convection high into the atmosphere.  ...云层通过对流把温暖湿润的空气送到高的大气层中。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6353','rewrite','''riraɪt','riː''raɪt','[v] 重写, 改写','I’ll have to rewrite most of the essay.  这篇论文大部分我都得重写。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6354','counterbalance',',kaʊntɚ''bæləns','''kaʊntə,bæl(ə)ns','[v] 使平均, 弥补; [n] 平衡量, 平衡力','Riskier investments tend to be counterbalanced by high rewards.  较高风险的投资往往报以高回报。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6355','creditor','''krɛdɪtɚ','''kredɪtə','[n] 债权人','The company said it would pay in full all its creditors except Credit Suisse.  该公司说将全额付款给除瑞士信贷以外的所有债权人。'),
