('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6379','keplerian','','','[adj] 开普勒理论的,开普勒定律的',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6380','grinder','''ɡraɪndɚ','''graɪndə','[n] 磨工, 研磨者','The grinder is used for making precision tooling.  这台研磨机用于制作精细工具。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6381','Galilean','',',gæli''li(:)ən','[adj] 伽利略的, 加利利的（位于巴基斯坦北部）','59About an hour later another asserted, "Certainly this fellow was with him, for he is a Galilean."  约过了一小时，又有一个人极力地说：“他实在是同那人一夥的，因为他也是加利利人。”'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6382','align','ə''laɪn','ə''laɪn','[v] 排列，使结盟','When war broke out, they aligned themselves with the rebel forces.  战争爆发以后，他们与叛军结了盟。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6383','diffusely','','','[adv] 广泛地,扩散地',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6384','caucasian','kɔˈkeʒən','','[n] 高加索人; [adj] 高加索的, 白种人的','Ann Hamilton was a Caucasian from New England.  安·汉密尔顿是来自新英格兰的白人。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6385','Korean','kə''riən','kə''riən','[n] 韩国人, 韩国语 a朝鲜人的, 朝鲜语的',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6386','crescent','''krɛsnt','''kresənt','[n] 新月, 月牙','a small crescent of pastry topped with cheese  顶上浇有奶酪的新月形油酥小糕点'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6387','dodge','dɑdʒ','dɒdʒ','[v] /n避开, 躲避','He ran across the courtyard, dodging a storm of bullets.  他跑过院子，躲避雨点般的子弹。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6388','surrender','sə''rɛndɚ','sə''rendə','[v&n] 放弃, 投降','Germany surrendered on May 7th, 1945.  德国于 1945 年 5 月 7 日投降。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6389','preach','pritʃ','priːtʃ','[v] 鼓吹','Alexander has been preaching patience.  亚历山大一直宣扬要坚忍。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6390','impatient','ɪm''peʃnt','ɪm''peɪʃ(ə)nt','[adj] 焦躁的,不耐心的','One thing I’ve noticed is that when people have to wait, they become impatient or uncomfortable.  我注意到一件事，就是当人们在等待的时候，人们会变的没有耐心、焦躁不安。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6391','gospel','''ɡɑspl','''gɒsp(ə)l','[n] 〈圣经·新约〉福音书','the Gospel according to St Luke  路加福音'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6392','thirst','θɝst','θɜːst','[n] 口渴,热望; [v] 渴望','Ice water is the only thing that really quenches my thirst (= gets rid of it ) .  只有冰水才能让我真正解渴。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6393','ductless','','','[adj] 无导管的','Endocrine system: Group of ductless glands that secrete hormones necessary for normal growth and development, reproduction, and homeostasis.  内分泌系统：由无管腺体组成的系统，分泌激素（荷尔蒙）以供身体正常生长、 发育、繁殖和自我恒定性之需。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6394','ridicule','''rɪdɪ''kjʊl','''rɪdɪkjuːl','[n] 嘲笑, 奚落; [v] 嘲笑','the ridicule of his peers  他同龄人的奚落'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6395','admiration',',ædmə''reʃən','ædmə''reɪʃ(ə)n','[n] 钦佩, 赞美, 羡慕','Daniel gazed at her in admiration .  丹尼尔用爱慕的眼神注视着她。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6396','garland','''gɑrlənd','''gɑːlənd','[n] 花环 vt戴花环','They wore blue silk dresses with cream sashes and garlands of summer flowers in their hair.  她们穿着配有米色腰带的蓝色丝质连衣裙，头上戴着夏季的花儿编成的花环。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6397','recreate',',rikrɪ''et','riːkrɪ''eɪt','[v] (使)得到休养, (使)得到娱乐','You can never recreate the feeling of winning for the first time.  你永远无法再次体会第一次获胜时的心情。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6398','uncritical',',ʌn''krɪtɪkl','ʌn''krɪtɪk(ə)l','[adj] 无批判力的,不加批判的','...the conventional notion of women as uncritical purchasers of heavily advertised products.  ...妇女是对广告轰炸宣传的商品不批判的购买者这一传统观点。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6399','resonator','''rɛzə''netɚ','''rez(ə)neɪtə','[n] 共鸣器',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6400','Jewett','''dʒu:it','''dʒu:it','[n] 朱厄特（姓氏）','Then, she took Sarah Orne Jewett''s suggestion to write novels about Nebraska life.  后来，她听从萨拉·奥恩·朱维特的建议开始创作反映内布拉斯加生活的小说。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6401','chaotic','ke''ɑtɪk','keɪ''ɒtɪk','[adj] 混乱的, 无秩序的','a chaotic mixture of images  杂乱无章的各种图像'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6402','fen','fɛn','fen','[n] 沼泽, 沼池','This is fen country – the mills drive pumps that drain the land.  这是一个沼泽国 - 这些工厂启动水泵排干地面积水。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6403','toss','tɔs','tɒs','[v] 投, 掷','I''ll toss you for who pays the bill.  我和你掷钱币决定谁来付账。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6404','glance','ɡlæns','glɑːns','[n] /v一瞥,匆匆一看','He gave her a quick glance and smiled.  他迅速地瞥了她一眼，笑了。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6405','pretension','prɪ''tɛnʃən','prɪ''tenʃ(ə)n','[n] 借口, 要求, 自负',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6406','remuneration','rɪ,mjunə''reʃən','rɪ,mjuːnə''reɪʃ(ə)n','[n] 报酬','high rates of remuneration  很高的报酬'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6407','expressiveness','','','[n] 表现, 表示','Moreover, it offers the expressiveness which helps to “simplify complex tasks”.  此外，它更具表现力，这有助于“简化复杂任务”。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6408','scant','skænt','skænt','[adj] 缺乏的,不足的 v节省,减少','The story has received scant attention in the press.  这件事没在报界引起多少注意。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6409','pancreatic',',pæŋkrɪ''ætɪk',',pænkrɪ''ætɪk','[adj] 胰的,胰腺的','...pancreatic juices.  ...胰液。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6410','pancreas','''pæŋkrɪəs','''pæŋkrɪəs','[n] [解]胰腺','And actually it damages the pancreas itself, after a while.  事实上，一段时间之后它对胰腺本身也会产生伤害。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6411','juice','dʒus','dʒuːs','[n] (水果)汁, 液','a carton of orange juice  一纸盒橙汁'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6412','celebratory','''sɛləbrətɔri','','[adj] 快乐的',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6413','digestion','daɪdʒɛstʃən','daɪ''dʒestʃ(ə)n; dɪ-','[n] 消化力, 领悟','Too much tea is bad for your digestion.  喝太多茶会影响消化。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6414','endocrinology',',ɛndokrə''nɑlədʒi',',endəʊkrɪ''nɒlədʒɪ','[n] 内分泌学','These findings shocked the endocrinology community and set off a new wave of research.  这些研究结果轰动内分泌学界，引起新一波研究热潮。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6415','intestinal','ɪn''tɛstɪnl','ɪnte''staɪn(ə)l; ɪn''testɪn(ə)l','[adj] 肠的','Cholera is an acute intestinal infection caused by ingestion of food or water contaminated with the bacterium Vibrio cholerae.  霍乱是由摄入受霍乱弧菌这种杆菌污染的食物或水引起的一种急性肠道感染。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6416','secretin','','sɪ''kriːtɪn','[n] 分泌素','Acidification of the duodenum and the presence of bile in the duodenum promote secretin release.  十二指肠酸化和十二指肠内胆汁有存在促进分泌素释放。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6417','hamlin','''hæmlin','''hæmlin','[n] 哈姆林（姓氏）','To contact the Bloomberg News staff on this story: Kevin Hamlin in Beijing on khamlin@bloomberg.net;  彭博新闻（Bloomberg News）本新闻联系人：凯文·哈姆林(Kevin Hamlin) （驻北京）khamlin@bloomberg.net。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6418','crustacean','krʌ''steʃən','krʌ''steɪʃn','[adj] 甲壳类的; [n] 甲壳纲动物','Researchers found the 70-millimeter crustacean in the dark shale of an Oklahoma quarry.  研究者在俄克拉荷马采石场的页岩层发现这些70毫米的甲壳纲动物。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6419','dragon','''dræɡən','''dræg(ə)n','[n] 龙, 凶暴的人',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6420','consultant','kən''sʌltənt','kən''sʌlt(ə)nt','[n] 顾问, 商议者, 咨询者','a management consultant  管理顾问'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6421','lobster','''lɑbstɚ','''lɒbstə','[n] 龙虾','She sold me a couple of live lobsters.  她卖给了我几只活龙虾。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6422','bliss','blɪs','blɪs','[n] 福佑, 天赐的福; [v] 狂喜','I didn’t have to get up till 11 – it was sheer bliss.  我可以睡到11点才起来，真幸福啊。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6423','empress','''ɛmprəs','''emprɪs','[n] 皇后, 女皇帝, 皇太后, 极有权力的女人',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6424','pomegranate','''pɑmɪɡrænɪt','''pɒmɪgrænɪt','[n] [植]石榴','So you may never know whether spending a fortune on pomegranate juice or the like is worth it.  所以，你可能永远不会知道，花了财富在石榴汁或爱好上是否值得。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6425','misunderstand',',mɪsʌndɚ''stænd',',mɪsʌndə''stænd','[v] 误解, 误会','Rachel, you must have misunderstood her! Ellie would never say something like that.  雷切尔，你一定是误会她了！埃莉绝不会说那样的话。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6426','spatter','''spætɚ','''spætə','[v] 溅污 n滴落','He stared at the rain spattering on the glass.  他注视着往玻璃上溅落的雨。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6427','refurbish',',ri''fɝbɪʃ','riː''fɜːbɪʃ','[v] 再磨光, 刷新','We have spent money on refurbishing the offices.  我们已在这些办公室的翻新上花了钱。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6428','mottle','''mɑtl','''mɒt(ə)l','[v] 使有斑点 n杂色, 斑点',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6429','indifferent','ɪn''dɪfrənt','ɪn''dɪf(ə)r(ə)nt','[adj] 漠不关心的,中性的','an indifferent cook  手艺平平的厨师'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6430','doubtful','''daʊtfəl','''daʊtfʊl; -f(ə)l','[adj] 可疑的, 不确的, 疑心的','For a time it seemed doubtful that he would move at all.  短期内他似乎不大可能搬走。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6431','idealization','','','[n] 理想化, 理想化的事物','Others — cosmology, for example — make hypotheses that are more remote from everyday causes, and involve a high level of mathematical abstraction and idealization.  另外一些——比如说宇宙学——则对远离日常生活的一些事情做出假设，然后通过很高级的数学技巧加以抽象和理想化。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6432','fidelity','fɪ''dɛləti','fɪ''delɪtɪ','[n] 忠实, 诚实, 忠诚, 保真度, (收音机, 录音设备等的)逼真度, 保真度, 重现精度','the importance of marital fidelity  对婚姻忠贞的重要性'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6433','appreciably','ə''pri:ʃəbli','ə''priːʃ(ɪ)əblɪ','[adv] 略微, 有一点',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6434','exceedingly','ɪk''sidɪŋli','ɪk''siːdɪŋlɪ; ek-','[adv] 非常,极度地','Thank you. You’ve been exceedingly kind.  谢谢，你真是太好了。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6435','immensely','i''mensli','ɪ''menslɪ','[adv] 极大地,无限地','If you don''t want to think about anything, just sit there silently and count your breaths - this will help you immensely as well.  如果你不愿意去想任何事，就默默坐在那里，数一下您的呼吸----这也将极大地帮助到你。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6436','interdependent',',ɪntɚdɪ''pɛndənt','ɪntədɪ''pendənt','[adj] 相互依赖的,互助的','countries with interdependent economies  经济上相互依赖的国家'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6437','understandably','','','[adv] 可理解地','Some parents, understandably, have a very hard time with this one. They may feel that anything their kids do is their business.  可以理解，有些家长要做到这一条不太容易，他们可能觉得任何孩子的事都是他们的事。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6438','misunderstanding',',mɪsʌndɚ''stændɪŋ',',mɪsʌndə''stændɪŋ','[n] 误会, 误解','There must have been some misunderstanding. I didn’t order all these books.  一定是弄错了，这些书不全是我订的。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6439','emblem','''ɛmbləm','''embləm','[n] 象征, 徽章; [vt] 用象征表示','...the emblem of the Soviet Union.  …苏联的国徽。'),
