('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6528','fever','''fivɚ','''fiːvə','[n] 发烧, 狂热 v(使)发烧, 狂热','Andy has a fever and won’t be coming into work today.  安迪发烧了，今天不来上班。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6529','loosen','''lusn','''luːs(ə)n','[v] 解开, 放松, 松开','You’ll need a spanner to loosen that bolt.  你需要扳手来拧开那个螺栓。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6530','Netherland','','','[n] 荷兰','Some of the best parts of “Netherland” are Chuck’s rambling political and cultural monologues, delivered as Hans drives him around the boroughs.  《荷兰》的一些最好的部分就是恰克漫谈政治和文化时的独白，是在汉斯开车带他时发表的。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6531','incorrectly',',ɪnkə''rɛktli','ˌɪnkə''rektlɪ','[adv] 错误地,不适当地',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6532','Athens','''æθɪnz','ˈæθɪnz','[n] 雅典(希腊首都)','Can you tell me something about the Acropolis in Athens?  你能给我讲一些关于雅典卫城的事吗?'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6533','tollgate','''təulɡeit, ''tɔl-','''təʊlɡeɪt','[n] 征收通行税的关卡, 关门',''),
