('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6629','watery','''wɑtəri','''wɔːt(ə)rɪ','[adj] (似)水的, 潮湿的','Her eyes were red and watery from crying.  她的眼睛哭得红红的，眼里含满泪水。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6630','fad','fæd','fæd','[n] 时尚, 一时流行的狂热','Interest in organic food is not a fad, it’s here to stay.  对有机食品的兴趣不是一时的风尚，它是长久的喜好。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6631','secretary','''sɛkrətɛrɪ','''sekrɪt(ə)rɪ','[n] 秘书, 部长','My secretary will fax you all the details.  我的秘书会把所有的细节发传真给你。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6632','shy','ʃaɪ','ʃaɪ','[adj] 怕羞的, 畏缩的','He was a quiet shy man.  他是个话不多、害羞的男人。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6633','catchment','''kætʃmənt','''kætʃm(ə)nt','[n] 排水,集水','But the world is also scattered with tales of roof catchment failures — and academics who say its potential for ending water insecurity is oversold.  但是全世界也存在着屋顶集水失败的故事——而且也有学术人士说它结束水不安全的潜力被夸大了。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6634','underscore',',ʌndɚ''skɔr','ʌndə''skɔː','[v] 画底线',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6635','tambourine',',tæmbə''rin',',tæmbə''riːn','[n] 小手鼓','She stood biting her lip, watching, for nearly an hour, until Joseph put his tambourine down and opened his eyes.  她咬着嘴唇站在那里，等着，等了将近一个小时，约瑟夫才放下手鼓、睁开眼睛。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6636','fluidity','flʊ''ɪdəti','fluː''ɪdətɪ','[n] 流动性,变移性','Because of the natural fluidity and immediacy of marketing, we are constantly building new areas of knowledge.  由于市场固有的流动性和即时性，所以我们经常构建新知识领域。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6637','ongoing','''ɑnɡoɪŋ','''ɒngəʊɪŋ','[adj] 正在进行的','their ongoing search for a new director  他们仍在寻找一个新主任'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6638','unhindered','ʌn''hɪndɚd','ʌn''hɪndəd','[adj] 无阻的, 不受阻碍的','he could proceed unhindered'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6639','fleet','flit','fliːt','[n] 舰队 v疾驰,掠过','the US seventh fleet  美国第七舰队'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6640','almanac','''ɔlmənæk','''ɔːlmənæk; ''ɒl-','[n] 历书, 年鉴','a football almanac  足球年鉴'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6641','breathtaking','''brɛθtekɪŋ','''breθteɪkɪŋ','[adj] 令人赞叹的,  壮观的','The view from my bedroom window was absolutely breathtaking.  我卧室窗外的景色美得令人窒息。'),
