('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6643','loyalist','''lɔɪəlɪst','''lɒɪəlɪst','[n] 忠诚的人, 反对独立者','Party loyalists responded as they always do, waving flags and carrying placards.  党的忠诚支持者们一如既往地以挥舞旗帜和高举海报作为回应。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6644','pray','pre','preɪ','[v] 祈祷, 恳求','They went to the mosque to pray.  他们去清真寺祷告。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6645','incoming','''ɪnkʌmɪŋ','''ɪnkʌmɪŋ','[adj] 引入的','When others check in their code, you will see it as incoming to your workspace.  当其他人核查他们的代码时，您将看到它像引入您的工作空间一样。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6646','unpredictably','ˌʌnprɪˈdɪktəblɪ','ˌʌnprɪˈdɪktəblɪ','[adv] 不可预见地,  不能预料地','Because the cave fish may not need less sleep—they may need to stay awake to forage more in an environment where food can be scarce and appear unpredictably.  因为穴居鱼可能并不需要睡得更少——它们可能需要保持清醒，以便更经常地在食物短缺和食物不常出现的环境中觅食。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6647','scraping','''skrepɪŋ','''skreɪpɪŋ','[v&n] 刮，擦','I can''t bear the sound of chalk scraping on a blackboard.  我忍受不了粉笔在黑板上的刮擦声。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6648','reorganize','rɪ''ɔrgə''naɪz',',ri:''ɔ:ɡənaiz','[v] 改组, 整顿','Our office is being completely reorganized.  我们办公室正在彻底改组。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6649','Turkic','''tə:kik','''tə:kik','[n] 土耳其语(的), 土耳其语系者(的)',''),
