('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6651','accuracy','''ækjərəsi','''ækjʊrəsɪ','[n] 精确性, 正确度','He passes the ball with unerring accuracy.  他传球准确无误。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6652','momentarily',',momən''tɛrəli','''məʊm(ə)nt(ə)rɪlɪ; ,məʊm(ə)n''terɪlɪ','[adv] 暂时地, 立刻地','She was momentarily lost for words.  她一时语塞。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6653','overconfident','','əʊvə''kɒnfɪd(ə)nt','[adj] 自负的, 过于自信的','God warns us never to get cocky and overconfident; that is the recipe for disaster.  神警告我们绝不可自高过于自信，那是招致灾难的处方。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6654','expansionist','ɪk''spænʃənɪst','','[n&a] 扩张主义(的)',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6655','bother','''bɑðɚ','''bɒðə','[v&n] 烦扰, 打扰 v','Danny, don’t bother Ellen while she’s reading.  丹尼，埃伦看书的时候不要去打扰她 。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6656','boss','bɑs','bɒs','[n] 老板, 上司 vt指挥','I’ll have to ask my boss for a day off.  我得向老板请一天假。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6657','crowbar','''krobɑr','''krəʊbɑː','[n] 撬棍, 铁橇','They cover him quickly as the crowbar clangs to the ground.  他们迅速掩盖了洞口，撬棍当啷一声，落在了地上。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6658','interdependence',',ɪntɚdɪ''pɛndəns',',ɪntədɪ''pendəns','[n] 互相依赖','...the interdependence of nations.  …国家间的相互依赖。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6659','magnitude','''mæɡnɪtud','''mægnɪtjuːd','[n] 大小, 数量,量级','An operation of this magnitude is going to be difficult.  一个这么大的手术会很难的。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6660','broaden','''brɔdn','''brɔːd(ə)n','[v] 放宽, 变宽, 扩大, 加宽','Mr Mates said the party must broaden its appeal to younger voters.  梅茨先生说该党必须扩大在年轻选民中的影响。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6661','till','tɪl','tɪl','[prep] 直到, 在以前','I didn’t have a boyfriend till I was 17.  我直到17岁才有男朋友。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6662','inappropriate','''ɪnə''proprɪət','ɪnə''prəʊprɪət','[adj] 不适当的, 不合宜的','There is no suggestion that clients have been sold inappropriate policies.  没有迹象表明向客户出售过不适当的保险单。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6663','jar','dʒɑr','dʒɑː','[n] 罐子 v刺激，震动','a jam jar  果酱罐'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6664','residue','''rɛzɪdu','''rezɪdjuː','[n] 残渣, 剩余物','The flies leave a sticky residue on crops.  苍蝇在庄稼上留下黏糊糊的分泌物。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6665','enterprising','''ɛntɚpraɪzɪŋ','''entəpraɪzɪŋ','[adj] 有事业心的, 有进取心的','Some enterprising students are designing software.  一些有创业精神的学生在设计软件。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6666','moisten','''mɔɪsn','''mɒɪs(ə)n','[v] 弄湿 vi变潮湿','Moisten the clay if it seems too dry.  如果黏土太干，就把它润润湿。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6667','medicinal','mɪ''dɪsənəl','mɪ''dɪsɪn(ə)l','[adj] 药物的，治疗的','Garlic is believed to have medicinal properties (= contain things that can cure medical problems ) .  大蒜被认为具有药用功效。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6668','tribespeople','''traɪbzpipl','''traɪbzpiːp(ə)l','[[复]n] 部落(或宗族等)成员',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6669','unattractive',',ʌnə''træktɪv','ʌnə''træktɪv','[adj] 无魅力的, 无吸引力的','an unattractive man  没有魅力的男子'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_6670','tug','tʌɡ','tʌg','[n&v] 用力拉, 拖船','The woman gently tugged his arm.  那女人轻轻拽了拽他的胳膊。'),
