('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7295','superbly','sʊ''pɝbli','sju:''pə:bli','[adv] 雄伟地, 壮丽地',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7296','shipwright','''ʃɪp,raɪt','''ʃɪpraɪt','[n] 造船者','What is he that builds stronger than either the mason, the shipwright, or the carpenter?  能比石匠、船匠和木匠建造出更坚固的建筑的人，他是谁？'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7297','ghostly','''ɡostli','''gəʊs(t)lɪ','[adj] 可怕的','...Sonia''s ghostly laughter.  …索尼娅可怕的怪笑。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7298','thrift','θrɪft','θrɪft','[n] 节俭','They were rightly praised for their thrift and enterprise.  他们因勤俭节约和开创精神而受到了应得的表扬。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7299','conservatism','kən''sɝvətɪzəm','kən''sɜːvə,tɪzəm','[n] 保守主义','people’s innate conservatism in matters of language  人们在语言方面天生的守旧'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7300','leaky','''liki','''liːkɪ','[adj] 漏的','The house had a leaky roof.  这房子的屋顶漏雨。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7301','blacken','''blækən','''blæk(ə)n','[v] 使变黑, 诽谤','The married women of Shitamachi maintained the custom of blackening their teeth.  下町的已婚妇女保留了染黑牙齿的习俗。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7302','fiercely','''fiəsli','''fɪəslɪ','[adv] 猛烈地, 厉害地','The elephant is not immediately susceptible to such blandishments, however, and usually lashes fiercely with its trunk in all directions.  然而大象不会立刻被这些讨好的话感动，而往往是用鼻子朝各个方向猛烈地甩动。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7303','fox','fɑks','fɒks','[n] 狐狸 v奸狡地行动','He was a sly old fox.  他是个狡猾的老狐狸。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7304','verb','vɝb','vɜːb','[n] [语]动词','The German verb is postponed.  德语动词放在句末。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7305','faultfinding','''fɔlt,faɪndɪŋ','''fɔːltfaɪndɪŋ','[n] 找茬,挑剔','He is a faultfinding man.  他是一个爱挑剔的人。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7306','steadfastly','''stɛd,fæstli','''stedfɑ:stlɪ','[adv] 踏实地, 不变地',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7307','untold',',ʌn''told','ʌn''təʊld','[adj] 未说过的,未透露的','The rumours will do untold damage to his reputation.  这些谣言会给他的名声造成无法估计的损害。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7308','intolerant','ɪn''tɑlərənt','ɪn''tɒl(ə)r(ə)nt','[adj] 不宽容的, 偏狭的','She’s lactose-intolerant (= unable to drink particular types of milk ).  她对乳糖过敏。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7309','venue','''vɛnju','''venjuː','[n] 审判地, 集合地',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7310','encapsulate','ɪn''kæpsjə''let','ɪn''kæpsjʊleɪt; en-','[v] 装入胶囊，压缩','The words of the song neatly encapsulate the mood of the country at that time.  这首歌的歌词言简意赅地表现出国家当时的氛围。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7311','evanescent',',ɛvə''nɛsnt','iːvə''nes(ə)nt; ev-','[adj] 迅速消失的, 短暂的','...the evanescent scents of summer herbs.  ...夏季香草逐渐消散的味道。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7312','archipelago','''ɑrkə''pɛlə''go',',ɑːkɪ''peləgəʊ','[n] 群岛, 多岛海',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7313','usefully','','','[adv] 有用地','I resolve to index data usefully.  我决心有效地索引数据。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7314','encyclopedia','ɪnˌsaɪkləˈpidiɚ','ɪnˌsaɪkləˈpiːdiə','[n] 百科全书','the Encyclopedia of Music  音乐百科全书'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7315','multivolume','','','[adj] 多卷的','So he planned a comprehensive, multivolume work to convince scientists and the world.  所以他计划写出一本无所不包、卷帙浩繁的著作以征服科学家们和这个世界。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7316','supportive','sə''pɔrtɪv','sə''pɔːtɪv','[adj] 支持的','My family were very supportive throughout the divorce.  离婚过程中我的家人自始至终都很支持我。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7317','anathema','ə''næθəmə','ə''næθəmə','[n] 诅咒','Campbell summed up by saying that nutrition is holistic, a concept which is “anathema” to most scientists’ method.  坎贝尔总结说，营养是全面的，这个概念是对大多数科学家的方法的“诅咒”。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7318','patty','''pæti','''pætɪ','[n] 小馅饼,','a beef patty  牛肉饼'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7319','workmanship','''wɝkmənʃɪp','''wɜːkmənʃɪp','[n] 手艺, 技艺','The problem may be due to poor workmanship.  问题可能是出在拙劣的工艺上。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7320','documentary','''dɑkjə''mɛntri','dɒkjʊ''ment(ə)rɪ','[n] 记录片 a纪录的, 文件的','...a TV documentary on homelessness.  …一部关于无家可归现象的电视记录片。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7321','untraditional','','','[adj] 非传统的,不符合传统的','He moved to New York and performed an untraditional roster of penniless actor jobs – yoga instructor, manure shoveller, railroad-loader.  他搬到纽约，成为一名一贫如洗的演员，他的工作表上有许多非传统工作——教瑜伽、铲肥料、铺铁路。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7322','thoughtless','''θɔtləs','''θɔːtlɪs','[adj] 欠考虑的','a selfish and thoughtless man  自私而不顾他人的人'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7323','modernist','''mɑdɚnɪst','','[n] 现代主义者, 现代人','There was a return to ornamentation—and there was a frivolity—something over and above the brutal structural form of the old modernist designs.  有对装饰的回归——有轻浮——那是一些凌驾于老套的现代主义设计这种残忍的结构形式的东西。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7324','bergere','','','[n] 围手椅','A vintage bergere chair has been infused with a fresh new vitality with some glossy raspberry paint and animal print upholstery, adding playful yet sophisticated style to this teen girl''s room.  一款古典的扶手椅被漆上了漂亮的红色油漆，并且用动物斑纹来装饰，给这个女孩房增添了生动的色彩。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7325','mainstream','''menstrim','''meɪnstriːm','[n] 主流','Genet started as a rebel, but soon became part of the literary mainstream.  热内起初很叛逆，但不久就回归了文学主流。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7326','photojournalism',',foto''dʒɝnəlɪzəm','fəʊtəʊ''dʒɜːn(ə)lɪz(ə)m','[n] 摄影新闻工作','...some of the finest photojournalism of the Civil Rights era.  ...一些民权运动时期最为优秀的摄影新闻。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7327','souvenir',',suvə''nɪr',',suːvə''nɪə','[n] 纪念品','a souvenir shop  纪念品商店'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7328','regionalist','','','[n] 地方主义者, 地方主义作家',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7329','reportedly','rɪ''pɔrtɪdli','rɪ''pɔːtɪdlɪ','[adv] 据传说, 据传闻','Her husband’s assets are reportedly worth over $15 million.  她丈夫的资产据传超过1,500万美元。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7330','reachable','''ritʃəbl','''riːtʃəbl','[adj] 可达成的, 可获得的','It then traverses the chain of references until all (directly or indirectly) reachable objects from the root set are marked.  跟踪然后遍历引用链直至标记完根集中所有（直接或间接）可获得的对象。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7331','paradox','''pærədɑks','''pærədɒks','[n] 似非而是的论点, 自相矛盾的话','It’s a paradox that in such a rich country there can be so much poverty.  在如此富有的国家却有这么多的贫穷现象，真是矛盾。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7332','stratosphere','''strætəsfɪr','''strætə,sfɪə','[n] 平流层, 高层次','Oil prices soared into the stratosphere .  石油价格飙升。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7333','Americana','ə''merikɑ:nə','ə''merikɑ:nə','[n] 有关美国的文物, 史料','...1950s Americana.  ...20世纪50年代美国史料集锦。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7334','desirability','dɪ,zaɪrə''bɪləti','dɪ,zaɪərə''bɪlɪtɪ','[n] 愿望, 希求',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7335','inflexibly','','','[adv] 不弯曲地, 不屈地',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7336','implausible','ɪm''plɔzəbl','ɪm''plɔːzɪb(ə)l','[adj] 难信的, 似乎不合情理的','It’s not entirely implausible that a galaxy could be identical to our own.  某个星系和我们这个星系完全相同并非完全不可能。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7337','convincingly','kən''vɪnsɪŋli','kən''vinsiŋli','[adv] 令人信服地, 有说服力地',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7338','unwillingness','','','[n] 不愿意, 不情愿','This may, however, not be entirely due to the unwillingness of government''s to use their gold reserves to pay back debt.  然而，这可能不完完全全是由于政府不愿意动用他们的黄金储备来偿还债务。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7339','generically','','','[adv] 属类地, 属类上',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7340','stronghold','''strɔŋhold','','[n] 要塞, 据点','The area is a Republican stronghold.  这个地区是共和党的大本营。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7341','drench','drɛntʃ','dren(t)ʃ','[v] 湿透','In the early morning they had got drenched in the grass.  一大清早他们在草丛里弄得浑身湿透。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7342','industrially','','','[adv] 企业[工业]地','He added: “You can imagine a situation when some of our industrially important but polluting processes are done in space and the finished products are brought back down to Earth.  他补充说：“你可以想象一种情况，当我们的一些工业污染的过程是重要的，但做的空间和成品带回了地球。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7343','vitality','vaɪ''tæləti','vaɪ''tælɪtɪ','[n] 活力, 生命力','Despite her eighty years, Elsie was full of vitality.  尽管已80岁了，埃尔茜依然充满活力。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7344','restatement','','','[n] 再声明, 重述','I hope this book is not yet another restatement of the prevailing wisdom.  我希望这本书不会又是重复一些流行的至理名言。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7345','constituency','kənˈstɪtʃʊənsɪ','kən''stɪtjʊənsɪ','[n] (选区的)选民,  支持者','a rural constituency  一个乡村选区'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7346','eclectic','ɪ''klɛktɪk','ɪ''klektɪk','[adj] 折衷的; [n] 折衷主义者','But they are the tip of an eclectic iceberg in the country.  其实这只不过是折衷主义在这个国家表现出来的冰山一角。'),
