('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7626','changeover','''tʃendʒ''ovɚ','''tʃeɪn(d)ʒəʊvə','[n] 转换, 大变更','He again called for a faster changeover to a market economy.  他再次呼吁一个更快的向市场经济的转换。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7627','meander','mɪ''ændɚ','mɪ''ændə','[v] 蜿蜒而行','We took a gravel road that meandered through farmland.  我们走上了一条蜿蜒穿越农田的石子路。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7628','skylight','''skaɪ''laɪt','''skaɪlaɪt','[n] 天窗','The very tall ceilings in the Master Bedroom allow for beautiful art display with perfect lighting with the skylight above.  主卧室非常挑高的天花板让上方的天窗为美丽的艺术展示提供了完美的照明。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7629','palatable','''pælətəbl','''pælətəb(ə)l','[adj] 味美的','a very palatable wine  口感极佳的酒'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7630','contender','kən''tɛndɚ','kən''tendə','[n] 竞争者','Her trainer said yesterday that she would be a strong contender for a place on the Olympic team.  她的教练昨天说，她会是取得奥运代表队里一个席位的一名强有力的竞争者。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7631','invariable','ɪn''vɛrərɪəbl','ɪn''veərɪəb(ə)l','[n&a] 不变的, 永恒的','Eluding is the invariable game.  逃避是不变的游戏。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7632','depreciation','dɪ,priʃɪ''eʃən','dɪ,priːʃɪ''eɪʃ(ə)n; -sɪ''eɪ-','[n] 贬值, 减价','the depreciation of the dollar  美元的贬值'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7633','unspecified',',ʌn''spɛsɪfaɪd','ʌn''spesɪfaɪd','[adj] 未详细说明的','The meeting will take place at an unspecified date in the future.  会议将于日后召开，具体日期不确定。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7634','disability',',dɪsə''bɪləti','dɪsə''bɪlɪtɪ','[n] 无力, 残疾','Facilities for people with disabilities are still insufficient.  供残疾人使用的设施仍然不足。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7635','helplessness','','','[n] 无能为力','When we look at the world around us, particularly as portrayed in the media, many of us feel a sense of helplessness at our perceived inability to manifest change.  当我们观察我们周围的世界，尤其是像媒体所描述的那个时，我们中的很多人都会有一丝无助，因为我们感到自己无力实现改变。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7636','retentive','rɪ''tɛntɪv','rɪ''tentɪv','[adj] 有记忆力的','Luke had an amazingly retentive memory.  卢克记忆力惊人。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7637','amplifier','''æmplɪfaɪɚ','''æmplɪfaɪə','[n] 扩音器, 放大器','We can use them as an amplifier.  我们可以将其当作放大器。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7638','scan','skæn','skæn','[n&v] 扫描；浏览','She scanned through the paper.  她浏览了一下报纸。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7639','unfailingly','','','[adv] 无穷尽地, 可靠地',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7640','swell','swɛl','swel','[v] (使)膨胀, 增大','The river was swollen with melted snow.  积雪融化，河水上涨。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7641','needless','''nidləs','''niːdlɪs','[adj] 不需要的, 不必要的','The report caused needless anxiety to women who have attended the clinic.  那份报告让去那家诊所就诊过的妇女产生了不必要的忧虑。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7642','bulge','bʌldʒ','bʌldʒ','[n&v] 膨胀，鼓起','The gun made a bulge under his jacket.  手枪从他的夹克里面鼓了出来。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7643','undiscovered','''ʌndis''kʌvəd','ʌndɪ''skʌvəd','[adj] 未被发现的','The name Vulcan was given to the undiscovered planet.  “伏尔坎”这个名字被用来给未被发现的星体命名。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7644','helplessly','','','[adv] 无能为力地',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7645','overnight','''ovənaɪt','əʊvə''naɪt','[ad& a] (在)整夜(的)；突然(的)',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7646','dentist','''dɛntɪst','''dentɪst','[n] 牙科医生','Visit your dentist twice a year for a checkup.  每年看两次牙医做检查。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7647','optometrist','ɑp''tɑmətrɪst','ɒp''tɒmɪtrɪst','[n] 验光师, 视力测定者','One evaluation has shown that 70% of the people who received the new glasses corrected their own vision at least as well, if not better, than a trained optometrist.  评价表明，在得到新型眼镜的人中，有70％的人最起码与一位训练有素的验光配镜师一样很好地矫正了其视力。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7648','merciless','''mə:silis','''mɜːsɪlɪs','[adj] 残忍的；无情的','a merciless attack  无情的攻击'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7649','strenuous','''strɛnjuəs','''strenjʊəs','[adj] 奋发的, 费力的, 积极的','a strenuous climb  艰难的攀登'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7650','passion','''pæʃən','''pæʃ(ə)n','[n] 激情，热情','The issue arouses strong passions .  那件事激起了人们强烈的情绪。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7651','emancipate','ɪ''mænsɪpet','ɪ''mænsɪpeɪt','[v] 释放, 解放','Slaves were emancipated in 1834.  奴隶于1834年获得了解放。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7652','protagonist','prə''tæɡənɪst','prə''tæg(ə)nɪst','[n] 提倡者，支持者','the main protagonists in the conflict  主要的冲突方'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7653','leo','','','[n] [天]狮子座，狮子宫',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7654','cruel','''kruəl','krʊəl','[adj] 残酷的, 悲惨的','His death was a cruel blow .  他的死是个无情的打击。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7655','grimly','''grɪmlɪ','''grɪmlɪ','[adv] 严格地,冷酷地','I have exercised like this — obsessively, a bit grimly — for years, but recently I began to wonder: Why am I doing this?  我痴迷得有点冷酷地这样锻炼了几年，可是，最近我开始疑惑：我为什么要这么做？'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7656','apportion','ə''pɔrʃən','ə''pɔːʃ(ə)n','[v] 分配','It’s not easy to apportion blame (=  say who deserves to be blamed  ) when a marriage breaks up.  婚姻破裂很难说是谁的错。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7657','commentator','''kɑmən''tetɚ','''kɒmənteɪtə','[n] 评论员, 解说员','political commentators  政治评论员'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7658','repay','ri''pɛi','riː''peɪ; rɪ-','[v] 偿还, 报答','I’d like to buy them something to repay all their kindness.  我想给他们买点东西来报答他们的好意。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7659','earning','''ɝnɪŋ','''ɜːnɪŋ','[n] 所得,收入','So how do you approach this potential clientele to maximize your earning at the end of the month?  因此在当月末你怎样对待你的潜在的客户从而达到最大化你的收入？'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7660','bankruptcy','''bæŋkrʌptsi','''bæŋkrʌptsɪ','[n] 破产','In 1999 it was revealed that he was close to bankruptcy.  1999年他被披露几近破产。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7661','subjugation',',sʌbdʒə''ɡeʃən',',sʌbdʒʊ''ɡeɪʃən','[n] 镇压, 平息',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7662','uncontrollably',',ʌnkən''trəuləbli','','[adj] 无法管束的, 控制不住的','This means your blood does not clot and you will bleed uncontrollably.  这意味着你的血液不会凝固，你会控制不住地出血。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7663','lazily','','','[adv] 懒洋洋地','A thin curl of smoke arose lazily from the cobin.  一缕薄烟懒洋洋地从小屋升起。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7664','radioactive','''redɪo''æktɪv',',reɪdɪəʊ''æktɪv','[adj] 放射性的，有辐射能的','the problem of how to dispose of radioactive waste  如何处理放射性废物的问题'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7665','consortium','kənˈsɔrʃiəm','kən''sɔːtɪəm','[n] 财团, 联合, 合伙','a consortium of oil companies  石油公司联合企业'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7666','preventive','pri''vɛntɪv','prɪ''ventɪv','[adj] 预防性的','preventive health programs  预防性的保健计划'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7667','supplementary',',sʌplɪ''mɛntri',',sʌplɪ''ment(ə)rɪ','[adj] 增补的，补充的','supplementary information  补充信息'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7668','multidirectional',',mʌltɪdaɪ''rɛkʃənəl',',mʌltɪdɪ''rekʃ(ə)n(ə)l; -daɪ-','[adj] 多方向的','A new nonlinear weighted average multidirectional morphological filtering algorithm is proposed, which is used in suppressing speckle noise.  提出了一种新的用于散斑噪声抑制的非线性加权均值多方向形态滤波算法。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7669','booklet','''bʊklət','''bʊklɪt','[n] 小册子','a free booklet on drug abuse  关于嗜毒问题的免费小册子'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7670','curio','''kjʊrɪo','''kjʊərɪəʊ','[n] 古董, 古玩','Red and blue spectacles, it was imagined, would be routinely employed to watch a film. Flat projection would be a historical curio.  当时人们认为那种红蓝3D眼镜将是未来观影必备物品，平板投射技术将成为历史古董。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7671','chandler','''tʃændlɚ','''tʃɑːndlə','[n] 杂货零售商',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7672','speck','spɛk','spek','[n] 斑点','He has even cut himself shaving. There is a speck of blood by his ear.  他甚至在刮脸时划伤了自己。他耳边有一点血迹。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7673','stair','stɛr','steə','[n] 楼梯','We walked up four flights of stairs (= sets of stairs ) .  我们往上走了四段楼梯。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7674','encircle','ɪn''sɝkl','ɪn''sɜːk(ə)l; en-','[v] 环绕, 围绕','The island was encircled by a dusty road.  那座岛屿为一条尘土飞扬的公路所环绕。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7675','surmount','sɚ''maʊnt','sə''maʊnt','[v] 克服；置于…顶上','He has had to surmount immense physical disabilities.  他不得不克服严重的身体残疾。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7676','heading','''hɛdɪŋ','''hedɪŋ','[n] 标题','chapter headings  章节标题'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7677','Californian','ˌkælɪˈfɔːnɪən',',kæli''fɔ:njən','[n] 加利福尼亚州人 a加州的',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7678','reaumur','','','[n&a] 列氏温度计(的)',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7679','mycology','maɪ''kɑlədʒi','maɪ''kɒlədʒɪ','[n] [植]真菌学','It is active in under- and postgraduate training in the fields of botany, mycology , and plant physiology.  该所积极参于植物学，真菌学，和植物生理学领域的本科生和研究生训练。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7680','glean','ɡlin','gliːn','[v] 拾落穗, 收集','At present we''re gleaning information from all sources.  目前我们正从所有渠道慢慢收集信息。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7681','nevus','''ni:vəs','''niːvəs','[n] [医]痣','Objective: To sieve out the best methods for nevus treatment.  目的：筛选皮肤色素痣的最佳治疗方法。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7682','watcher','''wɔtʃɚ','''wɒtʃə(r)','[n] 监票员, 看守人',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7683','filament','''fɪləmənt','''fɪləm(ə)nt','[n] 细丝, 灯丝','an electric filament  灯丝'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7684','thermal','''θɝml','''θɜːm(ə)l','[adj] 热的, 热量的','thermal energy  热能'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7685','ostrich','''ɔstrɪtʃ','''ɒstrɪtʃ','[n] 鸵鸟','Some Italians eat donkeys; South Africans eat ostrich.  有些意大利人吃驴；南非人吃鸵鸟。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7686','faintly','''fentli','''feɪntlɪ','[adv] 微弱地, 朦胧地','From the hall the clock calling out the quarter hour, then a moment of stillness - time stalling - before, faintly, the clock in her study responded.  客厅传来钟表敲打刻点的声音，接下来是短暂的静止——时间的停止，直到书房里的钟表微弱地做出了回应。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7687','dazzlingly','','','[adv] 灿烂地, 耀眼地','How to smile dazzlingly – it will light up your life.  怎样灿烂地笑——它会 点亮你的人生 。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7688','tint','tɪnt','tɪnt','[n] 色彩','paper with a yellowish tint  泛黄的纸张'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7689','varve','vɑrv','vɑːv','[n] [地质]纹泥','Recently the study of maar lake and varve chronology is becoming a new field for palaeoclimate research.  火山活动是影响全球变化的重要因素之一，玛珥湖和纹泥年代学是近年来古气候研究的新领域。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7690','server','''sɝvɚ','''sɜːvə','[n] 服务器','Well, only the server can do that.  嗯，只有服务器能做这项工作。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7691','benign','bɪ''naɪn','bɪ''naɪn','[adj] 仁慈的, 温和的, 良性的','He shook his head in benign amusement.  他被逗乐了，和蔼地摇了摇头。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7692','feathery','''fɛðəri','''feð(ə)rɪ','[adj] 生有羽毛的,柔软如羽毛的','The plant has feathery leaves.  这种植物长着羽状叶片。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7693','churn','tʃɝn','tʃɜːn','[v] 搅拌, 搅动','...dirt roads now churned into mud by the annual rains.  …土路现在被一年一度的雨水搅和得一片泥泞。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7694','awhile','ə''waɪl','ə''waɪl','[adv] 片刻, 一会儿','He worked awhile as a pharmacist in Cincinnati.  他在辛辛那提做了一阵子的药剂师。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7695','proudly','''praʊdli','''praudli','[adv] 骄傲地','I view it as a call to action, and proudly sport it as a title.  我却把它看作一个行为的调令，并骄傲地将它作为一个标题。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7696','pedestrian','pə''dɛstrɪən','pɪˈdestrɪən','[n] 步行者，行人','Ingrid was a walker, even in Los Angeles, where a pedestrian is a rare sight.  英格丽德是个步行者，即使在行人少见的洛杉矶也是如此。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7697','oilskin','''ɔɪlskɪn','''ɒɪlskɪn','[n] 油布, 防水布',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7698','splash','splæʃ','splæʃ','[n&v] 溅, 飞溅','The children were splashing about in the pool.  孩子们在水池里戏水。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7699','unnoticed',',ʌn''notɪst','ʌn''nəʊtɪst','[adj] 不被注意的, 被忽视的','Elsa stood unnoticed at the edge of the crowd.  埃尔莎悄悄地站在人群边上。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7700','thunderous','''θʌndərəs','''θʌnd(ə)rəs','[adj] 打雷的, 雷鸣般的','His speech was greeted with thunderous applause .  他的演讲赢得雷鸣般的掌声。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7701','faraway','''fɑrəwe','''fɑːrəweɪ; fɑːrə''weɪ','[adj] 遥远的','She dreamed of flying away to exotic faraway places.  她梦想着飞到遥远的异国。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7702','ploy','plɔɪ','plɒɪ','[n] 花招，手段','His usual ploy is to pretend he’s ill.  他惯用的花招是装病。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7703','noisily','','','[adv] 吵闹地','It’s a colorful scene - laborers unload noisily, and small groups of women haggle for the pots of crabs and sardines to sell at village markets.  在这个热闹的环境中，工人喧闹地卸着船，三五成群的妇女正在为一盆盆螃蟹和沙丁鱼讨价还价，以便在村里的鱼市出售。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7704','squeak','skwik','skwiːk','[n] 吱吱声; [v] 吱吱叫','With a third group, she activated the squeak as if by accident.  对于第三组，她则假装吱吱声是偶然发生的。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7705','crouch','kraʊtʃ','kraʊtʃ','[v] 蜷缩, 蹲伏','He crouched in the shadows near the doorway.  他蹲在门道近旁的阴暗处。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7706','regain','rɪ''ɡen','rɪ''geɪn','[v] 收回；恢复','The family never quite regained its former influence.  这个家族再也没有恢复往昔的影响力。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7707','outcome','''aʊt''kʌm','''aʊtkʌm','[n] 结果, 成果','People who had heard the evidence at the trial were surprised at the outcome.  在审判过程中听过证词的人都对此结果感到吃惊。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7708','heroism','''hɛroɪzəm','''herəʊɪz(ə)m','[n] 英雄品质, 英雄主义','...individual acts of heroism.  …个人英雄主义行为。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7709','inconspicuously','','','[adv] 难以觉察地, 不显著地',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7710','matron','''metrən','''meɪtr(ə)n','[n] 主妇；护士长',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7711','suspension','sə''spɛnʃən','sə''spenʃ(ə)n','[n] 暂停, 中止','He received a six-month suspension for unprofessional behaviour.  他因有违职业道德的行为被停职六个月。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7712','stratagem','''strætədʒəm','''strætədʒəm','[n] 战略, 计谋','Trade discounts may be used as a competitive stratagem to secure customer loyalty.  商业折扣可以用作保持顾客忠诚度的一种竞争策略。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7713','brood','brud','bruːd','[v] 沉思；孵蛋 n一窝','Don’t sit at home brooding all day.  别整天坐在家里闷闷不乐的。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7714','vole','vol','vəʊl','[n] 田鼠','And because of the oxytocin and vasopressin, they want to have sex with the same vole.  又因为催产素和垂体后叶加压素的作用，它们只想与同一田鼠做爱。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7715','mimic','''mɪmɪk','''mɪmɪk','[v] 模仿, 模拟','He could mimic all the teachers’ accents.  他能模仿所有老师的口音。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7716','unmanageable','ʌn''mænɪdʒəbl','ʌn''mænɪdʒəb(ə)l','[adj] 难处理的, 难控制的','People were visiting the house every day, sometimes in unmanageable numbers.  每天都有人来参观这座房子，有时人数多得难以管理。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7717','rivet','''rɪvɪt','''rɪvɪt','[n] 铆钉  v固定',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7718','hairy','''hɛri','''heərɪ','[adj] 毛发的，多毛的','a skinny guy with hairy legs  一个腿上多毛的干瘦男人'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7719','reception','rɪ''sɛpʃən','rɪ''sepʃ(ə)n','[n] 招待会；接受','It’s an ideal location for a wedding reception .  这里是举办喜宴的理想地点。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7720','flyway','''flaɪ,we','''flaɪweɪ','[n] 候鸟迁徙所经的路径','Yet the physical changes that go with affluence destroy the habitats of migratory shorebirds and seabirds, wreaking havoc on their numbers along the crucial East Asian-Australasian flyway.  然而开发所带来的自然地理变化破坏了迁徙滨鸟和海鸟的栖息地，也就给重要的东亚-大洋洲候鸟迁徙路线沿途上的这些鸟类带来了灾难性的破坏，导致它们数量的剧减。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7721','nozzle','''nɑzl','''nɒz(ə)l','[n] 管口, 喷嘴','If he put his finger over the nozzle he could produce a forceful spray.  如果他把手指按在喷嘴上，就可以产生强力的喷射。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7722','bonanza','bə''nænzə','bə''nænzə','[n] 走运，发财','2008 was a bonanza year for the oil industry.  2008年是石油业兴旺发达的一年。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7723','electrician','ɪ''lɛk''trɪʃən',',ɪlek''trɪʃ(ə)n; ,el-; ,iːl-','[n] 电工, 电学家','I''ve heard an electrician got hurt when he hiked.  我听说有个电工在高空检修电线时摔伤了。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7724','overburden','','əʊvə''bɜːd(ə)n','[v] 装载过多, 负担过多','Health services have been overburdened and are unable to care for many older people.  公共医疗保健服务已经负担过重，无法顾及许多老年人。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7725','lavish','''lævɪʃ','''lævɪʃ','[adj] 无节制的；浪费的 vt慷慨给予，挥霍','a royal palace on a lavish scale  庞大的皇宫'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7726','bravery','''brevəri','''breɪv(ə)rɪ','[n] 勇敢','an act of great bravery  非常勇敢的行为'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7727','creek','krik','kriːk','[n] 小溪, 小河,','Follow Austin Creek for a few miles.  沿着奥斯汀河走上几英里。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7728','waster','''westɚ','''weɪstə','[n] 挥霍者, 废品',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7729','Stamford','''stæmfəd','''stæmfəd','[n] 斯坦福德[美国康涅狄格州西南部城市]','Jake: Because almost everyone in Stamford used to work at the Yale factory.  杰克： 因为过去几乎每个斯坦福德人都在耶鲁锁厂工作过。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7730','gallon','''ɡælən','''gælən','[n] 加仑','a 20 gallon fish tank  一个20加仑的鱼缸'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7731','beer','bɪr','bɪə','[n] 啤酒','a pint of beer  一品脱啤酒'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7732','tact','tækt','tækt','[n] 机智, 手法',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7733','trapper','''træpɚ','''træpə','[n] 捕兽者, 捕捉器',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7734','romantically','','','[adv] 浪漫地, 空想地',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7735','prosecute','''prɑsɪ''kjʊt','''prɒsɪkjuːt','[v] 起(公)诉，告发','Shoplifters will be prosecuted.  在商店行窃者将被起诉。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7736','sonic','''sɑnɪk','''sɒnɪk','[adj] 音速的','...the sonic boom of enemy fighter-bombers.  …敌人战斗轰炸机隆隆的轰鸣声。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7737','enthusiast','ɪn''θuzɪæst','ɪn''θjuːzɪæst; en-','[n] 热心家, 狂热者',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7738','smoothly','''smʊðli','''smuːðlɪ','[adv] 平稳地','Traffic flowed smoothly.  路上交通畅通。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7739','gingham','''ɡɪŋəm','''gɪŋəm','[n] 条纹棉布','a red and white gingham tablecloth  红白相间的格子桌布'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7740','slipper','''slɪpɚ','''slɪpə','[n] 拖鞋','...a pair of old slippers.  …一双旧拖鞋。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7741','instantaneous',',ɪnstən''tenɪəs',',ɪnst(ə)n''teɪnɪəs','[adj] 瞬间的，即刻的','modern methods of instantaneous communication  现代的即时通信方法'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7742','shoeshine','','''ʃuːʃaɪn','[n] 鞋油, 擦皮鞋','a shoeshine stand  一个擦鞋摊'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7743','politely','pə''laɪtli','pə''laitli','[adv] 有礼貌地','Another thing, you should do is politely tell why could this happen, and what to do next.  还有一件事情需要注意，你应该客气地告诉他们为什么会发生这个问题，下一步该怎么做。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7744','modestly','mɑdɪstlɪ','ˈmɒdɪstlɪ','[adv] 谨慎地, 适当地','‘And I think you’ve got to have an awful lot of talent to then go and do what the Beatles did – he says modestly.  我想你一定得有相当出众的才华才能达到甲壳虫所达到的高度——他（书作者）说的很谨慎。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7745','balcony','''bælkəni','''bælkənɪ','[n] 阳台, 包厢','Has your flat got a balcony?  你的公寓有阳台吗？'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7746','loudspeaker',',laʊd''spikɚ','laʊd''spiːkə','[n] 扩音器, 喇叭','The loudspeaker''s stopped working.  扩音器不响了。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7747','confluence','''kɑnfluəns','''kɒnflʊəns','[n] 汇合','The 160-metre falls mark the dramatic confluence of the rivers Nera and Velino.  这处160米的瀑布是维拉河和维里诺河壮观的汇合处的标志。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7748','crunch','krʌntʃ','krʌn(t)ʃ','[vi&n] 嘎吱嘎吱地响(声)','The only sound was the crunch of tyres on gravel.  唯一的声音是轮胎压在砂砾上的嘎吱声。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7749','juggle','''dʒʌɡl','''dʒʌg(ə)l','[v&n] 玩杂耍','Soon she was juggling five eggs.  很快她就在抛接5个鸡蛋了。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7750','seize','siz','siːz','[v] 抓住,夺取','Suddenly he seized my hand.  他突然抓住我的手。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7751','mormon','''mɔ:mən','''mɔ:mən','[n] 摩门教徒, 一夫多妻主义者',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7752','atheist','''eθɪɪst','''eɪθɪɪst','[n] 无神论者','I was an atheist at the time.  那个时候我是一个无神论者。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7753','gallop','''ɡæləp','''gæləp','[n] /v疾驰, 飞奔','I was forced to attempt a gallop.  我被迫尝试一次骑马疾驰。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7754','trestle','''trɛsl','''tres(ə)l','[n] 架柱, 支架','Police allege that he tagged locations in the Massachusetts Avenue and Newbury Street area and the railroad trestle by the BU Bridge, said department spokesman Officer James Kenneally.  部门发言人James Kenneally警官称，警方有证据指控他在马萨诸塞大街，牛玻璃街区以及BU大桥附近的铁道支架上涂涂画画。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7755','ravine','rə''vin','rə''viːn','[n] 沟壑, 峡谷','The bus overturned and fell into a ravine.  这辆公共汽车翻了车，掉进了一处深谷。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7756','spidery','''spaɪdəri','''spaɪd(ə)rɪ','[adj] 蜘蛛(网)一般的, 细长足的','spidery handwriting  细长潦草的字迹'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7757','wildcatter','','','[n] 投机份子','It is the reason why the wildcatter, the independent oilman whose test drillings might come up dry 20 times before gushing in the end, is an enduring Texas symbol.  这就是为什么那些在投机商，那些个体石油商在石油喷发前可能要试钻探多达二十次的原因，这也是德州一直以来的标志。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7758','onlooker','''ɑnlʊkɚ','''ɒnlʊkə','[n] 旁观者','A crowd of onlookers had gathered at the scene of the accident.  一群旁观者围聚在事故现场。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7759','folly','''fɑli','''fɒlɪ','[n] 愚蠢, 荒唐事','Somerville bitterly regretted his folly at becoming involved.  萨默维尔对于把自己牵涉进去的愚蠢行为后悔不迭。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7760','lubricate','''lubrɪket','''luːbrɪkeɪt','[v] 润滑 v加润滑油','Lubricate all moving parts with grease.  给所有活动部件加润滑油。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7761','trespasser','','','[n] 侵入者, 侵犯者','Everson began filming after Christopher fired the first shot, the one that felled the man Meredith Vieira described as a “trespasser.  克里斯托弗开枪后艾弗森才开始拍摄，梅雷迪斯•维埃拉将被击倒的人称为“非法入侵者”。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7762','waxes','','','[n] 蜡，蜂蜡 vt给…上蜡','There were coloured candles which had spread pools of wax on the furniture.  彩色蜡烛在家具上留下了一摊摊的蜡油。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7763','grocery','''ɡrosəri','''grəʊs(ə)rɪ','[n] 食品杂货店','They run a small grocery store.  他们经营一家小食品杂货店。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7764','refiner','rɪ''faɪnɚ','','[n] 精炼者, 精炼机','The refiner defined a definite confine with her fine finger.  提炼者用她精细的手指定义了一个明确的界限。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7765','richly','''rɪtʃli','''rɪtʃlɪ','[adv] 富裕地, 丰富地','It is a difficult book to read, but it richly rewards the effort.  这是本难读的书，不过它会丰厚回报为之所付出的努力。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7766','remodel',',ri''mɑdl','riː''mɒd(ə)l','[v] 重新塑造, 改造','Workmen were hired to remodel and enlarge the farm buildings.  雇用了工人来改造和扩建农场的房子里。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7767','kier','kiə(r)','kɪə','[n] 漂煮锅','The kier is. loaded with cloth in rope form and the scouring chemicals are pumped through the cloth.  将织物以绳状方式送入煮布锅，煮练用的化学助剂通过泵的加压穿过织物。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7768','seepage','''sipɪdʒ','''siːpɪdʒ','[n] 渗流, 渗出的量','Chemical seepage has caused untold damage.  化学品泄漏已造成了难以估量的损失。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7769','cooperative','ko''ɑpərətɪv','kəʊ''ɒpərətɪv','[adj] 合作的, 协力的','He was doing his best to be cooperative.  他在尽全力配合。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7770','ponytail','''ponɪ''tel','''pəʊnɪteɪl','[n] 马尾辫(一种发型)','Her long, fine hair was swept back in a ponytail.  她那漂亮的长发向后梳成了一个马尾辫。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7771','disuse','dɪs''jus','dɪs''juːs','[n&v] 废弃, 废止','The building eventually fell into disuse .  该建筑物最终被废弃不用了。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7772','adequately','''ædikwitli','''ædikwitli','[adv] 充分地','They had equipped their workers adequately for such dangerous condition.  他们让工人们充分装备起来， 以应付这样的危险情况。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7773','wither','''wɪðɚ','''wɪðə','[v] 凋谢,枯萎','The flowers in Isabel''s room had withered.  伊莎贝尔房间里的花朵已经枯萎了。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7774','facsimile','fæk''sɪməli','fæk''sɪmɪlɪ','[n] 摹写, 传真','...a facsimile edition of Beethoven''s musical manuscripts.  ...一份贝多芬音乐手稿的摹本版。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7775','unproductive','''ʌnprə''dʌktɪv','ʌnprə''dʌktɪv','[adj] 不生产的, 徒劳的','an unproductive meeting  没有成果的会议'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7776','methodical','mə''θɑdɪkl','mɪ''θɒdɪk(ə)l','[adj] 有条理的，井然的','He always checked every detail in a methodical way.  他总是有条不紊地检查每一个细节。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7777','contest','kən''tɛst','''kɒntest','[n&v] 论争, 竞赛','Stone decided to hold a contest to see who could write the best song.  斯通决定举行一场比赛，看谁能够写出最佳歌曲。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7778','bike','baɪk','baɪk','[n] 脚踏车, 自行车','Let’s go for a bike ride .  我们去骑会儿自行车吧。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7779','indulge','ɪn''dʌldʒ','ɪn''dʌldʒ','[v] 纵容','His mother spoiled him, indulging his every whim.  他母亲对他纵容娇惯，百依百顺。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7780','unnoticeable','''ʌn''nəutisəbl','ʌn''nəʊtɪsəb(ə)l','[adj] 不引人注意的(','They might kill people slowly in a way that''s unnoticeable, taking effect over perhaps 10 - 30 years by accelerating degenerative diseases.  它们可能用不引人注意的方式缓慢地杀害人民，促进退化性疾病也许在10-30年生效。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7781','termination','''tɝmə''neʃən','tɜːmɪ''neɪʃ(ə)n','[n] 终止','This includes initialization, sharing resources, and resource termination or resource clean up.  这包括初始化、共享资源及终止资源或清理资源。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7782','dismay','dɪs''me','dɪs''meɪ','[n&v] 沮丧, 绝望','The thought of leaving filled him with dismay .  想到要离开，他心里充满了忧伤。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7783','irreparable','ɪ''rɛpərəbl','ɪ''rep(ə)rəb(ə)l','[adj] 无法修复的，不能挽回的','Extensive mining will cause irreparable damage to the area.  大量采矿会对该地区造成无法弥补的损害。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7784','birthright','''bɝθraɪt','''bɜːθraɪt','[n] 生来就有的权利, 长子继承权','Freedom of speech is every American’s birthright.  言论自由是每一个美国人与生俱来的权利。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7785','negotiation','nɪ,ɡoʃɪ''eʃən','nɪgəʊʃɪ''eɪʃ(ə)n','[n] 商议, 谈判','Warren said, "We have had meaningful negotiations and I believe we are very close to a deal."  沃伦说：“我们已经进行了富有意义的谈判，我相信我们很快就能达成协议。”'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7786','fruitless','''frutləs','''fruːtlɪs','[adj] 不结果实的','So far, their search has been fruitless.  到目前为止，他们的搜寻工作毫无结果。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7787','conscription','kən''skrɪpʃən','kən''skrɪpʃ(ə)n','[n] 征召','All adult males will be liable for conscription.  所有成年男子都将有义务服兵役。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7788','aloof','ə''luf','ə''luːf','[adj] 冷漠的','Beneath that aloof exterior, Gayle is a warm, sympathetic person.  在冷漠的外表下，盖尔是个有同情心的热心人。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7789','downtown','''daʊn''taʊn','''daʊntaʊn','[adv] 在市区; [adj] 市区的','By day he worked downtown for American Standard.  白天，他在市中心为美国标准公司工作。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7790','delectable','dɪ''lɛktəbl','dɪ''lektəb(ə)l','[adj] 使人愉快的','...delectable wine.  ...美味可口的葡萄酒。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7791','intermittent',',ɪntɚ''mɪtənt','ɪntə''mɪt(ə)nt','[adj] 间歇的，断断续续的','The weather forecast is for sun, with intermittent showers.  天气预报为晴，有阵雨。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7792','hatchery','''hætʃəri','''hætʃərɪ','[n] 孵卵所','Running along the brook, down to the hatchery, what heavenly joy this was when school was over!  放学后，有什么比沿着小溪跑到孵卵处更能给人如在天堂般的快乐！'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7793','doggedly','','','[adv] 固执地, 顽强地','Find your passion, and pursue it doggedly.  找到你所热爱的，顽强地追求它。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7794','depot','''dipo','''depəʊ','[n] 贮藏所, 仓库','...food depots.  …食物储藏室。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7795','Minnesota',',mini''səutə',',mini''səutə','[n] 明尼苏达州(美国州名)','This is a picture of a weasel I found in Northern Minnesota.  这是我在明尼苏达州北部所发现的一只黄鼠的照片。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7796','erupt','ɪ''rʌpt','ɪ''rʌpt','[v] 喷出 vi爆发','Violence erupted after police shot a student during the demonstration.  警察向示威人群中的一名学生开枪，暴乱随之发生。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7797','truck','trʌk','trʌk','[n] 卡车, 敞棚货车','a truck driver  卡车司机'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7798','phonetic','fə''nɛtɪk','fə''netɪk','[adj] 语音的,语音学的','a phonetic alphabet  音标'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7799','lap','læp','læp','[n] 膝上；一圈; [v] 舔(食)；拍打','Rubens Barrichello finished a lap ahead of his team-mate.  鲁本斯·巴里切罗领先队友一圈跑完全程。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7800','chic','ʃɪk','ʃiːk','[adj] 别致的, 时髦的','Margaret was looking very chic in blue.  玛格丽特穿着蓝色的衣服看上去很优雅。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7801','executive','ɪɡ''zɛkjətɪv','ɪg''zekjʊtɪv; eg-','[n] 主管，行政官a行政的','a marketing executive  营销主管'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7802','slapstick','''slæpstɪk','''slæpstɪk','[n] 闹剧, 趣剧','a slapstick comedy  打闹喜剧'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7803','hairdo','''hɛrdu','''heəduː','[n] 发型','I like your outfit and hairdo!  你的衣服和发型真好看！'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7804','maraca','məˈrækə','mə''rɑ:kə','[n] [音]沙球',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7805','beater','''bitɚ','''biːtə','[n] 搅拌器','an egg beater  打蛋器'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7806','picnic','''pɪknɪk','''pɪknɪk','[n] 野餐','We decided to have a picnic down by the lake.  我们决定在湖边野餐。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7807','craze','krez','kreɪz','[n] 狂热','At that time, scooters were the latest craze .  那时候，小型摩托车是最新的时尚。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7808','synthesizer','''sɪnθəsaɪzɚ','''sinθisaizə','[n] 综合者, [电子]合成器','Now he can only communicate through a voice synthesizer.  如今他只能通过声音合成器来进行交流。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7809','liberation',',lɪbə''reʃən','lɪbə''reɪʃ(ə)n','[n] 释放, 解放','They pant after liberation.  他们渴望解放。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7810','thunder','''θʌndɚ','''θʌndə','[n] 雷,雷声','We were woken in the night by thunder.  晚上我们被雷声惊醒。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7811','blip','blɪp','blɪp','[n] （在雷达屏幕显示出的）物体光点, 尖音信号','blips on a radar screen  雷达屏幕上的光点'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7812','excessively','ɪk''sɛsɪvli','ek''sesɪvlɪ','[adv] 过分地, 过度地, 极度地',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7813','indiscernible','',',ɪndɪ''sɜːnɪb(ə)l','[adj] 看不清的','The path was almost indiscernible in the mist.  迷雾中小路依稀难辨。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7814','lopsided',',lɑp''saɪdɪd','lɒp''saɪdɪd','[adj] 倾向一方的, 不平衡的','a lopsided 8-0 victory  8比0一边倒的胜利'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7815','hippopotamus','ˌhɪpəˈpɑtəməs','ˌhɪpəˈpɒtəməs','[n] 河马','Still, now we knew for sure where whales came from and that the hippopotamus theory wasn''t complete science fiction.  虽然，我们现在已肯定知道鲸来自何处，但是我们也清楚了，河马之说还不够完整。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7816','laugh','læf','lɑːf','[v&n] 笑, 笑声','Maria looked at him and laughed.  玛丽亚看着他大笑起来。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7817','groan','ɡron','grəʊn','[n&v] 呻吟, 叹息','The kids all groaned when I switched off the TV.  我关掉电视时，孩子们都发出不满的抱怨声。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7818','sneeze','sniz','sniːz','[n] 喷嚏 vi打喷嚏','There was a loud sneeze from someone in the back of the audience.  后面的观众中有人大声打了个喷嚏。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7819','tapir','','''teɪpə; -ɪə','[n] [动]貘','It is a small six-legged herbivore called a HEXAPEDE, about the size of a tapir.  这是一个小型六足草食动物 被称为 孔雀鹿 大概有貘那么大。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7820','scream','skrim','skriːm','[v] /n尖声叫, 尖叫声','After the first few shots, people started screaming.  几声枪响过后，人们开始尖叫起来。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7821','horsefly','''hɔrsflaɪ','''hɔːsflaɪ','[n] 马蝇','That horsefly is the only thing keeping this old horse moving.  那只马蝇是唯一能让这匹老马活动的东西。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7822','nonelectronic','','','[adj] 非电子的',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7823','vestige','''vɛstɪdʒ','''vestɪdʒ','[n] 痕迹','We represent the last vestige of what made this nation great – hard work.  我们代表了曾经使这个国家伟大的仅存的品质–勤奋。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7824','baseball','''besbɔl','''beɪsbɔːl','[n] 棒球(运动)','His cane answered for a baseball bat.  他的手杖可代用棒球棒。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7825','reverently','','','[adv] 恭敬地, 虔诚地','He spoke reverently about colleges and loved walking around the Stanford campus.  他虔诚地谈到大学，说自己喜欢在斯坦佛校园漫步。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7826','homeless','''homləs','''həʊmlɪs','[adj] 无家的, 无家可归的','Thousands of people have been made homeless .  成千上万人被逼得无家可归。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7827','mystify','''mɪstə''fai','''mɪstɪfaɪ','[v] 迷惑','Her disappearance has mystified her friends and neighbors.  她的失踪使她的朋友和邻居迷惑不解。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7828','mesmerize','''mɛzməraɪz','''mezməraiz, ''mes-','[v] 施催眠术',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7829','undifferentiated','''ʌndɪfə''rɛnʃɪ''etɪd',',ʌndɪfə''renʃɪeɪtɪd','[adj] 无差别的, 一致的','shows aimed at large undifferentiated groups of people  针对不加以细分的大众的节目'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7830','gravitation',',ɡrævɪ''teʃən','grævɪ''teɪʃ(ə)n','[n] 地心吸力, 引力作用','Newton’s law of gravitation  牛顿万有引力定律'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7831','springtime','''sprɪŋ''taɪm','''sprɪŋtaɪm','[n] 春天, 春季','Flowers bloom in springtime.  花在春天开放。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7832','sled','slɛd','sled','[n] (小)雪撬','She tumbled over a sled.  她被雪橇绊了一跤。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7833','ski','ski','skiː','[n] 滑雪板 vi滑雪','ski slopes  滑雪坡'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7834','swampy','''swɔmpi','''swɒmpɪ','[adj] 沼泽的，似沼泽的','Alternatively, the dead could have been killed on the spot in "the swampy valley environment", the paper concludes.  另一种可能是，这些死者是在有“沼泽河谷环境”的地点被杀害的——论文总结道。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7835','pickaxe','''pɪkæks','','[n] 鹤嘴锄, 手镐','He advanced towards the angle, and summoning all his resolution, attacked the ground with the pickaxe.  他向那个角落走去好象突然下了一个很大的决心似的，用鹤嘴锄猛击地面。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7836','cubic','''kjubɪk','''kjuːbɪk','[adj] 立方体的, 立方的','the cubic capacity of an engine  引擎汽缸的容积'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7837','taint','tent','teɪnt','[v] 感染 n污点','Baker argues that his trial was tainted by negative publicity.  贝克抗辩说他的审判受到了负面宣传的影响。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7838','pestilential',',pɛstɪ''lɛnʃl',',pestɪ''lenʃ(ə)l','[adj] 引起瘟疫的, 有害的','...people who were dependent for their water supply on this pestilential stream.  ...那些靠这条致病的河流来取水的人们。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7839','miasmic','','','[adj] 毒气的, 瘴气的',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7840','onstage','''ɔn''stedʒ','ɒn''steɪdʒ','[adj] 台上的,舞台表演区的','Even today I get nervous before I go onstage.  直到今天我上舞台前还是会感到紧张。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7841','holm','','həʊm','[n] (河，湖中的)小岛',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7842','anymore','ɛnɪ''mɔr','enɪ''mɔː','[adv] 不再, 再也不','Nick doesn’t live here anymore.  尼克不再住在这里了。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7843','trainload','''treinləud','''treɪnləʊd','[n] 装载量, 列车载重','A trainload more may soon be on the way.  承载更多运输量的列车即将出现。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7844','ziggurat','''zɪɡəræt','''zɪgʊræt','[n] 古代亚述及巴比伦之金字形神塔(顶上有神殿)',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7845','shapeless','''ʃepləs','''ʃeɪplɪs','[adj] 不成形的, 无定形的','a shapeless dress  松松垮垮不成形的连衣裙'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7846','troupe','trʊp','truːp','[n] 剧团','...troupes of travelling actors.  …巡回演出的演员剧团。'),
