('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7880','rescue','''rɛskju','''reskjuː','[v] ／ n营救，救援','Survivors of the crash were rescued by helicopter.  空难的生还者被直升机救了出来。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7881','nearness','','','[n] 靠近, 接近','God is nearer to me than I am to myself; my existence depends on the nearness and the presence of God.  上帝比我更靠近我自己；我的存在取决于上帝的存在以及上帝离我有多近。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7882','pavlova','','','[n] 奶油水果蛋白饼',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7883','nourishment','''nɝɪʃmənt','''nʌrɪʃm(ə)nt','[n] 食物, 营养品','lack of proper nourishment  缺乏适当的营养'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7884','schoolroom','''skulrum','''skuːlruːm; -rʊm','[n] 教室','They seemed like so many little flags dotted about the schoolroom.  这些卡片就像无数面小旗点缀着教室。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7885','helpless','''hɛlpləs','''helplɪs','[adj] 无助的,没用的','He began to feel depressed and helpless.  他开始觉得沮丧、无助。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7886','grandparents','''græn''pɛrənts','''græn(d)peər(ə)nts','[n] 外祖父母, 祖父母','Tammy was raised by her grandparents.  塔米是由她的祖父母抚养大的。'),
