('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7953','trespass','''trɛspəs','''trespəs','[n&v] 侵犯，擅自进入','He will be prosecuted for trespass.  他将因擅闯私地而被起诉。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7954','darn','dɑrn','dɑːn','[v] 缝补，补缀','Her cardigan had been darned at the elbows.  她的羊毛衫肘部缝补过。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7955','irony','''aɪrəni','''aɪrənɪ','[n] 反话, 讽刺','Life is full of little ironies.  生活中充满了小小的讽刺。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7956','cheerless','''tʃɪrləs','''tʃɪəlɪs','[adj] 不快活的','This is a cold cheerless place.  这是个寒冷、阴郁的地方。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7957','sovereignty','''sɑvrənti','''sɒvrɪntɪ','[n] 君主, 主权','the sovereignty of Parliament  议会至高无上的权威'),
