('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7969','overhead',',ovɚ''hɛd','əʊvə''hed','[ad& a] 在头顶上(的)','The thunder crashed overhead.  头顶上雷声隆隆。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7970','embroidery','ɪm''brɔɪdəri','ɪm''brɒɪd(ə)rɪ; em-','[n] 刺绣(品)','The shorts had blue embroidery over the pockets.  这条短裤口袋上有蓝色的刺绣。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7971','hobby','''hɑbi','''hɒbɪ','[n] 业余爱好','What are your hobbies?  你有些什么爱好？'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7972','radish','''rædɪʃ','''rædɪʃ','[n] [植]萝卜','She carved a flower out of a radish.  她把萝卜刻成一朵花。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7973','ventilation',',vɛntl''eʃən',',ventɪ''leɪʃ(ə)n','[n] 通风, 流通空气','This would solve the problem of ventilation, for if a train entered this tunnel, it would draw in fresh air behind it.  这样就可以解决通风的问题，当火车进入隧道的时候，它就会带来一股新鲜的空气了。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7974','babble','''bæbl','''bæb(ə)l','[v] 说蠢话，牙牙学语','Similar to us, birds learn to sing by mimicking the adults, and the early chirps are akin to a baby''s babble.  和人类一样，鸟类通过模仿长者学习鸣叫，最开始鸣叫时类似于婴儿的牙牙学语。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7975','belle','bɛl','bel','[n] 美女',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7976','fragility','frə''dʒɪləti','frə''dʒɪlɪtɪ','[n] 脆弱, 虚弱','If he was ill, why didn''t anyone do something about his fragility?  假如他生病了，为什么没有任何人为他的脆弱做些什么？'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7977','innocence','''ɪnəsns','''ɪnəsəns','[n] 清白','Can you prove your innocence?  你能证明自己清白吗？'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7978','nonconformity',',nɑnkən''fɔrmɪti','nɒnkən''fɔːmɪtɪ','[n] 不信奉国教',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7979','cardinal','''kɑrdɪnl','''kɑːd(ɪ)n(ə)l','[adj] 主要的, 最重要的','Having clean hands is one of the cardinal rules when preparing food.  双手洁净是准备食物时的一项最基本要求。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7980','willingly','''wɪlɪŋli','''wɪlɪŋlɪ','[adv] 自动地, 欣然地',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7981','fervor','''fə:və','''fɜːvə','[n] 热情, 热烈','The non religious version, which reads strong excitement of feeling or something inspiring zeal or fervor.  从非宗教论来说是指强烈的兴奋感，或者是对某事的热情或激情。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7982','undergraduate',',ʌndɚ''ɡrædʒuət','ʌndə''grædjʊət','[n] (尚未取得学位的)大学生','second-year undergraduates  大学二年级学生'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7983','rosy','''rozi','''rəʊzɪ','[adj] 蔷薇色的, 玫瑰红色的','the kids’ rosy cheeks  孩子们红润的双颊'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7984','telecommuter','','','[n] 远程工作者','Remote Accelerator is aimed at single users, and has many features aimed at the telecommuter.  远程加速器定位于独立用户，针对远程工作人员提供了许多功能。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7985','seduce','sɪ''dʊs','sɪ''djuːs','[v] 勾引；引诱','The head lecturer was sacked for seducing female students.  这个首席讲师因诱奸女学生而被解雇。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7986','programmer','''progræmɚ','''prəʊgræmə','[n] 程序师, 程序规划员','This has served me well in my analyst/programmer jobs over the years.  这一点对我这些年的分析师/程序员工作很有帮助。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7987','paycheck','''pe,tʃɛk','''peɪtʃek','[n] 薪水支票, 工资',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7988','disillusion',',dɪsɪ''luʒn',',dɪsɪ''l(j)uːʒ(ə)n','[v] 醒悟','I hate to disillusion you, but I don’t think she’s coming back.  我真不愿意让你失望，但我想她是不会回来了。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7989','accountant','ə''kaʊntənt','ə''kaʊnt(ə)nt','[n] 会计(员), 会计师','The boss dropped an accountant from the payroll.  老板把一名会计师从在职人员名单中除了名。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7990','tranquil','ˈtræŋkwəl','''træŋkwɪl','[adj] 安静的','a small tranquil village  宁静的小村庄'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7991','solitude','''sɑlətud','''sɒlɪtjuːd','[n] 孤独','the solitude of her house on the lake  她湖边那所房子的清静'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7992','chary','ˈtʃeri','''tʃeərɪ','[adj] 小心的，审慎的','I am chary of making too many idiotic mistakes.  我小心谨慎以免犯太多的愚蠢错误。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7993','farmhand','''fɑrmhænd','''fɑːmhænd','[n] 农业工人，农场工人','She looks better than a farmhand really should.  她比一个实际的农场工人好看多了。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7994','tardiness','''tɑrdɪnɪs','''tɑːdɪnɪs','[n] 缓慢','Would tardiness or being too talkative affect your grades?  说得太慢或说得太多会不会影响你的分数？'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7995','harvester','''hɑrvɪstɚ','''hɑːvɪstə','[n] 收割机','Both of Oscar''s hind legs were accidentally chopped off in a combine harvester.   奥斯卡的两只后腿不小心被一台联合收割机截断。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7996','reliant','rɪ''laɪənt','rɪ''laɪənt','[adj] 信赖的, 依靠的','These people are not wholly reliant on Western charity.  这些人并非完全依赖西方的施舍。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7997','facet','''fæsɪt','''fæsɪt; -et','[n] 小平面, 方面, 刻面','The issues are complex and multi-faceted.  这些问题很复杂，涉及诸多方面。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7998','transpose','træn''spoz','træns''pəʊz; trɑːns-; -nz-','[v] 调换, 颠倒顺序','The director transposes the action from sixteenth-century France to post-Civil War America.  导演把情节从16世纪的法国转换到内战后的美国。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_7999','culturally','''kʌltʃərəli','''kʌltʃərəli','[adv] 人文地, 文化地','Teaching materials need to be culturally appropriate.  教材从文化角度来看必须恰当。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8000','iconographic','','','[adj] 肖像的, 图像材料的',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8001','earnestness','''ə:nistnis','''ə:nistnis','[n] 坚定, 认真','We would admire both his earnestness and his self-aware irony.  我们由衷地钦佩他的认真和有自知之明的讽刺艺术。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8002','folkloric','','','[adj] 民间传说的, 民俗的','T here are films as lovely, but none lovelier than "Cinema Paradiso, " a folkloric salute to the medium itself, flickering with yesterday''s innocence and lingering on the mind like bubbles in wine.  世 界上有如《天堂电影院》一般动人的影片，但绝无出其右，一部对媒体自身的民俗的礼赞，闪烁着往日的纯真无邪，如同葡萄酒中的泡泡那般萦绕心头挥之不去。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8003','vibrant','''vaɪbrənt','''vaɪbrənt','[adj] 震动的；明亮的','a painting full of vibrant reds and blues  满是鲜亮的红色和蓝色的画作'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8004','unfold','ʌn''fold','ʌn''fəʊld','[v] 展开,显露，展现','As the story unfolds, we learn more about Max’s childhood.  随着故事的展开，我们对马克斯的童年有了更多的了解。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8005','coherence','ko''hɪrəns','kə(ʊ)''hɪər(ə)ns; kə(ʊ)''hɪərəns','[n] 一致','An overall theme will help to give your essay coherence.  一个总的主题将有助于使文章连贯紧凑。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8006','reprieve','rɪ''priv','rɪ''priːv','[n& v] 缓刑，暂时解救','Fourteen people, waiting to be hanged for the murder of a former prime minister, have been reprieved.  因谋杀前总理而等受绞刑的十四个人获得缓刑。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8007','malfunction',',mæl''fʌŋkʃən','mæl''fʌŋ(k)ʃ(ə)n','[n] 故障','a malfunction in one of the engines  其中一个引擎的失灵'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8008','eloquent','''ɛləkwənt','''eləkwənt','[adj] 雄辩的, 有口才的','an eloquent appeal for support  极具说服力的求助呼吁'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8009','introspective','''ɪntrə''spɛktɪv','ɪntrə''spektɪv','[adj] 反省的','a shy and introspective person  一个腼腆自省的人'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8010','etching','''ɛtʃɪŋ','''etʃɪŋ','[n] 蚀刻版画','Mary is very keen on etching.  玛丽很喜爱蚀刻艺术。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8011','gouache','ɡu''ɑʃ','guː''ɑːʃ; gwɑːʃ','[n] 树胶水彩画','Her preferred medium is oil, but she also enjoys acrylic, gouache , and pen and wash.  她主要是画油画，但对丙烯，水粉画，钢笔和水彩画也很感兴趣。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8012','frisky','''friski','''frɪskɪ','[adj] 活泼的, 欢闹的','a frisky horse  一匹欢蹦乱跳的马'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8013','yelp','jɛlp','jelp','[n] 咆哮',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8014','barrelful','''bærəlfʊl','''bærəfʊl','[n] 一桶之量, 大量','Biotech pharmaceuticals require networked intelligence to manage living soups as they flow by the barrelful from one vat to the next.  生物技术制药也需要这种网络化的智慧来管理那些“活体基液”在大桶容器之间的流动。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8015','chorus','''kɔrəs','''kɔːrəs','[n] 合唱(队)','I sing with the university chorus.  我在大学合唱队里唱歌。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8016','unwell','ʌn''wɛl','ʌn''wel','[adj] 不舒服的','She had been feeling unwell.  她觉得不舒服。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8017','displacement','dɪs''plesmənt','dɪs''pleɪsm(ə)nt','[n] 移置, 转移, 取代','...the displacement of traditional agriculture by industrial crops.  …经济作物对传统农业的替代。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8018','chaotically','','','[adv] 浑沌地',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8019','bathe','beð','beɪð','[v] 沐浴; [n] 洗澡','The top of Pea Hill was bathed in brilliant sunshine.  豌豆山的山顶沐浴在灿烂的阳光中。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8020','fearsome','''fɪrsəm','''fɪəs(ə)m','[adj] 可怕的','a fearsome weapon  可怕的武器'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8021','scour','''skaʊɚ','''skaʊə','[v] 四处搜索；洗涤','Rescue crews had scoured an area of 30 square miles.  救援人员已经搜遍了30平方英里的范围。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8022','philology','fɪ''lɑlədʒi','fɪ''lɒlədʒɪ','[n] 语言学, 文献学','I don''t know the philology side, I don''t know what disables to metaphysical questions.  我不知道者从语言学上来说对不对，我也不懂从形而上学角度看,有什么问题。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8023','gentleman','''dʒɛntlmən','''dʒent(ə)lmən','[n] 阁下, 先生','Could you serve this gentleman please, Miss Bath?  巴思小姐，请你接待一下这位先生好吗？'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8024','unobservable','''ʌnəb''zə:vəbl','ʌnəb''zɜːvəb(ə)l','[adj] 不可见的','It basically means that you have a theory about the unobservable psychological states that are governing — or causing — other people''s behaviors.  这基本上意味着你能推测到，那些支配或引起他人行为的不可观察的心理状态。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8025','sluggishly','','','[adj] 缓慢的, 懒惰的','You may have noticed this when driving: those distant phone poles pass sluggishly while the ones on the road go zooming by.  你或许会在开车时有这种感觉：远处的电线杆移动的很慢，而路边的电线杆则移动的很快。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8026','balsam','''bɔlsəm','''bɔːlsəm; ''bɒl-','[n] 香液','Soon a dark wall of trees—red spruce, balsam fir, beech, hemlock—surrounds you, and there''s a sudden stony persistence.  很快你会被一堵厚厚的树墙包围——红云杉、香脂冷杉、山毛榉和铁杉，这会持续一段时间。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8027','weightily','''weitili','''weɪtɪlɪ','[adv] 沉重地, 重要地',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8028','zoology','zəu''ɔlədʒi, zu:-','zuː''ɒlədʒɪ; zəʊ-','[n] 动物学, 生态','The scholarship money she won helped her attend Cornell University, where she majored in zoology.  她赢得的奖学金帮助她上康奈尔大学，在那里他主修动物学。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8029','horseback','''hɔrsbæk','''hɔːsbæk','[n] 马背, 隆起的条状地带','In remote mountain areas, voters arrived on horseback.  在偏远山区，选民们是骑着马来的。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8030','replant','','','[v] 再植, 改种','she replanted the bulbs that the dog had dug up'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8031','nonessential',',nɔni''senʃəl',',nɒnɪ''senʃəl','[adj] 非本质的','The crisis has led to the closure of a number of nonessential government services.  这场危机已导致了一些可有可无政府服务设施的关闭。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8032','grammatical','grə''mætɪkl','grə''mætɪk(ə)l','[adj] 语法的,合乎文法的','grammatical rules  语法规则'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8033','sensational','sɛn''seʃənl','sen''seɪʃ(ə)n(ə)l','[adj] 轰动的, 耸人听闻的','a sensational discovery  引起轰动的发现'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8034','filmy','''fɪlmi','''fɪlmɪ','[adj] 薄膜的, 朦胧的','...filmy nightgowns.  ...薄薄的睡衣。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8035','pearly','''pɝli','''pɜːlɪ','[adj] 珍珠似的','pearly white teeth  珍珠般洁白的牙齿'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8036','arrest','ə''rɛst','ə''rest','[v] 逮捕, 拘留','He was arrested and charged with murder.  他遭到逮捕并被指控谋杀。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8037','nationally','','','[adv] 全国性地, 在全国范围内','a nationally recognised qualification  国家认可的资格'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8038','listless','''lɪstləs','''lɪs(t)lɪs','[adj] 倦怠的, 冷漠的','The heat was making me listless.  炎热的天气使我懒洋洋的。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8039','aloft','ə''lɔft','ə''lɒft','[adv] 在高处, 在上','But in the stratosphere they can stay aloft for years, spread by fast winds known as jets, meaning the threat is global.  但在平流层，它们可以在高处停留数年，高速的风对其进行传播，这意味着全球都受到了威胁。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8040','hacienda',',hæsɪ''ɛndə',',hæsɪ''endə; æ''θjendæ; æ''sjendæ','[n] 庄园','...an old colonial coffee hacienda in the Andes.  ...安第斯山脉中的一个殖民地时代的老咖啡种植园。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8041','vaguest','','','[adj] 含糊的，不明确的','Describe project deliverables in the vaguest possible terms so sponsors and reviewers have plenty of leeway to reinvent the project outputs repeatedly as the project unfolds.  用尽可能模糊的语言描述项目可交付成果，让发起人及审核者随着项目的开展，能有足够的空间不断地重新定义项目成果。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8042','furnishing','''fə:niʃiŋ','''fɜːnɪʃɪŋ','[n] 供给(装备)',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8043','oversight','''ovɚsaɪt','''əʊvəsaɪt','[n] 疏忽,  看管','I assure you that this was purely an oversight on my part.  我向你保证，这纯粹是我的一时疏忽。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8044','veteran','''vɛtərən','''vet(ə)r(ə)n','[n] 老兵,老手; [adj] 经验丰富的','a Vietnam veteran  越战老兵'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8045','stinger','''stɪŋɚ','''stɪŋə','[n] 刺激者, 讽刺者',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8046','inundate','''ɪnʌndet','''ɪnʌndeɪt','[v] 淹没','The tidal wave inundated vast areas of cropland.  海啸淹没了大片农田。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8047','dusty','''dʌsti','''dʌstɪ','[adj] 满是灰尘的, 粉状的','Adrian cycled along the dusty road.  阿德里安沿着满是尘土的路骑自行车。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8048','suffice','sə''faɪs','sə''faɪs','[v] 足够; [v] 使满足','A light lunch will suffice .  简单的午餐就够了。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8049','luster','''lʌstɚ','''lʌstə','[n] 光彩, 光泽','Then it’s really no more than a means of transportation, it too loses its luster.  然后它就仅仅是一个名符其实的交通工具，失去了它的光彩。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8050','housewares','''haʊswɛrz','''haʊsweəz','[n] 家用器皿','The houses were left in haste and all the things were abandoned. It is so strange to see pieces of furniture, housewares and numerous photos with no people around.  匆忙中人们抛下了房子，任何东西都不可以带走。在空无一人的地方看着这些家具、生活用品和照片，感觉是如此诡异。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8051','drainpipe','''drenpaɪp','''dreɪnpaɪp','[n] 排水管','He evaded police by climbing through a window and shinning down a drainpipe.  他翻窗从排水管爬下，从而躲过了警察。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8052','trash','træʃ','træʃ','[n] 垃圾, 废物','Will someone take out the trash (= take it outside the house ) ?  谁把垃圾拿出去好吗？'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8053','clayware','','','[n] 黏土制品',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8054','weedy','''widi','''wiːdɪ','[adj] 杂草多的','We pulled into the weedy parking lot.  我们开进了杂草丛生的停车场。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8055','mermaid','''mɝmed','''mɜːmeɪd','[n] 美人鱼','But the little mermaid had no occasion to do this, for the polypi sprang back in terror when they caught sight of the glittering draught, which shone in her hand like a twinkling star.  可是小人鱼没有这样做的必要，固为当珊瑚虫一看到这亮晶晶的药水——它在她的手里亮得像一颗闪耀的星星——的时候，它们就在她面前惶恐地缩回去了。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8056','hart','hɑrt','hɑːt','[n] 雄赤鹿',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8057','chant','tʃænt','tʃɑːnt','[n] 圣歌','...a Gregorian chant.  …一首格列高利圣歌。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8058','plaza','''plæzə','''plɑːzə','[n] 广场，集市','Across the busy plaza, vendors sell hot dogs and croissant sandwiches.  忙碌的露天广场对面，小贩们在卖热狗和新月形面包三明治。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8059','slay','sle','sleɪ','[v] 杀死，宰杀','...the hill where St. George slew the dragon.  …圣乔治屠龙之丘。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8060','falsely','','','[adj] 虚伪地,  错误地','She apologized for accusing him falsely.  她为错误地咒骂他而道歉。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8061','emergent','ɪ''mɝdʒənt','ɪ''mɜːdʒ(ə)nt','[adj] 紧急的','Discovering these patterns is the key to emergent design.  发现这些模式是紧急设计的关键。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8062','landownership','','','[n] 土地所有','This may be partly for fear of making a near-reality of private landownership, which would undermine one of the last vestiges of the party’s communist heritage.  这要部分归结于中共害怕在实际上造成土地私有制之嫌，因为这样会摧毁其共产主义的最后一道防线。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8063','metaphysical',',mɛtə''fɪzɪkl','metə''fɪzɪk(ə)l','[adj] 形而上学的, 纯粹哲学的','A lot of scientists don’t like discussing metaphysical matters.  很多科学家不喜欢讨论形而上学的东西。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8064','feeble','''fibl','''fiːb(ə)l','[adj] 虚弱的, 衰弱的','His voice sounded feeble and far away.  他的声音听上去既无力又遥远。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8065','joyous','''dʒɔɪəs','''dʒɒɪəs','[adj] 快乐的, 高兴的','a joyous occasion  欢乐的场合'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8066','forceful','''fɔrsfl','''fɔːsfʊl; -f(ə)l','[adj] 有力的, 强烈的','a forceful attack on government policy  对政府政策的有力抨击'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8067','reluctance','rɪ''lʌktəns','rɪ''lʌkt(ə)ns','[n] 不愿, 勉强','Wells finally agreed, but with reluctance.  韦尔斯最终同意了，但很勉强。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8068','engagement','ɪn''ɡedʒmənt','ɪn''geɪdʒm(ə)nt; en-','[n] 约会, 婚约','Their engagement was announced in the paper.  他们订婚的消息在报上公布了。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8069','swear','swɛr','sweə','[v] 宣誓, 发誓','I never touched your purse, I swear!  我绝对没有碰过你的钱包，我发誓！'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8070','lover','''lʌvɚ','''lʌvə','[n] 爱人, 爱好者','He killed his wife’s lover.  他杀了妻子的情人。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8071','epithet','''ɛpɪθɛt','''epɪθet','[n] 绰号, 称号','But it is impossible to predict the reaction of a man accosted by another with the words "you rat" without referring to the meaning that the man spoken to attaches to the epithet.  但是，当你不带意识地，说出别人的绰号“老鼠”的时候，你还是无法预测这个人会有怎样的反应。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8072','collapsible','kə''læpsəbl','kə''læpsəbl','[adj] 可折叠的;可拆卸的','a collapsible chair  折叠式椅子'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8073','scruffy','''skrʌfi','''skrʌfɪ','[adj] 肮脏的，不洁的','a scruffy old pair of jeans  一条不干净的旧牛仔裤'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8074','derisive','dɪ''raɪsɪv','dɪ''raɪsɪv; -z-','[adj] 嘲笑的','derisive laughter  嘲讽的笑'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8075','messy','''mɛsi','''mesɪ','[adj] 肮脏的, 凌乱的','a messy room  凌乱的房间'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8076','misery','''mɪzəri','''mɪz(ə)rɪ','[n] 痛苦, 苦恼','What we are witnessing here is human misery on a vast scale.  我们在这里所目睹的情景是许许多多的人都生活困苦。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8077','fragmentary','''frægmən''tɛri','''frægm(ə)nt(ə)rɪ','[adj] 由碎片组成的','a fragmentary account  零星的叙述'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8078','oxidizable','','','[adj] 可氧化的','Description: Metal lumps or ingots, silver grey with metallic lustre , easily oxidizable in air.  说明：金属锭或块，银灰色，有金属光泽，在空气中易氧化。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8079','difluoride','','','[n] 二氟化物','It reacts violently with oxygen difluoride and barium peroxide .  一氧化碳同氟化氧、氧化钡会发生剧烈反应。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8080','zirconium','zɚ''konɪəm','zɜː''kəʊnɪəm','[n] 锆','It has zirconium/hydrogen reaction rate and where it occurred, obviously about the same place. The percentage reaction.  它有锆或氢的反应速率,它发生的位置，很明显是在同样位置,百分比反应。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8081','publicity','pʌb''lɪsəti','pʌb''lɪsɪtɪ','[n] 公开','The case has generated enormous publicity in Brazil.  这起犯罪事件已在巴西引起了公众的极大关注。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8082','relict','''rɛlɪkt','''relɪkt','[n] 残遗物',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8083','effortlessly','''efətlisli','''efətlisli','[adv] 毫不费力地, 轻易地',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8084','defensible','dɪ''fɛnsəbl','dɪ''fensɪb(ə)l','[adj] 可防御的',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8085','idealistic','ai,diə''listik,-kəl',',aɪdɪə''lɪstɪk; aɪ,dɪə''lɪstɪk; aɪ,diːə''lɪstɪk','[adj] 理想主义的, 空想的','idealistic young doctors  充满理想主义的年轻医生'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8086','blister','''blɪstɚ','''blɪstə','[n] 水泡','New shoes always give me blisters.  我穿新鞋脚上总是起泡。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8087','statuette',',stʃʊjʊ''ɛt','stætjʊ''et; -tʃʊ-','[n] 小雕像','The Prize consists of a statuette - “the Nkosi” - and 100,000 euros, which are to be awarded to a direct aid project in the spirit of the young winner’s efforts.  奖品是一座价值100，000欧元的“恩科西”小雕像，该奖旨在嘉奖年轻获奖者在直接参与帮助事件上所付出的精神努力。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8088','featureless','''fitʃɚləs','','[adj] 无特色的, 平凡的','featureless plains  毫无特色的平原'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8089','creed','krid','kriːd','[n] 信条','It has never been weaker as a political creed .  作为一种政治信条，它从来没有像现在这样衰微过。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8090','scraggly','''skræɡli','''skræɡlɪ','[adj] 零乱的, 锯齿状的','his scraggly gray beard  他那散乱的灰白胡子'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8091','zeal','zil','ziːl','[n] 热心, 热情','...his zeal for teaching.  …他对教学的热衷。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8092','slapdash','''slæpdæʃ','''slæpdæʃ','[adj] 匆促的','a very slapdash piece of work  干得非常马虎的工作'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8093','badge','bædʒ','bædʒ','[n] 徽章, 证章','We were each handed a badge with our name on it.  我们每个人都拿到一个徽章，上面有我们的名字。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8094','shrubby','''ʃrʌbi','''ʃrʌbɪ','[adj] 灌木的','...a shrubby tree.  ...一棵灌木状的树木。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8095','brutal','''brutl','''bruːt(ə)l','[adj] 残忍的, 兽性的','a brutal man  一个凶残的男人'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8096','impinge','ɪm''pɪndʒ','ɪm''pɪn(d)ʒ','[v] 撞击','...the cuts in defence spending that have impinged on two of the region''s largest employers.  ...已经对该地区两个最大雇主产生重大影响的防御开支消减。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8097','scrubbiness','','','[adj] 褴褛的,灌木丛生的',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8098','flavin','''flævɪn','''fleɪvɪn','[n] [化]黄素, 四羟酮醇',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8099','mountainside','''maʊntənsaɪd','''maʊntɪnsaɪd','[n] 山腹, 山腰','Great rocks rolled down the mountainside.  巨大的岩石顺着山坡滚落下来。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8100','sunbaked','''sʌnbeikt','''sʌnbeɪkt','[adj] 晒干的','Even if the air stays bitterly cold, these sunbaked rocks can warm enough to melt whatever tiny patches of snow have escaped the thirsty wind.  即使空气十分寒冷，这些裸晒的岩石仍然能有足够的热量去融化那些在饥渴的风里逃过一劫的小雪块。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8101','testimony','''tɛstə''moni','''testɪmənɪ','[n] 证词, 宣言','Barker’s testimony is crucial to the prosecution’s case.  巴克的证词对控方的指控起到了关键作用。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8102','alumina','ə''lumɪnə','ə''luːmɪnə','[n] [化]氧化铝(亦称矾土)','Methods outlined in the monograph include: use of crushed clay pots, bone charcoal, contact precipitation, or use of activated alumina (absorptive filter).  专著中概述的方法包括：使用粗砂壶、骨炭、接触沉淀，或使用活性氧化铝（吸收型过滤器）。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8103','hairlike','','','[adj] 毛一般的, 细微的','In this depiction of the rod-shaped E. coli, two flagella trail from one end while hairlike pili surround a capsule full of tangled nucleoids.  在创作这个杆状的大肠杆菌时，其表现出的形式为一端甩出两条鞭毛，同时细微的菌毛围绕在布满凌乱菌核的荚膜上。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8104','coating','''kotɪŋ','''kəʊtɪŋ','[n] 被覆, 衣料',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8105','wee','wi','wiː','[adj] 很少的, 微小的','My wee boy is three.  我的小儿子三岁。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8106','watertight','''wɔtɚtaɪt','''wɔːtətaɪt','[adj] 不漏水的, 无懈可击的','Lucky for him, his alibi is watertight.  算他走运，不在犯罪现场的证据无懈可击。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8107','rationalism','''ræʃnə''lɪzəm','''ræʃ(ə)n(ə)lɪz(ə)m','[n] 理性主义, 唯理论','philosophers who accept scientific rationalism  接受科学唯理论的哲学家们'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8108','willful','''wɪlfəl','''wɪlfʊl','[adj] 任性的, 故意的','There is a willful self-destructiveness in the air here as if America has all the time and money in the world for petty politics.  这里的空气里中弥漫着一种故意自我毁灭的气息，为了狭隘的政治，美国好像在全世界有的是金钱和时间。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8109','worthiness','','','[n] 价值,值得','So we must ask what lends objective worthiness to a life outside the moral realm.  所以在道德范畴之外，我们必须设问，是什么东西带给人生客观性的值得。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8110','moralistic',',mɔrə''lɪstɪk','mɒrə''lɪstɪk','[adj] 狭隘道德观的, 说教的','It’s difficult to talk to teenagers about drugs without sounding too moralistic.  跟青少年谈论毒品，又不能有太重的说教味道，这是很难的。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8111','conscientious','''kɑnʃɪ''ɛnʃəs',',kɒnʃɪ''enʃəs','[adj] 认真的，勤勤恳恳的','A conscientious teacher may feel inclined to take work home.  一个认真负责的教师可能会想着把工作带回家去做。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8112','syntax','''sɪntæks','''sɪntæks','[n] 语法, 句法','His grammar and syntax, both in oral and written expression, were much better than the average.  无论在口头还是笔头上，他的语法和句法都非常出众。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8113','nonsense','''nɑnsɛns','''nɒns(ə)ns','[n] 胡说, 废话','‘I’m a prisoner in my own home.’ ‘Nonsense!’  “我在自己家里就像个囚犯。”“胡说！”'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8114','loudness','','','[n] 大声, 喧闹',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8115','terminate','''tɝmɪnet','''tɜːmɪneɪt','[v] 停止, 终止','The court ruled that the contract must be terminated.  法庭裁决该合同必须终止。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8116','playful','''plefl','''pleɪfʊl; -f(ə)l','[adj] 爱玩耍的；幽默的','a playful little dog  活泼的小狗'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8117','discontinuity',',dɪs,kɑntə''nuəti','dɪs,kɒntɪ''njuːɪtɪ','[n] 不连续, 中断','discontinuity in economic development  经济发展的间断性'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8118','prosaic','prə''zeɪk','prə(ʊ)''zeɪɪk','[adj] 单调乏味的,平淡的','a prosaic writing style  乏味的写作风格'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8119','discrimination','dɪ,skrɪmɪ''neʃən','dɪ,skrɪmɪ''neɪʃ(ə)n','[n] 歧视；辨别力','laws to prevent discrimination  防止歧视的法律'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8120','vowel','''vaʊəl','''vaʊəl','[n&a] 元音(的)','But he could say vowel clearly and began to learn vocabulary.  但是他已经能清楚地说元音并开始学习词汇。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8121','dew','du','''djuː','[n] 露水','The dew gathered on the leaves.  露水在叶片上聚集。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8122','shroud','ʃraʊd','ʃraʊd','[n] 裹尸布, 寿衣; [v] 用裹尸布裹, 遮蔽','...the burial shroud.  …下葬裹尸布。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8123','fearless','''fɪrləs','''fɪəlɪs','[adj] 不怕的，无畏的','These dogs are absolutely fearless.  这些狗什么都不怕。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8124','doom','dʊm','duːm','[v] 注定，命定 n厄运','The plan was doomed from the start .  这个计划一开始就注定要失败。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8125','install','ɪn''stɔl','ɪnˈstɔ:l','[v] 安装, 安置','They’ve installed the new computer network at last.  他们终于安装了新电脑网络。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8126','landholder','''lænd,həuldə','''lændhəʊldə','[n] 地主, 土地拥有者','Land was seemingly limitless in extend and, therefore, not highly priced, and almost every colonist wanted to be a landholder.  土地似乎广阔无垠，因此价钱不高，而几乎所有的殖民地人都想成为土地拥有者。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8127','emergency','ɪ''mɝdʒənsi','ɪ''mɜːdʒ(ə)nsɪ','[n] 紧急情况, 突然事件','Lifeguards are trained to deal with emergencies.  救生员接受过应对紧急情况的训练。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8128','workable','''wɝkəbl','''wɜːkəb(ə)l','[adj] 可经营的, 可使用的','a workable solution to the problem  解决这一问题的可行方法'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8129','moralism','','''mɒr(ə)lɪz(ə)m','[n] 道德主义, 说教','His moralism is all-encompassing and as passionate as can be. He plans to replace state welfare provision with faith-based charitable organisations that would impose Christian family values.  他的道德说教可谓包罗万象,激情澎湃.他计划创建以信仰为基础的慈善机构来代替国家福利事业,以滋养基督家庭的社会价值观.'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8130','dune','dʊn','djuːn','[n] 沙丘','Large dunes make access to the beach difficult in places.  在有些地方大沙丘使得靠近海滩很难。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8131','monarchy','''mɑnɚki','''mɒnəkɪ','[n] 君主政体, 君主国','the abolition of the monarchy  君主制的废除'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8132','nationalism','''næʃnəlɪzəm','''næʃ(ə)n(ə)lɪz(ə)m','[n] 民族主义, 国家主义','Scottish national­ism  苏格兰民族主义'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8133','flowerpot','','''flaʊəpɒt','[n] 花盆, 花钵','Do you want me to eat dirt from a flowerpot?  你想让我把花盆里的土都吃了还是咋地？'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8134','resale','''risel','riː''seɪl','[n] 再贩卖, 转售','...a well-maintained used car with a good resale value.  …一部维护良好的、可以转卖个好价钱的旧车。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8135','dubious','''dubɪəs','''djuːbɪəs','[adj] 可疑的, 不确定的','The firm was accused of dubious accounting practices.  该公司被指控有不诚实的会计行为。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8136','centralization','','','[n] 集中, 中央集权化',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8137','profusion','prəˈfjuʒən','prə''fjuːʒ(ə)n','[n] 丰富','...a delightful river with a profusion of wild flowers along its banks.  ...一条令人愉悦的河，岸上开满了野花。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8138','seacoast','''si,kost','''si:,kəust','[n] 海滨','Armenia lacks a seacoast or a port.  亚美尼亚没有海岸和港口。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8139','lush','lʌʃ','lʌʃ','[adj] 茂盛的, 丰富的','a lush green mountainous island  草木茂盛苍翠、山峦起伏的岛'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8140','champagne','ʃæm''pen','ʃæm''peɪn','[n] 香槟酒','I drank a cup of champagne.  我喝了一杯香槟。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8141','pesky','''pɛski','''peskɪ','[adj] 讨厌的，烦人的','Those pesky kids!  那些讨厌的孩子！'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8142','sorrowful','''sɑrofl','''sɒrə(ʊ)fʊl; -f(ə)l','[adj] 悲伤的，使人伤心的','a sorrowful expression  悲伤的表情'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8143','overtone','''ovɚ''ton','''əʊvətəʊn','[n] 寓意；眩外音；暗示','The strike has taken on overtones of a civil rights campaign.  这次罢工带有民权运动的意味。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8144','towel','''taʊəl','''taʊəl','[n] 毛巾','Have you got a clean towel I could use?  你有没有干净毛巾给我用？'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8145','purposefully','''pə:pəsfuli','''pə:pəsfuli','[adv] 有目的地, 蓄意地','They purposefully keep people misinformed and fearful through their control of the media.  他们有目的地通过所控制的媒体来误导和恐吓民众。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8146','dislodge','dɪs''lɑdʒ','dɪs''lɒdʒ','[v] 驱逐','the revolution that failed to dislodge the British in 1919  未能推翻英国统治的1919年革命'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8147','lint','lɪnt','lɪnt','[n] 绷带用麻布',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8148','shortness','','','[n] 短缺','He never had a heart attack, but that surgery was similarly prompted by complaints about chest pain and shortness of breath.  他没有心脏病发作过，但是这个手术也同样被提示关于胸痛和气短的疾病。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8149','softness','''sɔftnɪs','','[n] 柔和, 温柔','She cannot accuse me of showing a bit of deceitful softness.  她不能控诉我说我表示过一点虚伪的温柔。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8150','domestically','də''mɛstɪkli','də''mestikəli','[adv] 家庭式地,国内地',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8151','behaviorist','','','[n] 行为主义者, 行为科学家','And from a behaviorist point of view this is because of the associative history of these things.  在行为主义者看来,这是在这些事物之间的联结历史造成的。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8152','foil','fɔɪl','fɔɪl','[n] 箔, 金属薄片','chocolates in foil wrappers  箔纸包的巧克力'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8153','newsworthy','''nuzwɝði','''njuːzwɜːðɪ','[adj] 有报导价值的','newsworthy events  值得报道的事件'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8154','imminent','''ɪmɪnənt','''ɪmɪnənt','[adj] 逼近的, 即将发生的','A new trade agreement is imminent.  一项新的贸易协定即将签署。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8155','proficiently','','','[adv] 熟练地','Pick a partner and practice passing, for if you pass proficiently, perhaps you''ll play professionally.  选择一位队员练习传球，如果你能熟练地传球，你或许会成为一位专业球员。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8156','locomotor','''lokə''motɚ','ləʊkə(ʊ)''məʊtə','[adj] 运动的','“This form of behavior — independence, locomotor capacity, parental care and development — could be similar to the life history of the theropod,” he said.  “这种行为形式，不管是独立性、运动能力，还是亲代抚育和发育过程，都与兽脚类恐龙的生活史相似，”他说。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8157','cloudy','''klaʊdi','''klaʊdɪ','[adj] 多云的, 阴天的','a cloudy night with some light rain  伴有些许小雨的多云的夜晚'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8158','wirephoto','','','[n] 有线传真',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8159','attractively','','','[adv] 有吸引力地，诱人地','In terms of valuation, the run of strong earnings combined with declining stock prices translate into some attractively priced stocks.  在估值方面，强劲的盈利走势加上下跌的股价，其结果就是价格具有吸引力的股票。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8160','snowy','''snoɪ','''snəʊɪ','[adj] 雪的, 多雪的','the snowy fields  被雪覆盖的田野'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8161','inaugurate','ɪ''nɔɡjəret','ɪ''nɔːgjʊreɪt','[v] 开始；举行就职典礼','The Turner Prize was inaugurated in 1984.  特纳奖于1984年正式设立。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8162','kit','','kɪt','[n] 成套工具, 用具包','Sally keeps her make-up kit in her bag.  萨莉把化妆包放在手提包里。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8163','comminute','''kɒməˌnjuːt','''kɒmɪnjuːt','[v] 使成粉末,粉碎',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8164','indebted','ɪn''dɛtɪd','ɪn''detɪd','[adj] 受惠的, 负债的','the 17 most heavily indebted nations  17个负债最重的国家'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8165','cache','kæʃ','kæʃ','[v] 贮藏，隐藏  n藏物处',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8166','germination',',dʒɝmə''neʃən','','[n] 萌芽, 发生','In this way, postmodernism might be seen as the delayed germination of an older seed, planted by artists like Marcel Duchamp, during modernism’s high noon of the 1920s and 1930s.  按这种理解，后现代主义可被看成一粒过往的种子延迟了的萌芽，这粒种子由马塞尔•杜尚等艺术家种在20世纪二三十年代现代主义的繁盛时期。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8167','unseen',',ʌn''sin','ʌn''siːn','[adj] 未见过的','Raj crept out of the house unseen.  拉杰悄悄地溜出了房子。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8168','guest','ɡɛst','gest','[n] 客人, 来宾','a banquet for 250 distinguished guests  250位贵宾出席的宴会'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8169','cognition','kɑɡ''nɪʃən','kɒg''nɪʃ(ə)n','[n] 认识','the regions of the brain that are responsible for memory and cognition  大脑主管记忆与认知的区域'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8170','forelimb','''fɔ:lim','''fɔːlɪm','[n] 前肢','The doctor said the problem lied in its forelimb and it would not die.  医生说问题在于它的前肢上，不过它不会死的。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8171','limy','''laɪmi','''laimi','[adj] 含石灰的, 石灰似的','Ultimately, the concretion mechanism of limy composite concretion earth is made certain by way of performance contrast among different specimens.  通过不同试件的性能对比，确定石灰类复合团结土的团结机理。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8172','lithographic',',lɪθə''græfɪk','','[adj] 石版印刷的, 石版的',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8173','lagoon','lə''gʊn','lə''guːn','[n] 泻湖 礁湖','a coastal lagoon  沿海潟湖'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8174','numeral','''numərəl','''njuːm(ə)r(ə)l','[n] 数字','...a flat, square wristwatch with classic Roman numerals.  ...一块扁平、有标准罗马数字的正方形手表。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8175','eloquently','''ɛləkwəntli','''eləkwəntli','[adv] 雄辩地, 有口才地',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8176','extravagantly','ɪk''strævəgəntli','ik''strævəgəntli','[adv] 挥霍无度地',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8177','crest','krɛst','krest','[n] 浪尖, 冠','exotic birds with colourful crests  羽冠鲜艳多彩的珍禽'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8178','centrality','sɛn''træləti','sen''trælətɪ','[n] 中心, 中央','Our bodies have no centrality either.  我们的身体也没有中心。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8179','insatiable','ɪn''seʃəbl','ɪn''seɪʃəb(ə)l','[adj] 不知足的, 贪求无厌的','A section of the reading public has an insatiable appetite for dirty stories about the famous.  阅读大众中有一部分人对名人的风流韵事的欲望总是无法满足。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8180','prospective','prə''spɛktɪv','prə''spektɪv','[adj] 预期的','The story should act as a warning to other prospective buyers.  这篇报道应该可以对其他可能的购买者起到警告作用。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8181','bewilder','bɪ''wɪldɚ','bɪ''wɪldə','[v] 使迷惑，使难住','He was bewildered by his daughter’s reaction.  他被女儿的反应弄糊涂了。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8182','obstruction','əb''strʌkʃən, ɔb-','əb''strʌkʃ(ə)n','[n] 阻塞, 妨碍','an operation to remove an obstruction from her throat  去除她喉咙里阻塞物的手术'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8183','procure','prə''kjʊr','prə''kjʊə','[v] 获得, 取得','It remained very difficult to procure food, fuel, and other daily necessities.  当时仍然很难获得食品、燃料和其他日用必需品。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8184','subsidiary','səb''sɪdɪɛri','səb''sɪdɪərɪ','[adj] 辅助的, 补充的','The marketing department has always played a subsidiary role to the sales department.  营销部一直都扮演着销售部的辅助角色。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8185','putrefaction','ˌpjutrəˈfækʃən',',pjuːtrɪ''fækʃ(ə)n','[n] 腐败, 腐败物','The time consuming process for making processed meats creates high bacteria counts and putrefaction in the meat which need to be treated with chemicals.  在加工面粉的时会产生大量细菌，还有腐败的肉制品需要用化学物品来处理。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8186','pasteurization',',pæstərə''zeʃən',',pæstəraɪ''zeɪʃən','[n] 加热杀菌法, 巴斯德杀菌法',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8187','summertime','''sʌmɚtaɪm','''sʌmətaɪm','[n] 夏季','It''s a very beautiful place in the summertime.  这里夏季时很美。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8188','meltdown','''mɛltdaʊn','''meltdaʊn','[n] 彻底垮台',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8189','chlorate','''klorɪt','''klɔːreɪt','[n] [化]氯酸盐','Electricity is the main material for chlorate production.  电是生产氯酸盐的主要原料。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8190','intersection',',ɪntɚ''sɛkʃən','ɪntə''sekʃ(ə)n','[n] 交集, 交叉点','We crossed at a busy intersection.  我们穿过了一个繁忙的道路交叉口。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8191','stepper','''stɛpɚ','''stepə','[n] 行走的人或动物, 跳舞者',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8192','supposition',',sʌpə''zɪʃən',',sʌpə''zɪʃ(ə)n','[n] 假定, 想象','His version of events is pure supposition .  他对事情的说法纯属推测。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8193','smoothness','''smʊðnɪs','','[n] 平坦， 光滑','Feel the cold, glass-like smoothness and the crevices and lines that make me what I am.  感觉玻璃般的冰冷与光滑，以及其中的裂缝和刮痕，感受我的存在。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8194','vertically','''vɝtɪkli','''və:tikəli','[adv] 垂直地','Well, we cut it into vertically simple pieces.  我们把它分割为垂直简单的部分。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8195','dichotomy','daɪ''kɑtəmi','daɪ''kɒtəmɪ; dɪ-','[n] 两分, 二分法','There is a natural dichotomy between the two sides of one’s personality that is usually displayed between the different types of social groups with which an individual may identify oneself.  在一个人性格的这两方面之间，存在着一种自然的两分法。 个人的性格一般就体现在这一个人所可能认同的不同社会群体之间。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8196','clipper','''klɪpɚ','''klɪpə','[n] 大剪刀, 快速帆船修剪者','nail clippers  指甲剪'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8197','fruitful','''frutfl','''fruːtfʊl; -f(ə)l','[adj] 果实结得多的, 多产的',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8198','flag','flæg','flæg','[n] 旗，旗帜','Children waving flags greeted the Russian leader.  孩子们挥舞着旗帜，欢迎俄罗斯领导人。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8199','acoustical','ə''kʊstɪkl','ə''kuːstɪkəl','[adj] 听觉的, 声学的','The ancient Greeks were aware of other acoustical principles, at least empirically.  至少在实践上，古希腊人也知道其他的声学原理。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8200','kitchenware','''kɪtʃɪnwɛr','''kɪtʃɪnweə; ''kɪtʃ(ə)n-','[n] 厨房用具','She has a huge amount of Victorian kitchenware.  她拥有维多利亚时代的大量厨房用具。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8201','intimidate','ɪn''tɪmɪdet','ɪn''tɪmɪdeɪt','[v] 胁迫','Attempts to intimidate her failed.  恐吓她的企图失败了。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8202','serviceable','''sɝvɪsəbl','''sɜːvɪsəb(ə)l','[adj] 有用地，耐用的','Some of these old tools are still serviceable.  这些旧工具有些仍可使用。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8203','chalky','''tʃɔki','''tʃɔːkɪ','[adj] 白垩的','white chalky soil  白色的白垩质土壤'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8204','Yorkshire','''jɔrkʃɚ','''jɔrkʃə','[n] 约克郡,约克夏(英国英格兰原郡名)','WL: I think, Yorkshire and the New Forest.  我想，是约克郡和新森林地区。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8205','royalty','''rɔɪəlti','''rɒɪəltɪ','[n] 皇室, 王权','At school the other children treated them like royalty .  在学校里，其他孩子将他们奉若王族。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8206','renowned','ri''naund','rɪ''naʊnd','[adj] 有名的, 有声誉的','The area is renowned for its Romanesque churches.  这个地区以其罗马式教堂闻名。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8207','worthy','wɜði','ˈwəːði','[adj] 值得的,有价值的','Leeds United were worthy winners of the competition.  利兹联队是比赛当之无愧的获胜者。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8208','kinfolk','''kinfəuk,-fəuks','''kɪnfəʊk','[n] 亲属','I sent my other son to the country to stay with kinfolk.  我把另一个儿子送到乡下和亲戚住在一起。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8209','prompt','prɑmpt','prɒm(p)t','[v] 推动；提示','‘I can’t decide,’ said Beatrice. ‘Decide what?’ prompted Marlon.  “我决定不了。”比阿特丽斯说。“决定什么？”马龙追问道。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8210','nonliving','nɒn''lɪvɪŋ','nɒn''lɪvɪŋ','[adj] 无生命的, 非活体的','In 1860 Louis Pasteur performed experiments that eventually disproved “spontaneous generation, ” the idea that life continually arose from nonliving things.  1860年，路易斯巴斯德做了个实验，最终反驳了“自然发生说”，这一说认为生命源源不断于无生命的物体。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8211','impervious','ɪm''pɝvɪəs','ɪm''pɜːvɪəs','[adj] 不透的；不受影响的','impervious volcanic rock  不透水的火山岩'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8212','deceptive','dɪ''sɛptɪv','dɪ''septɪv','[adj] 骗人的，造成假象的','Some snakes move with deceptive speed (= move faster than you think or expect ) .  有些蛇的爬行速度出乎意料地快。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8213','wok','wɑk','wɒk','[n] 锅，炒菜锅','Then Ky-Phuong Luong, the T.A., stirred a wok full of vegetables and soy-marinated crickets, and Dunkel passed a plate of fritters with yellowish wax worms protruding from their centers.  然后名叫罗芳婉的班主任老师炒了锅菜满是蔬菜和过了酱的蟋蟀，接着邓克尔端上一盘油炸面团，内馅儿是蜡蠕虫，一些淡黄的的蠕虫凸出面团。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8214','appraisal','ə''prezl','ə''preɪz(ə)l','[n] 估计, 评估','What is needed in such cases is a calm appraisal of the situation.  在此类情况下需要的是对形势的冷静估计。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8215','lone','lon','ləʊn','[adj] 孤独的，寂寞的','A lone figure was standing at the bus stop.  公交车站上站着一个孤单的身影。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8216','dissenter','di''sentə','dɪ''sentə','[n] 持异议者','Political dissenters were imprisoned.  持不同政见者遭到监禁。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8217','enure','ɪn''jʊr','ɪ''njʊə; ɪ''njɔː','[v] 使习惯于; [v] 变得更有利',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8218','conformity','kən''fɔrməti','kən''fɔːmɪtɪ','[n] 一致, 符合','We must act in conformity with local regulations.  我们必须按当地的法规行事。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8219','unanimity','ˌjunəˈnɪmətɪ','ˌju:nəˈnɪmətɪ','[n] 全体一致','All decisions would require unanimity.  所有决定都需要全体一致同意。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8220','pedagogical','pedə''gɔdʒikəl',',pedə''gɒdʒɪkl','[adj] 教学(法)的','The school district provides training to help teachers improve their pedagogical methods.  该学区提供培训以帮助教师们改进教学方法。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8221','hopper','''hɑpɚ','''hɒpə','[n] 单足跳者',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8222','affirm','ə''fɝm','ə''fɜːm','[v] 断言, 确认','The general affirmed rumors of an attack.  将军证实了袭击的传闻。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8223','scientifically','saɪən''tɪfɪkli','saiən''tifikli','[adv] 科学地, 系统地','He explained scientifically the most important questions of political economy.  他科学地阐述了政治经济学中一些最重要的问题。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8224','modus','','','[n] 方法, 形式','The problem is, I do not have any technique, process, or modus operandi.  问题是，我不知道任何技巧、步骤或操作方式。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8225','laborsaving','','','[adj] 节省劳力的;省力气的','The way to make self-sufficiency work on a small scale is to resist the temptation to buy a tractor and other expensive laborsaving devices.  小范围里实现自给自足的途径是抵制诱惑，不去购置拖拉机和其他昂贵的节省劳力的机械。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8226','spontaneity',',spɑntə''neəti',',spɒntə''neɪɪtɪ','[n] 自发性','He had the spontaneity of a child.  他有孩子般的自然举动。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8227','respectable','rɪ''spɛktəbl','rɪ''spektəb(ə)l','[adj] 可敬的；有身价的','...investments that offer respectable and highly attractive rates of return.  …提供不错的、极具吸引力的回报率的投资。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8228','paperback','''pepɚbæk','''peɪpəbæk','[n] 平装本, 纸面本','She said she would buy the book when it comes out in paperback.  她说等那本书的平装本面市后她会买一本。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8229','strap','stræp','stræp','[n] 带, 皮带; [v] 用带捆扎','a bra strap  胸罩肩带'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8230','topical','''tɑpɪkl','''tɒpɪk(ə)l','[adj] 有关时事的','The newscast covers topical events and entertainment.  该新闻广播涉及时事和娱乐。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8231','exclaim','ɪk''sklem','ɪk''skleɪm; ek-','[v] 呼喊, 惊叫','‘No!’ she exclaimed in shock.  “不！”她惊呼道。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8232','ratchet','''rætʃɪt','''rætʃɪt','[n] 棘轮, 棘齿','The chair has a ratchet below it to adjust the height.  这把椅子下面有一个棘轮来调整高度。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8233','humiliate','hju''mɪlɪet','hjʊ''mɪlɪeɪt','[v] 羞辱, 使丢脸','Her boss humiliated her in front of all her colleagues.  她的老板在所有同事面前羞辱了她。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8234','conduction','kən''dʌkʃən','kən''dʌkʃ(ə)n','[n] 传导','Temperature becomes uniform by heat conduction until finally a permanent state is reached.  通过热传导，温度变得一致，直到最终达到一个恒定状态。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8235','indefinitely','ɪn''dɛfɪnətli','ɪn''defɪnɪtlɪ','[adv] 不确定地','It can give you the ability to store indefinitely your session data where it can be retrieved not only after a restart, but from any of a number of machines in a cluster.  它可以给予您无限地存储会话数据的能力，使您的会话数据不仅可以在重新启动后检索，还可以从群集中许多机器中的任意一个检索。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8236','unused','''ʌn''jʊzd',',ʌn''juːzd','[adj] 不用的；未消耗的','unused land  闲置的土地'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8237','ala','''elə','''eɪlə','[n] (昆虫的)翼, 翅','We could give control completely over to robotic cars, ala Minority Report.  我们可以给机器人的控制完全交给车，翼少数派报告。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8238','virgin','''vɝdʒɪn','''vɜːdʒɪn','[n] 处女, 未婚女子','I was a virgin until I was thirty years old.  我到30岁时还是个处女。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8239','terrifyingly','','','[adv] 恐怖地',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8240','conference','''kɑnfərəns','''kɒnf(ə)r(ə)ns','[n] 会议, 讨论会','Representatives from over 100 countries attended the International Peace Conference in Geneva.  来自一百多个国家的代表出席了在日内瓦举行的国际和平大会。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8241','kinsman','''kɪnzmən','''kɪnzmən','[n] 男性亲戚, 同族者',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8242','Norman','''nɔrmən','''nɔ:mən','[n&a] 法国诺曼第人(的)','And of course he was also Norman Bates in Gus Van Sant’s remake of Psycho, but the less said about that the better.  当然他还在格斯-范-桑特重拍的一部关于精神病人的电影扮演诺曼贝茨，不过这个还是少说为妙。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8243','chaste','tʃest','tʃeɪst','[adj] 贞洁的, 朴素的','She led a chaste decent life.  她过着贞洁正派的生活。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8244','sully','''sʌli','''sʌlɪ','[v] 玷污','a scandal that sullied his reputation  玷污了他名誉的丑闻'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8245','incapable','ɪn''kepəbl','ɪn''keɪpəb(ə)l','[adj] 无能力的','She seemed incapable of making the decision.  她似乎无法做出这个决定。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8246','mouldy','''moldi','','[adj] 发霉的, 腐朽的, 旧式的','mouldy cheese  发霉的奶酪'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8247','condemn','kən''dɛm','kən''dem','[v] 判刑,谴责','Politicians were quick to condemn the bombing.  政治家们立即对爆炸事件进行了谴责。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8248','handicap','''hændɪ''kæp','''hændɪkæp','[n] 障碍; [v] 妨碍','Not speaking the language is a real handicap.  不会讲这种语言的确是一个障碍。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8249','dumb','dʌm','dʌm','[adj] 哑的,沉默的','...a young deaf and dumb man.  …一名年轻的聋哑人。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8250','hygiene','''haɪdʒin','''haɪdʒiːn','[n] 卫生, 卫生学','the importance of personal hygiene  个人卫生的重要性'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8251','happily','''hæpɪli','''hæpɪlɪ','[adv] 幸福地, 愉快地','Michelle smiled happily.  米歇尔高兴地笑了。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8252','slothful','''sloθfl','''sləʊθfʊl; -f(ə)l','[adj] 偷懒的','He was not slothful: he had been busy all night.  他可没偷懒：他忙了整整一夜。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8253','forefather','''fɔr''fɑðɚ','''fɔːfɑːðə','[n] 祖先, 祖宗','They were determined to go back to the land of their forefathers.  他们决意要回到老祖宗的土地。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8254','soundly','''saʊndli','''saundli','[adv] 完全地, 健全地','How can he sleep soundly at night? He''s the one responsible for all those crimes.  他晚上怎么能睡得香？他可是所有那些犯罪活动的罪魁祸首啊。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8255','asleep','ə''slip','ə''sliːp','[adj] 睡着的','Quiet! The baby’s asleep.  安静！ 宝宝在睡觉。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8256','torpor','''tɔrpɚ','''tɔːpə','[n] 麻木,不活泼','He had slumped into a state of torpor from which nothing could rouse him.  他陷入了一种麻木状态，什么事都不能唤起他的兴趣。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8257','lull','lʌl','lʌl','[v] 缓和 n暂时的平息',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8258','lash','læʃ','læʃ','[n& v] 鞭打','Oliver lashed the horses to go faster.  奥利弗快马加鞭。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8259','cementation',',simɛn''teʃən',',siːmen''teɪʃ(ə)n','[n] 粘固','Deep caries based by the glass ions cementation agent, could significantly reduce composite resin pulp stimulation to protect pulp, and better effect.  深龋经玻璃离子粘固剂垫底后，能明显减轻复合树脂对牙髓的刺激作用，从而护髓效果更佳。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8260','anyway','''ɛnɪ''we','''enɪweɪ','[adv] 无论如何, 总之','He got lost and spent hours looking for the station, and anyway it was past midnight by the time he got home.  他迷了路，找车站花了几个小时，总之过了午夜才到家。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8261','trumpeter','''trʌmpɪtɚ','''trʌmpɪtə','[n] 喇叭手, 号兵',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8262','breathless','''brɛθləs','''breθlɪs','[adj] 无声息的, 喘不过气来的','The long climb left Jan feeling breathless.  攀爬了那么长时间，简感到喘不过气来。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8263','convene','kən''vin','kən''viːn','[v] 召集, 集合','a report by experts convened by the National Institutes of Health  由全国健康协会召集的专家提出的一份报告'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8264','wingless','','','[adj] 无翼的, 没有翅膀的','It is a parable. We are the wingless birds, and our duties and tasks are the pinions God has made to lift us up and carry us heavenward.  读者，这是一个比喻，我们就是那些无翅的小鸟，我们的工作和职务是神替我们预备带领我们向天的翅翼。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8265','modal','''modl','''məʊd(ə)l','[adj] 模态的, 形态上的','The designers, unlike wizards, are non-modal and hence allow you the flexibility to simultaneously work on designing different database objects.  与向导不同的是，设计程序是非模态的，因此允许您灵活地同时设计不同的数据库对象。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8266','sweaty','''swɛti','''swetɪ','[adj] 出汗的, 吃力的','We came home hot and sweaty after the day’s work.  一天工作之后，我们回到家时热得满身是汗。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8267','brawl','brɔl','brɔːl','[v] 争吵, 怒骂','Fans brawled outside the stadium.  球迷们在体育馆外面闹事。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8268','useable','''ju:zəbl','''juːzəbl','[adj] 可用的, 有效的','But they can produce useable optical and infrared data.  但是它们可以提供可用的光学和红外数据。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8269','operational','''ɑpə''reʃənl','ɒpə''reɪʃ(ə)n(ə)l','[adj] 操作的, 运作的','The boat should be operational by this afternoon.  今天下午这艘船应该可以使用了。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8270','clockmaker','''klɔk,meikə','''klɒkmeɪkə','[n] 制造或修理钟表者',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8271','linkage','''lɪŋkɪdʒ','''lɪŋkɪdʒ','[n] 联接','In all, the nitrogen and carbon ligands, to be effective, require linkage to other electronegative centers.  总的来说，氮和碳配体如要有效，就需要连接上其它电负性中心。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8272','offensive','ə''fɛnsɪv','ə''fensɪv','[adj] 冒犯的, 无礼的','I found her remarks deeply offensive.  我觉得她的话令人非常恼火。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8273','midst','mɪdst','mɪdst','[n] 中部，中间','We were sitting in the midst of an elegant and well-dressed audience.  我们坐在一群举止优雅、衣着考究的观众中间。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8274','multifunctional','','','[adj] 多功能的','This hormone is multifunctional, but one of its main tasks is to act as a neurotransmitter and regulate serotonin levels.  这种激素是多功能的，但它的主要功能是作为神经递质并调节血清素含量。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8275','vigor','''vɪgɚ','''viɡə','[n] 精力, 活力','If you want to retain youthful vigor,you have to take regular exercise.  如果你想保持青春活力，你就得经常锻炼。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8276','singular','''sɪŋɡjəlɚ','''sɪŋgjʊlə','[n] 单数; [adj] 单一的','‘Datum’ is the singular of ‘data’. datum  是 data 的单数形式。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8277','parliament','''pɑrləmənt','''pɑːləm(ə)nt','[n] 国会, 议会','They demanded a free parliament and press.  他们要求议会自由和新闻自由。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8278','oust','aʊst','aʊst','[v] 剥夺,取代,罢免',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8279','promptly','''prɑmptli','''prɒm(p)tlɪ','[adv] 敏捷地, 迅速地','A reply came very promptly.  马上就有了答复。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8280','sage','sedʒ','seɪdʒ','[adj] 智慧的  n智者','sage advice  明智的忠告'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8281','rejoin',',ri''dʒɔɪn','riː''dʒɒɪn','[v] 再结合, 再加入','The prime minister of Fiji has said Fiji is in no hurry to rejoin the Commonwealth.  斐济总理称斐济并不急于重返英联邦。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8282','courage',' ''kɝrɪdʒ','''kʌrɪdʒ','[n] 勇气, 精神','Sue showed great courage throughout her illness.  休在生病期间表现出了极大的勇气。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8283','debtor','''dɛtɚ','''detə','[n] 债务人','...important improvements in the situation of debtor countries.  …债务国境况的重大改善。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8284','penal','''pinl','''piːn(ə)l','[adj] 刑事的','the penal system  刑罚制度'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8285','wrapper','''ræpɚ','''ræpə','[n] 包装材料,包装纸','old sweet wrappers  旧糖果纸'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8286','outright','''aʊtraɪt','aʊt''raɪt','[adj] 直率的, 彻底的 ad直率地, 彻底地','an outright refusal  断然拒绝'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8287','orphanage','''ɔrfənɪdʒ','''ɔːf(ə)nɪdʒ','[n] 孤儿院, 孤儿身份','He was raised in an orphanage.  他是在孤儿院里长大的。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8288','authentic','ɔ''θɛntɪk','ɔː''θentɪk','[adj] 可信的,真正的','authentic French food  正宗的法国食品'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8289','florist','''flɔrɪst','''flɒrɪst','[n] 种花人','He bought her some roses at the florist''s in the mall.  他在购物中心的花店里为她买了一些玫瑰。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8290','fragrance','''fregrəns','''freɪgr(ə)ns','[n] 芬芳, 香气','...a shrubby plant with a strong characteristic fragrance.  …一种有独特浓郁香味的灌木。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8291','daddy','''dædi','''dædɪ','[n] 爸爸','Daddy’s home!  爸爸回家啦！'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8292','eventual','i''ventʃuəl','ɪ''ven(t)ʃʊəl','[adj] 最后的, 结局的','Sweden were the eventual winners of the tournament.  瑞典队是锦标赛的最后赢家。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8293','agonize','''æɡənaɪz','''æɡənaiz','[v] 使极度痛苦, 折磨','As a mother, I agonize over what my children will inherit.  作为一个母亲，我对我的孩子们将要继承的东西感到极度痛苦。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8294','oft','ɔft','ɒft','[adv] 常常, 再三','Then came to him the disciples of John, saying, Why do we and the Pharisees fast oft, but thy disciples fast not?  那时，约翰的门徒来见耶稣说，我们和法利赛人常常禁食，你的门徒倒不禁食，这是为什么呢。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8295','horde','hɔrd','hɔːd','[n] 游牧部落',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8296','primer','''praɪmɚ','''praɪmə','[n] 初级读本,原始物','...the language used in reading primers.  ...初级读物中使用的语言。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8297','revert','rɪ''vɝt','rɪ''vɜːt','[v] 回复','Jackson said her boss became increasingly depressed and reverted to smoking heavily.  杰克逊说她的老板变得越来越抑郁，又重新大量吸烟了。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8298','copyright','''kɑpɪraɪt','''kɒpɪraɪt','[n] 版权, 著作权','Who owns the copyright of this book?  谁拥有这本书的版权？'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8299','nephew','''nɛfju','''nefjuː; ''nevjuː','[n] 侄子, 外甥','I am planning a 25th birthday party for my nephew.  我正在为侄子筹划他25岁的生日聚会。'),
