('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8326','priest','prist','priːst','[n] 牧师','He had trained to be a Catholic priest.  他接受培训成了一名天主教神父。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8327','obedient','oˈbidiənt','ə''biːdɪənt','[adj] 顺从的,孝顺的','an obedient child  听话的孩子'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8328','sty','staɪ','staɪ','[n] 猪栏 v住在猪圈里, 关入猪栏',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8329','undecided',',ʌndɪ''saɪdɪd','ʌndɪ''saɪdɪd','[adj] 未定的, (天气等)不稳定的','After college she was still undecided as to what career she wanted to pursue.  大学毕业后她仍无法决定自己要追求什么事业。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8330','oasis','o''esɪs','əʊ''eɪsɪs','[n] (沙漠中)绿洲,舒适的地方','The immaculately tended gardens are an oasis in the midst of Cairo''s urban sprawl.  那些打理得非常整洁的花园是杂乱扩张的开罗市区中的一片绿洲。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8331','irregularly','','','[adv] 不规则地,不整齐地','Good golfers do better if they give themselves little time to prepare for their shots--and even better if they are distracted by researchers asking them to count irregularly spaced sounds.  优秀的高尔夫球手在击球前准备的时间越少成绩越好—即使被研究人员骚扰，让他们数不规则间隔的声响，最后击球成绩依然不俗。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8332','gregarious','grɪ''gɛrɪəs','grɪ''geərɪəs','[adj] 社交的,群居的','She is such a gregarious and outgoing person.  她就是这样一个爱社交而且外向的人。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8333','honey','''hʌni','''hʌnɪ','[n] (蜂)蜜,宝贝 a甜美的','Hi, honey.  嗨，亲爱的。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8334','hitherto',',hɪðɚ''tu','hɪðə''tuː; ''hɪðətuː','[adv] 迄今,至今','a species of fish hitherto unknown in the West  迄今在西方还不为人知的一种鱼'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8335','heroic','hə''roɪk','hɪ''rəʊɪk','[adj] 英雄的, 英勇的','her heroic efforts to save her family  她拯救家人的英勇行为'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8336','pervasive','pɚ''vesɪv','pə''veɪsɪv','[adj] 普遍的,深入的','the pervasive influence of television  电视无所不在的影响'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8337','uninhabitable',',ʌnɪn''hæbɪtəbl','ʌnɪn''hæbɪtəb(ə)l','[adj] 不适宜居住的','Much of the country is uninhabitable because it is desert.  由于地处沙漠，这个国家的许多地区不适宜居住。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8338','venom','''vɛnəm','''venəm','[n] (蛇的)毒液, 恶意 vt放毒, 使恶毒','There was real venom in her voice.  她的声音非常凶狠。'),
