('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8340','spiny','''spaɪni','''spaɪnɪ','[adj] 多剌的, 剌状的','spiny sea urchins  多刺的海胆'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8341','anteater','''æntitɚ','''æntiːtə','[n] [动]食蚁动物','Why are you so boring?" the anteater asked.  食蚁兽问为什么你这么无聊?'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8342','postpone','po''spon','pəʊs(t)''pəʊn; pə''spəʊn','[v] 推迟, 使延期','The match had to be postponed until next week.  比赛不得不推迟到下周举行。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8343','modulate','''mɑdʒəlet','''mɒdjʊleɪt','[v] 调整, 调节, (信号)调制','He carefully modulated his voice.  他仔细地调节了自己的声音。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8344','vagary','''veiɡəri','''veɪg(ə)rɪ','[n] 奇特行为, 奇想',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8345','modulation',',mɑdʒu''leʃən',',mɒdjʊ''leɪʃən','[n] 调制','Yawning seems to be involved in the modulation of arousal process across the whole life span.  打呵欠似乎与调整觉醒行为的过程有关，并伴随人的一生。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8346','acoustic','ə''kʊstɪk','ə''kuːstɪk','[adj] 有关声音的, 声学的','In our case, we have found the true acoustic echo beacon.  但在这种情况下，我们发现了真正的声学‘回声灯塔’ ”。'),
