('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8407','cynthia','''sinθiə','''sinθiə','[n] 月亮女神, 月亮',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8408','struggler','','','[n] 奋斗者,斗争者','This novel is a legend of a struggler and explorer.  这小说是一个奋斗者和探索者的传奇。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8409','honorable','ˈɑnərəbəl','''ɒnərəbl','[adj] 光荣的,高贵的',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8410','impregnate','ɪm''prɛɡnet','''ɪmpregneɪt','[v] 使怀孕, 使受精 a怀孕的, 充满的','Undercover officers found drug-making equipment used to impregnate paper with LSD.  卧底警官发现了用于使迷幻药渗入纸张的毒品制造设备。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8411','enthusiastically','in,θju:zi''æstikəli','in,θju:zi''æstikəli','[adv] 热心地,满腔热情地','The others barely glanced at it and went back to their shovels, almost enthusiastically, searching for the French Woman, but I went up to the body and forced myself to look at it closely.  其他的人几乎连看都没看上一眼，就拿起他们的锹，差不多都很热心地去寻找那个法国女人的尸体，但我凑到那具尸体前，迫使我自己仔细地看看。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8412','consecutive','kən''sɛkjətɪv','kən''sekjʊtɪv','[adj] 连贯的,连续不断的','It had rained for four consecutive days.  雨接连下了四天。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8413','needy','''nidi','''niːdɪ','[adj] 贫困的, 缺乏生活必需品的','a needy family  贫困家庭'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8414','bequest','bi''kwest','bɪ''kwest','[n] 遗产, 遗赠','a bequest of $5,000  五千美元的遗产'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8415','childless','''tʃaɪldləs','','[adj] 无儿女的','couples who deliberately remain childless  故意不要孩子的夫妇'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8416','cuticle','''kjʊtɪkl','''kjuːtɪk(ə)l','[n] 表皮,角质层','What about the other parts of the cuticle?  有关的角质层的其他部分呢？'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8417','spiky','''spaɪki','''spaɪkɪ','[adj] 大钉似的, 尖刻的','Her short spiky hair is damp with sweat.  她又硬又直的短发被汗浸湿了。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8418','waxy','''wæksi','''wæksɪ','[adj] 象蜡的,苍白的, 柔软的,','the waxy blossoms of the water lily  睡莲那如蜡一般的花朵'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8419','unpalatable','ʌn''pælətəbl','ʌn''pælətəb(ə)l','[adj] 味道差的,难吃的','The unpalatable truth is that the team isn’t getting any better.  让人难以接受的事实是这个队没有任何进步。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8420','epidermis',',ɛpɪ''dɝmɪs',',epɪ''dɜːmɪs','[n] [生]表皮, 上皮','The pigment in the upper layer of skin (epidermis) that gives your skin its normal color is called melanin.  在浅层皮肤（表皮）中有种色素能让你的皮肤保持其正常的颜色，称为黑色素。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8421','immobilize','ɪ''mobə''laɪz','ɪ''məʊbɪlaɪz','[v] 固定不动','The broken limb must be immobilized immediately.  断肢必须立即加以固定。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8422','deterrent','dɪ''tɝənt','dɪ''ter(ə)nt','[n] 威慑 a遏制的','The small fines for this type of crime do not act as much of a deterrent .  对于这种罪行，小额罚金起不到多大的威慑作用。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8423','infest','ɪn''fɛst','ɪn''fest','[v] 骚扰,大批滋生','...pests like aphids which infest cereal crops.  …像蚜虫那样大肆侵害谷类作物的害虫。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8424','rancho','''ræntʃo','''rɑːntʃəʊ','[n] 大牧场(或大农场)工人住的棚屋',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8425','breach','britʃ','briːtʃ','[n] 破坏, 裂口 vt打破, 突破','She wanted to help heal the breach between them.  她想帮助他们修复破裂的关系。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8426','crayon','ˈkreɪən; ˈkreɪˌɑn','ˈkreɪən','[n] 有色粉笔, 蜡笔','He coloured the picture with crayon.  他用蜡笔给画上色。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8427','unwary','ʌn''wɛri','ʌn''weərɪ','[adj] 粗心的, 不警惕的','unwary travellers  毫无戒备的旅行者'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8428','sapiens','ˈsepiəns, -ɛnz','''seɪpjənz','[adj] （拉）现代人的','Homo sapiens are one of the most notable exceptions, leading some scientists to think fatherhood is an important part of what makes us human.  现代人是最值得注意的一个例外，致使一些科学家认为父道在培养孩子富有人情味方面起着重要作用。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8429','mastodon','''mæstə,dɑn','''mæstədɒn','[n] [古生]乳齿象, 庞然大物',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8430','suspicion','sə''spɪʃən','sə''spɪʃ(ə)n','[n] 猜疑, 怀疑','His conduct roused the suspicion of the police.  他的举动引起了警察的怀疑。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8431','preeminent','pri''ɛmɪnənt','prɪ''emɪnənt','[adj] 卓越的','Bombastic boasts—"We are positioned to become the preeminent provider of XYZ"—do not constitute a position.  言过其实的自夸——“我们定位于成为XYZ的卓越供应商”——并不能构建其地位。'),
