('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8451','mania','''menɪə','''meɪnɪə','[n] [医]颠狂, 狂躁, 癖好, 狂热','The mania for dinosaurs began in the late 1800s.  恐龙热兴起于19世纪晚期。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8452','basement','''besmənt','''beɪsm(ə)nt','[n] 地下室, 墙脚','They bought an old schoolhouse to live in and built a workshop in the basement.  他们买了座旧校舍居住，还在地下室建了个作坊。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8453','smuggle','''smʌgl','''smʌg(ə)l','[v] 走私, 偷带','My message is "If you try to smuggle drugs you are stupid."  我的讯息是，“你若企图走私毒品，那是犯傻。”'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8454','stash','stæʃ','stæʃ','[v] 存放 n隐藏处','We went for the bottle of whisky that we had stashed behind the bookcase.  我们去取那瓶我们藏在书柜后面的威士忌。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8455','quarrelsome','''kwɔrəlsəm','''kwɒr(ə)ls(ə)m','[adj] 喜欢吵架的,好争论的','He became quarrelsome after drinking too much.  他喝多了就爱找人吵架。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8456','speedy','''spidi','''spiːdɪ','[adj] 快的, 迅速的','a speedy recovery from injury  受伤后的迅速康复'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8457','prepay','pri''pe','priː''peɪ','[v] 预付','Participation in the program would be voluntary and participants could prepay the government loan at any time.  参加这以项目是自愿的，参与者可以在任何时间将贷款预付给政府。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8458','loathsome','''loθsəm','''ləʊðs(ə)m','[adj] 讨厌的','that loathsome little man  那个讨厌的小男人'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8459','counterfeit','''kaʊntɚ''fɪt','''kaʊntəfɪt; -fiːt','[n] 赝品  a伪造的 v伪造','Levi Strauss says counterfeits of the company''s jeans are flooding Europe.  利瓦伊·斯特劳斯说该公司牛仔裤的仿冒品充斥着欧洲市场。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8460','sender','''sɛndɚ','''sendə','[n] 寄件人,发送人','a package marked ‘ return to sender ’  标有“退回寄件人”字样的包裹'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8461','affix','ə''fɪks','ə''fɪks','[v] 使附于, 粘贴 n[语]词缀',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8462','obsess','əb''sɛs','əb''ses','[v] 迷住, 使困扰','A string of scandals is obsessing America.  一系列丑闻在困扰着美国。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8463','demolish','dɪ''mɑlɪʃ','dɪ''mɒlɪʃ','[v] 毁坏, 推翻, 粉碎','He demolished my argument in minutes.  他几分钟内就把我的论点驳倒了。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8464','golf','gɔlf','gɒlf','[n] 高尔夫球 vi打高尔夫球','He plays golf on Sundays.  他星期天都去打高尔夫球。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8465','glaciate','''ɡleisieit','''ɡleɪsɪeɪt','[v] 使结冰, 以冰(或冰河)覆盖',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8466','ambience','''æmbɪəns','''æmbɪəns','[n] 周围环境, 气氛','The overall ambience of the room is cosy.  这个房间的整体氛围是舒适的。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8467','cab','kæb','kæb','[n] 出租汽车','New York’s yellow cabs  纽约的黄色出租车'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8468','frenzy','''frɛnzi','''frenzɪ','[n] 狂暴, 狂怒 vt使发狂','Doreen had worked herself into a frenzy .  多琳一阵狂怒。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8469','melodrama','''mɛlədrɑmə','''melə(ʊ)drɑːmə','[n] 情节剧','He was behaving like a character in a Victorian melodrama.  他表现得就像维多利亚时代情节剧里的角色。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8470','treasure','''trɛʒɚ','''treʒə','[n] 财宝, 财富 vt珍爱','The Book of Kells is Trinity College’s greatest treasure.  《凯尔经》是三一学院的镇院之宝。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8471','Cincinnati',',sɪnsə''næti',',sinsi''næti','[n] 辛辛那提（美国俄亥俄州西南部城市）','We never went back. Instead, we moved to a house near Cincinnati, far from the river.  我们再也没有回去，而是举家迁往离河很远的辛辛那提附近的另一幢房子。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8472','trove','trov','trəʊv','[n] 被发现的东西, 收藏的东西','But at the stern of the ship, divers found a trove of gold and silver and high-grade ceramics whose significance is more mysterious.  但是潜水人员在船尾部发现了一个由金、银以及高级陶瓷打造的收藏品，这件收藏品的意义更加神秘。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8473','acronym','''ækrənɪm','''ækrənɪm','[n] 只取首字母的缩写词',''),
