('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8475','vault','vɔlt','vɔːlt','[n] 拱顶 v做成弧形',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8476','labyrinth','''læbərɪnθ','''læb(ə)rɪnθ','[n] 迷路, 迷宫, 难解的事物','...the labyrinth of corridors.  …迷宫般的走廊。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8477','rubble','''rʌbl','''rʌb(ə)l','[n] 碎石','Brick rubble is useful as the base for paths and patios.  碎砖可用作道路和天井的基石。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8478','recipe','''rɛsəpi','''resɪpɪ','[n] 处方','Large-scale inflation is a recipe for disaster.  大规模的通货膨胀有可能导致灾难。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8479','rainer','','','[n] 人工降雨装置,喷灌装置',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8480','yesteryear','''jɛstɚjɪr','''jestəjɪə; -jɜː','[n] 去年 ad过去不久的岁月','The modern-day sex symbol has now taken the place of the old-fashioned hero of yesteryear.  当今的性感偶像已经取代了往昔过时的英雄形象。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8481','lore','lɔr','lɔː','[n] 学问,（动物的）眼光知识','According to local lore, a ghost still haunts the castle.  根据当地人的传说，城堡里至今仍然闹鬼。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8482','adjoin','ə''dʒɔɪn','ə''dʒɒɪn','[v] 邻接, 毗连','A vacant plot of land adjoins his house.  有一块空地紧挨着他家。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8483','mortar','''mɔrtɚ','''mɔːtə','[n] 灰泥,迫击炮 vt用灰泥结合','A cameraman was killed when his vehicle came under mortar fire .  一名摄影师因所乘坐的汽车遭到迫击炮袭击而丧生。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8484','incongruity',',ɪnkɑŋ''grʊəti',',ɪnkɒŋ''gruːɪtɪ','[n] 不调和的, 不适宜的','The incongruity of her situation struck Gina with unpleasant force.  吉娜猛然意识到自己处境尴尬，心里很不舒服。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8485','tableland','''tebllænd','''teɪb(ə)llænd','[n] 高原','The northwestern tableland area has a continental plateau climate with long and chilly winter and cool humid summer.  西北高原地区是大陆高原气候，有漫长而寒冷的冬季，凉爽而湿润的夏季。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8486','perfection','pɚ''fɛkʃən','pə''fekʃ(ə)n','[n] 尽善尽美, 完美, 完成','My father expected perfection from all of us.  父亲期望我们都尽善尽美。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8487','fullness','''fʊlnəs','''fʊlnɪs','[n] 满, 丰富, 成熟','Use a red gloss on your bottom lip to give it fullness.  下唇使用红色唇彩让它显得丰盈饱满。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8488','recoil','''rikɔɪl','rɪ''kɒɪl','[n] 畏缩, 弹回 vi退却, 畏缩','...his small body jerking in recoil from the volume of his shouting.  …他小小身体在他大声的叫喊中畏缩地抽搐着。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8489','musicologist','','','[n] 音乐学者','Rakae Jamil, a musicologist with the Sanjan Nagar Institute of Philosophy and Arts in Lahore, says there is no doubt that Michael Jackson influenced the pop scene in Pakistan.  拉齐.贾米尔是拉合尔的桑贾恩.纳加尔哲学和艺术研究所的音乐理论家。 他说，迈克尔.杰克逊影响了巴基斯坦的流行歌坛，这点是毫无疑问的。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8490','forte','''fɔrte','''fɔːteɪ; ''fɔːtɪ; fɔːt','[n] 长处','He found that running long distances was not his forte .  他发现长跑并不是他的强项。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8491','percussive','pɚ''kʌsɪv','pə''kʌsɪv','[adj] 冲击的,叩诊的','...using all manner of percussive effects.  ...运用各种打击乐效果。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8492','multistory','','','[adj] 多层的,有多层楼的','The abbey was a maze of multistory wings, each added in a differing century, the architecture conspiring to create a jumbled complex that now housed four hundred brothers.  修道院的结构是迷宫似的多层侧翼，每个侧翼都在不同的世纪里被添上，那建筑拼成一混乱的复合体，里面现在住着四百多个圣殿武士。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8493','hammerhead','''hæmɚhɛd','''hæməhed','[n] 锤头 a锤头状的, 鲁钝的',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8494','induct','ɪn''dʌkt','ɪn''dʌkt','[v] 感应,引导','The government shoulders ethic obligation, she has to induct and maintain the rationalization of the living world.  政府在生活世界中引导和维护生活世界的合理化，肩负著伦理责任；'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8495','coincident','ko''ɪnsɪdənt','kəʊ''ɪnsɪd(ə)nt','[adj] 一致的,符合的','Their aims are coincident with ours.  他们的目标和我们的一致。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8496','assort','ə''sɔrt','ə''sɔːt','[v] 分类配全',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8497','forgiveness','fɚ''ɡɪvnəs','fə''gɪvnɪs','[n] 宽恕, 宽仁之心','...a spirit of forgiveness and national reconciliation.  …一种宽恕与民族和解的精神。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8498','spoonful','''spʊn''fʊl','''spuːnfʊl','[n] 一匙','He took a spoonful of the stew and ate it.  他舀起一匙炖菜吃了下去。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8499','oat','ot','əʊt','[n] [植]燕麦, 麦片粥','Instead of eating hunched pleasurably over a book, I look out of the window and chew every mouthful thoroughly, aware of every single oat and nut and dried bit of apple as it goes down.  送孩子们去学校后，我不再放松地边吃早饭边看书，而是盯着窗外，仔细地嚼着嘴里的食物：每一粒燕麦、每一颗坚果、每一片苹果干。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8500','differentiating',',dɪfə''rɛnʃɪ,etɪŋ',',dɪfə''renʃɪ,eɪtɪŋ','[adj] 微分的','So it appears that banks do an unusually lousy job of differentiating themselves.  如此看来，银行业者通常在区分自己的工作上太过糟糕。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8501','symphonic','sɪm''fɑnɪk','sɪm''fɒnɪk','[adj] 交响乐的, 和声的','Of course, anyone knows that it is impossible to play a symphonic work with just three strings.  当然，每个人都知道，只用三根弦来演奏交响乐是不可能的。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8502','sad','sæd','sæd','[adj] 忧愁的, 悲哀的','The relationship had been important to me and its loss left me feeling sad and empty.  这种关系对我一直都很重要，失去它让我感到难过而空虚。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8503','violinist',',vaɪə''lɪnɪst',',vaɪə''lɪnɪst','[n] 小提琴演奏者, 小提琴家','Rose''s father was a talented violinist.  罗斯的父亲是一位天才的小提琴手。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8504','cellist','''tʃɛlɪst','''tʃelɪst','[n] 大提琴演奏家','A cellist is always shortening and lengthening the strings.  大提琴演奏家总是在压缩或拉长弦'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8505','upsurge','''ʌpsɝdʒ','''ʌpsɜːdʒ','[n] 高潮 vi涌起','A new upsurge in construction is in the making.  一个建设的新高潮正在兴起。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8506','phenomenal','','fɪ''nɒmɪn(ə)l','[adj] 现象的,显著的','the phenomenal success of computer games in recent years  近年来电脑游戏的惊人成功'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8507','midocean','','','[n] 海洋中央','In fact, he wrote his dissertation on the midocean ridge.  实际上，他的博士论文就是关于中央山脊的研究。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8508','deformation','''difɔr''meʃən',',diːfɔː''meɪʃ(ə)n','[n] 变形','B: It occurs when a component reaches its limit for deformation.  B：当一个部件达到了变形的极限时，就会发生断裂。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8509','omnibus','''ɑmnɪbəs','''ɒmnɪbəs','[n] 公共汽车, 精选集 a综合性的','the Saturday omnibus edition of ‘Brookside’  《小溪边》的周六综合版'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8510','accessibility','æk,sɛsə''bɪləti','ək,sesə''bɪlətɪ','[n] 易接近, 可到达的',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8511','unoccupied',',ʌn''ɑkjupaɪd','ʌn''ɒkjʊpaɪd','[adj] 空闲的,未占领的','However, to do so, it must find an unoccupied territory and a member of the opposite sex with which to mate.  然而，要想成为领头狼，必须找到一块未被占领的领地和一头能够与之交配的异性狼。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8512','catalyze','''kætə,laɪz','''kætəlaɪz','[v] 催化, 刺激, 促进',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8513','vacant','''vekənt','''veɪk(ə)nt','[adj] 空的, 头脑空虚的,空缺的','Only a few apartments were still vacant.  只有几套公寓仍然空着。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8514','suite','sut; swit','swiːt','[n] (一批)随员, (一套)家具, 组','a honeymoon suite  蜜月套房'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8515','scavenge','''skævɪndʒ','''skævɪn(d)ʒ','[v] 打扫, 以(腐肉)为食','Pigs scavenged among the rubbish.  猪在垃圾堆里觅食。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8516','subdivision',',sʌbdɪ''vɪʒn','''sʌbdɪvɪʒ(ə)n; sʌbdɪ''vɪʒ(ə)n','[n] 细分, 一部','Months are a conventional subdivision of the year.  月份是年的常规分支。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8517','juvenile','''dʒʊvənaɪl','''dʒuːvənaɪl','[adj] 青少年的 n青少年, 少年读物','juvenile crime  少年犯罪'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8518','betray','bɪ''tre','bɪ''treɪ','[v] 出卖, 背叛','He felt that she had betrayed him.  他感觉她背叛了自己。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8519','sensible','''sɛnsəbl','''sensɪb(ə)l','[adj] 有感觉的, 明智的','She seems very sensible.  她好像很明智。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8520','treetop','''tri''tɑp','''triːtɒp','[n] 树稍','Boardwalks on the forest floor and the treetop level let visitors experience the rain forest up close.  在树顶上搭建的森林地面走道可以让游客近距离地接触热带雨林。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8521','ancestry','''ænsɛstri','''ænsestrɪ','[n] 祖先(集合称), 血统','Most people of European or African ancestry have the "wet" kind: thick and sticky.  大多数欧洲或者非洲血统的人耳垢是湿的，厚的，有粘性的。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8522','virginal','''vɝdʒɪnl','''vɜːdʒɪn(ə)l','[adj] 处女的, 无瑕的','Somehow she''d always been a child in his mind, pure and virginal.  不知何故，她在他心里一直是个天真无邪的孩子。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8523','dulcimer','''dʌlsɪmɚ','''dʌlsɪmə','[n] [乐] 洋琴','The ancestry of the piano can be traced to the early keyboard instruments of the fifteenth and sixteenth centuries -- the spinet, the dulcimer, and the virginal.  钢琴的家系可以追溯至15至16世纪早期的键盘乐器，包括小型拨弦琴、洋琴和维金娜琴。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8524','unpublished',',ʌn''pʌbliʃt','ʌn''pʌblɪʃt','[adj] 未公开出版的,未发表过的',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8525','paddle','''pædl','''pæd(ə)l','[n] 短桨, 划桨 v划桨,拌','We might be able to push ourselves across with the paddle.  我们或许可以自己划桨过去。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8526','twine','twaɪn','twaɪn','[n] 合股线 v织, (使)缠绕','a bundle of papers tied up with twine  用双股线捆扎起来的一摞文件'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8527','jumble','''dʒʌmbl','''dʒʌmb(ə)l','[v] 混杂, 搞乱 n混乱','The photographs were all jumbled up.  照片乱七八糟地堆在一起。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8528','bituminous','bə''tʊmənəs','bɪ''tjuːmɪnəs','[adj] 沥青的,含沥青的',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8529','practicable','''præktɪkəbl','''præktɪkəb(ə)l','[adj] 可实行的,可用的','The only practicable course of action is to sell the company.  唯一可行的做法是把公司卖掉。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8530','acquaint','ə''kwent','ə''kweɪnt','[v] 使熟知, 通知','Have steps been taken to acquaint breeders with their right to apply for licenses?  已经采取措施让饲养动物者了解他们申请执照的权利了吗？'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8531','toil','tɔɪl','tɒɪl','[n] 苦工, 圈套 v费力地做',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8532','insurmountable',',ɪnsɚ''maʊntəbl',',ɪnsə''maʊntəb(ə)l','[adj] 不能克服的,不能超越的','The language difference proved an insurmountable barrier.  语言差异是难以克服的障碍。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8533','instantaneously',',ɪnstən''tenɪəsli',',instən''teinjəsli','[adv] 即刻,突如其来地',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8534','prohibitively','','','[adv] 禁止地,过分地',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8535','video','''vɪdɪo','''vɪdɪəʊ','[n] 录象, 视频 a视频的','a video clip shown on the Internet  因特网上的一段视频'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8536','unprocessed','','','[adj] 未被加工的','Reduce packaging by eating more whole, unprocessed foods and using the bulk bins for items that have a long shelf-life.  减少包装，通过吃全食品、未经加工的食品以及对物品使用有很长的保质期的散装箱。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8537','standardize','''stændɚdaɪz','''stændədaɪz','[v] 使符合标准, 使标准化','Attempts to standardize English spelling have never been successful.  统一英语拼写的尝试从未成功过。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8538','uncooked',',ʌn''kʊkt','ʌn''kʊkt','[adj] 未煮过的','Always wash your hands after handling uncooked meat.  碰过生肉后一定要洗手。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8539','forecaster','''fɔrkæstɚ','''fɔːkɑːstə','[n] 预报员','the weather forecaster  气象预报员'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8540','stormy','''stɔrmi','''stɔːmɪ','[adj] 暴风雨的, 激烈的, 暴怒的','The sky was starting to look stormy.  开始变天了，看上去暴风雨将至。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8541','untouched','ʌn''tʌtʃt','ʌn''tʌtʃt','[adj] 未触及的, 未改变的','Several papers lay untouched on the desk.  有几份文件原封不动地放在书桌上。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8542','mennonite','''mɛnən,aɪt','''menənait','[n] 门诺派教徒',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8543','police','pə''lis','pə''liːs','[n] 警察 vt管辖 a警察的','Police surrounded the courthouse.  警察围在法院大楼四周。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8544','humility','hju''mɪləti','hjʊ''mɪlɪtɪ','[n] 谦卑','...a deep sense of humility.  …深深的谦卑感。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8545','torrential','tə''rɛnʃl','tə''renʃ(ə)l','[adj] 猛烈的,汹涌的',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8546','dissipate','''dɪsɪpet','''dɪsɪpeɪt','[v] 驱散, 消散','As he thought it over, his anger gradually dissipated.  他想明白后，怒气就渐渐消了。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8547','advantageously','','','[adv] 有利地,方便地',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8548','merchandis','','','[n] 商品,货物 v买卖',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8549','hospital','''hɑspɪtl','''hɒspɪt(ə)l','[n] 医院','They are building a new hospital.  他们正在建一家新医院。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8550','proboscidean',',prəubə''sidiən, prə,bɔsi''di:ən',',prɒbə''sɪdɪən','[adj] 长鼻类的 n长鼻目动物',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8551','sift','sɪft','sɪft','[v] 详审','Police are sifting through the evidence.  警方在筛查证据。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8552','premium','''primɪəm','''priːmɪəm','[n] 额外费用, 奖金, 奖赏','Consumers are prepared to pay a premium for organically grown vegetables.  消费者愿意多花钱购买有机蔬菜。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8553','neat','nit','niːt','[adj] 整洁的, 灵巧的, 优雅的','neat handwriting  工整的笔迹'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8554','precursor','pri''kɝsɚ','prɪ''kɜːsə','[n] 先驱','Error is often the precursor of what is correct.  错误常常是正确的先导。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8555','economize','ɪ''kɑnə''maɪz','ɪ''kɒnə''maɪz','[v] 节省, 有效地利用','We''re going to have to economize from now on.  我们得从现在起节省开支。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8556','haven','''hevn','''heɪv(ə)n','[n] 港口, 避难所',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8557','tranquillity','','','[n] 宁静','But in states organized like that of France, it is impossible to hold them with such tranquillity.  但是在像法兰西那样组织的国家里，以这样的平静来维持政权是不可能的事情。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8558','competitiveness','kəm''pɛtətɪvnɪs','kəm''petətɪvnɪs','[n] 竞争力,好竞争','New machinery has enhanced the company’s productivity and competitiveness.  新机器帮助公司提高了生产力，增强了竞争力。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8559','atomization','','','[n] 分离成原子, 雾化',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8560','custodian','kʌ''stodɪən','kʌ''stəʊdɪən','[n] 管理人','...the custodian of the holy shrines in Mecca and Medina.  …在麦加和麦地那的圣地的管理员。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8561','stagnate','stæɡ''net','stæg''neɪt; ''stægneɪt','[v] (使)淤塞, (使)停滞, (使)沉滞, (使)变萧条','Industrial production is stagnating.  工业生产停滞不前。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8562','emigrate','''ɛmɪɡret','''emɪgreɪt','[v] 移居, 移民','He emigrated to Belgium.  他移民去了比利时。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8563','regret','rɪ''ɡrɛt','rɪ''gret','[n] /v遗憾, 抱歉,后悔','Larry said he had no regrets about retiring.  拉里曾说他对于退休没有任何遗憾。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8564','civility','sə''vɪləti','sɪ''vɪlɪtɪ','[n] 礼貌, 端庄','Please have the civility to knock before you enter next time.  下次你进来之前要有点礼貌——先敲门。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8565','unbridgeable','','','[adj] 不能架桥的,不能逾越的','...the so-called unbridgeable gap between the world of humans and that of chimpanzees.  ...人类社会和黑猩猩社会间所谓的不可逾越的鸿沟。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8566','determinedly','','','[adv] 决然地,断然地',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8567','abandonment','ə''bændənmənt','ə''bændənm(ə)nt','[n] 放弃','...memories of her father''s complete abandonment of her.  …她父亲对她的彻底抛弃的那些记忆。'),
