('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8600','humanist','''hjʊmənɪst','''hjuːmənɪst','[n] 人道主义者, 人文主义者','Vernon said that as he watched the tsunami come ashore, he was unable to divorce the scientist in him from the humanist.  弗兰克说，当他观看到海啸逼近的时候，他不能使自己从科学家和人道主义者中脱离出来。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8601','cannibalism','''kænəbl,ɪzəm','''kænɪbəlɪzəm','[n] 同类相食','They were forced to practise cannibalism in order to survive.  为了生存，他们被迫同类相食。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8602','satirist','''sætərɪst','''sætərɪst','[n] 讽刺作家','He built a reputation in the 1970s as a social satirist.  他在20世纪70年代作为社会讽刺作家而出名。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8603','distend','dɪ''stɛnd','dɪ''stend','[v] (使)扩大, (使)扩张','Blood vessels in the lungs are filled and distend. Capillary changes have been observed in the animal model of simulated microgravity.  肺血管充盈、扩张，并在模拟微重力动物模型中观察到肺微血管损伤。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8604','balmy','''bɑmi','''bɑːmɪ','[adj] 芳香的, 温和的','a balmy summer night  一个宜人的夏夜'),
