('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8622','ethically','''ɛθɪkli','''eθikli','[adv] 伦理(学)上','What is technically possible and what is ethically appropriate is a matter of heated debate.  什么在技术上是可行的与什么在伦理上是适当的，这是一个激烈辩论的问题。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8623','juxtaposition',',dʒʌkstəpə''zɪʃən',',dʒʌkstəpə''zɪʃ(ə)n','[n] 毗邻, 并置','This juxtaposition of brutal reality and lyrical beauty runs through Park''s stories.  残酷的现实和抒情诗般的美并存贯穿于帕克的故事之中。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8624','platitudinous','','','[adj] 平凡的,  陈腐的','It has lived because readers appreciate a refreshing stimulus, an irreverent reminder that they live in a world of platitudinous thinking, cheap moralizing, and foolish philosophy.  它的存在是因为读者欣赏使人耳目一新的刺激，毫不客气地提醒他们活在一个思相陈腐、道德低廉、哲学荒谬的世界里。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8625','moralize','''mɔrəlaɪz','''mɒr(ə)laɪz','[v] 教化 ,说教','politicians moralizing about people’s sexual behaviour  就人们的性行为进行说教的政客们'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8626','platitude','''plætɪtud','''plætɪtjuːd','[n] 陈词滥调','His excuse was the platitude ‘boys will be boys.’  他还是那一套理由:“男孩总归是男孩。”'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8627','irreverent','ɪ''rɛvərənt','ɪ''rev(ə)r(ə)nt','[adj] 不敬的,  无礼的','his irreverent sense of humour  他失礼的幽默感'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8628','megalopolis',',mɛgə''lɑpəlɪs',',megə''lɒp(ə)lɪs','[n] 巨大都市, 人口稠密地带','...the densely populated megalopolis that stretches down the East Coast from Boston to Washington.  ...沿着从波士顿到华盛顿的东海岸连绵不断、人口稠密的特大城市带。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8629','comer','''kʌmɚ','''kʌmə','[n] 来者, 新来者','The contest is open to all comers.  该项竞赛所有人都可参加。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8630','conurbation','''kɑnɝ''beʃən','ˌkɒnɜːˈbeɪʃn','[n] 有卫星城的大都市',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8631','elusive','ɪ''lusɪv','ɪ''l(j)uːsɪv','[adj] 难懂的, 难捉摸的','She enjoys a firm reputation in this country but wider international success has been elusive.  她在这个国家享有稳固的声誉，但却一直难以在国际上取得更大的成功。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8632','scowl','skaʊl','skaʊl','[n] 愁容, 皱眉 v皱眉',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8633','subterranean',',sʌbtə''renɪən',',sʌbtə''reɪnɪən','[adj] 地下的','subterranean passage  地下通道'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8634','ramble','''ræmbl','''ræmb(ə)l','[n] 漫步  vi闲逛；漫谈','I quite like the idea of going for a ramble one weekend.  我觉得找个周末去乡下走走这个主意不错。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8635','pharmacy','''fɑrməsi','''fɑːməsɪ','[n] 药房, 药剂学','an all-night pharmacy  通宵药店'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8636','gyration','dʒaɪ''reʃən','dʒaɪ''reɪʃ(ə)n','[n] 旋回, 回转','He had been caught in a vortex and was being whirled on with a velocity of advance and gyration that made him giddy and sick.  一个巨大的漩涡紧紧地抓住了他，他的身体随着漩涡快速前进，快速旋转；他眼花缭乱，头晕目眩，想要呕吐出来。 转眼间他被狠狠地摔在左岸下方的砂砾上。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8637','miraculous','mɪ''rækjələs','mɪ''rækjʊləs','[adj] 奇迹的,不可思议的','She made a miraculous recovery from her injuries.  她受伤后奇迹般地康复了。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8638','grainy','''ɡreni','''greɪnɪ','[adj] 粒状的, 木纹状的','...grainy black and white photos.  ...有颗粒的黑白照片。'),
