('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8993','unmarried',',ʌn''mærɪd','ʌn''mærɪd','[adj] 未婚的, 单身的','unmarried mothers  未婚母亲'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8994','gentility','dʒɛn''tɪləti','dʒen''tɪlɪtɪ','[n] 文雅, 出身高贵, 有教养','The hotel had an air of discreet gentility.  这家酒店有一种不露痕迹的典雅气派。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8995','plasticity','plæ''stɪsəti','plæ''stɪsɪtɪ','[n] 可塑性, 塑性','This kind of plasticity may play a vital role in evolution as well as during the lifetime of individuals.  这种可塑性不仅贯穿生命个体的一生，也许对进化也产生了至关重要的作用。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8996','carpet','''kɑrpɪt','''kɑːpɪt','[n] 地毯','My bedroom carpet is green.  我卧室里的地毯是绿色的。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8997','adolescent',',ædə''lɛsnt','ædə''les(ə)nt','[adj] 青春期的; [n] 青少年','It is important that an adolescent boy should have an adult in whom he can confide.  一个青春期男孩应该有一个他能倾吐心声的成年人，这是很重要的。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8998','regimentation',',redʒimen''teiʃən','','[n] 管辖,严格控制','Democracy is incompatible with excessive, bureaucratic regimentation of social life.  民主与受到过度的、官僚化的管制的社会生活是不相容的。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_8999','rarer','','','[adj] 稀罕的,  珍贵的',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9000','jibe','dʒaɪb','dʒaɪb','[v] 嘲笑, 与一致, 使转向','"No doubt he''ll give me the chance to fight him again," he jibed.  “毫无疑问，他会给我机会与他再打一次。”他嘲讽道。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9001','knead','nid','niːd','[v] 揉(面等)成团, 按摩','Knead the dough for three minutes.  将面团揉三分钟。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9002','nonchalant',',nɑnʃə''lɑnt','''nɒnʃ(ə)l(ə)nt','[adj] 若无其事的, 不关心的, 冷淡的','‘Has he got a girlfriend?’ Jill asked, trying to sound nonchalant.  “他有女朋友吗？”吉尔装出无所谓的样子问道。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9003','humanlike','','','[adj] 似人类的','In terms of career advice, the most obvious message is: Focus on jobs and areas of expertise that appear to require humanlike general intelligence.  从职业建议上将，最明显的一点是：关注与那些需要人类总体智能的工作或专业领域。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9004','boron','''borɑn','''bɔːrɒn','[n] [化]硼','He said there should be an element under boron.  他认为在，硼的下面也有个元素。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9005','dump','dʌmp','dʌmp','[v] 倾倒(垃圾), 倾卸; [n] 堆存处','We dumped our bags at the nearby Grand Hotel and hurried toward the market.  我们把包扔在附近的格兰德旅馆，急匆匆地向市场赶去。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9006','topographically','','','[adv] 地形地','Dubai is a part of the Arabian Desert, but is topographically different from it.  迪拜虽然是阿拉伯沙漠的一部分，但从地形上来说，它却不同于阿拉伯沙漠。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9007','mandatory','''mændətɔri','''mændət(ə)rɪ','[adj] 命令的, 托管的','Murder carries a mandatory life sentence .  谋杀罪依照法律要判无期徒刑。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9008','scholarly','''skɑlɚli','''skɒləlɪ','[adj] 学者气质的, 学者风度的','a scholarly journal  学术期刊'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9009','offering','''ɔfərɪŋ','''ɒf(ə)rɪŋ','[n] 提供, 奉献物',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9010','chlorine','''klɔrin','''klɔːriːn','[n] [化]氯','Salt decomposes into sodium and chlorine.  盐分解成钠和氯。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9011','bromine','''bromin','''brəʊmiːn','[n] [化]溴','In this way a bromine ''handle'' for adding extra resveratrol units can be placed in one position or in two positions in a controlled manner.  通过这种方法，一个用于结合其他白藜芦醇单元的溴“把手”就可以可控地放置在一个或两个位置。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9012','gush','ɡʌʃ','gʌʃ','[v] 涌出,滔滔不绝; [n] 迸发','Piping-hot water gushed out.  滚烫的水涌了出来。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9013','kea','''kiə','''kiːə','[n] 食肉鹦鹉',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9014','hillbilly','''hɪlbɪli','''hɪlbɪlɪ','[n] 山地内部的贫农,乡下人','Blinking in amazement, the hillbilly drawled, "I should have brought my wife!  乡下人惊奇地眨着眼睛，慢吞吞地说：“我应该把我的老婆带来!”'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9015','pont','','','[n] (南非的)缆拉渡船',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9016','resettle','','','[v] (使)重新定居,再坐下来','The area was resettled in the latter half of the century.  在该世纪下半叶这个地区重新有人定居。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9017','pivotal','''pɪvətl','''pɪvətl','[adj] 重要的, 轴的','The Bank of England has a pivotal role in the London money market.  英格兰银行在伦敦货币市场中起着关键性的作用。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9018','untimely','ʌn''taɪmli','ʌn''taɪmlɪ','[a&ad] 不适时的, 不合时宜的',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9019','sack','sæk','sæk','[n] 大袋, 大袋之量; [v] 解雇, 洗劫','They couldn’t sack me – I’d done nothing wrong.  他们不能解雇我——我没做错什么事。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9020','pointe','','','[n] （芭蕾舞中的）足尖舞',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9021','woodcutting','','','[adj] 木雕的; [n] 伐木, 木刻','Roadwork is all done with spades, heavy woodcutting with hand-axes – and all work is to meet specified quotas or food was immediately reduced.  道路施工都是用铁锹完成的，沉重的伐木工作是用斧头——所有工作都要符合规定的进度，否则立刻就减少食物。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9022','chapter','''tʃæptɚ','''tʃæptə','[n] (书籍)章,回','Read Chapter 11 as your homework.  家庭作业是阅读第 11 章。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9023','homely','''homli','''həʊmlɪ','[adj] 家常的,平凡的','Mrs Keane is a comfortable, homely person.  基恩太太平易近人，亲切好客。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9024','circulatory','''sɝkjələtɔri','''sɜːkjʊlət(ə)rɪ; sɜːkjʊ''leɪt(ə)rɪ','[adj] 循环的, 循环系统的','the heart and circulatory system  心脏和血液循环系统'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9025','variance','''vɛrɪəns','''veərɪəns','[n] 不一致, 变化,','a price variance of 5%  5%的价格差异'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9026','affiliate','ə''fɪlɪet','ə''fɪlɪeɪt','[v] 使隶属于; [n] 附属机构','He wanted to affiliate with a U.S. firm because he needed expert advice in legal affairs.  他想成为一家美国公司的会员，因为他需要法律事务方面的专家意见。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9027','unquestioning','ʌn''kwɛstʃənɪŋ','ʌn''kwestʃ(ə)nɪŋ','[adj] 无条件的, 不犹豫的','an unquestioning belief in God  对上帝的信不移'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9028','primatology',',praɪmə''tɑlədʒi',',praɪmə''tɒlədʒɪ','[n] 灵长类动物学','The study of our human nature encompasses a variety of fields ranging from anthropology, primatology, cognitive science and psychology to paleontology, archaeology, evolutionary biology and genetics.  从人类学，灵长类动物学，认知科学和心理学到古生物学，考古学，进化生物学和基因学，人们对人类属性的研究包括很多领域。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9029','demerit','di''mɛrɪt','diː''merɪt','[n] 缺点,过失','Demerits were given to students for late attendance at prayers.  祷告会上迟到的学生被记过了。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9030','inferiority','ɪn,fɪrɪ''ɔrəti','ɪn,fɪərɪ''ɒrɪtɪ','[n] 自卑, 次等','This kind of sentiment is a very interesting combination of superiority and inferiority.  这种情感是非常有趣的，是一种高傲和自卑的结合体。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9031','tyrannical','tɪ''rænɪkl','tɪ''rænɪk(ə)l; taɪ-','[adj] 暴虐的, 压制的, 残暴的','a tyrannical parent  一位专横的家长'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9032','potentiality','pə,tɛnʃɪ''æləti','pəʊtenʃɪ''ælɪtɪ','[n] (用复数)潜能,可能性','All of these are useful breeds whose potentiality has not been realized.  所有这些都是有益的品种，其潜力尚未被认识到。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9033','applicability',',æplɪkə''bɪləti',',æplɪkə''bɪlətɪ','[n] 适用性, 适应性','As a source of knowledge the strength of rational statements lies in reliability and predictability, but not in breadth or applicability.  作为知识的来源之一，理论叙述的作用在于可靠性和预见性，而不在于广泛性和实用性。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9034','enlightenment','ɪn''laɪtnmənt','ɪn''laɪt(ə)nm(ə)nt; en-','[n] 启迪, 教化','Stella had a moment of enlightenment.  斯特拉恍然大悟。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9035','terrible','''tɛrəbl','''terɪb(ə)l','[adj] 很糟的, 极坏的,骇人的','The hotel was absolutely terrible.  这家宾馆糟糕透了。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9036','glossy','''ɡlɑsi','''glɒsɪ','[adj] 平滑的, 有光泽的','her glossy black hair  她那亮泽的黑发'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9037','relevance','''rɛləvəns','''reləvəns','[n] 中肯, 适当','I think we can all appreciate the relevance of that now.  我想，我们大家现在都能领会这句话中肯。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9038','wanderer','''wɑndərɚ','''wɒnd(ə)rə(r)','[n] 流浪者, 徘徊者, 迷路的动物',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9039','rebirth',',ri''bɝθ','riː''bɜːθ','[n] 复活, 新生','the cycle of birth, death and rebirth  生死轮回'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9040','unfertilized','','ʌn''fɜːtɪlaɪzd','[adj] 未施肥的,  未受精的','an unfertilized ovum'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9041','untreated',',ʌn''tritɪd','','[adj] 未经处理的, 未经治疗的','untreated sewage  未经处理过的污水'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9042','folklore','''foklɔr','''fəʊklɔː','[n] 民间传说, 民俗学','In Chinese folklore the bat is a symbol of good fortune.  在中国民间传说中，蝙蝠是好运的象征。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9043','fumigate','''fjumɪɡet','''fjuːmɪgeɪt','[v] 熏制, 以烟熏消毒','...fruit which has been treated with insecticide and fumigated.  ...杀过虫、消过毒的水果。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9044','unverified','ʌn''vɛrɪ,faɪd','ʌn''verɪfaɪd','[adj] 未经证实的,  未经核对的','The general goal was to close all "unverified defects" before a specific date.  主要的目标是在一个具体日期前消除所有“未经核对的缺陷”。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9045','veil','vel','veɪl','[n] 面纱; [v] 遮蔽, 掩饰','She lifted her veil with both hands.  她用双手揭开面纱。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9046','uncontested',',ʌnkən''tɛstɪd','ʌnkən''testɪd','[adj] 无争论的, 无异议的','After an uncontested divorce, Peggy married Charlie.  和平离婚之后，佩姬嫁给了查利。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9047','inspector','ɪn''spɛktɚ','ɪn''spektə','[n] 检查员, 巡视员','ticket inspectors  查票员'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9048','nutritionist','nu''trɪʃənɪst','njʊ''trɪʃ(ə)nɪst','[n] 营养学家','Nutritionists say only 33 percent of our calorie intake should be from fat.  营养学家说我们所摄入的卡路里中只应有33%来自脂肪。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9049','dismal','''dɪzməl','''dɪzm(ə)l','[adj] 阴沉的, 凄凉的n沼泽','The future looks pretty dismal right now.  目前前景似乎相当暗淡。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9050','thicken','''θɪkən','''θɪk(ə)n','[v] (使)变厚, (使)变粗','The fog was beginning to thicken.  雾气渐浓。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9051','courageous','kə''redʒəs','kə''reɪdʒəs','[adj] 勇敢的','He was wrong, and courageous enough to admit it.  他是错了，而且有勇气承认自己错了。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9052','roe','ro','rəʊ','[n] 鱼卵,獐鹿','...cod''s roe.  ...鳕鱼子。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9053','unrecognizable',',ʌnrɛkəɡ''naɪzəbl',',ʌnrekəg''naizəbl','[adj] 未被承认的, 无法识别的','I hadn’t been to the city for 20 years and it was almost unrecognizable.  我已经 20 年没有到过这座城市，几乎认不出来了。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9054','soup','sup','suːp','[n] 汤','homemade tomato soup  自制的番茄汤'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9055','directive','daɪ''rɛktɪv','dɪ''rektɪv; daɪ-','[n] 指示; [adj] 指导的','Thanks to a new directive, food labelling will be more specific.  由于官方的一项新指令，食品标签将会更明确具体。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9056','september','sɛp''tɛmbɚ','sep''tembə','[n] 九月(略作Sep)','Her son, Jerome, was born in September.  她的儿子杰罗姆出生于9月。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9057','unreachable','','','[adj] 不能到达的,  不能得到的','Objects that are unmarked at the end of the mark phase are unreachable by the application (dead) because there''s no path from the root set through any series of references to find them.  标记阶段最后也没有标记的对象是应用程序不可获得的对象（死对象），因为不存在从根集经过任何引用序列找到这些对象的路径。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9058','stew','stu, stju','stjuː','[v] 炖, 焖','stewed apples  炖苹果'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9059','slowness','''slonɪs','','[n] 缓慢, 迟钝','Hard working often counterbalances slowness at learning.  勤奋往往能弥补智力的迟钝。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9060','slavery','''slevəri','''sleɪv(ə)rɪ','[n] 奴隶身分, 奴隶制度','attempts to abolish slavery  废除奴隶制的努力'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9061','herculean',',hə:kju''li:ən; hə''ku:liən',',hə:kju''li:ən; hə''ku:liən','[adj] 极困难的,需要大力气的','a herculean task  艰巨的任务'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9062','colossal','kə''lɑsl','kə''lɒs(ə)l','[adj] 巨大的,  <口>异常的','a colossal statue of the King  国王的巨大雕像'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9063','prudent','''prʊdnt','''pruːd(ə)nt','[adj] 审慎的,小心谨慎的','prudent house buyers  谨慎的购房者'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9064','liable','''laɪəbl','''laɪəb(ə)l','[adj] 有责任的, 易的, 有倾向的','She will grow into a woman particularly liable to depression.  她将变成一个特别易于消沉的女人。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9065','imprisonment','ɪm''prɪznmənt','ɪm''prɪz(ə)nm(ə)nt','[n] 关押,监禁','She was sentenced to seven years'' imprisonment.  她被判处7年监禁。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9066','sour','''saʊɚ','saʊə','[adj] 酸的, 发酵的; [v] 变酸','Rachel sampled the wine. It was sour.  雷切尔尝了尝葡萄酒，是酸的。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9067','treason','''trizn','''triːz(ə)n','[n] 叛逆, 通敌, 背信','The defendant was convicted of high treason (= treason of the worst kind ) and sentenced to death.  被告被判犯有严重叛国罪，并处以死刑。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9068','wold','''wəuld','wəʊld','[n] 无树木的山地, 荒野',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9069','abalone',',æbə''loni',',æbə''ləʊnɪ','[n] [动]鲍鱼(软体动物)','The highly reflective surface and the abalone shell made this photograph a real challenge to take.  高度反光的表面和鲍鱼壳使这张照片的拍摄成为真正的挑战。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9070','mime','maɪm','maɪm','[n] 哑剧; [v] 做哑剧表演','The children learn through role-play, dance and mime.  儿童通过角色表演、舞蹈和哑剧来学习。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9071','dram','dræm','dræm','[n] 液量特兰(药衡系统中的容量单位),  少量','...a dram of whisky.  ...一点威士忌。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9072','desperate','''dɛspərət','''desp(ə)rət','[adj] 不顾一切的, 拚死的, 令人绝望的','I had no money left and was desperate.  我身无分文，已经走投无路了。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9073','retool',',ri''tul','riː''tuːl','[v] 将机械重新整备, 重组','The College Board has retooled the admission exams.  大学委员会重新调整入学考试。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9074','urchin','','''ɜːtʃɪn','[n] 顽童, [动物]刺猥, [动物]海胆','The spines of the omnivorous pencil-spined urchin extend outward from its body.  这个铅笔状的杂食性海胆的刺从它们的身体里伸出来。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9075','relational','rɪ''leʃənl','rɪ''leɪʃ(ə)n(ə)l','[adj] 有关系的, 亲属的','One of these tables contains only traditional relational columns, while the second contains relational columns and one XML column.  这两个表的其中之一仅包含传统的关系列，而另一个包含关系列和一个 XML 列。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9076','demobilize','di''mobəlaɪz','di:''məubilaiz','[v] 使复员, 使退伍, 遣散','programmes to help demobilized soldiers fit into civilian life  帮助复员军人适应平民生活的方案'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9077','bid','bɪd','bɪd','[v] 出价, 投标; [n] 投标,企图','She wanted to bid for it.  她想出价买下它。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9078','palimpsest','''pælɪmpsɛst','''pælɪm(p)sest','[n] 重写本','Some of it is lost, as the DNA palimpsest has been erased and re-written.  它们的一些已经丢失了，因为一些DNA手稿已经被擦去重写。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9079','hermetic','hɝ''mɛtɪk','hɜː''metɪk','[adj] 密封的, 与外界隔绝的','Its film industry operates in its own curiously hermetic way.  它的电影业以奇特而封闭的方式运作。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9080','lust','lʌst','lʌst','[n] 繁殖力, 强烈的性欲; [v] 强烈欲望','My feelings for Lauren were pure lust.  我对劳伦的感觉纯粹是肉欲。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9081','posthumously','''pɔstjuməsli','''pɔstjuməsli','[adv] 在死后','This has been cited as the reason she was not included with the others: The Nobel Prize is not awarded posthumously.  她的死已被引证为她没有和其他三位一起包括在内的原因：人死之后不授予诺贝尔奖。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9082','outfit','''aʊtfɪt','''aʊtfɪt','[n] 用具, 全套装配, vt配备, 装备','She bought a new outfit for the party.  她为了这次派对买了套新衣服。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9083','revolt','rɪ''volt','rɪ''vəʊlt','[v& n] 反抗,反叛','The prime minister is now facing a revolt by members of his own party.  首相现在面临着党内倒戈。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9084','maw','mɔ','mɔː','[n] 动物的胃,口部','The explanation for all this is undoubtedly the open maw and changing dietary habits of the world’s fast-expanding population.  世界肥料行业之所以这么活跃，无疑是因为世界快速增长的人口大开胃口和饮食习惯的改变。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9085','utmost','''ʌt''most','''ʌtməʊst','[n] 极限, 最大可能; [adj] 极度的, 最远的','The medical staff did their utmost(= tried as hard as they could ) to save the patient’s life.  医护人员竭尽全力挽救那位病人的生命。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9086','bryn','','','[n] 布琳',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9087','consistency','kən''sɪstənsi','kən''sɪst(ə)nsɪ','[n] 坚固性, 浓度, 一致性','She scores goals with remarkable consistency.  她以非凡的连贯性进球得分。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9088','sentimentalism',',sɛntə''mɛntl,ɪzəm',',sentɪ''mentəlɪzəm','[n] 感情主义, 沉于情感',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9089','philosophic',',fɪlə''sɑfɪkl',',fɪlə''sɒfɪk','[adj] 哲学的, 哲学家的','But such acuteness is mistaken in the conceit that, when it examines these objects and pronounces what they ought to be, it is dealing with questions of philosophic science.  但是，如果把能够指出周围琐屑事物的不满处与应当处的这一点聪明，便当成在讨论哲学这门科学上的问题，那就错了。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9090','trilogy','''trɪlədʒi','''trɪlədʒɪ','[n] 三部剧, 三部曲','part 2 of a trilogy  三部曲的第二部'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9091','diction','''dɪkʃən','''dɪkʃ(ə)n','[n] 措辞, 用语, 言语',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9092','stylish','''staɪlɪʃ','''staɪlɪʃ','[adj] 时髦的, 漂亮的, 流行的','a stylish woman in her forties  一名40多岁的时髦女子'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9093','embarrass','ɪm''bærəs','ɪm''bærəs; em-','[v] 使困窘, 使局促不安','He didn’t want to embarrass her by asking questions.  他不想提问让她尴尬。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9094','vocation','vo''keʃən','və(ʊ)''keɪʃ(ə)n','[n] 召唤,天职,职业','Her vocation is her work as an actress.  她适合的职业就是当演员。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9095','arena','ə''rinə','ə''riːnə','[n] 竞技场, 舞台','a sports arena  运动场'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9096','waist','west','weɪst','[n] 腰部, 衣服的上身部分','The skirt was too big around the waist.  那条裙子腰围太大。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9097','irritate','''ɪrɪtet','''ɪrɪteɪt','[v] 激怒, 使急躁','It really irritates me when he doesn’t help around the house.  家里的事情他一点都不帮忙，真让我恼火。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9098','storehouses','''stɔrhaʊs','''stɔːhaʊs','[n] 仓库,  储藏所,  宝藏',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9099','uncharted',',ʌn''tʃɑrtɪd','ʌn''tʃɑːtɪd','[adj] 地图上没标明的,未知的','an uncharted island  地图上未标明的岛屿'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9100','hanker','''hæŋkɚ','''hæŋkə','[v] 渴望, 追求','I hankered after a floor-length brown suede coat.  我渴望一件垂地长度的棕色麂皮大衣。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9101','rattlesnake','''rætlsnek','''ræt(ə)lsneɪk','[n] <美>[动]响尾蛇','The rattlesnake tissues provoked the strongest response of all the species in the study.  响尾蛇的组织在本次所有研究物种中所作出的反应最强烈。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9102','glamorous','''glæmərəs','''glæmərəs','[adj] 富有魅力的, 迷人的','She led an exciting and glamorous life.  她生活奢华，充满刺激。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9103','brim','brɪm','brɪm','[n] (杯, 碗等)边, 边缘; [v] 注满','Rain dripped from the brim of his baseball cap.  雨水从他的棒球帽檐上滴下来。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9104','boot','but','buːt','[n] <美> (长统)靴','hiking boots  远足靴'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9105','garb','ɡɑrb','gɑːb','[n] 服装; [v] 装扮','priestly garb  牧师装束'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9106','flannel','''flænl','''flæn(ə)l','[n] 法兰绒(衣服)','a flannel shirt  法兰绒衬衫'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9107','thigh','θaɪ','θaɪ','[n] 大腿, 股','chicken thighs  鸡腿'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9108','collarless','''kɔləlis','','[adj] 无领的,无马轭(或颈圈)的','Originally the collarless shirt and trousers were nondescript, of flannel or wool.  起初无领的衬衫和长裤是没用固定特征的，或者是法兰绒的或者是羊毛的。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9109','cowhand','''kaʊhænd','''koʊ,hænd','[n] <美>(牧场的)牧牛工',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9110','taxonomy','tæk''sɑnəmi','tæk''sɒnəmɪ','[n] 分类法, 分类学','However, some people consider glossary and taxonomy as metadata as well.  不过，有些人认为词汇表和分类法也属于元数据的范畴。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9111','narrower','','','[adj] 有限的, 精密的; [n] 海峡',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9112','waterfall','''wɔtɚfɔl','''wɔːtəfɔːl','[n] 瀑布, 瀑布似的东西','...Angel Falls, the world''s highest waterfall.  …安赫尔瀑布，世界上最高的瀑布。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9113','hibernation','','','[n] 过冬, 冬眠, 避寒','Heart rate tracking for three of the Alaska bears showed a drop from 55 beats per minute on average before hibernation to 14 erratic ones per minute in winter.  对三头阿拉斯加的黑熊的心率追踪显示出它们在冬眠前的平均每分钟 55 下降低到了冬天里每分钟飘忽不定的 14 下。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9114','evenness','','','[n] 平均, 平等, 平坦',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9115','poikilotherm','','','[n] [动]变温动物,冷血动物','Fish are poikilotherm whose body temperature changes as the ambient water temperature changes.  鱼类是变温动物，其体温随环境的水温变化而变化。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9116','unload','''ʌn''lod','ʌn''ləʊd','[v] 卸货; [v] 摆脱之负担','Unload everything from the boat and clean it thoroughly.  从小船上卸下所有的货物并彻底地清洗。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9117','depositor','dɪ''pɑzɪtɚ','dɪ''pɒzɪtə','[n] 寄托者, 存款人','Notice that the St. Louis memo tiptoes around the question of telling a depositor that he has a demand deposit while telling the rest of the country that he has a time deposit.  请注意，圣路易斯储备银行的备忘录一直在一个问题上遮遮掩掩，那就是把存款人的活期存款说成定期存款，欺骗国人。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9118','lyrically','','','[adv] 抒情地,  狂热地','He lyrically described the countryside around his home.  他以抒情的笔调描绘了住宅周围的乡村景致。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9119','theatrically','','','[adv] 戏剧化地','He theatrically turned his head to watch a butterfly flutter by.  他戏剧化的转头看飞过的蝴蝶。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9120','splinter','''splɪntɚ','''splɪntə','[n] 尖片, 碎片; [v] 分裂','I’ve got a splinter in my finger.  我的手指扎了一根刺。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9121','tonnage','''tʌnɪdʒ','''tʌnɪdʒ','[n] 登记吨位, 排水量','A huge tonnage of bombs has already been dropped on the area.  巨大吨数的炸弹已被投到该地区。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9122','seagoing','''sɪ''goɪŋ','''siːgəʊɪŋ','[adj] 适于远航的,出海的','a seagoing ship  远洋轮'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9123','jacket','''dʒækɪt','''dʒækɪt','[n] 夹克,护封; [v] 给穿夹克','...a black leather jacket.  …一件黑色皮夹克。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9124','fisherman','''fɪʃɚmən','''fɪʃəmən','[n] 渔民, 渔夫','The Algarve is a paradise for fishermen whether river anglers or deep-sea fishermen.  阿尔加维对河边的垂钓者或深海的渔民都是一个天堂。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9125','mainsheet','''men,ʃit','''meɪnʃiːt','[n] 主桅帆操纵索',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9126','oblivious','ə''blɪvɪəs','ə''blɪvɪəs','[adj] 没注意到, 健忘的','She lay motionless where she was, oblivious to pain.  她一动不动地躺在原地，感觉不到疼痛。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9127','coaming','''komɪŋ','''kəʊmɪŋ','[n] 舱口栏板, 边材','The acetic acid is corrosive. Please put them in both sides of No. 5 deck, leaving a passage between the hatch coaming and the cargo.  醋酸（乙酸）有腐蚀性，请把其装在五舱甲板两边，在货物和舱口围板间留一条通道。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9128','lad','læd','læd','[n] 少年, 青年男子','a young lad  小伙子'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9129','tilt','tɪlt','tɪlt','[v] (使)倾斜, 以言词或文字抨击','My mother tilted her head and smiled.  我妈妈歪着头笑了。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9130','choppy','''tʃɑpi','''tʃɒpɪ','[adj] （海等）波浪起伏的, (指风)不断改变方向的','The small boat bobbed about on the choppy water.  小船在波浪起伏的水面上颠簸。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9131','illustrator','''ɪləstretɚ','''ɪləstreɪtə','[n] 插图画家,说明者','Called up for military service, Mr. Marokvia spent the war as an illustrator for the Wehrmacht, applying brush and pencil in Ukraine, Italy, Finland and Yugoslavia.  玛洛克维亚先生被征召入伍，他作为一名德国国防军的插图画家，在乌克兰、意大利、芬兰和南斯拉夫留下了自己的墨迹。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9132','ectothermic','','','[n] 变温动物','Determination of death in ectothermic animals may be more difficult due to differences in their physiology.  断定因安乐死死亡的动物可能更为困难因为不同的动物有不同的生理情况。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9133','poikilothermic','','','[adj] [动]变温的, 冷血动物的','Unlike most terrestrial animals, aquatic animal species used for human consumption are poikilothermic, meaning their body temperatures vary according to ambient temperatures.  与大多数陆地动物不同，供人类消费的水生动物为冷血品种，也就是说它们的体温会根据环境温度而变化。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9134','locomote','','','[v] 移动, 行动','Since plants cannot locomote , the sensation of experiencing pain would be superfluous. Thus, plants differ completely physiologically from mammals.  由于植物无法移动，它们不太需要具备感知痛苦的能力，因此，植物与哺乳动物在生理上全然不同。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9135','inadequately','','','[adv] 不够地,  不够好',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9136','onetime','','','[adj] 从前的,  一度的; [adv] 从前','The onetime heir apparent had played an instrumental role this year in propping up his father''s rule and his crackdown against the rebellion that ultimately ended his 42-year grip on power.  曾一度作为卡扎菲继承人的赛义夫今年在巩固其父亲的统治并帮助镇压反抗武装一事中起到积极作用。 这场反抗活动最终结束了卡扎菲对利比亚42年的统治。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9137','citation','saɪ''teʃən','saɪ''teɪʃ(ə)n','[n] 引用,表扬','...a 50-minute manifesto with citations from the Koran.  …一段长达50分钟、带有《古兰经》引文的宣言。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9138','stillness','''stɪlnəs','''stɪlnɪs','[n] 静止, 沉静','This is your true nature, one of effortless peace and stillness.  这就是你的本质，一个完全不需费力的平静和静止。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9139','eyesight','''aɪsaɪt','''aɪsaɪt','[n] 视力, 目力','He had a problem with his eyesight.  他的视力有问题。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9140','comical','''kɑmɪkl','''kɒmɪk(ə)l','[adj] 好笑的, 滑稽的','The note of pure panic in his voice was almost comical.  他那种十分慌张的口气几乎有点滑稽。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9141','mollusk','''mɔləsk','''mɒləsk','[n] [动]软体动物','Atype of mollusk, the lined chiton has colorful lines on its valves andwhite or yellow spots or bands on its girdle.  条纹石鳖是一种软体动物，瓣膜上有彩色条纹，条带上有白色或黄色斑点或环状物。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9142','rediscover',',ridɪ''skʌvɚ','riːdɪ''skʌvə','[v] 重新发现','...a one-time rebel who had rediscovered his faith.  ...重新发现了自己信仰的一个曾经的反叛者。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9143','eminent','''ɛmɪnənt','''emɪnənt','[adj] 著名的,  卓越的','an eminent lawyer  杰出的律师'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9144','bleak','blik','bliːk','[adj] 寒冷的,荒凉的, 黯淡的','a bleak January afternoon  一月里一个阴冷的下午'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9145','silence','''saɪləns','''saɪləns','[n] 寂静, 沉默; [v] 使沉默','There was a brief silence before anyone answered.  沉默了片刻才有人回答。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9146','sequester','sɪ''kwɛstɚ','sɪ''kwestə','[v] 使隐退, 扣押, 没收',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9147','metazoan',',mɛtə''zoən',',metə''zəʊən','[n&a] [动]后生动物(的)','As the scientists conclude: "Our results expand the known metazoan bio-sphere and demonstrate that deep ecosystems are more complex than previously accepted.  科学家总结道：“我们的研究结果扩展了已知的后生生物圈的范围，并揭示出，深层生态系统比我们之前想象的要复杂。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9148','abreast','ə''brɛst','ə''brest','[adv] 并肩地, 并排地','As the car drew abreast of him, Jack suddenly recognised the driver.  那辆车追上来与杰克并行时，他一下子就认出了驾车的人。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9149','serum','''sɪrəm','''sɪərəm','[n] 浆液, 血清','...painful injections of anti-cancer serum.  …令人痛苦的抗癌血清注射。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9150','adrenaline','æˈdrɛnəˌlɪn','ə''drenəlɪn','[n] 肾上腺素(使激动兴奋等)','But for some people merely imagining this scene creates an adrenaline surge.  但是对于某些人但是想象这一幕就会肾上腺素激增。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9151','milieu','mi''ljɜː','''miːljɜː; mɪ''ljɜː','[n] 周围, 环境','Proust’s work reflected his own social and cultural milieu.  普鲁斯特的作品反映了其所在的社会和文化背景。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9152','compensatory','kəm''pɛnsə,tori','kɒmpen''seɪtərɪ','[adj] 赔偿的, 补偿的','She was awarded a large sum in compensatory damages .  她得到了一大笔损失赔偿金。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9153','unconventional',',ʌnkən''vɛnʃənl','ʌnkən''venʃ(ə)n(ə)l','[adj] 非传统的, 不合惯例的','Linus Pauling is an unconventional genius.  莱纳斯·鲍林是个奇才。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9154','gibe','','dʒaib','[v] 嘲笑,讥笑; [n] 嘲笑','“Please don’t gibe me,” Lydia said.  “请不要嘲笑我，”利迪娅说。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9155','proprietor','prə''praɪətɚ','prə''praɪətə','[n] 所有者, 经营者','For example, many states require a sole proprietor to use their own name for the business name unless they formally file another name as a trade name, or fictitious name.  举例来说，许多国家要求独资经营者使用自己的名称为业务名称，除非他们正式文件中有另一个名字作为商标名或化名。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9156','mess','mɛs','mes','[n] 混乱, 脏乱; [v] 弄乱','What a mess!  太乱了！'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9157','silly','''sɪli','''sɪlɪ','[adj] 愚蠢的, 可笑的','Stop asking silly questions.  别再问傻问题了。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9158','metric','''mɛtrɪk','''metrɪk','[adj] 米制的, 公制的','a metric tonne  一公吨'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9159','lintel','''lɪntl','''lɪnt(ə)l','[n] [建]楣, 过梁',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9160','untapped',',ʌn''tæpt','ʌn''tæpt','[adj] 塞子未开的, 未使用的','Older people are an untapped resource in the employment market.  年龄较大的人是就业市场中有待利用的资源。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9161','mysteriously','mɪs''tɪrɪəsli','mis''tiəriəsli','[adv] 神秘地,  故弄玄虚地',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9162','corral','kə''ræl','kə''rɑːl','[n] 畜栏; [v] 关进畜栏','They corralled the cattle before loading them onto the truck.  他们在把牛装上车以前，先把牛赶入了畜栏。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9163','prevention','pri''vɛnʃən','prɪ''venʃn','[n] 预防, 防止','a fire prevention officer  消防官员'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9164','playwright','''pleraɪt','''pleɪraɪt','[n] 剧作家','The playwright does something remarkable in this scene, but without any impression of straining after an effect.  剧作家在这场中有许多惊人妙笔，但并不给人留下竭力追求表面效果的印象。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9165','Cuban','''kju:bən','','[n] 古巴人; [adj] 古巴(人)的','But he says pressure for broad reform on the next Cuban leader, from inside Cuba and outside, will grow.  可是他说，来自古巴境内和境外要求古巴下任领导人进行广泛改革的压力将会增加。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9166','char','tʃɑr','tʃɑː','[v] 烧焦; [n] 碳','Roast the peppers until the skin begins to char and blister.  把这些辣椒烤到表皮发黑起泡为止。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9167','tavernkeeper','','','[n] 小餐馆老板',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9168','upgrade',',ʌp''ɡred','ʌp''greɪd','[n] 升级, 上升; [v] 使升级, 提升; [adv] 往上','...equipment which needs expensive upgrades.  …需要进行昂贵升级的设备。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9169','incident','''ɪnsɪdənt','''ɪnsɪd(ə)nt','[n] 事件; [adj] 附带的, 易于发生的','Am I at risk because of some incident in my sexual past?  我过去性生活中的某件事会使我处于危险境地吗？'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9170','slavish','''slevɪʃ','''sleɪvɪʃ','[adj] 奴隶的, 盲从的, 专横的','a slavish adherence to the rules  对规章的盲目遵从'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9171','emotive','ɪ''motɪv','ɪ''məʊtɪv','[adj] 感情的, 引起强烈感情的','Embryo research is an emotive issue.  胚胎研究是个让人情绪激动的问题。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9172','physic','''fɪzɪk','''fɪzɪk','[n] 医术; [vt] 治愈','Furthermore, there are entity models created by polygon mesh in many applications such as cartoon, vision environment, network browse, physic scanning, computer games.  此外，在动画、虚拟环境、网络浏览、医学扫描、计算机游戏等领域已经可以看到许多由多边形网格构建的实体模型。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9173','synapsis','si''næpsis','sɪ''næpsɪs','[n] [生]染色体结合, 突触',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9174','unsophisticated',',ʌnsə''fɪstɪketɪd','ʌnsə''fɪstɪkeɪtɪd','[adj] 不谙世故的, 不复杂的','an unsophisticated audience  老土的观众'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9175','unspoiled','''ʌn''spɔɪld',',ʌn''spɔild','[adj] 未损坏的, 未宠坏的','unspoiled countryside  未遭到破坏的乡村'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9176','arthritis','ɑr''θraɪtɪs','ɑː''θraɪtɪs','[n] 关节炎','I have a touch of arthritis in the wrist.  我的手腕有轻微关节炎。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9177','whim','wɪm','wɪm','[n] 一时的兴致, 奇想','On arrival, she buys a glass factory on a whim, and challenges him to transport a church built entirely of glass by boat from Sydney 250 miles up the coast.  到达目的地后，她突发奇想买了一个玻璃厂，并向他挑战，让他用船沿着 250 英里长的海岸线从悉尼运来建造一整座玻璃教堂。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9178','hospitable','hɑ''spɪtəbl','hɒ''spɪtəb(ə)l; ''hɒspɪt-','[adj] 好客的, 宜人的','The local people were very kind and hospitable.  当地人非常友好热情。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9179','carnivorous','kɑrˈnɪvərəs','kɑː''nɪv(ə)rəs','[adj] 食肉的, 肉食性的','Snakes are carnivorous.  蛇都是食肉动物。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9180','depredation',',dɛprə''deʃən',',deprɪ''deɪʃ(ə)n','[n] 掠夺, 破坏痕迹','Much of the region''s environmental depredation is a result of poor planning.  这个地区的环境破坏大都是规划不周的结果。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9181','nostalgia','nə''stældʒə','nɒ''stældʒə','[n] 乡愁, 怀旧之情','He might be influenced by nostalgia for the surroundings of his happy youth.  他也许被他对快乐青年时代的环境的怀念影响了。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9182','stewpot','''stjʊ,pɑt','''stjuːpɒt','[n] 双把炖锅','A hungry wolf''s attempts to fatten a chicken for his stewpot have unexpected results.  一条饥饿的狼想把鸡养肥来做炖鸡，却产生了意想不到的结果。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9183','adolescence',',ædə''lɛsns','ædə''les(ə)ns','[n] 青春期','Some young people suddenly become self-conscious and tongue-tied in early adolescence.  一些年青人在青春期早期突然变得害羞结舌。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9184','ministry','''mɪnɪstri','''mɪnɪstrɪ','[n] (政府的)部门','...the Ministry of Justice.  …司法部。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9185','Toronto','tə''rɑnto','təˈrɒntəʊ','[n] 多伦多（加拿大）','Julia: What can you do in Toronto?  朱莉娅：在多伦多能玩些什么？'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9186','narrowly','''næroli','''nærəʊlɪ','[adv] 勉强地, 精细地','He was narrowly defeated in the election.  他在选举中以微弱差距败北。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9187','proficiency','prə''fɪʃənsi','prə''fɪʃ(ə)nsɪ','[n] 熟练, 精通, 熟练程度','I brought her proficiency up to the required level.  我把她的熟练程度提高到所规定的水平。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9188','spar','spɑr','spɑː','[n] 争论,园材(如桅,桁等)','Meanwhile, industry, civil society groups and governments continue to spar over the application of intellectual property rights to products and genetic sequences derived from natural resources.  其间，工业、民间社会团体以及政府持续对申请产品和得自自然资源的基因序列的知识产权问题产生争论。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9189','hometown','''homtaʊn','''həʊm''taʊn','[n] 故乡','Do you like your hometown?  你喜欢你的家乡吗？'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9190','sociology',',sosɪ''ɑlədʒi','səʊsɪ''ɒlədʒɪ; səʊʃɪ-','[n] 社会学','Out with every theory of human behavior, from linguistics to sociology.  从语言学、社会学的人类行为原理里解脱吧。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9191','dough','do','dəʊ','[n] 生面团','Add some raisins to the dough.  在生面团中加一些葡萄干。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9192','flair','flɛr','fleə','[n] 才能, 本领','Jo has a flair for languages.  乔有语言天赋。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9193','esoteric',',ɛsə''tɛrɪk',',esə''terɪk; ,iːsə-','[adj] 秘传的,  神秘的,  难懂的','...esoteric knowledge.  …深奥难懂的知识。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9194','potion','''poʃən','''pəʊʃ(ə)n','[n] 一服, 一剂','...a magic potion that will make Siegfried forget Brunnhilde and fall in love with Gutrune.  …一种会使齐格弗里德忘掉布伦希德尔德而爱上古特鲁内娜的魔剂。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9195','laboriously','','','[adv] 艰难地,  辛勤地',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9196','elixir','ɪ''lɪksɚ','ɪ''lɪksə; -sɪə','[n] 炼金药, 不老长寿药','the search for the elixir of life  寻找长生不老药'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9197','inextricably','ˌɪnɪkˈstrɪkəbli','ˌɪnɪkˈstrɪkəbli','[adv] 分不开地, 无法摆脱地','Our survival is inextricably linked to the survival of the rainforest.  我们的生存与雨林的生存息息相关。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9198','imprecise','''ɪmprɪ''saɪs','ɪmprɪ''saɪs','[adj] 不精确的','vague imprecise estimates  粗略的、不精确的估计'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9199','bestow','bɪ''sto','bɪ''stəʊ','[v] 给予,利用','The United States bestowed honorary citizenship upon England''s World War II prime minister, Sir Winston Churchill.  美国授予了二战期间的英国首相温斯顿·丘吉尔爵士荣誉公民的称号。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9200','bless','blɛs','bles','[v] 祝福, 保佑','He’s always willing to help. Bless him!  他一向乐于助人，愿上帝保佑他！'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9201','quaker','''kweikə','''kweikə','[n] 教友派信徒, 贵格会会员',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9202','alternately','''ɔltɚnɪtli','ɔːl''tɜːnɪtlɪ','[adv] 交替地,轮流地','The idea is that if a gravitational wave passes through GEO600, it will alternately stretch space in one direction and squeeze it in another.  其基本原理是，当引力波经过GEO600时，它将交替地在一个方向上拉伸空间，在另一个方向上挤压空间。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9203','thermodynamic',',θɝmodaɪ''næmɪks',',θɜːməʊdaɪ''næmɪk','[adj] 热力学的, 使用热动力的','After that, the formalism of statistical mechanics takes over, and calculates partition functions and thermodynamic functions.  从那以后，都是统计力学的内容，计算配分函数,和热力学函数。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9204','uncrumple','','','[vt] 去掉…的皱纹,使回复到平整状态',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9205','dinner','''dɪnɚ','''dɪnə','[n] 正餐, 宴会','What time do you usually have dinner?  你通常什么时候吃饭？'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9206','untwist','ʌn''twɪst','ʌn''twɪst','[v] 拆开(搓合的绳,线等), 解开','Allow any part of the subtle bodies that is twisted to untwist and separate from any other that one is intertwined with.  允许精细身体中扭曲的任何部分解开扭曲，从混杂在一起的其它部分中分离开来。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9207','selfless','sɛlflɪs','''selflɪs','[adj] 无私的','selfless devotion to their work  他们对工作的无私奉献'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9208','obligation',',ɑblɪ''ɡeʃən','ɒblɪ''geɪʃ(ə)n','[n] 义务, 职责, 债务','Employers have an obligation to treat all employees equally.  雇主有责任对所有员工一视同仁。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9209','fanatical','fə''nætikl','fə''nætɪkəl','[adj] 狂热的, 入迷的','He is a fanatical fan of Mozart.  他是一名莫扎特音乐的狂热爱好者。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9210','coax','koks','kəʊks','[v] 巧妙地（耐心地）处理,哄','‘Please, Vic, come with us,’ Nancy coaxed.  “求你了，维克，跟我们一起去吧。”南希哄劝道。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9211','flue','flu','fluː','[n] 烟道, 暖气管',''),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9212','pivot','''pɪvət','''pɪvət','[n] 枢轴; [v] 在枢轴上转动','The pedal had sheared off at the pivot.  这个踏板已经在轴处断裂。'),
('TOEFL_2','TOEFL_2_9213','coordination','ko,ɔrdɪ''neʃən','kəu,ɔ:di''neiʃən','[n] 协调','Too much alcohol affects your coordination.  喝酒太多会影响你动作的协调。'),
('CET4_3','CET4_3_1','cancel','''kænsl','''kænsl','[vt] 取消， 撤销； 删去','Our flight was cancelled.  我们的航班取消了。'),
('CET4_3','CET4_3_2','explosive','ɪk''splosɪv; ɪk''splozɪv','ɪk''spləusɪv','[adj] 爆炸的； 极易引起争论的; [n] 炸药','Because the gas is highly explosive, it needs to be kept in high-pressure containers.  由于这种气体极易爆炸，因此需要保存在高压容器内。'),
('CET4_3','CET4_3_3','numerous','''numərəs','''njuːmərəs','[adj] 众多的','Numerous attempts have been made to hide the truth.  为掩盖事实作了很多尝试。'),
('CET4_3','CET4_3_4','govern','''ɡʌvɚn','''gʌvn','[vi] 居支配地位， 占优势; [vt] 统治，治理，支配','the leaders who govern the country  治理这个国家的领导人'),
('CET4_3','CET4_3_5','analyse','''æn(ə)laɪz','''ænəlaɪz','[vt] 分析； 分解； 解析','She still needs to analyse the data.  她仍需要分析这些数据。'),
('CET4_3','CET4_3_6','discourage','dɪs''kɝɪdʒ','dɪs''kʌrɪdʒ','[vt] 使泄气， 使灰心； 阻止， 劝阻','You should not let one failure discourage you.  你不该失败一次就灰心丧气。'),
('CET4_3','CET4_3_7','resemble','rɪ''zɛmbl','rɪ''zembl','[vt] 像， 类似于','It’s amazing how closely Brian and Steve resemble each other.  布赖恩和史蒂夫真是惊人地相像。'),
('CET4_3','CET4_3_8','remote','rɪ''mot','rɪ''məut','[adj] 遥远的； 偏僻的； 关系疏远的； 脱离的； 微乎其微的； 孤高的， 冷淡的； 遥控的','a remote border town  一个偏远的边境小镇'),
('CET4_3','CET4_3_9','salary','''sæləri','''sæləri','[n] 薪金， 薪水','The average salary for a teacher is $39,000 a year.  教师的平均工资是39,000美元一年。'),
('CET4_3','CET4_3_10','pollution','pə''luʃən','pə''luːʃn','[n] 污染， 污染物','California’s tough anti-pollution laws  加利福尼亚州严厉的反污染法'),
('CET4_3','CET4_3_11','pretend','prɪ''tɛnd','prɪ''tend','[vt] 装作， 假装','Let’s pretend we’re on the moon.  我们假装自己是在月球上吧。'),
('CET4_3','CET4_3_12','kettle','''kɛtl','''ketl','[n] 水壶','She filled the kettle and switched it on.  她把水壶灌满，打开了开关。'),
('CET4_3','CET4_3_13','wreck','rɛk','rek','[n] 失事；残骸；精神或身体已垮的人; [vt] 破坏','He was still alive when they pulled him from the wreck.  他们把他从失事的车辆中拖出来时，他还活着。'),
('CET4_3','CET4_3_14','drunk','drʌŋk','drʌŋk','[adj] 醉的； 陶醉的','You’re drunk.  你喝醉了。'),
('CET4_3','CET4_3_15','calculate','''kælkjulet','''kælkjuleɪt','[vt] 计算； 估计； 计划','These instruments calculate distances precisely.  这些仪器计算距离非常精确。'),
('CET4_3','CET4_3_16','persistent','pə''zɪstənt','pə''sɪstənt','[adj] 坚持的， 不屈不挠的； 持续不断的； 反复出现的','persistent rumours  持续流传的谣言'),
('CET4_3','CET4_3_17','sake','sek','seɪk','[n] 缘故， 理由','He moved to the seaside for the sake of his health.  他为了健康而迁居海滨。'),
('CET4_3','CET4_3_18','conceal','kən''sil','kən''siːl','[vt] 把…隐藏起来， 掩盖， 隐瞒','The shadows concealed her as she crept up to the house.  她借着阴影蹑手蹑脚地走向房子。'),
('CET4_3','CET4_3_19','audience','''ɔdɪəns','''ɔːdiəns','[n] 听众， 观众， 读者','The audience began clapping and cheering.  观众开始鼓掌欢呼。'),
('CET4_3','CET4_3_20','meanwhile','''minwaɪl','''miːnwaɪl','[adv] 与此同时','Cook the sauce over a medium heat until it thickens. Meanwhile start boiling the water for the pasta.  用中火把调味汁煮到变稠，同时烧水准备煮意大利面。'),
('CET4_3','CET4_3_21','possess','pə''zɛs','pə''zes','[vt] 占用， 拥有','Different workers possess different skills.  不同的工人拥有不同技能。'),
('CET4_3','CET4_3_22','competent','''kɑmpɪtənt','''kɒmpɪtənt','[adj] 有能力的， 能胜任的','A competent mechanic should be able to fix the problem.  一名合格的机修工应该能够解决这个问题。'),
('CET4_3','CET4_3_23','investment','ɪn''vɛstmənt','ɪn''vestmənt','[n] 投资， 投资额； 投入','We plan to buy some property as an investment.  我们打算买些房地产作为投资。'),
('CET4_3','CET4_3_24','neutral','''nʊtrəl','''njuːtrəl','[adj] 中立的； 中性的','I always tried to remain neutral when they started arguing.  他们争论起来的时候我总是努力保持中立。'),
('CET4_3','CET4_3_25','scratch','skrætʃ','skrætʃ','[v] 抓，搔，扒；刮，擦；刻出; [n] 抓痕， 划痕； 抓， 搔， 刮','John yawned and scratched his leg.  约翰打了个呵欠，挠了挠腿。'),
('CET4_3','CET4_3_26','optional','''ɑpʃənl','''ɒpʃənl','[adj] 可以任选的','three optional courses  三门选修课'),
('CET4_3','CET4_3_27','require','rɪ''kwaɪr','rɪ''kwaɪə','[vt] 需要； 要求； 命令','Campbell’s broken leg will probably require surgery.  坎贝尔的一条腿骨折，可能需要手术。'),
('CET4_3','CET4_3_28','circular','''sɝkjəlɚ','''sɜːkjələ','[adj] 圆的；循环的；兜圈子的; [n] 通知， 通告','a circular table  圆桌'),
('CET4_3','CET4_3_29','analysis','ə''næləsɪs','ə''næləsɪs','[n] 分析， 分析报告； 分解； 解析','She’s been in analysis for three years.  她接受精神分析治疗已经三年了。'),
('CET4_3','CET4_3_30','click','klɪk','klɪk','[v] 发出咔嗒声；点击; [n] 咔嗒声','The door clicked shut behind me.  门在我身后咔嗒一声关上了。'),
('CET4_3','CET4_3_31','fashionable','''fæʃnəbl','''fæʃnəbl','[adj] 流行的， 时髦的','Strong colours are very fashionable at the moment.  眼下流行艳丽的色彩。'),
('CET4_3','CET4_3_32','devise','dɪ''vaɪz','dɪ''vaɪz','[vt] 设计， 发明','She devised a method for quicker communications between offices.  她想出一种加快办公室之间通信联络的方法。'),
('CET4_3','CET4_3_33','apparent','ə''pærənt','ə''pærənt','[adj] 表面上的， 明显的','The difference in quality was immediately apparent .  质量的差异显而易见。'),
('CET4_3','CET4_3_34','journalist','ˈdʒɝ​nlɪst','''dʒɜːnəlɪst','[n] 新闻工作者， 新闻记者','a well-known journalist and broadcaster  一位著名的新闻记者兼播音员'),
('CET4_3','CET4_3_35','exposure','ɪk''spoʒɚ','ɪk''spəuʒə','[n] 暴露， 揭露； 曝光','Exposure to lead is known to damage the brains of young children.  已知接触铅会损害幼童的大脑。'),
